hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"38077","(38077) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: A man from his children said: Al-Du'al ibn Bakr: I wish I had seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and heard from him, so he said to a man: Go with him. He said: I am afraid that Khuza’a will kill me. So he remained silent until he set off, and a man from Khuza’a met him and he recognized him and struck him. He stabbed him with a sword and said: I told you that they would kill me. That was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up. So he thanked God and praised him, then he said: Indeed, God has made Mecca sacred, but the people have not made it unlawful, rather it has been made lawful for me for an hour of Day, and after the Sacred Mosque, and the enemies of people against God are three: he who kills therein, or kills someone other than the killer, or asks for his departure. The pre-Islamic era, let us condemn this man.\n Amr bin Murrah said: So I narrated this hadith to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and I said: May God protect you, and he said: May God protect you."
"38078","(38078) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaidullah Bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in the year of the conquest, when Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib came to him with Abu Sufyan, and he converted to Islam by passing Al-Dhahran, and Al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves this kind of pride, so if you would make something for him? He said, yes, whoever enters Abu Sufyan’s house is safe, and whoever closes his door is safe.\n(Abu Dawud 3015, Bayhaqi 3016)"
"38079","(38079) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: This is a sanctuary, meaning Mecca. God made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and placed these two It was not permissible for anyone before me, nor is it permissible for anyone after me, and it was not permissible for me except for an hour of the day, not supported by its thorns. And its hunting will not be dispersed, nor will its cells be taken apart, nor will its flocks be raised except for a vocalist. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, indeed The people of Mecca are impatient to provide for their livelihood and their buildings, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Except Al-Idhkhar (Daraqutni 235. Tahawi 260)"
"38080","(38080) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: When Mecca was conquered, he went up Bilal entered the house and gave the call to prayer, and Safwan bin Umayyah said to Al-Harith bin Hisham: Don’t you see this servant? Al-Harith said: If God hates it and changes it."
"38081","(38081) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Bilal gave the call to prayer on the Day of Conquest above the Kaaba."
"38082","(38082) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The Prophet came out, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in the year of conquest, from Medina eight thousand or ten thousand, and from the people of Mecca two thousand. (Ibn Saad 139)"
"38083","(38083) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Mara The servant of Aqeel bin Abi Talib, on the authority of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, opened In Mecca, two men from my relatives from Banu Makhzum fled to me. She said: So I hid them in my house, and my brother Ali came in. Ibn Abi Talib, and he said: I will kill them both. She said: So I closed the door on them, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted the highest place in Mecca, while he was bathing in his eyelid. Indeed, there were traces of dough in it, and his daughter Fatima was covering it.\n When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished washing, he took a garment and wrapped himself in it, then he prayed eight rak’ahs of the sacrifice. Then he came back and said: Welcome, Umm Hani. What brings you? She said: I said: O Prophet of God, two men from my close-in-laws fled to me, so Ali bin Abi Talib entered and claimed that he had killed them. He said: No, we have rewarded whomever you have rewarded, O Umm Hani, and we have protected whomever you have believed."
"38084","(38084) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: When this surah was revealed: {When God’s victory and conquest come}, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read it until he concluded it, and said: The people are isolated, and I and my companions are isolated, and he said: No. He performed emigration after the conquest, but it was jihad and intention. So Marwan said to him: You lied, and with him were Zayd bin Thabit and Rafi’ bin Khadij, and they were sitting with him on the bed, so he said Abu Sa`id: If these two had wanted, they would have told you, but this man fears that you will remove him from the divination of his people, and this man fears To deprive him of the truth. They remained silent, then Marwan raised the stone to hit him. When they saw that, they said: He spoke the truth. (Ahmad 22. Tabarani 4444)"
"38085","(38085) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no emigration after the conquest, but it is jihad and intention, and when you are mobilized, then mobilize. (Bukhari 1587, Muslim 986)"
"38086","(38086) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Umm Yahya bint Ali, on the authority of My father, he said: I brought my father on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and I said: O Messenger of God, this man is pledging his allegiance to you on the island. He said: No emigration after the conquest, but rather jihad and intention."
"38087","(38087) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No emigration after the conquest, but jihad and intention. (Bukhari 3080, Muslim 1488)"
"38088","(38088) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Mujashi’ bin Masoud, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless me and my brother. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God: Give us the pledge of allegiance to migrate. He said: The Hijra has passed. To her family, so I said: Why do we pledge allegiance to you, O Messenger of God? He said: On Islam and jihad. He said: So I met his brother and asked him? He said: Mujasha spoke the truth. (Bukhari 2962, Muslim 1487)"
"38089","(38089) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fasted in the year of the conquest until he reached al-Kadaid, then he broke his fast. Rather, the last part of the verb is taken into account. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"38090","(38090) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed for fifteen days where he conquered Mecca, shortening the prayer until he went to Hunayn."
"38091","(38091) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Mecca on the day of the conquest of Mecca. The people were safe except four. (Daraqutni 167)"
"38092","(38092) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: {Indeed, We have opened for you a clear conquest} until the end of the verses, a reference from Al-Hudaybiyah, and his companions were mixed with him. Sadness and depression. He said: A verse was revealed to me that is dearer to me than the world and all that is in it. So when the Messenger of God recited it, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A man from among the people said: Good and innocent. God has made clear what He will do to you, so what will He do to us? Then God revealed the following verses: {That He may admit the believing men and believing women to Gardens beneath which rivers flow} until He concluded The verse\n(Bukhari 4172, Muslim 1413)"
"38093","(38093) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Makhoul narrated to us; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca, the jinn met him with evil and threw evil at him, so Gabriel said: Seek refuge with me. Muhammad, so he sought refuge with those words, and they were turned away from him, and he said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither righteousness nor An immoral person, from the evil of what descends from the heavens and what ascends therein, and from the evil of what is spread on the earth and what emerges from it, and from the evil of the night. And the daylight, and from the evil of every one who knocks, except the one who knocks with goodness, O Most Merciful."
"38094","(38094) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, he said: Khaled bin Al-Walid on Al-Lat, and he said:\nO glory of Your disbelief, no, Glory be to You\nIndeed, I saw that God had insulted you (Tabarani 3811)"
"38095","(38095) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Safr, he said: When a messenger entered God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Shayba bin Uthman for the key, the key to the Kaaba, so he hesitated and said to Omar: Get up and go with him. If he brings her, otherwise, lash his head. He said: Then he brought her. He said: Then he placed her in his lap. And Shaybah was standing, he said: Then Shaybah cried, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Break her thighs, for God has been satisfied with it for you in the pre-Islamic era and in Islam."
"38096","(38096) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’, on the authority of Ibn Sabit; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Othman bin Talha the key from behind the garment."
"38097","(38097) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah. Ibn Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left in the year of the conquest, ten days before Ramadan.\n(Ahmad 315. Ibn Saad 137)"
"38098","(38098) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the statues around the Kaaba be obliterated on the day of the conquest of Mecca."
"38099","(38099) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah in the year of the conquest of the scarab, and when he completed his Umrah, he appointed Abu Bakr as the successor. Mecca, and commanded him to teach the people the rituals, and to announce to the people: Whoever performs Hajj in the year is safe, and should not perform Hajj after the year. A polytheist, and no one should circumambulate the Kaaba naked."
"38100","(38100) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdul Hamid bin Jafar told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata’ On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace in the year of the conquest, saying: Indeed, God and His Messenger are sacred. He sold wine, pigs, dead bodies, and idols. He said: Then a man said: O Messenger of God, what do you see in the fat of dead bodies? So ships and hides are anointed with it and people use it in the morning? He said: God fought the Jews. When God forbade their fat, they took it, bulked it up, then sold it and ate it. Our prices"
"38101","(38101) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Usama ibn Zayd informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Azhar said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest, and I, a young boy, was asking about the house of Khalid bin Al-Walid, a drinker was brought to them, and he ordered them to hit him with whatever was on their hands. Some of them struck with a whip and a sandal. And with a stick, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, threw dust on him. When Abu Bakr was there, a drinker was brought to him and he asked his companions: How many times did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hit the one he struck? So forty people attacked him, so Abu Bakr struck forty people. (Bayhaqi 320, Ahmad 88)"
"38102","(38102) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Uqil, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amr bin Abd al-Rahman ibn Umayyah, the son of my brother Ali ibn Muniyah, that his father told him that Ali said: I came as a messenger May God bless him and grant him peace upon my father, Umayyah, on the day of the conquest. I said: O Messenger of God, give my father the pledge of allegiance on the Hijra. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, I pledge allegiance to him on the basis of jihad, for the migration has ended. (Nasa’i 7791, Ahmad 223)"
"38103","(38103) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of The loose one; Before Islam, he used to participate in trade with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when it was the day of the conquest he came to him. He said: Welcome to my brother and partner. He did not care or ignore me, Sa’ib. You were doing some work in... The pre-Islamic era will not be accepted from you, but today it will be accepted from you. And he was a predecessor and a relative. (Ahmad 425. Hakim 61)"
"38104","(38104) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, who said: On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered May God bless him and grant him peace from the top of Mecca, and Khalid bin Al-Walid entered from the bottom of Mecca. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Do not kill. So he put his hand in killing and said: What made you do what you did? He said: O Messenger of God, I cannot do anything except what I have done."
"38105","(38105) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Ibn Juraij narrated to us, saying: Muhammad (bin Abbad) bin Jafar narrated to me. A hadith that was transmitted to Abu Salama bin Sufyan and Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I attended the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace on the day of the conquest. He prayed in front of the Kaaba, then he took off his sandals and placed them on his left side. Then he opened Surah Al-Mu'minin, and when he mentioned Jesus or Moses, a cough took hold of him, so he bowed. (Muslim 336. Ahmad 3)"
"38106","(38106) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, he said: Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out from some of his chambers and sat at its door. He sat alone, and no one came to him to invite him. He said: Call Abu Bakr for me. He said: Then he came and sat before him. So he conversed with him for a long time, then he ordered him to sit on his right or on his left, then he said: Call for Omar for me, so he came and sat down. Abu Bakr debated with him for a long time, then Omar raised his voice and said: O Messenger of God, they are the head of disbelief, they are the ones who claimed that you A sorcerer, and that you are a soothsayer, and that you are a liar, and that you are a slanderer, and he did not abandon anything of what the people of Mecca used to say except He reminded him, so he ordered him to sit on the other side, so one of them sat on his right and the other on his left.\n Then he called the people and said: Shall I not speak to you like these two companions of yours? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so he turned his face to Abu Bakr and said: Indeed, Abraham was the softest person in God. The oil is in the milk, then he came to Omar and said: Indeed, Noah was more powerful in God than the stone, and the matter was Omar’s command, so they prepared themselves, so they stood up. So they followed Abu Bakr, and said: O Abu Bakr, we hated to ask Omar, what is this that the Messenger of God spoke to you about? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He said to me: How do you command me to invade Mecca? He said: I said: O Messenger of God, they are your people. He said: Until I saw that he would obey me. He said: Then he called Omar, and Omar said: They are the root of disbelief. Until he mentioned every evil they used to mention it. By God, the Arabs will not be humiliated until their people are humiliated. Mecca, so he commanded you to wage jihad to invade Mecca."
"38107","(38107) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, and Mara said: On the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif, but did not get anything from them, so he said: We will convoy tomorrow. So the Muslims said: We will return, but we did not open it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come in the morning to fight. So they went in the morning. They were wounded, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We will be convoying tomorrow. They liked that, and the Messenger of God laughed at him. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 4325. Muslim 1402)"
"38108","(38108) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Jabr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he departed to Taif. So he besieged them for nineteen or eighteen days and did not open it, then he took his soul or his morning into hiding, and he descended, then fled. Then he said: O people, I am generous to you, so I advise you to do good to my family, and your appointment is the basin, and by my soul. With his hand, that you may establish prayer and pay zakat, or I will send to you a man of my own, or like myself, and they will strike the necks of To fight them and to take their descendants captive. He said: Then the people saw that it was Abu Bakr, or Omar, so he took Ali’s hand, and he said: This"
"38109","(38109) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif, and his companions came to him and said: O Messenger of God, you have burned us. The arrows of Thaqif, so pray to God for them. He said: Oh God, guide Thaqif, twice.\n He said: And his maternal uncle came to him, and he said: I was informed that the daughter of Khuza’a has beautiful jewellery, so let us give her jewelery to me if God grants victory to you. Al-Taif tomorrow, he said: If not, will we be allowed to fight them? Then a man, whom Omar saw, said: O Messenger of God, what is your standing over a people against whom you have not been given permission to fight? He said: So he gave the people the call to leave, so the scarab came down and divided the spoils of Hunayn with it, then he entered it with Umrah, then he left. To Medina"
"38110","(38110) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was freed. May God bless him and grant him peace on the Day of Taif, every one of the slaves of the polytheists who went out to it."
"38111","(38111) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It came out Two boys were brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Taif, and he freed them. One of them was Abu Bakra, and they were his masters."
"38112","(38112) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Besieging Wadi Al-Quraya. (Bayhaqi 324)"
"38113","(38113) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Qays informed us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif for twenty-five days, praying for them at the end of every prayer."
"38114","(38114) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I heard a sheikh from Banu Amir, one of Banu Sawa’i, being told: To him: Ubaid Allah bin Mu’iyah. He said: Two men were injured on the day of Taif. He said: So they were carried to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he was informed about them, so he ordered them to be buried where they were injured and met."
"38115","(38115) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Nafi’ ibn Umar informed us, on the authority of Umayyah ibn Safwan, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abu Zuhair Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father; He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in his sermon about the prophet, or the prophets, and the prophets from Taif: You are about to know the people of Paradise from the people of Hell, and the best of you from the worst of you. They said: Why, O Messenger of God? He said: With good praise and bad praise, you are God’s witnesses on earth. (Ibn Majah 4221 and Ahmed 416)"
"38116","(38116) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, he said: Abdul-Malik said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, He was besieged by Thaqif: I have not seen the king since I came to this place of mine. He said: Then his maternal aunt, bint Hakim al-Salamiyah, set off. So she narrated that to Omar, so Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned what she had said to him, and he said: She has told the truth, so Omar indicated to him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed."
"38117","(38117) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said: When the Messenger of God departed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, after Hunayn after Al-Taif, he said: Bring the tailor and the needlewoman, for the deceit is a fire, a disgrace, and a curse upon me. On the Day of Resurrection, it will be his family except a fifth. Then he took some hair from a camel and said: I have nothing of this wealth of yours except a fifth. The fifth will be returned to you. (Abdul Razzaq 9498 and Ahmed 184)"
"38118","(38118) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Taman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Utba Mawla Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from Taif, the scarab came down and divided With the spoils, then he performed Umrah from it, and that was for the remaining two nights of Shawwal. (Ibn Saad 171, Abu Ali 2370)"
"38119","(38119) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Zurarah, on the authority of his sheikhs, on the authority of Al-Zubair; On the Day of Taif, he ruled over his maternal aunts, so he freed them through his rule."
"38120","(38120) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent to his dead person, so he appointed Zaid. If Zaid was killed, then Ja’far, and if he was killed Ja'far and Ibn Rawahah, then Ibn Rawahah remained behind and gathered with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him. He greeted you and said: What left you? He said: I agree with you. He said: His morning, or his soul in the way of God is better than this world and what is in it."
"38121","(38121) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Samir, he said: A slave came to us Allah bin Rabah Al-Ansari, he said: The Ansar used to teach him jurisprudence, he said: Abu Qatada, the knight of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent an army of princes and said: Zaid bin Harithah is upon you. Zayd was injured, then Ja`far bin Abi Talib was injured, and if Ja`far was injured, then Abdullah bin Rawahih, then Ja`far jumped up and said: O Messenger By God, I was not afraid that you would appoint Zaid over me. So he said: Go ahead, for you do not know which of that is better.\n So they set off and stayed for as long as God willed, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ascended the pulpit and gave orders that they should be called: “Prayer.” A university, so the people gathered to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: It will be better, it will be better, three times. I will tell you about... This invader army of yours, they set out and met the enemy, and Zayd killed a martyr, so ask forgiveness for him, then Major General Jaafar bin Abi Talib refused, so he oppressed the people until he killed a martyr. They called him to witness the martyr’s name and asked forgiveness for him. Then he took the general, Abd. Allah ibn Rawahi, so he remained firm until he was killed as a martyr, so ask forgiveness for him.Then he took General Khalid bin Al-Walid, and he was not one of the princes, so he commanded himself, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Oh God, it is one of your swords, so you will help him. Since then, it has been called the drawn sword of God, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Go forth, and support your brothers, and do not leave any of you behind. So go forth, on foot and on horseback, and that is In extreme heat.\n While they were sedating one night from the road, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became sleepy until he turned away from his journey. So I came to him and supported him with my hands. When he found that he had touched the hand of a man, he straightened up and said: Who is this? So I said: Abu Qatada. So he walked too, then he drowsed until he left his mount, so I went to him and supported him with my hand. When he found his hand, he touched A man stood up and said: Who is this? So I said: Abu Qatada. He said in the second or third. He said: He did not see me except that I had been annoyed with you since the night before. He said: I said: : No, by my father and mother, but I think that fatigue or drowsiness has become difficult for you, so if you change your mind and get down until the fatigue goes away He said: I fear that people will let him down. He said: I said: No, for the sake of my father and mother.\n He said: So we sought a fertile place. He said: So I turned away from the road, and behold, I saw a knot of trees, and I came.So I said: O Messenger of God, these are knots from a tree that you have injured. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made amends and made amends. He had with him some of his friends from the people of the road, so they disembarked and took cover from the road at Al-Aqda, and we did not wake up except for the sun shining upon us. So we got up and were lost, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Little by little, until the sun had risen, then he said: Whoever prays these two rak'ahs before the lunch prayer, let him pray them. He who used to pray them will pray them. And whoever does not pray them.\n Then he gave orders and we were called to pray. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and led us in prayer. When he said the prayer, he said: We praise God. We were not in the hands of God to distract us from our prayers, but our souls were in the hands of God. He sent them. If you wish, whoever is able to perform this prayer from a righteous servant, let him perform the same prayer with it.\n They said: O Messenger of God, he is thirsty. He said: No, he is thirsty. O Abu Qatada, show me the water. He said: So I brought it to him. So he put it in his mouth, then he scooped it up with his mouth. God knows best whether he blew it or not, then he said: O Abu Qatada, show me. The flood was on the departing woman, so I brought him a cup between the two cups, so he poured it into it and said: Give the people something to drink.And the Messenger of God called out and raised his voice: Whoever is given his vessel, let him drink it. So I went to a man and gave him something to drink, then I returned to him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thanked him for the cup, so I went and gave water to the one who loved him, and I even gave water to the people of that city. The throat, then I returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his bounty of the cup, so I went and watered the throat another time, until... I watered it seven times a day.\n I began to look around to see if there was anything left in it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, poured it into the cup and said to me: Drink. He said: I said: By my father and my mother, I do not find myself thirsty. He said to you on my behalf, for I have been the people’s cupbearer ever since. Today, he said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, poured into the cup and drank, then he poured into the cup and drank, then poured into The cup and he drank, then he rode and we rode.\n Then he said: What do you think the people did when they lost their prophet and their prayer exhausted them? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Aren’t Abu Bakr and Omar among them? If they obey them, then they have rightly guided them, and their nation has rightly guided them, and if they disobey them, then they have gone astray, and their nation has gone astray. He said it three times. Then he walked and we walked, until, when we were in the middle of the desert, people were following the shade of the tree, so we came to them.Then, behold, some of the emigrants among them was Omar ibn al-Khattab. He said: So we said to them: What did you do when you lost your Prophet? Did your prayers exhaust you? They said: We, by God, will inform you. Omar jumped up and said to Abu Bakr: Indeed, God said in His Book: “Indeed, you will die, and they will die.” They will die. And indeed, by God, I do not know. Perhaps God has caused His Prophet to die. So arise, pray, and go. Indeed, I am watching after you and am to blame. I saw something, otherwise I will catch up with you. He said: And the prayer was performed, and the conversation ended.\n(Abu Dawud 438 Tirmidhi 177)"
"38122","(38122) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Umrah; She heard Aisha say: When the obituary came for Ja’far bin Abi Talib, Zayd bin Harithah, and Abdullah bin Rawah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat, and the sadness was evident on his face. Aisha said: As I looked through the crack in the door, Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, the wives of Ja’far. He remembered some of their crying, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded him. And He granted us permission to prohibit it."
"38123","(38123) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he claimed; Ja'far bin Abi Talib was killed on the day of his death in Balqa', so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, succeed Ja'far. May his family be rewarded with the best of what you have left behind one of your righteous servants."
"38124","(38124) Abdullah bin Idris and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I heard Khalid bin Al-Walid, He says: Ninety swords pierced my hand on the day of my death, and nothing remained in my hand except the blade of a Yemeni sword."
"38125","(38125) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mourned the three who were killed, then he prayed upon them."
"38126","(38126) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr al-Saksaki, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr. He said: When the grief of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became intense for those of them who were afflicted with Zaid on the day of his death, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Certain people will overtake the Messiah from this nation. They are like you, or Good, three times, and God will never disgrace any mother. I am her first and the Messiah is her last."
"38127","(38127) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: When she came and Ja`far died, we saw sadness on the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: He entered A man was upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, the women are crying. He said: Go back to them and silence them, if they refuse. So dig dust into their faces. He said: Aisha said: I said to myself: By God, you have not abandoned yourself, nor are you obedient to the Messenger. God"
"38128","(38128) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The one who breastfed me from among the children of Mara told me, he said: It is as if I were looking at Ja’far on the day Mutaa, he mounted a horse that had a blonde hue, and hobbled it, then he went on and fought until he was killed."
"38129","(38129) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maymun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Saad, he said: When news came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the news of the killing of Zaid, Ja’far, and Abdullah bin Rawahim, he mourned them. To the people, and left names until they suffused with their words: Then he came to her and consoled her, and said: Call for my brother’s sons for me. He said: So she brought three sons, as if they were young ones. She said: He called the barber and he shaved their heads, and he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our two uncles. Abu Talib, and as for God’s help, he is similar to my character and mine, and as for Abdullah, he took him by the hand and lowered it, then said: Oh God Bless Abdullah on his right side. He said: Then their mother rejoiced for him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: And peace be upon him: Do you fear loss for them while I am their guardian in this world and the hereafter? (Ibn Saad 36. Ahmed 204)"
"38130","(38130) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbă narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja`d, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was shown to them in sleep, and he saw Ja’far, an angel with two wings, covered in blood. And Zaid was facing him on the bed, saying: And Ibn Rawahhi was sitting with them, as if they were turning away from him."
"38131","(38131) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Maysara; When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to kill Ja’far, Zaid, and Abdullah bin Rawahi, he mentioned their matter. He said: O God, forgive Zaid, O God, forgive Jafar and Abdullah bin Rawahih."
"38132","(38132) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, he said : Usama bin Zayd came after his father was killed, and he stood before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his eyes shed tears. The next day he came and stood in his place, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will receive from you today what I received from you yesterday?"
"38133","(38133) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Wa’il bin Dawud narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Bayhi speaking; Aisha used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never sent Zayd bin Harithah to an army unless he ordered him upon them, and if he had remained after him, he would have appointed him as his successor."
"38134","(38134) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Amir, that Aisha She used to say: If Zaid were alive, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would have appointed him as his successor."
"38135","(38135) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had cut off a mission before his death, and he had appointed Usama bin Zayd over them, and in that The resurrection, Abu Bakr and Omar, said: And there were people from among us who were disputing that, according to the command of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Asama greeted them. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed the people, then he said: Some of you have been stabbed. Ali in the appointment of Asama, but they challenged the appointment of Asama just as they challenged the appointment of his father before him. By God, if he is a true ruler, even if he is one of the most beloved people to me, and his son is one of the most beloved people to me after him, and I I hope that he will be among your good deeds, so treat him well."
"38136","(38136) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Ja`far ibn Abi Talib was killed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his wife Asma bint Umays until she succumbed. They crossed her, and some of her sadness went away, then he came and comforted her, and he called Banu Ja’far and he called for them, and he called for Abdullah bin Jafar wanted to be blessed in the deal he had on his hand, as he would not buy anything except that he would gain from it.\n Then Asmaa said to him: O Messenger of God, these people claim that we are not among the immigrants, so he said: They lied, to you. You migrated twice, you migrated to the Negus, and you migrated to me."
"38137","(38137) Abu Ishaq Al-Azdi told us, he said: Abu Uwais told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I was in Muta, and when we lost Jafar bin Abi Talib, we searched for him among the dead, and we found fifty among him; Between his stabbing and throwing, and we found that in the front part of his body.\n Abu Abdul Rahman told us, Abu Bakr told us,"
"38138","(38138) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: A man said to Al-Bara’: Have you been your guardian? On the day of Hunayn, O Abu Amara? He said: I bear witness to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as long as he ruled. But a group of people departed and fled to this neighborhood from Hawazin. They are a people who are archers, and they shot them with arrows of arrows as if they were locusts. He said: Then they were exposed, so the people approached. We will take you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith is leading his mule, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended May God bless him and grant him peace, so he sought victory, and he said:\nI am the Prophet, there is no lie. I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib.\n Oh God, send down your victory. He said: By God, when the battle becomes red, we will protect ourselves from it, and the brave is the one who is surrounded by it. (Muslim 1401, Bayhaqi 134)"
"38139","(38139) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: No, by God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not take charge of him. On the day Hunayn returned, he said: Al-Abbas and Abu Sufyan were holding the reins of his mule, and he said:\nI am the Prophet, there is no lie. I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib."
"38140","(38140) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was one of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Day of Hunayn: O God, if You will, You will not be worshiped after this day."
"38141","(38141) Affan narrated to us, Sulaym bin Akhdar narrated to us, Ibn Aoun narrated to me, Hisham bin Zaid narrated to me, on the authority of Anas, He said: When it was the day of Hunayn, a large crowd gathered for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. At that time, there were ten thousand, or more than ten thousand. He said: And with him were the freedmen. He said: So they came. With blessings and offspring, they were placed behind their backs. He said: When they met, the people took turns, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. At that time, he was on a white mule. He said: So he descended and said: Indeed, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. He said: And he called out two calls at that time. He was mingling their words, so he turned to his right and said: Yes, the Ansar. They said: At your command, O Messenger of God. We are with you. Then he turned to his left and said: That is, Ansar. They said: At your command, O Messenger of God, we are with you.\n Then he went down to the land and they met, and were defeated and took some of the spoils. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the freedmen and divided Therein, the Ansar said: We will be called upon in times of distress and the spoils will be divided among others. This was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he gathered them together, sat in a cupboard, and said: O people of the Ansar, what hadith has reached me about you? They remained silent, and he said: O Ansar, if the people were to take a valley and the Ansar were to take a path, I would take the Ansar’s path. Then he said: Aren't you satisfied that people should go with the world, and that you should take the Messenger of God and take him to your homes? They said: We are satisfied, we are satisfied, O Messenger of God.\n Ibn Aoun said: Hisham bin Zaid said: I said to Anas: Did you witness that? He said: Where can I be absent from that? (Bukhari 4333 and Muslim 735)"
"38142","(38142) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Talhah came one day."
"38143","(38143) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever kills someone, he will have his plunder. So, on that day, Abu Talha was killed. Twenty men, so he took their gear."
"38144","(38144) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, who said: The Muslims were defeated on the day of Hunayn. So they called out: O Companions of Surah Al-Baqarah. He said: They returned and they were mourning, meaning weeping."
"38145","(38145) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yusuf bin Suhayb narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn, the people left him, and only a man remained with him who was told: Zaid, holding his young female mule, which the Negus had given him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Woe to you, Zaid! Call the people. So he called out: O people! This is the Messenger of God. They are calling you. He did not answer him. Someone at that time, and he said: Woe to you. He called out the Aws and the Khazraj, and said: O people of the Aws and the Khazraj, this is the Messenger of God. They invite you, but no one answered him at that time, so he said: Woe to you, invite the immigrants, for God has a gift on their necks. He said: Buraidah told me that a thousand of them came, they threw down the eyelids and broke them, then they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings be upon him until it was opened to them.\n(Bazzar 1828)"
"38146","(38146) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, he said: Umar, the servant of Ghufari, informed me, he said: It was revealed The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported on the authority of a mule that was on it, and he started shouting to the people: O people of Surat Al-Baqarah, O people of Surah Al-Baqarah. He sold the tree. I am the Messenger of God and His Prophet. And they turned away, retreating."
"38147","(38147) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: I saw Abdullah bin He struck him with his hand, so I said: What is this? He said: I beat her on the day of Hunayn. He said: I said to him: Did you witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Hunayn? He said: Yes. (Bukhari 4314)"
"38148","(38148) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Musa informed us, on the authority of his brother Abdullah ibn Ubaidah; After the incident, a group of people from Hawazin came and said: O Messenger of God, we desire the Messenger of God. He said: What is that? Do you desire wealth or wealth? They said: Rather, in lineage, mothers, and daughters. As for money, God will provide for us. He said: As for me, I will return what is in my hand. And help Banu Hashim from your private parts, and as for the people, I will intercede for you when you pray, God willing, so rise up and say Such and such, so he taught them what to say, so they did what he commanded them to do, and he interceded for them, so not one of the Muslims remained but responded to what he said. In his hands were some of their private parts, other than Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis and Uyaynah ibn Hisn. They captured two women who were in Their hands"
"38149","(38149) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, who said: When the people fled from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace On the day of Hunayn, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said:\nI am the Prophet, there is no lie. I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib.\n He said: Only four people remained with him: three of Banu Hashim, and a man from others: Ali bin Abi Talib and Al-Abbas. And it is between his hands, and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith is holding the reins, and Ibn Masoud is on his left side, and he said: It is not No one will do anything like it unless he is killed, and the polytheists around him will kill me with the reward of a wreath."
"38150","(38150) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave May God bless him and grant him peace from the spoils of Hunayn Al-Aqra’ bin Habis gave him a hundred camels, and Ayna bin Hisn gave him a hundred camels, so some people said From the Ansar: The Messenger of God will give our spoils to people whose blood will drip our swords, or will their swords drip with our blood? This reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent for them and they came, and he said to them: Are there others among you? They said: No, except our sister’s son. He said: The nephew of one of the people, so he said: You said such-and-such. Are you not satisfied that he should go? People with sheep and camels, and you take Muhammad to your homes? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people are a cover, and the Ansar are a symbol. The Ansar are a caravan. My shame, had it not been for the Hijra, I would have been one of the Ansar."
"38151","(38151) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ubaidah; That Abu Sufyan, Hakim ibn Hazzam, and Safwan ibn Umayyah went out on the day of Hunayn to see who the backs were. Then a Bedouin passed by them, and they said: O Abdullah, what did the people do? He said: Muhammad will never face her. He said: That was when his companions separated from him, and some of them said to one another: There is no Lord who Quraysh are more beloved to us than a lord than any of the Bedouins. O so-and-so, go and bring us the news. A companion of theirs said: So he went until He was among the people, and he heard them saying: Oh the Aws, oh the Khazraj, and they rose above the people, and the slogan was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"38152","(38152) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Labid, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided the captives with scarabs, he gave gifts Quraysh and other Arabs, but there was nothing among the Ansar among them, so the words increased and spread, until he said They said: As for the Messenger of God, he met his people. He said: So he sent for Saad bin Ubadah and said: What has been said to me about Sa’d? Your people, increase in it? He said: Then Saad said to him: It is as you heard. He said: Where are you in that? He said: I am nothing but a man from my people. He said: Then his anger increased, and he said: Gather your people, and let no one be with them except them. He said: So he gathered them into one of the capes of the captives, and stood at its gate, and made that no one should leave except those who were among his people, and he left Men from among the immigrants, and he sent some people back. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and the anger on his face was evident, and he said: O community of Ansar, did I not find you astray, so may God guide you? So they started saying: We seek refuge in God from the wrath of God and from the wrath of His Messenger. O people of Ansar, did I not find you on high? So God made you rich? So they started saying: We seek refuge in God from the wrath of God and the wrath of His Messenger. O people of Ansar, did I not find you to be enemies, so God has sufficed. Between your hearts? They say: We seek refuge in God from the wrath of God and the wrath of His Messenger. He said: Will you not answer? They said: Allah and His Messenger are safer and better.\n When he was told, he said: And if you had wished, you could have said, and you have spoken the truth, and you have spoken the truth: Did we not find you expelled, and give you shelter, and a lie? So We gave you charity, We helped you in poverty, We helped you in poverty, We helped you in need, and We helped you. So they began to weep and say: Allah and His Messenger are safer and better. He said: Have you found anything of this world that I have given to people? I teach them to Islam, and I assign you to your Islam, even if the people walked through a valley, or a path, and you walked through a valley, or People, I would have walked your valley, or your people, you are a symbol, and the people are a covering, and had it not been for the migration, I would have been one of Ansar\n Then he raised his hands so that I could see what was under his shoulders, and he said: O God, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar. And to the sons of the Ansar, are you not satisfied that the people should go with sheep and camels, and that you should go with the Messenger of God to your homes? Then the people wept until they soaked their beards, and they departed, saying: We are satisfied with God as our Lord, and with His Messenger as a share and share."
"38153","(38153) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Ata told us, on the authority of Abu Hammam Abdullah. Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Firi, who said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his campaign. Hunain, we walked on a very hot, sweltering day, and we came down under the shade of the trees. When the sun had set, I put on my clothes and rode. My horse, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in his tent, and I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. And may God have mercy on him, the spirits came, and he said: Yes, and he said: O Bilal, and he rose from under his sundress, as if his shadow was the shadow of a bird. He said: I am at your service and I am pleased with you, and I may be your ransom. So he said: Saddle my horse for me. So he took out a saddle with a cover made of fiber, not As for what is bad, and there is no recklessness, he said: So he saddled.\n So he rode, and we rode, so we lined up with them during our evening and night, and the two horses became happy, so the Muslims turned away, as he said. God, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O servants of God, I am the servant of God and His Messenger, then he said: O people Emigrants, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, galloped off his horse and took a handful of dirt. Then the one who was closer to him than me told me that he struck their faces with it, and he said: Their faces saw it. He said: So God defeated them.\n Ali bin Ata’ said: Their children told me, on the authority of their fathers. They said: Not one of us remains except that his eyes and mouth are filled with dust, and we hear the sound of the sound between the heavens and the earth, like a passing sound. Iron on the iron pan. (Abu Dawud 1371, Ahmed 286)"
"38154","(38154) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; On the day of Hunayn, she brought boys, women, camels, and sheep to Hawazin, and they arranged them in rows to outnumber the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When they met, the Muslims turned to each other as God said. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Servants of God, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. Then he said: O community of immigrants, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. He said: So God was defeated. The polytheists, and he was not struck with a sword, nor stabbed with a spear. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on that day: Who He killed an infidel and took his spoils. He said: Abu Talha killed twenty men on that day and took their spoils.\n Abu Qatada said: O Messenger of God, I struck a man while he was free, and he was wearing his armor, and I had an abortion on him. Hammad said: So I hastened from him. He said: So look who took it. He said: Then a man stood up and said: I took it, so take some of it away. And give it to me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not ask for anything unless he gave it to him, or remained silent, so the Messenger of God remained silent. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Then Omar said: No, by God, God will not reward her with any of his lions and give her to you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at you and said: Omar spoke the truth.\n Abu Talha found Umm Sulaim with a dagger, and Abu Talha said: O Umm Sulaim, what do you have with you? She said: If some polytheists approached me, I wanted to disturb his stomach, so Abu Talha said: O Messenger of God, will you not hear what Umm Salim says? She said: O Messenger of God, those who were freed were killed after us. They were defeated by you, O Messenger of God, and he said: Indeed, God has sufficed and done good. (Abu Dawud 2712 and Ahmed 279)"
"38155","(38155) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Ikrim bin Ammar told us, he said: Iyas bin Salamah told us, he said: Tell me. My father, he said: I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Hawazin, while we were offering the sacrifice, and our common people were walking, among us Double, when a man came on a red camel, took a piece of wood from its belt, and tied a young man with it to his camel, then he came to have lunch with him. The people, when he saw their weakness and lack of appearance, he went out to run to his camel and let it go, then he made him cry and he sat on it. Then he went out running, and a man from among the Prophet’s companions who had converted to Islam, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed him, riding a camel and a slave. I followed the back of the people, so he sat down and I followed him, so I went out running and overtook him while the camel’s head was at the camel’s hip, and I was at your hip. The camel, and I advanced until I took hold of the camel's snout and cut him off. When he put his knees on the ground, I pierced him with my sword. So I hit him on the head, and he turned away, so I came with his camel, and what was on it, I led him, so I met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Coming forward, he said: Who killed the man? They said: Ibn Al-Akwa', so he plundered him."
"38156","(38156) Affan told us, Wahib told us, Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, he said: When God gave His Messenger a reward on the day of Hunayn, he did not give it to him, he swore among the people by reconciliation of their hearts, but he did not swear. He did not give the Ansar anything, and it was as if they had found themselves, since what had befallen the people had not befallen them. So he addressed them and said: O people. Ansar, did I not find you astray and God guided you through me? And you were dispersed, but God brought you together through me? And He is exalted, so God has enriched you through me. He said: Whenever he said something, they said: God and His Messenger are safe. He said: What prevents you from Do you answer? They said: God and His Messenger have believed. He said: If you wish, you could say: You brought us such-and-such. Are you not satisfied that the people go with the thing? And the camels, and do you take the Messenger of God to your camps? Were it not for the Hijra, I would have been one of the Ansar. If the people had taken a valley or a path, I would have taken the Ansar’s valley and their path. The Ansar are a symbol, and the people are a cover, and you will meet a trail after me, so be patient until you meet me at the Fountain."
"38157","(38157) Hashim bin Al-Qasim Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Iyas bin Salamah told me, On the authority of his father, he said: I came to Medina at the time of Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I and Rabah, a boy, left. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him with camels, and I went out with him with Talha’s horse. He rode with the camels, and when he was sitting, Abd al-Rahman bin Uyaynah raided the camels of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he killed her shepherd, and he went out and chased her away, along with some people with him, on horses. I said: O Rabah, sit on this horse. So he joined him with his weapon, and informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he had been attacked to free him.\n He said: So I stood up on a hill, and I made my face towards the city, then I called three times: O morning, then I followed the people. I have with me my sword and arrows, so I started to shoot at them and hit them, and that was when the trees were abundant. He said: When a knight returned to me, I sat down. He was at the root of a tree, then I threw, and no knight would approach me without me attacking him, so I started throwing at them and saying:\nI am the son of Al-Akwa' and today is the day of infants.\n So I catch up with a man and shoot him while he is on his journey, and my arrow falls into the man.Until his shoulder was straightened, I said: Take it:\nI am the son of Al-Akwa' and today is the day of infants.\n So, when I was in the tree, I burned them with arrows, and when the two came together at the top of the mountain, I pelted them with stones. This is still my business and their business. I follow them and tremble, until God has not created anything from the appearance of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, except that I left him behind me and rescued him from their hands. He said: Then I did not stop attacking them until they threw More than thirty spears, and more than thirty hailstones, they hide from them, and they do not throw anything of that except I placed piles of stones on it, and gathered them together in the way of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until, when the sacrifice was extended, Ayn bin Badr Al-Fazari came to them, extending to them, while they were in a narrow fold, then I ascended the mountain and was above them. Uyaynah said: What is this that I see? They said: We met with such joy, and no magic has left us until now, and He took everything in our hands and left it behind us. His back, and Ayaynah said: Had this man not seen that there was a search behind him, he would have left you. He said: Let a group rise up to him. Of you, then a group of four of them came up to me and went up the mountain. When I heard the voice from them,I said to them: Do you know me? They said: Who are you? I said: I am Ibn Al-Akwa', and he is the one who honored the face of Muhammad. No man among you will ask me and he will overtake me, and I will not ask him. Then he will miss me. One of them said: I think so.\n He said: I had not left that seat until I saw the cavalry of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as they were penetrating the trees, and suddenly The first of them was Al-Ahram Al-Asadi, and after him was Abu Qatada, the knight of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and after him was Abu Qatada. Al-Miqdad Al-Kindi, he said: So turn the polytheists back, turning back, and I will come down from the mountain, and I will turn towards the akhram, and I will take two reins. His horse, I said: O Akhram, warn the people, meaning, warn them, for I do not believe that they will cut you off, so prepare until The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace and his companions, caught up with him and said: Oh, peace be upon him, if you believe in God and the Last Day, And you know that Paradise is real and Hell is real, so do not come between me and the witness. He said: So I let the reins of his horse go, so he will catch up. With Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah, and he was sympathetic towards Abd al-Rahman, so they differed and stabbed him twice, so he bit the acrom of Abd al-Rahman, and they stabbed him. Abd al-Rahman and killed him, and Abd al-Rahman attacked Al-Ahram’s horse.Then Abu Qatada followed Abd al-Rahman, and they disagreed twice. He stabbed Abu Qatada, and Abu Qatada killed him, and Abu Qatadah converted. On the acromion horse.\n Then I went out running in the wake of the people, until I saw nothing of the dust of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And before the setting of the sun, they would go to a place where there was water, and it would be called: Dhū Qardā, and they wanted to drink from it. Then they saw me running after them, so they turned away from him and pulled in the two men, the two of Dhu Thabir, and the sun had set so he joined them. A man and throw it away, and I said: Take it.\nI am the son of Al-Akwa' and today is the day of infants.\n He said: O my mother, my mother has bereaved me, my elbow is a virgin. I said: Yes, that is, an enemy of his own soul, and it was the one I threw away a virgin. So I followed him with another arrow, but two arrows got stuck in it, and they fell behind two horses, so I brought them to take them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he is by the water that you have cleared from him: Dhu Qard.\n Then, behold, the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was among the five hundred, and behold, Bilal had slaughtered a camel of what I had left behind, and he was roasting it. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from her liver and hump. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, leave me alone, so choose a hundred men from your companions.Then the infidels were attacked by a massacre, and not a single person among them would remain informing me unless I killed him. He said: Did you do that, O Salamah? He said: Yes, by the One who honored your face. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until I saw his molars in the light. Fire\n He said: Then he said: They are now close to the land of Ghatfan, so a man from Ghatfan came and said: They passed by so-and-so Ghatfan, and he slaughtered a sacrifice for them. Insolently, when they started scraping her skin, they saw dust, so they left her and went out fleeing. When we woke up, the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best of our cavalry today is Abu Qatada, and the best of our men is Salamah, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave me May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, both the horseman and the footman, then he led me back to the hills after him, returning to Medina.\n When there was a relative of Dhuhu between us and her, and among the people was a man from the Ansar, he was unprecedented, so he started calling: Is there anyone who races? Except a man who races to Medina. He did that many times, and I am following the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In addition, I said to him: Do you not honor a generous person, and do not respect an honorable person? He said: No, except the Messenger of God. I said: O Messenger of God, leave me alone with my father and my mother, so that I may race with the man. He said: If you wish, I said: Go to you,So he arose from his camel, and I bent my legs and arose from the camel, then I tied an honor upon her, or two honors, meaning I kept myself ahead of myself, then I ran until I caught up with him, then I held him close between his shoulders with my hand, then I said, “By God, I have outpaced you.” Or He said something like that, then he laughed and said: I think so, until we came to Medina. (Muslim 1433. Ahmad 52)"
"38158","(38158) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm bin Sukhairah al-Adawi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear In Dhu Qard, a land from the land of Banu Sulaym, so the people lined up behind him in two rows: a line behind him, a line parallel to the enemy, so he prayed in a row. He bowed down, then these people bowed down to the rows of these, and these people went to the rows of these, and he led them in prayer. Rakaa"
"38159","(38159) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukin Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Zaid bin constant; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear, so he mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"38160","(38160) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of His father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to wage a campaign, he would show him something else until his campaign took place. Tabuk, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled in extreme heat, and he embarked on a far journey, so he was revealed to the Muslims from He commanded them, and informed them of that, so that they might be aware of their enemy, and informed them of the face he wanted. (Abu Dawud 2430, Ahmed 387)"
"38161","(38161) Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, Amr bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, On the authority of Abu Hamid al-Sa’idi, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of Tabuk, until we came to Wadi al-Qura. And when a woman was talking to her, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Be quiet. He said: So the people remained silent, and he remained silent. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took ten awsuqs, and he said to the woman: Count what comes out of her until I return to you. God willing\n He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and reached Tabuk, and said: A scent will blow upon you at night. It is severe, and not a man will stand up therein. So whoever has a camel, let him tie its bands. He said: Abu Hamid said: So we tied it. Then, during the night, a strong wind blew, and a man got up in it, and it threw him into my mountain.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the king of his people, and he brought gifts to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A white mule, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, covered him with a cloak, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote for him With their sea.\n He said: Then he came, and we went with him until we came to Wadi al-Qura, and he said to the woman: How much is your garden? She said: Ten awsuq. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a hurry. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is in a hurry. So whoever among you likes to be hasty, let him do so. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and we went out with him until... He came to Medina and said: This is good. Then when he saw Uhud, he said: This is a mountain. It loves us and we love it. (Bukhari 1481, Muslim 1011)"
"38162","(38162) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, He said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, on the authority of his father Ka’b, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he set out with the Banu al-Asfar to attack them, he made their affairs clear to the people, and he rarely wanted to invade unless he hid it. Then he was faced with intense heat, a long journey, and a new enemy, so he revealed to the people The face with which He brought them forth, so that they might prepare themselves for their enemy.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prepared himself, and the people prepared with him, and I went off in the morning to prepare myself, but I returned without making up the time. Something, until the people had finished, and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is leaving and going to face him, so I said: I will prepare myself. A day later, or two days later, then I overtook them, and there were two journeys with me. Two journeys had never met with me before them. I am powerful in myself and strong in my equipment, so I continued to go out in the morning after him and come back and did not fulfill anything, until the people took care of me. They hastened, and I started to go in the morning to talk, and the traveling kept me busy, so I kept sitting until the people overtook me, and I started to go in the morning, but nothing I see only a man whom God has excused.Or a man who is immersed in hypocrisy, and that makes me sad.\n So I began to prepare an excuse for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he came, and the speech would be prepared, and it would be appreciated for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, did not mention me until he came to Tabuk, and he said to the people in Tabuk while he was sitting: What did Ka’b bin Malik do? Then a man from my people came up to him and said: He was busy with his coldness and looking at his kindness. He said: Then another man spoke and said: By God, O Messenger of God, if we know anything but good, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent. When it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has kept coming. Falsehood has been removed from me, and what I used to do was nothing but lies and excuses, and I knew that he would never The only thing that saves me from it is honesty, so I agreed to tell the truth, and in the morning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived in Medina and arrived. So I went to him in the morning, and behold, he was among the people sitting in the mosque, and whenever he came from a journey he would enter the mosque and kneel in it. I prayed two rak'ahs, then he entered upon his family, and I found him sitting in the mosque. When he looked at me, he called me and said: Come. Kaab, what left you behind? He smiled with the smile of an angry person and said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have no excuse. I have never been stronger or easier than when I fell behind. About you,Those who remained behind came to him swearing, but he would accept from them, ask forgiveness for them, and entrust their secrets in that matter to God. God Almighty, when I spoke the truth about him, He said: This one has spoken the truth, so stand up until God decides about you as He is a judge, so I stood up.\n Then some men from the Banu Salamah stood up to me and said: By God, you have not done anything. By God, if that were to be sufficient for you of your sin, You committed a sin by asking the forgiveness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for you, just as he did that for others, so he accepted their excuse from them. And he asked forgiveness for them, but they continued to blame me until I was about to go back and deceive myself. Then I said to them: Did he? Is this article anyone? Or did he apologize in the same way you apologized? They said: Yes, I said: Who? They said: Hilal bin Umayyah Al-Waqifi, and Rabi’ bin Marara Al-Amiry, and they mentioned to me two righteous men who testified. Badr, they apologized the same way you apologized, and they were told the same as what you were told.\n He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from talking, so we began to go among the people, and no one spoke to us, nor Someone greets us and does not return our greeting, until, when forty nights have passed, the messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes to us. Peace and blessings of God be upon you, keep away from your wives. As for Hilal bin Umayyah,Then his wife came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: He is old and his eyesight has weakened, so did he hate it? Should I make him food? He said: No, but he will not bring you near. She said: By God, he has not moved at all, and God has been crying ever since. This was his affair until this day. He said: Then some of his family said to him: If only you had asked the permission of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon your wife, just as Hilal bin Umayyah’s wife asked for permission. He gave her permission to serve him. He said: So I said: By God, I will not ask him for permission, and I do not know what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say if I asked for his permission. He is an old man, and I am a young man, so I said to your wife: Go with your family, until God decides what He is the judge. And we began to walk among the people, and no one spoke to us or returned our greeting.\n He said: So I approached, until I surrounded a wall of a cousin of mine in the wall, so I greeted him, but he did not move his lips to return my greeting, so I said: I adjure you by God. Do you know that I love God and His Messenger? He did not speak a word to me. Then I returned and he did not speak to me, even when On the third or fourth, he said: Allah and His Messenger know best.\n So I went out, and I was walking in the market when people were pointing at me with their hands.And when a Nabataean from the Levant asked about me, they started pointing to him, until he came to me and handed me a letter from... Some of my people in the Levant: We have heard what your friend did to you, and you turned away from him, so join us, for God did not make you In an abode of humiliation, and no abode of loss, your consolation for our wealth. He said: I said: We belong to God. The people of disbelief have coveted me. So I filled an oven with it, and lit it with it.\n By God, perhaps this is the situation that God has mentioned. The earth has become narrow for us, despite its spaciousness, and our souls have become narrow for us. On the morning of fifty nights since you forbade us from speaking, repentance was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, announced God’s repentance upon us when he prayed dawn, so the people went to give us good tidings, and he ran A man came to me with a horse, and he ran fast from one of the safest, so he finished on the mountain, and the voice was faster than the horse, so he called: O Ka’b bin Malik, give good news. So I fell down prostrating, and I knew that relief had come, so when the one whose voice I heard came to me, I lightened two garments for him. With good tidings, by God, I will not have two garments other than these.\n I borrowed two garments and went out before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and people met me, group after group.They congratulated me on God’s repentance upon me, until I entered the mosque, and Talha bin Ubad Allah came running to me. He shook my hand and congratulated me, and no other emigrants came to me, and it was an unforgettable gesture to his face. Then I approached. Until I stood over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if his face was cut off by the moon. When he walked, his face was illuminated. Likewise, he called me: Come, Ka’b, give good tidings of the best day that has passed since your mother gave birth to you. He said: So I said: I am safe with you. God, or is it from you? He said: No, but from God. You told the truth to God, and he told you the truth.\n He said: So I said: Part of my repentance today is that I give out of my wealth alms to God and to His Messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Hold back some of your money. I said: Hold back my share of Khaybar. Ka’b said: By God, God has not afflicted you. A man whose hadith is truthful and who has not failed me. (Bukhari 4418 and Muslim 2120)"
"38163","(38163) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out May God bless him and grant him peace. In his invasion of Tabuk, he left Ali behind in charge of the women and boys, and he said: O Messenger of God, will you leave behind me in charge of the women? And the boys? He said: Aren't you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?"
"38164","(38164) Zaid bin Harun told us, Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Othman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with dinars during his invasion of Tabuk, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made He placed her heart in his lap and said: Othman bin Affan is not responsible for what he did after this. (Tirmidhi 3701, Ahmed 63)"
"38165","(38165) Zaid bin Harun told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from his invasion of Tabuk, and approached Medina, he said: Indeed, in Medina For a people you have never traveled, nor crossed a valley without being with you in it. They said: O Messenger of God: And they are in Medina? He said: Yes, while they were in Medina, their excuse detained them.\n(Bukhari 2838 and Ibn Majah 2764)"
"38166","(38166) Hushaym told us, Dawud bin Amr told us, on the authority of Busr bin Ubaid Allah Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Idris. Al-Khawlani, Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i told us; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered wiping over the socks during the three-day raid on Tabuk. Their nights are for the traveler, and their days and nights are for the resident."
"38167","(38167) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Awsat, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Kabsha. Al-Anmari, on the authority of his father, said: When he was on the campaign against Tabuk, people rushed to the owners of the stone, and they entered upon them. This reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered that he be called: “Indeed, the prayer is unified.” He said: “So I came to him while he was holding his hand.” With his camels, and he says: Why do you go against a people upon whom God is angry? He said: Then a man called to him in amazement: O Messenger of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not inform you of what Is it more amazing than that? A man from among yourselves, telling you about what happened before you and what will happen after you. Be upright and direct, for God does not Your torment will be of no consequence, and God will bring a people who will not defend themselves with anything. (Ahmad 231. Tabarani 851)"
"38168","(38168) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Abdullah bin Abi Hadrad Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, Abdullah bin Abi Hadrad, said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, peace be upon him, on his journey to Idham. He said: Then we met Aamir bin Al-Adbat. He said: He greeted with the greeting of Islam, so we departed from him. And Muhallam bin Jathama attacked him and killed him. When he killed him, he plundered his camels, his livestock, and his possessions. So when we came, We came about him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we informed him of his matter, and this verse was revealed: {O O you who have believed, when you strike in the way of God, then seek to understand each other and do not say to him who has bestowed peace upon you.\n Ibn Ishaq said: Then Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed me, on the authority of Zayd ibn Damira,\n He said: My father and uncle told me, and they were witnesses with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace at noon, then he sat under a tree, and Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis, the master of Khandaf, came to him and responded to the blood of And Uyaynah ibn Hisn stood up to demand the blood of Amir ibn al-Adbat al-Qaisi, and he was an Ashja’i.He said: I heard Uyaynah bin Hisn saying: I will make his wives taste sadness like what he made my wives taste, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do you accept the blood money? They refused, so a man from Banu Layth, called Mikatil, stood up and said: By God, O Messenger of God, I am not like this. The one who was killed in the absence of Islam is like a sheep that came back and was thrown away, then the last of them ran away. Change it today and change it tomorrow. He said: Then the Prophet said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with his hand: You have fifty on this journey of ours, and fifty when we return. He said: So accept the blood money.\n He said: So they said: Bring your companion, may the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ask forgiveness for him. He said: So he was brought, and he described She was dressed, and he was wearing a dress in which he was preparing to be killed, until I sat in the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What is your name? He said: Muḥalīm ibn Jathāmah. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said with his hand, and described that he raised them, “O God, do not forgive.” By Muhalim bin Jathama, he said: So we talked among ourselves that he had only shown this, and he had asked forgiveness for it in secret.\n Ibn Ishaq said: Amr bin Ubaid informed me, on the authority of Al-Hasan,He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did you believe in God and then you killed him? By God, he only stayed for seven years until Muhallam died. He said: I heard Al-Hasan swear by God: He would be buried three times, all of that. The earth spoke to him. He said: So they placed him between the two sides of a mountain and piled stones on him, and wild beasts devoured him. So they mentioned his matter. to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: By God, the earth will cover whoever is worse than him, but God wanted to He informs you of your sanctity among you. (Abu Dawud 4496)"
"38169","(38169) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to curse The people of Najran accepted the reward to be given to them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The good news has come to me. By this, the people of Najran will be destroyed, if they complete the curses, even the bird on the tree, or the sparrow on the tree, and when they come to them in the morning The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Hassan and Hussein by the hand, and Fatima was walking behind them."
"38170","(38170) Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, Mujalid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He wrote The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the people of Najran, who are Christians: Indeed, whoever among you pledges a pledge of allegiance on the basis of usury, he shall not be held accountable. No"
"38171","(38171) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Omar evacuated the people of Najran, the Jews and Christians, and bought their land and vineyards, so Omar dealt with the people; If they bring the cows and iron from them, then he gets two-thirds and Omar gets a third, and if Omar brings the seeds from him, He owned the half, and he treated them with the palm trees on the basis that they had a fifth, and four-fifths for 'Umar, and he treated them with the vineyard on the basis that they had a third, and for 'Umar The two-thirds"
"38172","(38172) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, he said: The people of Najran had reached forty thousand, he said: And it was Omar was afraid that they would incline against the Muslims, so they would envy each other. He said: So they came to Omar, and they said: We have envy among ourselves. So we postponed. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had written a letter for them not to be deported. He said: So Omar took advantage of it. So he evacuated them, but they regretted it, so they went to him and said: We told him, but he refused to tell them. So when Ali came, they went to him, and they said: We We ask you, by the line of your right hand, and your intercession with your Prophet, if you will protect us, but he refused, and said: Woe to you, for Omar was Rashid. The matter\n Salem said: They were of the opinion that if Ali had disobeyed Omar in any of his affairs; He was attacked by the people of Najran."
"38173","(38173) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the bishops of Najran. Al-Aqib and Al-Sayyid, so they said: Send with us a truly trustworthy man, truly trustworthy, truly trustworthy. So he said: I will send with you a truly trustworthy man. Then the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to her and said: Get up, O Abu Ubaidah bin al-Jarrah, and he sent him with them."
"38174","(38174) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Najran, and they said to me: You recite: {O sister of Aaron} and between Moses and Jesus for as many years as God wills? I did not know what to answer them with, until I returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I asked him, and he said: Didn’t you tell them? That they were called by their prophets and the righteous before them? (Muslim 1685. Ahmad 252)"
"38175","(38175) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his followers, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Bishop of Najran: O Abu Al-Harith, convert to Islam. He said: I am a Muslim. He said: O Abu Al-Harith, convert to Islam. He said: I converted to Islam before you. A prophet said. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: You lied. Three things prevented you from Islam: your claiming to have a son from God, and your eating pigs, And your drinking of wine."
"38176","(۳۸۱۷۶) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ فُضَیْلٍ، عَنْ أَبِیہِ ، عَنْ نَافِعٍ، عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: لَمَّا قُبِضَ رَسُولُ اللہِ صَلَّی اللَّہُ عَلَیْہِ And peace be upon him. Abu Bakr was in the vicinity of Medina, and he came and entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was under cover. So he put his mouth on the forehead of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to kiss him and make him cry and say: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. You were good when you were alive, and you were good when you died. When he came out, he passed by Omar ibn al-Khattab, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has not died. He will not die until God has killed the hypocrites, and until God has disgraced the hypocrites. He said: And they had rejoiced of the death of the Messenger of God. Then they raised their heads, and he said: O man, take care of yourself, for the Messenger of God has died. Didn’t he? You hear God saying: {Indeed, you are dead, and they will die} And He said: {And We did not assign to human beings before you immortality; if you die, then Immortals}۔\n He said: Then he came to the pulpit, ascended it, and thanked God and praised Him. Then he said: O people, if Muhammad is your God. Which you worship, then your God, Muhammad, has died, and if your God is in the heavens, then your God has not died, then He recited: {And Muhammad is no more than a messenger. Messengers have passed on before him. But if he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?} until he concluded the verse, Then it descended, and the Muslims were rejoiced by this and their joy increased, and the hypocrites became depressed.\n Abdullah bin Omar said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is as if our faces were covered, then uncovered. (Bazzar 852)"
"38177","(38177) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of his father; They had doubts about the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Where should they bury him? Abu Bakr said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The Prophet will not be turned away from his place, and he will be buried where He died, so they removed his bed, so they dug a place for his bed for him. (Tirmidhi 1018 and Ibn Majah 1428)"
"38178","(38178) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir, he said: I was in Yemen, and I met two men from the people of Yemen, Dha Kila’ and Dha Amr, so I started telling them about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They said: If what you say is true, then your companion passed by three days ago, so I and they came with him. Until, when we were on some road, a group was brought up for us from Medina, so we asked them, and they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has been arrested. May God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr was appointed as successor, and the people are righteous. He said: So they said to me: Tell your friend that we have come, and perhaps we We will return, God willing, and they returned to Yemen. He said: So I informed Abu Bakr of their hadith. He said: Why did you not bring them? He said: When It was after that, Dhu Amr said to me: O Jarir, you are an honor upon me, and I will inform you of news. You Arabs will never Remain in good health as long as you were. If one prince dies, you conspire in the affairs of another. When it is by the sword, they become kings who become angry. Kings are angry, and they are satisfied with the content of kings. (Bukhari 4359. Ahmad 363)"
"38179","(38179) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We have been informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he died, he said: People came in and prayed for him, then they left, and others entered as well. He said: I said to Ataa: Do they pray and supplicate? He said: They pray and ask forgiveness."
"38180","(38180) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: No imam was appointed over the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they would enter in crowds, praying for him and leaving."
"38181","(38181) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: When the Prophet was arrested May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Umm Ayman was made to cry, and it was said to her: Why are you crying, O Umm Ayman? She said: I cry over the news of the heavens, being cut off from us. (Ibn Saad 226. Tabarani 227)"
"38182","(38182) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested Peace be upon him, Abu Bakr said to Omar, or Omar to Abu Bakr: Go with us to Umm Ayman and we will visit her, so they went to her. She began to cry, and they said to her: O Umm Ayman, what is with God is better for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So she said: It is better. I know that what God has is better for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I cry for you at the news of the heavens, that he has been cut off from us. So she provoked them to cry, and they started crying with her. (Muslim 1907. Ibn Majah 1635)"
"38183","(38183) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: Safiyya went out, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was arrested. He said hello, and she was shining in her dress, meaning she was pointing at him, and she was saying:\nThere have been news and tidings after you. If you had witnessed them, the sermons would not have multiplied."
"38184","(38184) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; The one who buried the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his funeral, were four people, excluding people: Ali, Abbas, and Al-Fadl. And Saleh, the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they bowed down to him and set up a pillar of bricks on him."
"38185","(38185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amer, who said: He entered the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace, grace, and blessings be upon Ali.\n Al-Sha’bi said: Marhab, or Ibn Abi Marhab, told me; That Abd al-Rahman bin Awf entered the grave with them.\n(Ibn Saad 300, Bayhaqi 395)"
"38186","(38186) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, washed himself. And virtue, and its honors.\n He said: Ibn Abi Marhab told me; That Abd al-Rahman bin Awf entered the grave with them.\n He said: Al-Sha’bi said: Whoever takes care of the dead except his family.\n And in the hadith of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled: And Ali began to say: By my father and my mother, you are blessed alive and dead."
"38187","(38187) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was washed. In a shirt, Ali was on his way, and Al-Fadl was embracing him, and Al-Abbas was pouring water. He said: And Al-Fadl was saying: Have mercy on me. I cut my tendon, I find something descending on me. He said: And he washed himself from the well of Saad bin Khaythamiya with a Quba, and that is the well. Which is called: Aris Well. He said: By God, I drank from it and took a bath. (Abdul Razzaq 6077)"
"38188","(38188) Abdul-Ala and Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; That Ali sought from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same way one seeks from a dead person, but he did not find anything, so he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for it. You were blessed alive and you were blessed dead."
"38189","(38189) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: When they wanted to wash the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He was wearing a shirt, and they wanted to take it off, so they heard a call from the house: Do not take off the shirt."
"38190","(38190) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah Bin Utbah, on the authority of Aisha and Ibn Abbas; That Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after he died. (Bukhari 4455, Ibn Majah 1457)"
"38191","(38191) Abd al-Aziz bin Aban bin Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Messenger of God was arrested The people cried, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so Omar stood up in the mosque and preached, and said: I do not hear anyone claiming that Muhammad is dead. But his Lord sent to him, just as He sent to Moses his Lord. God sent to Moses, and he remained for his people for forty. Night, by God, I hope that the hands and feet of men who claim that he is dead will be cut off."
"38192","(38192) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us one day while we were in the mosque, and he was tying his head with a rag. The illness in which he died, so he retreated before the pulpit, until he sat on it, so we followed him, and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, He was standing at the basin at the hour, and he said: A servant was presented with this world and was beautified, so he chose the other and did not understand it. Nobody except Abu Bakr. Then his eyes filled with tears and he cried and said: By my father and my mother, but rather we will ransom you with our fathers and our mothers. And our lives and our wealth. He said: Then he descended, and did not rise until the Hour, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"38193","(38193) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy, he said: Where will I be? Tomorrow? They said: At so-and-so’s house. He said: Where will I be the day after tomorrow? They said: With so-and-so, and their wives knew that he only wanted Aisha, so they said: O Messenger of God, we have granted our days. To our sister Aisha. (Ibn Saad 233)"
"38194","(38194) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah said: I came to Aisha and said: Tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill and became heavy and fainted. She said: Then he woke up and said: Put some water in it for me. The one who was dyed, so we did. She said: So he took a bath, so he went to sleep and fainted. She said: Then he woke up, so he said: Give him some water. In the bath, she said: We did that, she said: So he took a bath, then he went to sleep, and he fainted, then he regained consciousness, and he said: Have people prayed yet? So we said: No, O Messenger of God, they are waiting for you. She said: And the people are sitting back and waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. To pray the evening prayer with them.\n She said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath, then he went to sleep and fainted, then he regained consciousness and said: I pray. People yet? I said: No, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So the Messenger came to him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to lead the people in prayer. He said: O Omar, lead the people in prayer, so he said: You have more right. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to you. She said: So Abu Bakr led them in prayer those days.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found a shoe on himself, so he went out for the noon prayer, between Abbas and another man. So he said to them: Make me sit on your right. When Abu Bakr heard what he felt, he went back and ordered him to stand still. His place, she said: So they made him sit on his right, and Abu Bakr was leading the prayer with the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He saluted while sitting, and the people were praying with the prayer of Abu Bakr.\n He said: So I came to Ibn Abbas and said: Shall I not show you what Aisha told me? He said: Come, so I showed him this, and he did not deny anything of it, except that he said: I told you about the other man? He said: I said: No, and he said: He is Ali, may God have mercy on him."
"38195","(38195) Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: When he died The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the preachers of the Ansar stood up, and a man among them began to say: O community of immigrants, indeed the Messenger of God If God, may God bless him and grant him peace, employed a man from among you, he would pair with him a man from among us, so we see that this matter will be the case. two men; One of them is from you and the other from us. He said: Then the Ansar’s preachers continued on that, then Zayd ibn Thabit stood up and said: Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was one of the immigrants, and the Imam is only one of the immigrants, and we are his supporters as we were. Supporters of the Messenger of God, so Abu Bakr stood up and said: May God reward you, O people of Ansar, and your speaker was steadfast, then he said: By God, if you had done otherwise, we would not have reconciled with you. (Ahmad 1851, Ibn Saad 212)"
"38196","(38196) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Harmala narrated to me, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, he was placed on his bed, and people were entering Groups of groups came upon him. They prayed over him and went out, but no one led them in prayer. He died on a Monday and was buried on the same day. The Three, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Saad 288)"
"38197","(38197) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba. He narrates, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: Omar performed Hajj and wanted to address the people, so Abd said Al-Rahman bin Awf: Indeed, the rabble of people and their lowly people have gathered around you, so delay that until you come to Medina. He said: Then when I arrived at Medina and approached the pulpit, and I heard him say: I have come to know that some people say: I refuse to disagree with you. A virgin was a fuss, but it was a fuss, but God protected him from the evil of it. Indeed, there is no disagreement except with your advice."
"38198","(38198) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Utba, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I used to disagree with Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, while we were in Manna with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, I was teaching Abdul-Rahman bin Awf the Qur’an, so I went to him at the house, but I did not find him. It was said: He is with Amir. The believers, so I waited for him until he came, and he said to me: He has become angry this day, as I have never seen him angry since he was. He said: I said why that? He said: He heard that two men from the Ansar mentioned that he sold out to Abu Bakr, and they said: By God, it was nothing but a mess, so what prevented him? If this man were to perish, he should go to the one he loves and strike him by the hand, and it would be as it was. He said: Then Omar understood. To speak to the people. He said: So I said: Do not do that, O Commander of the Faithful, for you are in a country where the ravages of the Arabs have gathered. All of them, and if you say something that will be carried about you and spread throughout the earth, you do not know what that means, but rather He will help you whom you know will go to Medina.\n When we arrived at Medina, I fled, until I took the right side of the pulpit, and Sa’id bin Zayd bin Amr went to me. Ibn Nufayl, until he sat with me.So I said: They will say something this day. He has not said it since he was appointed successor. He said: What might he say? I said: You will hear that.\n He said: When the people gathered, Omar went out until he sat on the pulpit, then he praised and praised God, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned Peace and blessings of God be upon him, so he prayed for him, then he said: God has kept His Messenger among us, and the revelation from God will come down to him. It is lawful and forbidden, then God took His Messenger, and He raised from him what He wished to be raised, and left from him what He wished to remain. So we clung to some, and we missed some, and among what we used to read from the Qur’an was: Do not turn away from your fathers, for that is disbelief in you. That you have shied away from your fathers, and the verse of stoning was revealed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned us and we stoned with him, and the same Muhammad is in his hand. You have preserved it, taught it, and understood it. And had it not been said: Omar wrote in the Qur’an what was not in it, I would have written it in My hand as a book, and stoning depends on three conditions: a clear burden, or a confession from its owner, or just witnesses, As God commanded.\n It has reached me that men say regarding the dispute with Abu Bakr: It was a frivolity, and by my life if it was like that, But God gave good and protected evil.And which of you is the one to whom necks are cut off just as they were cut off to Abu Bakr?\n It was a matter among the people: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so we came, and it was said to us: The Ansar had I gathered in the Saqifah of Banu Sa’id with Sa’d bin Ubadah to pledge allegiance to him, so I stood up, Abu Bakr stood up, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah was like them, and they were afraid that they would create a rift in Islam, so we met two men from the Ansar; A truthful man, Awaym bin Sa`idah and Maan bin Adi, and they said: Where do you want? So we said: Your people, when we heard of their matter, and they said: Go back, for you will not disobey, and nothing will be given to you that you dislike. So we refused but to go, and I was falsifying words that I wanted to speak, until we came to the people, and behold, they... Akar came to you upon Saad bin Ubadah, and he was on the bed of a sick man. When We concealed them, they spoke and said: O people. Quraysh, one of us is a leader and one of you is a leader. Then Al-Hubab bin Al-Mundhir stood up and said: I am its woven tail and its neck. Al-Murjib, if you wish. By God, We will return you to Him in a strong way.\n Abu Bakr said: On your messengers, so I went to speak, and he said: Listen, O Omar, so he thanked God and praised him, then He said: O people of Ansar, by God, we do not deny your bounty.Neither is your affliction in Islam, nor is your right obligatory upon us, but you have known that this neighborhood is from Quraysh. In your position among the Arabs, no one else has it, and that the Arabs will not gather except against one of them, so we are the princes and you Ministers, fear God, and do not divide Islam, and do not be the first to innovate in Islam. Indeed, I have approved anyone for you. These two men are mine and my father Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, so whichever of them you pledge allegiance to, you have trust in him. He said: By God, there is nothing left that I would have loved to say except that He said it, on that day, other than these words. By God Because to be killed, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, without disobedience, is more beloved to me than to be a leader over my people. Among them is Abu Bakr.\n He said, Then I said: O community of Ansar, O community of Muslims, indeed the people are most worthy of the command of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. After him: {The second of the two when they were in the cave} Abu Bakr Al-Sabāq Al-Matin, then I took him by the hand, and a man rushed to me. From the Ansar, he struck his hand before I struck his hand, then I struck his hand, and the people followed suit, and he inclined towards Sa’d. Ibn Ubad, and the people said: Saad was killed, so I said: Kill him, may God kill him, then we left.God had united the affairs of the Muslims regarding Abu Bakr, and it was a blessing for God’s life, as you said. God gave him goodness and protection. It is evil, so whoever calls for something similar to it, then he is the one to whom no pledge of allegiance is made, nor to the one to whom he pledged allegiance. (Bukhari 2484, Abu Dawud 4417)"
"38199","(38199) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of God was arrested May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Ansar said: Among us is a leader and there is a leader among you. He said: Then Omar came to them and said: O people of the Ansar, Do you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? They said: Yes, he said: Which of you would like to precede Abu Bakr? They said: We seek refuge in God lest we approach Abu Bakr."
"38200","(38200) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, Zayd bin Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of his father Aslam; When the pledge of allegiance was made to Abu Bakr after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ali and Al-Zubayr used to enter upon him. Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They consulted her and returned about their matter. When that reached Omar bin Al-Khattab went out until he came to Fatima and said: O daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, there is no one among creation who loved to us than your father, and there is no one more beloved to us after your father than you, and I swear to God, that is not an obstacle to me if they come together. These people are with you. I order them to burn down the house.\n He said: When Omar left, they came to her, and she said: You know that Omar came to me, and he swore by God that if you return, he will burn you. House, and I swear to God, they will go ahead with what they swore to do. So depart, guided, so decide what you think, and do not return to me. So they left it and did not return to it until they pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr."
"38201","(38201) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; Abu Bakr and Omar did not witness the burial of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They were among the Ansar, so they were sold out before he was buried. They come back."
"38202","(38202) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar entered upon my father. Bakr, and he was gnawing with his tongue, and Omar said to him: God, God, the successor of the Messenger of God, and he said: Ha. Indeed, this brought me resources."
"38203","(38203) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulika, who said: A man said to Abu Bakr: Oh The successor of God. He said: I am not the successor of God, but I am the successor of the Messenger of God. I am satisfied with that."
"38204","(38204) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of a servant of Rabi’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I do not know how long I will stay. among you, so follow the example of those after me, and he referred to Abu Bakr and Omar, and follow the guidance of Ammar, and Ibn Masoud is afraid of something, so believe him."
"38205","(38205) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salim Al-Muradi Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of Amr bin Harim, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, and Abi Abdullah, a man from Hudhayfah’s companions, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned Like the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, except that he said: Hold on to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd. (Tirmidhi 3463. Ibn Saad 334)"
"38206","(38206) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of a man from Banu Zurayq, who said: When that happened Today Abu Bakr and Omar went out until they came to the Ansar, and Abu Bakr said: O people of the Ansar, we do not deny your right. Let no believer deny your rights. By God, we have never done anything good except what you shared with us, but neither the Arabs nor the Arabs are satisfied with it. You only approve of a man from Quraysh, because they are the most eloquent of people, the most beautiful of people, the middle of the Arabs in family, and the most people. We were embarrassed by the Arabs, so they went to Omar and they sold him allegiance. He said: They said: No, so Omar said: Why? They said: We fear the impact. Omar said: As long as I live, no. He said: So they pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr.\n Abu Bakr said to Omar: You are stronger than me, and Omar said: You are better than me, so they said it the second time, and when it was the third time, Omar said to him: Indeed, my strength is yours with your grace. He said: So they pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr.\n Muhammad said: And the people came when Abu Bakr sold Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, and he said: Do you come to me while there are a third of three among you? Meaning, Abu Bakr.\n Ibn Aoun said: So I said to Muhammad: From the third of three. He said: God’s saying: {The second of two when they were in the cave}"
"38207","(38207) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: I heard Aisha and she was asked: O Mother of the Believers, who was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appoint a successor, or was he appointed as a successor? She said: Abu Bakr. He said: Then it was said to her: Then who? She said: Then Omar. It was said: Who after Omar? She said: Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, then she ended with that."
"38208","(38208) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: I heard Ali saying: He was arrested. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was the best of the prophets ever condemned, and he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praised him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Then Abu Bakr was appointed as successor, so he did the work of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his Sunnah, then he was arrested. Abu Bakr was the best of anyone who was arrested, and he was the best of this nation after its Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Omar was appointed as their successor, and he followed their actions and their traditions, then he was arrested as best as anyone has ever been arrested, and he was the best of them. The Ummah after her Prophet and after Abu Bakr."
"38209","(38209) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Utbah, he said: When someone who apostatized against the covenant of Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr wanted to strive with them, so Omar told him : Should I fight them when I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Who bears witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger? God has forbidden his property and blood except according to what is due to him, and his account is with God? Abu Bakr said: I will not fight anyone who differentiates between prayer and zakat? By God, I will fight whoever separates them until they are united. Omar said: So we fought with him, and by God he was of the right path. When he defeated whoever He was victorious among them. He said: They chose between two plans: either a shameful war, or a shameful mistake. They said: This We have known the shameful war, so what is the shameful mistake? He said: You bear witness that those who killed us are in Paradise, and that those who killed you are in Hell. So they did."
"38210","(38210) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salama, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Abi Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, that she used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. So he descended upon Abu Bakr, and if he had descended upon the mountains, he would have conquered them. Hypocrisy was full of hypocrisy in Medina, and the Arabs apostatized. By God, they did not differ. At one point, my father was overtaken by her luck and hardship in Islam, and she used to say along with this: And whoever saw Omar ibn al-Khattab knew that he He was created to sing for Islam. By God, he was an Ahwazi, a weaver alone, and he was prepared for similar matters. (Ahmed 68)"
"38211","(38211) Waki’ and Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith; When death approached him, Abu Bakr sent to Omar to appoint him as his successor, and the people said: Will you succeed us with harsh words, even if you And to us, he was harsher and harsher, so what will you say to your Lord when you meet him, and you have left Umar behind us? Abu Bakr said: “My Lord! Do you scare me? I say: Oh God, I have left over them the best of your creation.\n Then he sent for Omar and said: I have given you a commandment if you keep it: Indeed, God has a right by day that He does not accept by night. Indeed, God has a right by the night, which He does not accept by the day, and He does not accept a voluntary prayer until you perform the obligatory prayer. The scales of those whose scales are heavy on the Day of Resurrection will be heavy because they follow them in this world. The truth will be heavy on them, and it will be heavy on them. For a scale in which nothing can be placed except what is right so long as it is heavy, and the scales will be light only for those whose scales will be light on the Day of Resurrection. By their following falsehood and its lightness for them, and the right of a balance in which nothing is placed except falsehood that it should be light, and indeed God He reminded the people of Paradise of the righteousness of what they did, and that He overlooked their evil deeds, so the one who said: I will not inform these people. He reminded the people of Hell of the worst of what they had done, and that He would return to them the good of what they had done, so someone would say: I am better than these. And he mentioned the signs of mercy and the signs of punishment, so that the believer might be willing and in awe, not wishing upon God other than the truth, nor He throws his hand into destruction.\n If you keep my will, no one absent is dearer to you than death, and if you neglect my will, there will be no He is absent, more hateful to you than death, and you will not be able to defeat him."
"38212","(38212) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I saw Omar ibn al-Khattab with A grove of palm trees, and he would make people sit and say: Listen to the words of the successor of the Messenger of God. He said: A servant of Abu Bakr came. It was said to him: He is strong in his manuscripts, so he read them to the people, and he said: Abu Bakr says: Listen and obey whoever is in this. Al-Sahifa, by God, I have not given you permission. Qays said: I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab after that on the pulpit."
"38213","(38213) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The most mare of people Three: Abu Bakr, when he looked into Omar and appointed him as his successor, and she said: “Hire him. Indeed, the best of those whom you hire is the strong.” The Trustworthy} and the Mighty when he said to his wife: {Honour my resting place}"
"38214","(38214) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I came and behold, Umar was standing on a hut. And Othman bin Hanif, and he said: You are afraid that you will burden the earth with what it cannot bear. Hudhayfah said: If I wished, I could weaken my land. Othman said: My land has brought something that is worthy of it, and there is not much bounty in it, so he said: Look at what you two have. You two have burdened the earth beyond its capacity. Then he said: By God, if God gives me peace, I will leave the widows of the people of Iraq so that they will not need me after me. Never to anyone. He said: Only four people came to him until he was injured.\n He said: When he entered the mosque, he would stand between the rows and say: “Stand on.” When they had leveled, he would go forward and say “Allahu Akbar.” He said: “And when he said “Allahu Akbar,” he would be stabbed. His place. He said, I heard him say: The dog killed me, or the dog ate me. Amr said: I don’t know which one he said? There was no one between me and him except Ibn Abbas, so Omar took Abdul Rahman bin Awf by the hand and brought him forward, and the cure flew away. And in his hand was a double-edged knife. He did not pass by a man to the right or to the left without stabbing him until he killed thirteen of them. A man, and nine of them died. He said: When a man from among the Muslims saw that, he laid down a robe for him to take, and when he thought He was caught and killed himself.He said: We prayed a light Fajr prayer. He said: As for the areas around the mosque, they did not know what the matter was except that they were where they lost the voice of Omar, they started saying: Glory be to God, twice, and when they left, the first one to enter upon them was Ibn Abbas, and he said: Look who He killed me? He said: So he walked around for a while, then he came and said: The boy of al-Mughirah al-Sinaa, and he was a carpenter. He said: Then Omar said: Praise be to God who did not He places my death in the hand of a man who claims Islam. May God kill him. I have commanded him to be kind. He said: Then he said to Ibn Abbas: I have You and your father loved to go to Medina a lot. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: If you wish, we can do so. He said: After Speak your words, perform your prayers, and perform your rituals?\n He said: Then the people said to him: There is nothing wrong with you. He said: So he called for wine and drank, and it came out of his wound. Then he called for milk and he drank it. Then he came out of his wound, and he thought it was death, so he said to Abdullah bin Omar: Look at what debt I owe and consider it, so he said: Six. Eighty thousand, and he said: If he pays it with the wealth of the family of Umar, then he will pay it on my behalf from their wealth, otherwise the Banu Adi bin Ka’b will fail. Give back some of their wealth, otherwise take away a Quraysh, and do not return it to anyone else, so pay it back on your behalf.Go to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and salute and say: Omar bin Al-Khattab seeks permission, and do not say: Commander of the Believers, for I I have no authority today to be buried with his companion. He said: So Abdullah bin Omar came to her and found him sitting. He cried, so he greeted him, then said: Omar bin Al-Khattab asks permission to be buried with his two companions. She said: By God, I wanted him. For myself, and I would prefer him today over myself. When he came, it was said: This is Abdullah bin Omar. He said: So he said: Arfa’ani. Then a man led him to him and said: What do you have? He said: I give you permission. He said: Then Omar said: Nothing was more important to me than that. Then he said: If I die, carry me. My bed, then ask for permission, then say: Omar bin Al-Khattab asks for permission, so if I give you permission; So let me in, and if you do not give the call to prayer, take me back to the Muslim graves. He said: When the load was carried, it was as if no calamity had befallen the people except At that time, he said: Abdullah bin Omar greeted him and said: Omar bin Al-Khattab is asking permission, so I gave him permission, as God has honored him with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr.\n So they said to him when death approached him: He became a successor, and he said: I do not find anyone more deserving of this matter than this group.The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and he was satisfied with them. So whichever of them they left behind is the caliph after me. He named Ali, Uthman, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, and Sa’d. If it is similar to Sa’d, then so be it. Otherwise, So whoever of them is appointed a successor, let him seek help, for I did not remove him due to inability or betrayal.\n He said: He made Abdullah bin Omar consult with them, but he had nothing to do with the matter.\n He said: When they gathered, Abdul Rahman bin Awf said: Make your command to three people. He said: So Al-Zubair made his command to me. Ali, and Talha handed over his authority to Uthman, and Saad handed over his authority to Abd al-Rahman. He said: So command those three when he was appointed The matter is up to them. He said: Then Abdul Rahman said: Which of you disavows himself from the matter and leaves the matter up to me? May God bless you so that I do not turn away from it. Who is the best of you and the best among Muslims? Then the two sheikhs, Ali and Othman, were silent, and Abdul Rahman said: You will give it to me and I will leave it. By God, I will not stop you from doing so. Who is the best of you and the best among Muslims? They said: Yes, so he went alone with Ali and said: You are related to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by ancestors, and may God be upon you. If you were left behind, you would surely be just.And if Othman is appointed successor, will you listen and obey? He said: He said: Yes. He said: He was alone with Uthman. He said: Like that. Uthman said to him: Yes. Then he said: O Uthman, extend your hand. So he extended his hand and pledged allegiance to him, and Ali and the people pledged allegiance to him.\n Then Omar said: I enjoin upon the caliph after me to fear God, as did the first emigrants, to know their rights, and to recognize them. To them I have forbidden them, and I enjoin goodness upon the people of the lands, for they are the repugnance of Islam, the anger of the enemy, and the collectors of wealth. If it is not taken from them, then he will curse them with their consent, and he will advise the Ansar well. Those who have lived in the land and the faith, that He may accept from their doers of good and overlook their wrongdoers, and I advise them to treat the Bedouins well. For they are the origin of the Arabs and the foundation of Islam, to be taken from their wealth and returned to their poor, and I enjoin them to be pious. God and His Messenger have protected him, that he should fulfill his promise to them, and that they should not be burdened with anything except what he can bear, and that he should fight whomever Behind them (Bukhari 1392)"
"38215","(38215) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi; When Omar bin Al-Khattab came, he said: Call for me Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Uthman, Abd Al-Rahman bin Awf, and Sa’d. He said: He did not speak to any of them except Ali and Othman, so he said: O Ali, perhaps these people know you. Your kinship, and whatever God has given you of knowledge and jurisprudence, fear God, and if you are given charge of this matter, do not exalt the sons of so-and-so above the necks of the people. And he said to Othman: O Othman, these people may know your brother-in-law from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And your age, and your honour, so if you are in charge of this matter, fear God, and do not raise the son of so-and-so above the necks of the people. So he said: Pray for him. Suhaib, and he said: Lead the people in three, and let this group gather and be alone, and if they agree on a man, then strike the head of the one who He disagreed with them."
"38216","(38216) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of his uncle Isa ibn Talha, and Urwah ibn Al-Zubair, they said: Omar said: Let Suhayb pray for you three times, and wait. If that is the case, otherwise it is the command of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he does not leave it for more than three days."
"38217","(38217) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d al-Ghatfani??, on the authority of Ma’dan Ibn Abi Talha Al-Amari; Omar ibn al-Khattab stood up to give a Friday sermon, or delivered a Friday sermon, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he mentioned The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, then he said: O people, I have seen a vision as if it were a rooster He reddened me twice, and I do not see that except for the coming of my time, and the people are ordering me to become a successor, and God has not He will waste his religion and his caliphate, and the one with whom he sent his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. If something is hastened, The dispute was a matter of consultation between these six people, on whose behalf the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. He is satisfied, so which of them have you pledged allegiance to, so listen to him and obey him, and I knew that some men would challenge this matter, and I I fought them with my own hand for the sake of Islam, but if they did that, then those are the misguided, infidel enemies of God.\n By God, I will not leave behind me anything more important to me than the matter of God. I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he was not harsh. He was harsh to me about something, until he stabbed me with his finger in my side or chest, then he said: O Omar, The verse of summer that was revealed at the end of the women is sufficient for you, and if I live, I will fulfill a matter concerning which no one will disagree. He reads the Qur’an, or he does not read the Qur’an.\n Then he said: Oh God, I call you to witness over the princes of the lands, for I have only sent them to teach the people their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they divide among them, and they do justice among them, so whoever makes anything difficult for him, it will be exonerated. To him\n Then he said: O people, you are eating two trees, and I do not see them as anything but evil. This garlic and this onion, I used to see the man at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was a smell coming from him. Then it will be taken in the hand until it is taken out to Al-Baqi’, and whoever eats it must die by cooking it.\n He said: So Omar proposed to her on Friday, and he came to her on Wednesday, for the remaining four days of Dhul-Hijjah."
"38218","(38218) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Jariyat bin Qadamah Al-Saadi, he said: I performed Hajj The year in which Omar was injured, he said: Then he delivered a speech, and said: I saw that a rooster pecked me two or three times, and then it did not It was only a Friday prayer, or something similar, until he was struck. He said: So he gave permission to the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he gave permission. to the people of Medina, then permission was given to the people of the Levant, then permission was given to the people of Iraq, so we were the last to enter upon him, and his stomach was bound. With black hail, and blood flowing, whenever a people entered, they wept and praised him, so we said to him: Hosanna, and he did not ask of him. No one other than us advised you, so he said: Follow the Book of God, for you will not go astray as long as you follow it, and I advise you By the immigrants, for the people are many and few, and I advise you to treat the Ansar, for they are the people of the faith to which they have taken refuge. And I enjoin upon you to treat the Bedouins, for they are your origin and origin, and I enjoin upon you the protection of your people, for they are the protection of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and may he provide for your children. Arise from me, for we have not added to these words."
"38219","(38219) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: When Omar was stabbed, the people quarreled with each other. In some cases, until the sun was about to rise, then a caller called out: Prayer, so they brought Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and he led them in prayer, so he recited With the two shortest surahs in the Qur’an: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar}, and: {When God’s victory comes}, and when the morning came, the doctor came to him, His wound was bleeding, so he said: Which drink do you like best? He said: Wine, so he called for wine and drank it and it came out from his wound. He said: This is pus, bring me milk. So he brought milk. So he drank and his wound came out, and the doctor said to him: I advise you, for I do not think that you are dead today, or tomorrow."
"38220","(38220) Ishaq al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Amir, who said: He swore by God, Omar had been stabbed And it is among the bees that they recite it."
"38221","(۳۸۲۲۱) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ إِدْرِیسَ ، عَنْ شُعْبَۃَ ، عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ إِبْرَاہِیمَ ، عَنِ ابْنِ مِینَائَ ، عَنِ الْمِسْوَرِ بْنِ مَخْرَمَۃَ ، قَالَ : سَمِعْتُ عُمَرَ ، وَإِنَّ إِحْدَی أَصَابِعِی فِی جُرْحِہِ ہَذِہِ ، أَوْ ہَذِہِ ، أَوْ ہَذِہِ ، وَہُوَ یَقُولُ : یَا مَعْشَرَ قُرَیْشٍ ، إِنِّی لاَ أَخَافُ النَّاسَ عَلَیْکُمْ ، إِنَّمَا أَخَافُکُمْ عَلَی النَّاسِ ، إِنِّی قَدْ تَرَکْتُ فِیکُمْ ثِنْتَیْنِ ، لَنْ Rejoice in goodness as long as you adhere to them: justice in judgement, and justice in oath. Indeed, I have left you in a state of delusion. Blessings, unless a people deviates, and they are deviant."
"38222","(38222) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramima, he said: I and Ibn Abbas entered upon Omar after he had been stabbed and had fainted, so we said: He is not paying attention to anything. He finished the prayer for him, so we said: The prayer, O Commander of the Faithful. Then he took notice and said: The prayer. No one has any share in Islam. He left the prayer, so he prayed, even though his wound was bleeding."
"38223","(38223) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, who said: I used to leave the row. The first one was for Omar, and I was in the second row the day he was injured, so he came and said: Prayer is servants of God, be level. He said: So he prayed. With us, Abu Lulu’a stabbed him two times, or three times. He said: And Omar wore a yellow garment. He said: So he gathered it on his chest, then Ahwa, and he says: {And the command of God is a decreed decree} So he killed and stabbed twelve or thirteen. He said: And the people turned aside. Ali, then he leaned on his dagger and killed himself. (Ibn Saad 348)"
"38224","(38224) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Harith Al-Khuza’i, who said: I heard Omar saying in his sermon: Yesterday I saw a rooster that pecked me, and I saw it being carried away by the people, and I I swear to God, if I remain, I will make the lowest of the Muhajireen in giving two thousand two thousand. Only three people stayed. Until Al-Mughirah’s servant, Abu Lulu’a, killed him."
"38225","(38225) Ja`far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: Omar did not single out anyone from The people of Shura, not anyone else, except that he was alone with Ali and Uthman, each one of them alone, and he said: O so-and-so, fear God. If God tests you with this matter, do not raise the son of so-and-so above the necks of people and say the same to another."
"38226","(38226) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hassan bin Muhammad, who said: Omar said to Uthman: Fear God. And if you are in charge of any of the people’s affairs, do not burden the Banu Abi Mu’it on the necks of the people. And he said to Ali: Fear God. Any of the people’s affairs, so do not burden Banu Hashim on the necks of the people."
"38227","(38227) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Omar, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Zur’a, a scholar from among the scholars of the people of the Levant. He said: I said to him: Who prayed for Omar? He said: Suhayb."
"38228","(38228) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; When Omar was stabbed, people came to praise him and pray for him, so Omar, may God have mercy on him, said: Will the Emirate purify me? I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was satisfied with it. I accompanied Abu Bakr, so I listened and obeyed. So Abu Bakr died while I was listening and obedient, and I no longer feared for myself except your leadership."
"38229","(38229) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salama narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, and sheikhs, they said: Omar bin Al-Khattab saw in a dream, and he said: I saw a red rooster that pecked me three times. The second one and the secret one. Asma’ bint Umays, the mother of Abdullah bin Ja’far, said: Tell him “Filus,” and she used to express visions. I do not know whether he was informed of that or not, so Abu Lulu’a, the infidel Magian, Abd al-Mughirah ibn Shu`ba, came to him and said: Al-Mughirah has imposed on me an amount of tax that I cannot bear. He said: How much has he imposed on you? He said: Such and such. He said: What did you do? He said: I will bring the millstones. He said: And that is not too much trouble for you. There is no one on our land who can make it except you. Will you not make a millstone for me? ? He said: Yes, by God, I will make for you a coffin that the people of the far-flung lands will hear of.\n So Omar went out for Hajj, and when he left, he lay down on the gravel, and put his cloak under his head, and he looked at the moon and was amazed. His perfection and goodness, and he said: He started out weak, then God continued to increase and develop him until he became good, so he was better. As it was, then it decreases until it returns to how it was, and so is all of creation. Then He raised His Hand and said: Oh God, my flock has increased and spread,So take me to You, neither helpless nor lost.\n So he went to Medina, and it was reported to him that a Muslim woman had died in the desert, lying on the ground. He passed by. No one would shroud it, nor would anyone hide it, until Kulayb ibn al-Bukayr al-Laythi passed by it and stayed there. Ali, until he shrouded her and showed her, so he mentioned that to Omar, and he said: Who among the Muslims passed by her? They said: Abdullah bin Omar passed by her. Among the Muslims who passed by her, he called him and said: Woe to you, did you pass by? A Muslim woman was lying on the side of the road. Why did you hide her or shroud her? He said: I did not feel it, nor did anyone mention it to me. He said: I was afraid that there would be no good in you. He said: Who saw it? And who shrouded us? They said: Kulaib bin Bukair Al-Laythi. He said: By God, it is certain that something good should happen to Kulaib.\n So Omar went out to wake the people in his courtyard for the morning prayer, but the infidel Abu Lulu’a met him and stabbed him three times between The double and the navel, and Kulayb bin Bukair was stabbed and killed, and the people shouted, then a man shot him on the head. With Burnus, then they took him to him, and Omar was carried to the house, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf led the people in prayer, and Omar was told: The prayer. So he prayed while his wound was broken,And he said: There is no share in Islam for one who does not pray. So he prayed while his blood was shed, then the people went away to him and said: O Amir. Believers, there is no harm in you, and we hope that God will be pleased with you and delay you for a while, or To the best.\n Then Ibn Abbas came to him and was amazed at him, so he said: Go out and see who is my companion? Then he came out and said: Give good news, O Commander of the Faithful, your companion is Abu Lulu’a al-Majusi, the servant of al-Mughirah ibn My people, so he said Allahu Akbar until his voice came out from the door, then he said: Praise be to God who did not make him a man of the Muslims. He is asking me about his prostration. He prostrated to Him on the Day of Resurrection. Then he turned to the people and said: Was this on behalf of a group of you? They said: God forbid, by God, we wish we had ransomed you for our fathers and given you more lives than ours. Indeed, there is no harm in you.\n He said: Yes, give me a drink. Then he brought him a goblet containing sweet wine and he drank it, and he pressed his robe to his stomach. He said: When the drink fell into his stomach, the stab wounds came out. They said: Praise be to God. This is blood that settled in your stomach, so God took it out. From your stomach, he said: Yes, it will heal, and itching, give me milk to drink. So he brought milk and drank it, and when it fell into his stomach, the wounds came out.When they saw that, they knew that he was perished.\n They said: May God reward you with good. You used to act among us according to the Book of God and follow the Sunnah of your companion, never deviated from it. Others, may God reward you with the best reward, said: You make me happy with the Emirate. By God, I wish I could be saved from it on a sufficiency. Ali, nor for me. Arise and consult yourselves. Appoint a man from among you over you, and whoever disagrees with him, strike his head. He said: So they stood up, and Abdullah bin Omar was leaning against his chest. Abdullah said: Will you be appointed commander while the Commander of the Faithful is alive? So Omar said: No, and let Suhayb pray three times, and wait for Talha, and consult about your matter, then appoint a man from among you over you. If he disagrees with you, then strike his head. He said: Go to Aisha, and extend my greetings to her, and say: Omar says: If As long as it does not harm you or make you difficult, I would love to be buried with my companion, even if it would harm you. And it is difficult for you, because by my life, some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace and his mothers, were buried in this place. Who is better than Omar for the believers? Then the Messenger came to her and she said: This will not harm me, nor will it be difficult for me. He said: So bury me with them. Abdullah bin Omar said: Then he let death cover him, and I am holding him to my chest.He said: Woe to you, put my head on the ground. He said: Then he was seized by a fainting spell, and I found out about that, so he regained consciousness. He said: Woe to you, put My head on the ground, so I placed his head on the ground, and he covered it with dirt, and said: Woe to Omar, and woe to his mother if God does not forgive him. No\n Muhammad bin Amr said: The people of Shura: Ali, Uthman, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Saad, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf."
"38230","(38230) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, who said: I performed Hajj in an emirate. Omar, but they did not doubt that the caliphate after him would be for Uthman."
"38231","(38231) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan, who said: Abdullah said when Uthman was appointed successor: What Deviate us from the Most High, the One Above."
"38232","(38232) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud He said when Othman was pledged allegiance: We did not turn away from the highest of them."
"38233","(38233) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: Haram bin Al-Harith narrated to me, And Asama bin Khurraym said: They were fighting, so they both told me, and not one of them felt that his companion was He told me, on the authority of Al-Bahzi, who said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day on the road From the roads of Medina, he said: How will you deal with a trial that will erupt throughout the ends of the earth as if they were cows’ cows? They said: What shall we do, O Prophet of God? He said: This and his companions are upon you. He said: So I hastened until I felt compassion for the man, and said: Is this, O Prophet of God? He said: This, then it is Othman."
"38234","(38234) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Wathhab informed me, and he was among those who The emancipation of the Commander of the Faithful Omar caught up with him, and he was still in the hands of Othman. He said: I saw two stab wounds in his throat. It was as if they had been stabbed on the day of the house, the house of Othman. He said: The Commander of the Faithful, Othman, sent me. He said: Call for Ashtar. Then he came, and Ibn Aoun said: I think he said: So I put out a cushion for the Commander of the Faithful, and he had a cushion, so he said: O Ashtar, what What do people want from me? He said: Three, none of them are necessary. They give you a choice between you submitting their affairs to them and saying: This is your command. Choose for him whomever you wish, and be sure that you will be cut off from yourself. If you refuse, they will come to you, for the people have fought you. He said: There is no Is one of them bad? He said, “None of them is bad.”\n He said: As for me taking off their affairs for them, I would never take off the garment that God Almighty has apparated for me, ever. Ibn Aoun said: And he said Not good: To come forward and have my neck be beheaded is more beloved to me than to be separated from Muhammad’s mother, one over the other. Ibn Aoun said: This is similar to what he said, and as for me telling them about myself, by God, I know that my two companions were in my presence. They will retaliate on their own, and my body cannot retaliate, but as for them killing me, by God, even if they killed me, they would not love one another. after me forever, and they will never fight an enemy altogether after me.\n He said: So Al-Ashtar got up and left, so we stayed, so we said: Perhaps the people, then a man came as if he were a wolf, and he came out of the door, then He returned, and Muhammad bin Abi Bakr stood up on the thirteenth day until he came to Uthman, took his beard, and said with it: Until I heard his molars knock, and he said: Mu’awiyah is of no use to you, Ibn Amir is of no use to you, your books are of no use to you, He said: Send me my brother’s beard, send me my nephew’s beard.\n He said: I saw him antagonize a man from among the people to help him, so he stood up to him with a knife until he brought him to his head. So I confirmed it. He said: Then what? He said: Then they entered upon him and killed him."
"38235","(38235) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, who said: I heard Abu Layla al-Kindi, who said: I saw Othman looking at the people while he was besieged, and he said: O people, do not kill me but take me as a prisoner. By God, if You killed me, you will never fight all of you, and you will never fight an enemy, and you will disagree until you become like this, and network between His fingers, {O my people, do not let my discord with me cause you to suffer lest something befall you like what befell the people of Noah, or the people of Jews, or A righteous people, and the people of Lot are not far from you. He said: And he sent for Abdullah bin Salam and asked him, and he said: Stop, stop, for he has informed you of the Hajj. So they entered upon him. So they killed him."
"38236","(38236) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, who said: I heard Uthman say: Indeed, the greatest of you in singing in my eyes is the one who restrains his weapons and his hands."
"38237","(38237) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit came to Uthman and said: These are the Ansar at the door. They said: If you wish, we can be Ansar Allah twice? He said: As for fighting, no."
"38238","(38238) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubair, he said: I said to Uthman On the Day of Resurrection: Go out and fight them, for with you are those whom God has helped with less than Him, and by God, fighting them is lawful. He said: But he refused. He said: Whoever listens and obeys me, let him obey Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, and his authority at that time was in charge of the house. He was fasting that day."
"38239","(38239) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’; That a man called: Jajaja took a stick that was in the hand of Othman, broke it with his knee, and was thrown away. The place is eaten."
"38240","(38240) Ishaq al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Othman began speaking to people. He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a dream that night, and he said: O Othman, He broke his fast with us, then he fasted in the morning and died from that day."
"38241","(38241) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, he said: You have seen me trustworthy. Omar and his sister accepted Islam, and if he rejected any of what you did to Othman, it would have been true."
"38242","(38242) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, Abu Salih told us, he said: Abdullah bin Salam said: When Othman was confined to the house He said: Do not kill him, for only a few lives are left for him, and by God, if you kill him, you will never be able to pray together."
"38243","(38243) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Abi Imran, he said: Abu Al-Afour narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Mawla. Abdullah bin Masoud said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: By God, if you kill Othman, you will not obtain a successor from him."
"38244","(38244) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; That a man from Quraysh was called: Thumama was in charge of Sana’a, and when he came to him, he killed Uthman, he cried, and he wept for a long time, so when He woke up, he said: Today the prophecy has been taken away, or he said: The caliphate came from the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she became king. It is forced, so whoever overpowers something, he eats it."
"38245","(38245) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: When Uthman was killed, Elijah’s preachers stood up, and he stood up. Among the last of them was a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was called: Murā ibn Ka’b, and he said: Were it not for a hadith I heard from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as I stood up, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a temptation I thought it would be, and he said: So he approached her, and a man masked in his robe passed by, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is the case at that time, and his companions will be upon the truth. So I set off and turned his face to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This? He said: Yes, then it is Othman."
"38246","(38246) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If the people had gathered to kill Othman, they would have stoned him just as the people of Lot were stoned."
"38247","(38247) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: Othman supervised them from Palace, and he said: Bring me a man to whom I will recite the Book of God. So they brought to him Sa`sa` bin Suhan, who was a young man, and he said: Did you not find anyone? Do you bring someone other than this young man? He said: Then Sa`sa spoke some words, and Uthman said to him: Recite, and he said: {Give permission to those who They are fighting because they have been wronged, and indeed, God has power over them. He said: You lied. It is not for you, nor for your companions. But it is for me and for my companions. Then Othman recited: {Permission is given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and indeed, God has power to grant them victory.} Until he reached: {And to God is the end of all matters}"
"38248","(38248) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Al-Hadi used to imitate Uthman and he said:\nThe prince after him is Ali, and in al-Zubayr there is a successor, pleased with him.\n He said: Then Ka’b said: But he is the companion of the gray mule, meaning Mu’awiyah, so it was said to Mu’awiyah: Indeed, Ka’b is making fun of With you, and he claims that you are following this matter. He said: So he came to him and said: O Abu Ishaq, how can you be? Here is Ali. Al-Zubair, and the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are her companion."
"38249","(38249) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi, he said: When Abu Bakr was sold, he said: He said: Salman: You were wrong and you were right. But if you had placed it among the family of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, You would have eaten it freely."
"38250","(38250) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Jawshan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra said: Nothing came to me from our treasury until it left us except a stuffed robe and a khamis. Darabjardia."
"38251","(38251) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, who said: I saw Ali when they were crowding in on him until they made his foot bloody, and he said: Oh God, I have hated them, and they have hated me. So give me relief from them, and give them relief from me."
"38252","(38252) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Muljim and Shabib were surrounded. Al-Ashja'i Ali when he went out at dawn, but Shabib hit him but missed him, and his sword stuck in the wall, then he was trapped. Towards the gates of Kinda, and the people said: On you is the one who wields the sword. So when he feared that he would be taken, he threw the sword and entered into the public view. As for Abd al-Rahman, he struck him with the sword on his horns, then he was besieged towards the elephant’s gate, and a broad, or a wide, overtook him. Al-Hadrami took him and brought him to Ali, and Ali said: If I die, then kill him if you wish, or call him, and if I I survived, it was retaliation."
"38253","(38253) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Suba’, who said: I heard Ali saying: Let it be dyed. This is one of these, so what is expected of the most miserable? They said: So inform us of it. Nabir, his family, said: Then, by God, you would kill others. Kill me. They said: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: No, but I am leaving you to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left you. They said: What do you say to your Lord? If you meet him? He said: I say: Oh God, You left me among them, then You took me to You while You were among them. If You wish, You can reconcile them, and if You wish, You can reconcile them. You spoiled them. (Ahmad 1300, Ibn Saad 34)"
"38254","(38254) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ali saying: What bloodshed, This, meaning his beard, will be dyed with the blood of his head."
"38255","(38255) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: Ali said: What The most wretched of them are prevented from coming and killing me. O God, I am tired of them and they are tired of me, so give me relief from them. And have mercy on them from me. (Ibn Saad 34)"
"38256","(38256) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace for the night of Al-Aqaba: Bring out to me twelve of you, and they will be guarantors over your people. The disciples’ sponsorship was given to Isa bin Maryam, and he was the head of Banu al-Najjar. Ibn Idris said: They are the maternal uncles of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: As’ad bin Zurarah Abu Umamah, and he was the captain of the Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, Abdullah bin Rawahiha, and Saad bin Rabi’, and the captains of Banu Salamah were Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram, and Al-Bara’ bin Ma’rur, and he was The captains of Banu Sa’id were Saad bin Ubadah and Al-Mundhir bin Amr, and the captain of Banu Zurayq was Rafi’ bin Malik, who was The captain of the Banu Awf bin Al-Khazraj, and they are the Qawaqilites, was Ubadah bin Al-Samit, and the captain of the Banu Abd al-Ashhil was Usayd bin Al-Hudayr, and Abu Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan, and he was the captain of Banu Amr bin Awf: Saad bin Khaythamiya. (Ibn Saad 602)"
"38257","(38257) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of God promised us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he arrived at the end of the Day of Sacrifice, and we were seventy men. He said: “I am one of the youngest of them.” So he came to us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make the sermon brief, for I fear for you the infidels of Quraysh. He said: We said: O Messenger of God, we asked for your Lord, we asked for yourself, we asked for your companions, and tell us what the reward will be for God and for you.\n He said: I ask you for my Lord that you believe in Him and do not associate anything with Him, and I ask you for Myself that you obey Me. I guide you to the path of righteousness, and I ask you, for me and my companions, to console us in your own hands, and to prevent us from what You have prevented yourselves from it, and if you do that, the jinn will be yours upon God and upon me. He said: So we extended our hands. So we pledged allegiance to him. (Ahmad 120, Hamid 238)"
"38258","(38258) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Abbas set out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. To the Ansar, and he said: Speak and do not prolong the sermon. Indeed, eyes are upon you, and I fear that the infidels of Quraysh will attack you. Then a man among them spoke, nicknamed: Abu Imamah, and he was their preacher at that time, and he was As’ad bin Zurarah, and he said: To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: We asked for your Lord, we asked for yourself, we asked for your companions, and what is the reward for that? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I ask you for the sake of my Lord to worship Him and not to associate anything with Him, and for myself to Believe in me and prevent me from what you prevent yourself and your children, and for my companions consolation is in your hands. They said: : So what do we have if we do that? He said: May God reward you with Paradise. (Ahmad 1198, Ibn Saad 9)"
"38259","(38259) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, he said: He was among Hudhayf And a man from among them, from the people of Al-Aqaba, was talking to someone who was among the people, and he said: I adjure you by God, how many companions there were. The consequence? So the people said: So tell him, he asked you. Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari said: We were told that there were fourteen of them, so he said Deleted: And if I were among them, they were fifteen. I bear witness to God that twelve of them were at war with God and His Messenger. In the life of this world and on the Day when witnesses will rise, and three will be excused. They say: We did not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted us, and we did not know what the people wanted. (Muslim 2144, Ahmad 391)"
"38260","(38260) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa And he was among those who pledged allegiance under the tree. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicated for the Ahzab and said: O God! The Book, quick to reckon, defeats parties, O God, defeat them and shake them."
"38261","(38261) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Muriya, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Or is it more accurate to say: The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who pledged allegiance under the tree, were one thousand and four hundred, or One thousand and three hundred, and Aslam was one eighth of the emigrants. (Muslim 1485, Tayalisi 820)"
"38262","(38262) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, who said: The first to pledge allegiance under the tree was Abu Sinan. Al-Asadi Wahb came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I pledge allegiance to you. He said: What do you pledge allegiance to? He said: On what is in your mind. He said: So he pledged his allegiance to him. He said: And another man came to him and said: I pledge my allegiance to you on what Abu Ali pledged his allegiance to you. Sinan, so he pledged allegiance to him, then the people pledged allegiance to him."
"38263","(38263) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, he said: The first predecessors are those who realize the Bay’a al-Ridwan."
"38264","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(38264) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka’bah, who said: I came to Abdullah bin Amr and he was sitting in the shade of the Kaaba and the people were gathered around him, and I heard him say: While We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey when we camped at a certain place. Some of us struck his tents, and some of us He is praying, and among us is someone who is in a crowd when his herald calls out: “Prayer is unified.” So we gathered, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up. He greeted us and addressed us, saying: There was no prophet before me except that it was God’s right upon him to guide his nation to what He intended. It is good for them, and He warns them of what He knows is bad for them, and indeed, this nation of yours has been placed in its first place. And at the end of it, they will be afflicted with calamity and matters that you disapprove of, and then temptation will come, and the believer will say: This My doom, then it will be revealed, then tribulation will come, and the believer will say: This is it, then it will be revealed, so who among you has kept it secret? That he may be removed from the Fire and enter Paradise, so that his end may come to fruition, and he may believe in God and the Last Day, and let him come. The people he likes to come to him, and whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him the hand of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as long as he He is able, so if anyone comes to dispute with him, strike the neck of the other. He said: So I brought my head in from among the people, and I said: I adjure you by God. Did you hear this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: So he pointed with his hand to my ears, my ears heard him and my heart understood him. He said: I said: This is your cousin, he commands us. That we consume our property among ourselves unjustly, and that we kill ourselves, and God has said: {Do not consume your property among yourselves. falsehood and point it to the judges} until the end of the verse, he said: So he gathered his hands and placed them on his forehead, then he turned back. Then he said, “Obey him in obedience to God, and disobey him in disobeying God.”\n(Muslim 46 Abu Dawud 4247)"
"38265","(38265) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Rabb al-Ka’bah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with a similar narration, except that it was broken. He said: And the last of it will befall. Trials and temptations exacerbate one another, and he said: Whoever would like to be saved from the Fire and enter Paradise, let him realize his end. Then he mentioned something similar. (Ibn Majah 3956. Ahmed 191)"
"38266","(38266) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, he said: Muslim bin Abi Bakra narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There will be a trial, and the one lying down during it is better than the one sitting, and the one sitting is better than the one standing. And the one who stands is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks is better than the one who runs. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, what do you command me to do? He said: Who was she? He who has camels, let him follow his camels, and whoever has sheep, let him follow his sheep, and whoever has land, let him follow his land. And whoever does not have any of that, let him reach for his sword and strike it on a rock with its sharp edge, then he will be saved. He was able to survive. (Muslim 13. Ahmad 48)"
"38267","(38267) Abdul-Ala and Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Sa’d, who was raised by Ubaidah. Abdul-Ala did not raise it. He said: There will be a trial, in which the one who sits is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands is better than the one who runs, and the one who runs Better than the place. (Hakim 441)"
"38268","(38268) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Najih, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Sakhr bin Badr, on the authority of Khaled bin Suba’i, Or Suba` ibn Khalid, he said: I went to Kufa and brought animals from it. I was near its mosque, when a man came, and the people had gathered. Ali, so I said: Who is this? They said: Hudhayf ibn al-Yaman. He said: So I sat next to him, and he said: People used to ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Good, and I was asking him about evil. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, have you seen this good that we were in? Was there evil before him? Will there be any evil after it? He said: Yes, I said: What is the infallibility of it? He said: The sword. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, is there anything left after the sword? He said: Yes, a truce. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, what comes after the truce? He said: He called for misguidance, so if you see a caliph, adhere to him, and if he beats you up and takes your money, then if there is not one A successor, then flee until death comes to you while you are biting a tree. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, so what comes after that? He said: The emergence of the Antichrist. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, what will the Antichrist bring? He said: He will bring fire and river, so whoever falls into his fire will have his reward incumbent, and his burden will be removed, and whoever falls into his fire will have his reward forfeited. And his burden became due. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, what comes after the Antichrist? He said: If one of you had produced a horse, he would not have ridden its foal until the Hour comes.\n(Abu Dawud 4246. Ahmad 387)"
"38269","(38269) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya, he said: Humaid said: Nasr bin Asim Al-Laythi narrated to us, He said: Al-Yashkari told us, he said: I heard Hudhayf saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to ask people about Good, and I used to ask him about evil, and I knew that good would not overtake me. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, is there yet Is this better than evil? He said: O Hudhaifa, learn the Book of God and follow what is in it. Three times, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, after this? Is good evil? He said: Trial and evil. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, will there be any good after this evil? He said: O Hudhayfy, learn the Book of God and follow what is in it three times. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, come after this. Is good evil? He said: It is a blind and deaf temptation upon which there is an invitation at the gates of Hell, so if you die, O Hudhayf, while you are biting in fear, It is better than following any of them. (Abu Dawud 4243. Ahmad 386)"
"38270","(38270) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabab, he said: narrated to me Ikrimah said: Abdullah bin Amr told me, he said: We were around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he mentioned temptation, or it was mentioned to him, he said: so he said: when the people saw it, their vows were postponed and their trusts were feared, and they were Thus, he interlaced his fingers and said: So I stood up to him and said: What should I do then? May God make me your ransom. He said: So he said to me: Stay at home, keep your tongue, take what you know, leave what you disavow, and keep what is within yourself. And leave the affairs of the public behind you. (Abu Dawud 4245. Ahmed 212)"
"38271","(38271) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Al-Ansari, on the authority of His father, he heard Abu Sa`id say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is about to be the best wealth. A Muslim is a sheep with which he follows the tops of mountains and the places of the countryside, escaping with his religion from temptations. (Bukhari 19. Ahmad 30)"
"38272","(38272) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Hujar bin Al-Rabi’, he said: He said to me: Imran bin Husayn: Go to your people, for they should be afraid in this matter. So I said: Indeed, they are unconcerned, but I am not. He was obedient to them. He said: Then inform them about me, because I am an Ethiopian slave with a flock of goats that I take care of at the top of a mountain. Until death overtakes me is more beloved to me than being shot at one of the two battle groups with an arrow if I miss, or get hit."
"38273","(38273) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Hudhayfy said: Indeed, temptation has pauses. And resurrections. If you are able to die while standing there, then do so. (Hakim 433)"
"38274","(38274) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ziyad bin Samin Kush Al-Yamani, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: There will be a turmoil or turmoil that will wipe out the Arabs. They will be killed in the Fire, the tongue therein is more severe than the impact of the sword. \n(Abu Dawud 4264, Ahmed 211)"
"38275","(38275) Ali bin Musir and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Kabshah Al-Sadusi, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: He addressed us, and he said: Indeed, behind you are temptations like pieces of a dark night, during which a man becomes a believer in the morning and in the evening. An unbeliever, and an unbeliever in the morning and a believer in the evening. The one who sits is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands is better than the one walking, and the one who walks Better than the passenger. They said: What do you command us to do? He said: Be the most beautiful in the houses. (Abu Dawud 4261, Ahmed 408)"
"38276","(38276) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Clearly The hands of the Hour are temptations like parts of a dark night. A man in the morning is a believer and the evening is an unbeliever, and he is a believer in the evening and becomes a believer. An infidel, and he sells people their religion for the offer of this world. (Abu Naim 13)"
"38277","(38277) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Dhayl, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Break your bows, meaning in temptation, And cut the strings and close the insides of the houses, and be in them like the best of the sons of Adam. (Ahmed 408)"
"38278","(38278) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Abu Dharr, what have you seen if people fought until the stones sank? Oil from blood, how do you make it? He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: You enter your house. He said: I said: Should I carry a weapon? He said: Then he participated. He said: I said: What should I do, O Messenger of God? He said: If you fear that the sun's rays will overcome, then throw part of your cloak over your face, and it will conceal your sin and his sin. (Ahmad 1498 Hakim 156)"
"38279","(38279) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: Indeed, behind you are days in which ignorance will descend, knowledge will be raised, and confusion will increase. They said: O Messenger of God, what is the chaos? He said: killing. (Muslim 2057, Ahmad 389)"
"38280","(38280) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, he said: Hudhayfah said : Trials have come upon you like pieces of a dark night, in which every brave man will be destroyed as a hero, every rider will be defeated, and every preacher will be destroyed. splattered"
"38281","(38281) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Kurz bin Alqamiya Al-Khuza’i, who said: A man said : O Messenger of God, is there an end to Islam? He said: Yes, whichever family, whether Arab or non-Arab, God intends good for them, will He admit Islam to them. He said: Then what? He said: Then the temptations will fall like shadows and you will return to it black in the morning, striking the necks of one another, and black: the snake rises. Then it becomes accusative. (Ahmad 477. Tabarani 442)"
"38282","(38282) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Asama, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He looked at one of the ruins of the city, then said: Do you see what I see? I see the sites of temptations in your homes, like the sites of The diameter\n(Bukhari 7060, Muslim 2211)"
"38283","(38283) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal Sayyar bin Salamah, who said: When there was a time Ibn Ziyad narrated: Marwan jumped in the Levant when he jumped, Ibn al-Zubayr jumped in Mecca, and the Qur’aites jumped in Basra, He said: Abu Al-Minhal said: My father was very sad. He said: He used to praise his father well. He said: My father said to me: Yes. Son, go with us to this man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we go to Abu Barza. Al-Aslami was on a very hot day, and he was sitting in the shade of a reed, and my father set out to seek food from him. Hadith, so he said: O Abu Barzah, don’t you see? Don't you see? So the first thing he spoke was, he said: As for me, I have become angry with the revival of Quraysh. You Arabs were against The situation that you have learned due to your smallness and ignorance, and God has revived you with Islam and with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Until what you see has reached you, and this is the world that has created corruption among you. Indeed, it is the one in the Levant. By God, Marwan means that he only fights for the sake of this world, and he is the one in Mecca, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr. By God, he He fights only for the sake of this world, and you call those around you your readers. By God, they fight only for the sake of this world. He said: When he did not leave anyone, my father said to him: Aba Barza, what do you think? He said: I do not see anything better today than a robe of clothing, the soles of whose bellies are made of people’s money, the soles of their backs made of their blood. (Hakim 470)"
"38284","(38284) Abu Muawiyah, Ibn Numayr, and Hamid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, He said: We were sitting with Omar, and he said: Which of you memorizes the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in times of temptation, as he said? So I said: I am. He said: So he said: You are bold, but how? He said: I said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: A man is tempted by his family, his wealth, his soul, and his neighbour. Fasting, charity, and enjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil expiate for her. Omar said: This is not what I want, I only want Which ripples like the waves of the sea. He said: I said: What is the matter with you, O Commander of the Faithful? Indeed, between you and it is a closed door. He said: Will the door be broken or opened? He said: I said: No, rather it will be broken. He said: That is better for it never being closed. He said: We said: To Hudhayfah: Did Omar know from the door? He said: Yes, as I know, that tomorrow is not the night before. Indeed, I narrated to him a hadith. Not with errors. He said: So Hudhayf let us ask him about the topic, so we said to Masruq: Ask him, so he asked him, and he said: Omar. (Muslim 2218. Ibn Majah 3955)"
"38285","(38285) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The whip’s temptation is worse than his temptation. The sword. They said: How is that? He said: A man can be beaten with a whip until he rides on a piece of wood."
"38286","(38286) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, who said: We were at The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned a temptation and its situation was great. He said: So we said, or they said: O Messenger of God, if we overtake This is for us to perish. He said: No, indeed death is sufficient for you.\n Saeed said: I saw my brothers killed. (Ahmad 1898, Tabarani 346)"
"38287","(38287) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Amer bin Wathili, who said: Hudhayfy said: There will be three temptations: the fourth will drive you to the Antichrist, the one that averts dryness, the one that averts flattery, and the unjust one that It ripples like the waves of the sea."
"38288","(38288) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, he said: Humaid said: Nasr bin Asim narrated to us, he said: narrated to us Al-Yashkuri said: I heard Hudhayfah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A blind and deaf trial will befall her. A supplication at the gates of Hell. If you die, Hudhayfah, while you are biting on a mountain, it is better for you than to follow any of them."
"38289","(38289) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, who said: A man said to Hudhayf: How is it? What should I do if the worshipers fight? He said: You enter your house. He said: I said: What should I do if he enters my house? He said: Say: I will not kill you {Indeed, I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds}. (Naim bin Hammad 350)"
"38290","(38290) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Trials have been waged. With three things: with the hard-hitting one who does not want anything to happen to him except to suppress him with the sword, and with the preacher who makes supplications. To God of affairs, and with the honorable mentioned, as for the slaughtered goat, you will quarrel with it, and as for these two, you will search for them and you will be tested. When"
"38291","(38291) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Hudha, on the authority of Kharsha bin Al-Hurr, He said: Hudhayfah said: How are you when she is blessed, dragging her snouts, and she comes to you from here and from here? They said: No. We do not know, by God. He said: But I, by God, know. On that day you will be like a slave and his master, if the master takes him captive and is not able to The servant may curse him, and if he strikes him, the servant cannot strike him."
"38292","(38292) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-Salt bin Bahram narrated to us, on the authority of Mundhir bin Hudhahi, on the authority of Kharsha, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: How will you be if you separate from your religion, just as a woman separates from her qiblah, not preventing anyone from He will come to her. They said: We do not know. He said: But I, by God, know. On that day you will be between helpless and immoral. Then a man from The people: How ugly is the one who is unable to do that. He said: He struck his back repeatedly, then said: You are ugly, you are ugly."
"38293","(38293) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-Salt bin Bahram narrated to us, saying: Al-Mundhir bin Hudhahi narrated to us, on the authority of Kharsha, that Hudhayfy entered the mosque, and he passed by a people who were reciting recitation to one another, and he said: If you are on the path, You have indeed gone far ahead, and if you call on Him you have gone astray. He said: Then he sat down to his audience and said: We were a people who believed before that. We recite, and some people will recite before they believe. Then a man from among the people said: That is the temptation. He said: Yes, it has come to you from In front of you wherever your faces are darkened, then it will come to you constantly. Indeed, the man will return and do two things: One is impotence and the other is immorality. Kharsha said: I had only gone a little while until I saw the man coming out with his sword and showing off. People"
"38294","(38294) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Husayrah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: It was said: For Hudhayfa: What are the stops of temptation, and what are its resurrections? He said: Its resurrections are unsheathing the sword, and its stops are sheathing it."
"38295","(38295) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed informed us that Abu Al-Zubayr informed him, about Abu al-Tufayl Aamir ibn Wathilah said that Hudhayfy said to him: How can you and the best of people be tempted by a secret wealth? He said: I said: How? Indeed, it is the gift of one of us with which every throw is thrown away, and with it every thrown thing is thrown away. He said: Be then like the son of labor. Ride it and you will be ridden, or milk it and you will be milked."
"38296","(38296) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Rawa’, on the authority of Hudhayf. He said: There will be a temptation that will come to the beginning of the month and turn back from its end. If that is the case, then the Bedouins would love the shepherd on his staff to follow his sheep. No. The torrent will take you away."
"38297","(38297) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: It was said to Hudhayfah: Did the Children of Israel become disbelievers in one day? He said: No, but temptations were presented to them and they rejected it. They were forced to force her, then she was presented to them, but they rejected her until they beat her with whips and swords until they fought. He immersed himself in water until they did not recognize any good and did not deny any evil."
"38298","(38298) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Raba’i, who said: I heard a man at Hudhayf’s funeral. He says: I heard the owner of this bed saying: There is nothing wrong with me since I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: And if you fight I will enter my house, and if it enters upon me, I will say: Behold, my sin and your sin. (Ahmad 389. Tayalisi 417)"
"38299","(38299) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saad, who said: Hudhayfah said: Whoever separates from the group by an inch has separated Islam"
"38300","(38300) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhaifa, he said: They will come. There will be a time for people in which no one will be saved except the one who prays with supplications like the supplications of a drowning man."
"38301","(38301) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Ammar, he said: Hudhayfy said: They will come to me. People are in a time in which no one will be saved except those who pray with supplications like the supplications of a drowning man."
"38302","(38302) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: By God, the man To see in the morning, then in the evening, and he will not see with a finger."
"38303","(38303) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, who said: Hudhayf recited these verses: “So fight the Imams.” Unbelief} He said: The people of this verse have not been killed after that."
"38304","(38304) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Muhammad bin Muslimah said: The Messenger gave me God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sword, and he said: Fight with it the polytheists as long as you are killed, so if you see people striking each other some, or speak to him of the like, then take him to a rock and strike him with it until he breaks, then stay in your house. Until a sinful hand comes to you, or a determinate sperm comes to you. (Ahmed 225)"
"38305","(38305) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: Beware of fighting the blind and the death of a man of ignorance. He said: I said: What is fighting an blind man? He said: When it is said: O so-and-so, ya. The son of so-and-so. He said: I said: He did not die as a Jahiliyah. He said: To die without an imam over you."
"38306","(38306) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever is killed in a fight blind, his death will be the death of a blind person. ignorant"
"38307","(38307) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, who said: When the people became divided in Attacking Uthman: My father got up and prayed during the night, then he fell asleep and said: He was told: Get up and ask God to protect you from temptation. From which He protected His righteous servants. He said: Then he got up and fell ill, and he was not seen leaving until he died."
"38308","(38308) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Ali, who said: Islam is diminished until it is not said: God is God. If he does that, he multiplies the burden of debt with his sin. If he does that, he will be resurrected. A people who gather as the autumn leaves gather, and by God, I know the name of their prince and the climate of their passengers."
"38309","(38309) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saad bin Hudhayfy, he said: Hudhayfy said: Whoever separated The group removed the necklace of Islam from its neck by a hand."
"38310","(38310) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Marthad, he said: My uncle Abu Sadiq narrated to me, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Imams are from Quraysh, and whoever separates from the group by a span has removed the tie of Islam from his neck."
"38311","(38311) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abdullah said: How will you be if I wear your clothes? Trials cause the small to grow up in them, and the big ones to grow old in them, and people take them as a norm, even if anything about it is changed. It was said: The Sunnah was changed. They said: When will that happen, O Abu Abdul Rahman? He said: When your readers are many and your trustworthy ones are few, and your rulers are many, and your jurists are few, and you seek the world By doing the hereafter."
"38312","(38312) Abu Asama Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: God placed this in The nation has five trials: a general trial, then a specific trial, then a general trial, then a specific trial, then a rippling trial. Like the waves of the sea, the people therein become like animals. (Abdul Razzaq 20733 Hakim 437)"
"38313","(38313) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Ahmar, or Ibn Ahmar, speaking, on the authority of Abu Raja’ Al-Atardi, He said: I heard Ibn Abbas delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: Whoever separates from the group by a span and dies will die the death of a generation."
"38314","(38314) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd bin Yatha’, he said: Hudhayfy said: How are you? When you were asked for the truth, you were given it, but were denied your right? He said: Then we will be patient. He said: You have entered it by the side of the Kaaba."
"38315","(38315) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, who said: A man came to Hudhayf and to Abu Masoud Al-Ansari while they were sitting in the mosque, and the people of Kufa had expelled Saeed bin Al-Aas, so he said: Why are you sitting? People have left? By God, we are following the Sunnah. They said: How can you be following the Sunnah when you have expelled your imam, and by God you are not following the Sunnah? Until the shepherd is compassionate and the flock is advised. He said: Then a man said to him: If the shepherd is not compassionate and the flock is advised, then what do you command us to do? He said We will leave and leave you."
"38316","(38316) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Suhayb al-Faqir, who said: It has reached me that he A man wields a sword during a trial, but it remains drawn until he puts it down."
"38317","(38317) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding the Farewell Hajj: Which day he entered into ihram three times, so they said: The greatest day of Hajj. He said: Your blood, your property, and your honor are sacred, just as this day of yours is sacred, in this company of yours, in This is your country. No offender can harm anyone but himself. No offender can commit harm except against himself. No father can commit harm against me. His children, and there is no child over his father, except for his followers, have you conveyed the message? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness, three times. (Abu Dawud 3327. Tirmidhi 2159)"
"38318","(38318) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Majid Abi Amr, who said: I heard al-Adādī ibn Khalid ibn Hudḥa, saying: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Farewell Hajj, and I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing in the stirrups. And he says: Do you know what month this is? What country is this? He said: Your blood and your wealth are as sacred to you as this day of yours is sacred to you in this month of yours in your country. This, have you conveyed the message? They said: Yes, he said: O God, give me witness. (Abu Dawud 1912. Ahmed 30)"
"38319","(38319) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What month is this? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Then we remained silent until we thought that he would give it another name. He said: Isn’t it Dhul-Hijjah? We said: Yes, he said: What country is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then we remained silent, so much so that we thought that he would call it by a different name. He said: Is it not the Sacred City? We said: Yes. He said: What day is this? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Then we remained silent until we thought that he would call it by another name. He said: Isn’t it the Day of Sacrifice? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Your blood and your wealth. Muhammad said: I think so. He said: And your honor is upon you. Forbidden, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this country of yours, in this month of yours, and you will meet your Lord, and He will ask of you. About your deeds (Bukhari 44061 Muslim 30)"
"38320","(38320) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Concerning Hajj: Do you know which day is the most sacred? He said: So we said: This is our day. He said: Which country is more sacred? He said: We said: This is our country. He said: Which month is more sacred? We said: We shared this. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your blood and your property are sacred as sacred. This is your day, this is in your country, this is this polytheism of yours. (Ibn Majah 3931, Ahmad 80)"
"38321","(38321) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose among us on a young, red-brown she-camel. He said: Do you know what I am? This day of yours. Do you know what kind of company this is? Do you know what kind of country of yours this is? He said: For your blood and your wealth Sacred to you, as sacred as this day of yours, is this in your country, in this month of yours."
"38322","(38322) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, who said: When it was the day of Al-Jar’a, it was said to Hudhaifa: No. You go out with the people. He said: Why should they take me out with them? I know that they have not shed a cup of blood among them until they return. Many hadiths were mentioned in the hadith of Al-Jar’iyya: “I do not like to have any of it in your house. Indeed, temptation is approaching.” Who looks forward to it? (Ahmed 394)"
"38323","(38323) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Zurr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I wished that I have with me a hundred men whose hearts are made of gold, so I will ascend upon a rock and speak to them, and no temptation after him will ever harm them. Then I go away little by little, but I do not see them and they do not see me."
"38324","(38324) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Hudhaifa, he said: If I have told you what I know. You have split into three groups: one group that will fight me, another group that will not support me, and another group that will deny me."
"38325","(38325) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Dirar bin Murah narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hanzaliah, he said : Hudhayfah said: There is no man without a mother who has been impure by nails, except two men: one of them has emerged and the other is disputing about him. As for the one that has emerged, it is Umar, and as for the one about which there is a dispute, it is literal."
"38326","(38326) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Azdi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hanafiyah, He said: May God have mercy on a man who restrained his hand, restrained his tongue, enriched himself, and sat in his house. He had what he sought, and he On the Day of Resurrection, he will be with those he loves. Indeed, deeds will come to them quicker than the swords of the believers. Indeed, the truth will have a side. It will come. By God, if He wills."
"38327","(38327) Abd al-Sulaiman, Waki`, and Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of al-Sanabihi, He said: I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: I will leave you at the basin, and I will multiply with you. Nations, so do not fight each other after me. (Ahmad 351, Ibn Hibban 5985)"
"38328","(38328) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmed 351)"
"38329","(38329) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Waqid bin Muhammad bin Zayd, that he heard his father speaking, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said during the Farewell Hajj: And may he judge, or he said: Woe to you, no. You will return as infidels after me, striking the necks of one another. (Bukhari 6166 and Muslim 82)"
"38330","(38330) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: We have been informed that Jarir said: A messenger said to me God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The people listened, then he said: I will not make you known after I see you. You will return as infidels after me. You strike each other's necks."
"38331","(38331) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, who said: I heard Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir. It is narrated, on the authority of Jarir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during the Farewell Hajj: The people listened, and he said: Do not return after me. As infidels, you strike the necks of one another. (Bukhari 6869 and Muslim 118)"
"38332","(38332) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I will divide you over the basin and I will dispute with people, then I will prevail over them, so I say: O Lord, my companions, It will be said: You do not know what they did after you. (Muslim 1797. Ahmad 388)"
"38333","(38333) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Al-Kawthar is a river that my Lord has promised me. There is much good upon it. It is my basin, to which my nation will return on the Day of Resurrection. The Day of Resurrection is as certain as the number of stars, so the servant will be overwhelmed by them and I will say: My Lord, he is from my nation. Then he will say: You do not know what It happened after you."
"38334","(38334) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on this pulpit: I am a predecessor of yours upon Al-Kawthar, so while I Upon him, when he passed by you with messengers, opposing you, then he called: Come. Then a herald called and said: Indeed, they have changed after you. So I say: Screw it."
"38335","(38335) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up among us and said: I will leave you at the basin. I will see you. And I will multiply over you the nations, so do not disgrace your face."
"38336","(38336) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: Indeed, people are alienated from their authority, so I seek refuge in God lest grudges that are borne and worldly influence overtake me and you. And his desires are followed, and the tribes will be summoned, and that is our envy of Satan. If that is the case, then the sword is the sword. Murder, murder. They say: O people of Islam, oh people of Islam."
"38337","(38337) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Whoever is connected with tribes, then join him with his father’s family and do not be proud of him. (female)"
"38338","(38338) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali bin Damra, on the authority of Ubayy, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 963. Ahmad 136)"
"38339","(38339) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Umar said: Whoever takes pride in the tribes, join him, or So they sucked it."
"38340","(38340) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaidullah bin Kariz, who said: Omar wrote To the commanders of the soldiers: When the tribes fall apart, strike them with the sword until they follow the call of Islam."
"38341","(38341) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sahl Abi Al-Asad, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Who said, “O the family of Banu” So-and-so, he is only calling to the Hellfire."
"38342","(38342) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. We will bring you to it, and after me you will return as infidels, striking the necks of one another. A man will not be taken for his brother’s crime, nor will By his father's crime. (Nasa’i 3593)"
"38343","(38343) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, he said: Abdullah said: There will be tribulations and matters. Doubtful matters, so you must perform them, so that you will be a follower in goodness, better than being the leader in evil."
"38344","(38344) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that a man said: O lizard. He said: So he wrote to Omar, He said: So Omar wrote to him to punish him, or he said: discipline him, for the lizard had never warded off harm from them, nor had he run to them. Very good"
"38345","(38345) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: He narrated to us Zaid bin Thabit, on the authority of the Messenger of God, said: Seek refuge in God from temptations, whether apparent or latent. We said: We seek refuge in God from The temptations are what is apparent and what is hidden."
"38346","(38346) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When Othman was sent to He ordered him to go out to Medina. The people gathered around him and said to him: Stay, do not go out, for we will prevent you. He will not reach you. There was something that he disliked, so Abdullah said: There will be matters and temptations, and I do not like to be the first to open it, and Allah is upon me. He obeyed, he said: He turned the people back and went out to them."
"38347","(38347) Abu Usama narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Yusir bin Amr, he said: We joined When Ibn Masoud went out, he stopped on the road to Al-Qadisiyah and entered an orchard. He fulfilled his needs, then he performed ablution and wiped over his socks. Then he came out, and his beard was dripping with water, so we said to him: Return to us, for people have fallen into temptations and we do not know it. Will we meet you or not? He said: Fear God and be patient until a righteous man is relieved, or he is relieved from an immoral person, and you must join together, for May God not unite the mother of Muhammad upon his misguidance."
"38348","(38348) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: There will be kings, then titans, then tyrants."
"38349","(38349) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: It came out Messenger of God to the people of the chambers, and he said: O people of the chambers, the fire has burned and temptations have come as if they were pieces of a dark night. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry much. (Bazzar 1772)"
"38350","(38350) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak and Muffasal ibn Yunus, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: Indeed, it is a tribulation that has spread like the sheep’s foreheads, in which most of the people will perish, except those who He knew her before that."
"38351","(38351) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Safar, on the authority of a man from Banu Abs, who said: Hudhayfah said to us: How would you be when God neglected the matter of the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man said: You will not continue to bring us evil. May God bless the matter of the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Have you seen, when she is in charge of her, one who does not weigh in the sight of God? In compensation: Did you invent the matter of the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, that was lost on that day?"
"38352","(38352) Affan and Aswad bin Amir told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Uthman, On the authority of Khalid bin Arafat, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: O Khaled, there will be events and differences Affan said: And if that is the case, then if you are able to be the one killed and not the killer, then Affan said: Then do it. (Bazzar 3356, Ahmed 292)"
"38353","(38353) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Thabit, or Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: I entered upon Muhammad ibn Muslimah, and I said to him: May God have mercy on you, you are in a state of this matter, so if you leave To the people, so you commanded and forbade, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be strife and division. There is a difference. If that is the case, then bring someone with your sword and strike him until you cut him down, then sit in your house until A wrong hand or a judge comes to you, so I fell and did what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me. (Ahmad 493. Tabarani 517)"
"38354","(38354) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I have been informed that the Levant is still Suitable as long as they are not Bedouins from the Levant."
"38355","(38355) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever dies without obeying him dies the death of a pre-Islamic era, and whoever takes it off after having contracted it There is no proof for him. (Ahmad 4468, Abu Ali 7168)"
"38356","(38356) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Al-Ahwas bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abd. The Most Gracious, he said: Asim Al-Bajlili said: Ask your questions, meaning Nouf, about the verses in Sha’ban and the two hadiths in Ramadan. The distinction is in Shawwal, the sense, meaning killing, and the battle in Dhul-Qa'di, and the judiciary in Dhul-Hijjah."
"38357","(38357) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Adiy bin Adiy, On the authority of Salman bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Omar, he said: There will be princes and workers who will be accompanied by temptations and to separate from them will be blasphemy. He said: I said: God is Great, come back to me, O Commander of the Faithful. So you relieved me, and he returned to me. Salman bin Rabi’a said: He said: God: {And temptation is more severe than killing} and temptation is more beloved to me than killing."
"38358","(38358) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Abu Masoud Al-Ansari entered upon me. Hudhayf was in his illness during which he died, so he embraced him, and he said: separation, and he said: yes, a lover came to me, one who lost his way, no one is more successful than he who regrets. Do I not yet know of temptations?"
"38359","(38359) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us parables: one, three, five, seven, ninety, and eleven, and he explained We had one of them, but he remained silent about the rest of them, saying: A people who were people of weakness and poor homes, so they fought people who were people of neighbourhood. And hostility, so they prevailed over them, and they used them and gave them authority, so they displeased their Lord with them. (Ahmed 407)"
"38360","(38360) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim told us, he said: A Bedouin of ours told me, he said: She migrated. To Kufa, and I took it and gave it to me. Then he seemed to leave, and the people said: No, he left for you, so I met Suwayd bin Ghafali. So I told him that, and he said: I wish I had a burden, and I could not live with it while I was in some of these aspects."
"38361","(38361) Abu Asama told us, he said: Thabit bin Zaid told us, he said Hilal bin Khabab Abu Al-Ala told us, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubair, I said: O Abu Abdullah, what is the meaning of the destruction of the people? He said: When their scholars were destroyed. (Dharmi 241)"
"38362","(38362) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, he said: Hudhayfah said: By God, nothing comes to them that they are upset about except that something comes to them that distracts them from it."
"38363","(38363) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazeed bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: What is between The epic, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Antichrist are only seven months, and that is only the end of the decade. It is interrupted and some of it follows another."
"38364","(38364) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, that Muadh ibn Jabal said: The construction of the Holy House is the ruin of Yathrib, and the emergence of the epic is the conquest of Constantinople, and the conquest of Constantinople is the exit Antichrist, then he struck a man on the shoulder with his hand and said: By God, that is true. (Abu Dawud 4295, Hakim 420)"
"38365","(38365) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hazzaz, on the authority of Yatha’, who said: If you see a kufa, you will be surrounded. There is a wall over her, so get out of her, even if by crawling, to drive her back like a mound of horses and their horses until two men quarrel in the mirror. This one says: I have one end, and this one says: I have two legs."
"38366","(38366) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: If only Ali had understood this matter of ours. This was the place of his journey, meaning the people."
"38367","(38367) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, he said: Abu Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Suhar, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Hour will not begin until it overwhelms a tribe and it is said to a man: Who is left of the people? The son of so-and-so? He said: So I learned that Arabs are called to their tribes, and that non-Arabs are called to their villages. (Ahmad 483; Abu Ali 6799)"
"38368","(38368) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Indeed, among my nation there is eclipse, distortion, and slander. (Ibn Majah 4062, Hakim 445)"
"38369","(38369) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of Zainab bint Jahsh, Anna, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up from his sleep red. His face while saying: There is no god but Allah, and woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has approached. The day has been opened from the ashes of Gog and Magog. And he held it with his hand, meaning ten. Zainab said: I said: O Messenger of God, we will destroy you and among us are the righteous. He said: Yes, then Malice has appeared.\n(Muslim 2207, Ibn Majah 3953)"
"38370","(38370) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When evil appears in the land, God sends down calamity upon the people of the earth. I said: The Messenger of God, and among them are those who obey God, he said: Yes, then they will come to God’s mercy. (Ahmad 41. Hakim 523)"
"38371","(38371) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: At the hands of the Hour there will be temptations like pieces of a dark night. A man will wake up as a believer and go to bed in the evening. An unbeliever, and he becomes an unbeliever in the morning and a believer in the evening, and a people sells their religion for the value of the world."
"38372","(38372) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ishmael, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, that the Messenger of God raised his head to the heavens, then He said: Glory be to God, temptations will be sent upon them like rain. (Tabarani 2272)"
"38373","(38373) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: A man said while he was with Omar: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from temptation or temptation. Omar said: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from temptations. Do you not like that He does not provide for you? God has wealth and children. Whoever of you has sought refuge from temptations, let him seek refuge from its misguidance."
"38374","(38374) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn al-Qubtiyya, who said: Al-Harith bin Abu Rabi`a and Abdullah bin Safwan came to Umm Salamah and I was with her, so they asked her about the army that was being defeated. That was during the time of Ibn al-Zubayr, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He seeks refuge in the House, and will be sent back. He was sent to him, and when they were in the middle of the earth, they were swallowed up, so we said: O Messenger of God, how about he who is a hater? He said: He will be eclipsed with them, but he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection according to his intention. Abu Ja`far said: He will be resurrected. Medina (Muslim 2208, Abu Dawud 4288)"
"38375","(38375) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If two Muslims confront each other with their swords and one of them kills his companion, then they will be in Hell. They said: O Messenger of God, this is the killer, so what is the matter with the one who was killed? He said: He wanted to kill his companion. (Nasa’i 3584, Ahmad 410)"
"38376","(38376) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Razin al-Janni told us, he said: Abu al-Raqqad told us, he said: I went out with My master, and I am a boy, so I was given to Hudhayf and he says: If a man was to speak the word at the time of the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, then he becomes a hypocrite. Indeed, I can hear it from one of you in one seat four times, so that you may be instructed. To do what is right and forbid what is wrong, and to encourage one another to do good, or Allah will certainly anoint you with a punishment all together, or He will command us to do good. The worst of you will be upon you, then the best of you will call and they will not be answered. (Ahmed 390)"
"38377","(38377) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tharwan bin Malhan, he said: We were sitting In the mosque, Ammar bin Yasser passed by us and we said to him: We narrated the hadith of the Messenger of God regarding temptations, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: After me there will be princes who will fight for the kingdom, some of whom will kill others for it, so we said: To him: If someone else had told us about it, we would have lied to him. He said, “As for it, it will be.” (Ahmad 263; Abu Ali 1646)"
"38378","(38378) Affan narrated to us, he said: Imran Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A pledge of allegiance is made to a man between a corner and a station, counting the people of Badr. Then the Asaib al-Iraq and the Abdāl al-Sham will come to them, and an army of the people of the Levant will attack them until, when they are in the desert, they will be destroyed. With them, then a man from Quraysh, whose maternal uncle was a dog, attacked them, and they met each other and God defeated them, and it was said: The disappointed one. Whoever loses his spoils is a dog. (Abu Dawud 4287, Hakim 431)"
"38379","(38379) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Idris. Al-Murabibi, on the authority of Muslim bin Safwan, on the authority of Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No people desist. From the invasion of this house until an army invades, even if they are with desert, or with warriors from the earth, it will be eclipsed. With the first of them and the last of them, and the middle of them did not escape. I said: If there was among them those who disliked him, he said: May God resurrect them on what In themselves (Tirmidhi 2184. Ahmad 336)"
"38380","(38380) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Saad bin Aws, on the authority of Bilal Al-Absi, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us one day: How will you be when religion fades and desires appear and differences The Brotherhood and the ancient house was burned. (Ahmad 333. Tabarani 67)"
"38381","(38381) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Sa’d, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, I heard Abu Huraira says, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He will destroy the Ka’bah with two stalks from Ethiopia."
"38382","(38382) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama ibn Kulayl, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, on the authority of Alim Al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, said: This house will be destroyed at the hands of a man from the Al-Zubayr family."
"38383","(38383) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He heard Ibn Amr saying: As if With it, I will become bald, and I will stand over it and demolish it with his wipes. When Ibn al-Zubayr demolished it, I started to look at its surface. Ibn Amr did not see her."
"38384","(38384) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn al-Zubayr agreed on To destroy it, we left for Minna three times, awaiting the torment."
"38385","(38385) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is as if I see a man from Ethiopia, bald and with hairless legs, sitting on it while it is being destroyed."
"38386","(38386) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mina, who said: I heard Ibn Amr say: If you see the Quraysh demolishing the House, then rebuilding it and decorating it, then if you are able to die, then die!"
"38387","(38387) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, who said: I was holding the bridle of an animal. Abdullah bin Amr, and he said: How will it be if you demolish the House and do not leave one stone upon another? They say: And we are upon Islam? He said: And you are Muslims. I said: Then what? He said: Then it will be built as best as it has ever been, so if you see Mecca, it will be as gigantic as a mountain, and you will see the building towering over the tops of the mountains. Know that the matter has overshadowed you."
"38388","(38388) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: Enjoy this House before it is raised, for it will be raised and demolished twice and raised on the third time."
"38389","(38389) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr, who said: A man came to Abdullah, and he said: When will I go astray? He said: When there are rulers over you, if you obey them they will mislead you, and if you disobey them they will kill you. (Hakim 462)"
"38390","(38390) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Kamil Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Seek refuge in God from the age of seventy and from the command of young children. (Ahmad 326. Bazzar 3358)"
"38391","(38391) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Ar-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: Woe to the Arabs. Of the evil that has approached: the command of the boys. If they obey them, they will be admitted to Hell, and if they disobey them, they will behead them."
"38392","(38392) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Maymun bin Abi Shabib speaking, on the authority of Ubadah bin The silent one said: I wish for my beloved that his wealth be reduced, or that his death be hastened. They said: We have not seen anyone wishing so lovingly for his beloved. He said: I fear that the leaders will overtake you. If you obey them, they will admit you to Hell, and if you disobey them, they will kill you. So he said A man: Tell us who they are until we go out their eyes. His people said: Or we throw dust into their faces. He said: Perhaps we will You will overtake them, and they will be the ones who gouge out your eyes and throw dust in your face."
"38393","(38393) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Hudhayfah said: There is no one you can overtake. temptation, but I fear it for him, except for Muhammad ibn Muslim, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say He said: Do not be harmed by temptation. (Abu Dawud 4630, Hakim 433)"
"38394","(38394) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, that Ali was sent to Muhammad bin Muslimama asked him to come to him, so he sent for him and said: If he does not come to me, then carry him. So they brought him, but he refused. If he comes to him, they said: We have been commanded, if you do not come to him, to carry you until we bring you to him. He said: Return to him and say To him: Your cousin and my friend have made a promise to me that there will be strife, division, and disagreement, so if that happens, sit down. In your house and break your sword until the fate of a judge or a sinful hand comes to you, so fear Allah, O Ali, and do not That was the wrong hand, so they brought him and informed him, and he said: Call him."
"38395","(38395) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of sheikhs, who said: Hudhayfy said: There will be a trial. Then there will be repentance and community after it, and then there will be a trial after which there will be neither repentance nor community."
"38396","(38396) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar bin Maimun, who said: A sheikh of ours from Abdul Qais, called Bashir, narrated to me. Ibn Ghouth, he said: I heard Ali saying: When the year was one hundred and forty-five, the sea blocked its side, and when At the age of one hundred and fifty, righteousness blocked his side, and when it was the age of sixty and a hundred, eclipse, distortion, and shaking appeared."
"38397","(38397) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A monk met me in the midst of temptation, and he said: O Saeed bin Jubayr, clarify who worships God or worships the tyrant."
"38398","(38398) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: Ghaylan bin Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Qais bin Riyah Al-Qaisi said: I heard Abu Hurairah narrating, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He said: Whoever abandons obedience and separates from the community and dies the death of a pre-Islamic era, and whoever goes out under blind opinion will become angry. To your group, or to support your group, or to call to your group and be killed, so he will be killed by a pre-Islamic group, and whoever rebels against your nation He strikes the righteous and the immoral. He does not avoid a believer or fulfill his covenant. He is not of him, and I am not of him. (Muslim 53. Ahmad 306)"
"38399","(38399) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sam’an, he said: I heard Abu Huraira tells Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: He pledges allegiance to a man between a pillar and a station. No one will make the House lawful except its own family. If they make it lawful, do not ask about its destruction by the Arabs, then come the Abyssinians. They will wreak havoc that will never last again, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure. (Ahmed 291. Ahmed 312)"
"38400","(38400) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Ali, he said: My father told me, he said: Ali said: By the One who split the grain and brought forth the breeze, removing mountains from their place is easier than removing a deferred kingdom. So if they disagree Among them, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if the hyenas had come upon them, they would have defeated them."
"38401","(38401) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The Hour will not begin until the women’s buttocks are disturbed around the idols. (Bukhari 7116 and Muslim 2230)"
"38402","(38402) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Amr bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The nations are about to He pleads against you as people plead over their bowl. Weakness is removed from the hearts of your enemies and placed in your hearts. And the world becomes endearing to you. They said: Because of the few. He said: Most of you are scum like the scum of a stream. (Ahmad 278, Talisi 992)"
"38403","(38403) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Hudhayfy bin Al-Yaman, He said: There will be a tribulation, and men will rise up against it and hit it in the face until it goes away, then there will be another, and it will rise up against it. Men come and hit her on the cheeks until she goes away, then there will be another one, and men will stand up for her and hit her on the cheeks until It will go away, then there will be the fifth majestic blood, spewing forth in the earth just as water spews forth."
"38404","(38404) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: A man said: O Banu Tamim, so Omar bin Al-Khattab withheld their gift for a year, then gave it to them from the following year."
"38405","(38405) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Najaba, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, said: Whoever reaches that time must neither stab nor strike with a spear. With a sword and do not throw a stone, and be patient, for the outcome is for the righteous. (Tabarani 2801)"
"38406","(38406) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Huraira says: Woe to the Arabs for the evil that has approached. They have cast shadows, by the Lord of the Kaaba. They have cast shadows, and God is quicker to attack them than The fast-tracked horse, the blind and deaf temptation, the man in it morning upon a matter and the evening upon a matter. The one who sits in it is better than the one who stands, the one who stands in it is better than the one walking, and the one who walks in it is better than the one who runs, even if I were to speak to you. With all that I know, you would have cut off my neck from here, and Abdullah pointed to the back of his neck with the letter kafa yahzah, and said: Oh God, do not let Abu Hurairah ignore the command of the two boys."
"38407","(38407) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Woe to the Arabs from evil. It has come near. He who restrains his hand has succeeded. (Abu Dawud 4248, Ahmed 441)"
"38408","(38408) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Mankhil bin Ghadban, who said: I accompanied Asim bin Amr Al-Bajli and I heard him say: O my nephew, if the Maghrib door is opened, it will not be closed."
"38409","(38409) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhariq bin Sulaym, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: I do not see these people as anything but victorious over you, to separate you from your truth and to unite against your falsehood. And the imam is not uneven with his hair, and he makes mistakes and is right, so if there is an imam over you, he will be just with the people. And he swears by the righteous, so listen to him and obey him, and that the people cannot be corrected except by a righteous imam, or an immoral one, and if he is righteous, It is for the shepherd and for his flock, and if it is an immoral one, the believer will worship his Lord therein, and the immoral person will work therein for his sake, and you are You will be exposed to my captivity, and to disavow me, for whoever takes me captive will be freed from my captivity, and do not disavow my religion, for I am free from my captivity. Islam"
"38410","(38410) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Kathir bin Nimr, who said: A man with several men came to Ali, and he said: I saw these people threatening you, so they fled, and I took this one. He said: Should I kill those who did not He will kill me. He said: He cursed you. He said: He cursed you, or he left you."
"38411","(38411) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of a man, who said: I was a sergeant in the time of Ali. He said: So he ordered us to do a matter, and he said: Did you do what I ordered you to do? We said, No. He said: By God, you will do what you are commanded to do, or he will ride on us. Your necks are the Jews and Christians."
"38412","(38412) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya, Ubaid Allah, and Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God gave us the pledge of allegiance to listen and obey in times of hardship and ease. And the stimulant and the detester, and he has influenced us, and we must not dispute the matter with his people, and we must speak the truth wherever we are, no We fear God's blame, the blamer. (Bukhari 7199. Muslim 42)"
"38413","(38413) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit to Junadd ibn Abi Umayyah al-Ansari: Come, so that I may tell you what is for you and what is upon you, listening and obedience. In your hardship, your ease, your invigorator, your detester, and his influence on you, and to speak with your tongue, and not to dispute the matter, O people. Unless you see clear disbelief."
"38414","(38414) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir, he said: Dhu Amr said: Oh Jarir Indeed, you are an honor upon me, and I will inform you of the news. Indeed, you are a group of Arabs. You will not cease to be well as long as you were, if you perish. You took charge of another prince, but when it was by the sword, you became angry as kings are, and you are satisfied with the pleasure of kings."
"38415","(38415) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Furat, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, the Children of Israel used to have their prophets rule over them, whenever he went A prophet is succeeded by a prophet, and there will not be a prophet among you after me. They said: What will it be, O Messenger of God? He said: It will be. Caliphs, and they multiplied. They said: So how should we do? He said: Fulfill your first pledge, then the first. Pay back what you owe. Then God will ask them about The One upon them.\n(Muslim 1472 and Ibn Majah 2871)"
"38416","(38416) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, who said: Al-Ja’fi rose and greeted him to the Messenger of God, and he said: O Messenger of God, what have you seen if after you there will be a people over us who will seize the truth from us and deny the truth of God? He said: Then why? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, answered him with something. He said: Then he stood for the second time, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not answer him. He greeted something, then the third person stood up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Upon them is what they have been burdened with, and upon you is what you have been burdened with. So listen to them and obey them. (Tabarani 6322)"
"38417","(38417) He told us his youth, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Bukhari 1995)"
"38418","(38418) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: Trials have overtaken you like pieces of a dark night. The people were saved therein by a fierce companion who ate from the messengers. His sheep, or a man from behind the path, holding the reins of his horse, eating from the spoils of his sword. (Hakim 432)"
"38419","(38419) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Abu Hurairah said to me If you are able to die, then die. He said: I said: I cannot die before my time comes."
"38420","(38420) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him: Indeed, after me there will be traces and matters that you will deny. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, what do you command whoever overtakes you? From that, he said: You are given the right that is due to you and you ask God for what is yours. (Bukhari 3403, Muslim 1472)"
"38421","(38421) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during the Farewell Hajj: O people, what day is this? They said: It is a forbidden day. He said: What country is this? They said: A forbidden country. He said: What month is this? They said: A forbidden month. He said: Your wealth. And your blood and your honor are as sacred to you as this day of yours, in this country of yours, in this company of yours. Then he repeated it repeatedly, saying: Then he raised his head to the heavens and said: Oh God, have I conveyed the message repeatedly? He said: Ibn Abbas says: By God, Indeed, this is my will to his Lord. Then he said: Let the witness inform the absent person. Do not return to me as an infidel. He strikes You are the necks of one another. (Bukhari 1739. Tirmidhi 2193)"
"38422","(38422) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Hudhayfah was with Ka'b was on a ship, and he said to Ka'b one day: O Ka'b, do you find this in the Torah? How do you conduct it and how? And how? Ka'b said to him: Do not mock the Torah, for it is the Book of God, and what is in it is truth. He said: Then he went back and told him a parable. That, then he came back and told him the same thing, then he said: No, but I find that a man from Quraysh with a sharp fang was coming into it. Trials are like a donkey dismounting on its leash, so fear Allah and do not be it. Muhammad said: So it was it."
"38423","(38423) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Raw’a, he said: I mentioned The temptation is according to Ibn Masoud. He said: Enter your house, and if it enters upon you, be like a fattened camel, only springing back. He is a hater, and he does not walk except as a hater."
"38424","(38424) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, who said: I heard Abu Salih, who said: A man from The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of al-Jar’ah. He said: Uthman ibn Affan had sent Sa’id ibn al-Aas to Al-Kufa, he said: Then the people of Al-Kufa came out and overtook you, he said: Then a man from the people said: We are following the Sunnah, so he said: You are not following it. The Sunnah until the shepherd is compassionate and the flock is advised."
"38425","(38425) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Tawus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Today, Gog and Magog are like this. Wahib held ninety pieces in his hand. (Bukhari 3347, Muslim 1208)"
"38426","(38426) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amr, on the authority of my father. Hakim, the servant of Muhammad bin Usama, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: How are you if it is not obligatory for you? A dinar or a dirham. They said: When will that happen? He said: If you break the covenant, God will harden the hearts of the enemy against you, so refrain from you."
"38427","(38427) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Murra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: A time will come upon the people when a man will have a red garment that he carries to the Levant on which it is dearer to him than an offering. The world."
"38428","(38428) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: If the year is one hundred and thirty-six and you do not see a sign, then the curse is in my grave."
"38429","(38429) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Huwarith, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The verses are beads arranged in a wire. The wire has been cut, and some of them are followed. Some (Hakim 473. Ahmad 219)"
"38430","(38430) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Murrah, on the authority of Hudhafiyah, he said: If a man had an affair A horse in the path of God, and it produced a foal. At the beginning of the verses, the foal would not ride until he saw the last of them."
"38431","(38431) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sala, on the authority of Hudhafi, he said: I heard him say: When you see the first verses, they follow each other."
"38432","(38432) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas saying: The Hour will not come until people travel on the roads like donkeys. (Hakim 455. Ibn Hibban 6767)"
"38433","(38433) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Time is approaching, knowledge is decreasing, scarcity will prevail, temptations will appear, and confusion will increase. They said: Oh Messenger of God, what is the chaos? He said: killing. (Bukhari 7061. Muslim 2057)"
"38434","(38434) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: We came to Omar, and he said: How? Your livelihood, so we said: The most fertile people are those who fear the Antichrist. He said: What comes before the Antichrist is more fearful of the Haraj for you? I said: And what Al-Harj, he said: murder, to the point that a man kills his father."
"38435","(38435) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Saeed, he said: Qatadah told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And no one will speak to you after me. He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Indeed, among the signs What is sought is for knowledge to be raised and ignorance to be made apparent, for alcohol to be drunk and fornication to be made apparent, for men to be few and women to be many. (Bukhari 81. Muslim 2056)"
"38436","(38436) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan and Mus’ar, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’athi, on the authority of Raja’ bin Hiyawah, on the authority of Muadh He said: You were afflicted with the tribulations of adversity, but you were patient, and you will be afflicted with the tribulations of good times, and the most fearful thing I fear for you is tribulations. When women are garlanded with gold and wear the Levant, they make the rich tired and burden the poor with what he cannot find. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 785)"
"38437","(38437) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Osama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I have not left upon my nation after me a trial more harmful to men than women."
"38438","(38438) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, He said: Whatever signs were mentioned have already passed except four: the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjal, the creatures of the earth, and the coming of Gog. And Magog, he said: And the verse with which deeds are concluded is the rising of the sun from the west. Have you not listened to the words of God Almighty: {Day Some of the signs of your Lord will come; no soul will benefit if it had not believed before. (Tabarani 101)"
"38439","(38439) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Al-Hasan claimed that the Prophet of God, Moses, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, asked his Lord to show him the animal. He said: So it came out for three days without anyone seeing either end of it. He said: He said: Lord, return it, and it was returned."
"38440","(38440) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayf, he said: The beast will come out twice before the Day of Resurrection until men are beaten on it, then it will come out a third time. At the largest of your mosques, then you come to the people and they are gathered with a man, and you say: What will gather you with the enemy of God, so they disperse? So you brand the infidel to the point that the two men exchange allegiance, and this one says: Take it, O believer. And this one says: Take it, O disbeliever. (Naim 1851)"
"38441","(38441) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The beast emerges from Mount Jiyad on the days of the East, while the people are at Minna. He said: For this reason the pilgrim greets the one who precedes him when he comes in the safety of the people."
"38442","(38442) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Fudail bin Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Amr, he said: The animal comes out From a crack in the coffin, the horse ran for three days, not emerging for a third of them."
"38443","(38443) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told me, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, he said: Three people from The Muslims went to Marwan bin Al-Hakam and heard him narrating about the signs, that the first of them would be the emergence of the Antichrist, so the group departed to Abd Allah ibn Amr, so they told him what they had heard from Marwan ibn al-Hakam regarding the verses, that the first of them would be the emergence of the Antichrist, so Abdullah said: No. Marwan says something: I have memorized a hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which I have not yet forgotten. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The first of the signs of emergence is the rising of the sun from the west, or the emergence of an animal upon it. People sacrificed, and whoever was before her companion, the other will soon follow her, then Abdullah said, and it was He reads the scriptures: I think the first of them will arise when the sun rises from the west, and that is because whenever it sets, it comes under the Throne. So she prostrated and asked permission to return, and he gave her permission to return until, when God willed, she should rise from her west and come under the Throne. So she prostrated and asked for permission, but he did not respond to her with anything. Then she came back and asked for permission to return, but he did not respond to her with anything. Then She comes back and asks for permission to return, but he does not respond to her with anything, until some part of the night is gone, God willing, for him to go. And she knew that if permission had been given to her, she would not have reached the East. She said: My Lord, how far is the East. She said: My Lord, who can protect me from people? The horizon was illuminated as if it were a collar. She asked permission to return. It was said to her: “Where you are, come out.” So she came out to the people from her west. Then Abdullah recited these verses and that: {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit if it does not believe. before or has earned good in her faith}"
"38444","(38444) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: Count everyone who spoke Islam. He said: We said: O Messenger of God, you fear for us while we are between six hundred and six hundred. To the Seven Hundred, and he said: You do not know, perhaps you will be tested. He said: So we were tested until a man among us began to pray except in secret. (Muslim 131. Ahmad 384)"
"38445","(38445) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: What is between you and that He is sent? Evil will be upon you for many lengths, except for his death on the neck of a man who dies, and that is a lifetime. (Naim 53)"
"38446","(38446) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Husayn ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, He said: I do not know anything except prayer."
"38447","(38447) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: A man who was selling food narrated to me, he said: When it was served Hudhayf Ali Jokha came to Abu Masoud to greet him, and Abu Masoud said: What is the matter with this sword of yours, Abu Abdullah? ? He said: Othman commanded me to go to Jokha, and he said: O Abu Abdullah, are you afraid that this will be a trial when the people expelled Saeed? Ibn Al-Aas, Hudhayfah said to him: Do you not know your religion, Abu Masoud? He said: Yes, he said: Verily, no matter what temptation, You know your religion, but when temptation is suspected of right and wrong and you do not know which one to follow, then that is temptation."
"38448","(38448) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: The temptation did not overtake any of us except Abdullah bin Umar."
"38449","(38449) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Khalid, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: O people, this You have been afflicted by the ruler. If he is just, he will have the reward and you must be grateful. If he is unjust, then there will be a burden on him and you must be patient."
"38450","(38450) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai, who said: My father said to me: May the people of this decade be destroyed. By the Lord of the Kaaba, they were destroyed and destroyed many, but by God, there is no sorrow for them, but for those of their mother whom they will destroy. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Nasa’i 882, Ibn Khuzaymah 1573)"
"38451","(38451) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Dhabi bin Muhsin, on the authority of Umm Salamah She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, there will be matters in which you recognize and deny, so whoever denies is acquitted. And whoever dislikes it, then he is safe, but whoever is satisfied and follows it, they said: O Messenger of God, should we not fight them? He said: No, they did not pray. (Tirmidhi 2245. Ahmad 295)"
"38452","(38452) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: Abu Hurairah said: They will be taken. Let her womb be swallowed, then let what is in the womb be taken, and let her renounce the fear of the child."
"38453","(38453) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: Abu Hurairah said: Oh, Wahih By God, he will be removed just as a job is removed. Woe to him. He will be removed just as a young man is removed."
"38454","(38454) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muslim bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Mu’awiyah. Ibn Qurrah, on the authority of Maqil Ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The servants in times of temptation like Caliphate. To him (Tabarani 492)"
"38455","(38455) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Aqna’. Al-Bailili, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais, who said: I was sitting in the mosque of Medina, when a man approached, whom no group of people could see, but they fled. From there, he reached the circle that I was in, so I remained steadfast and they fled, so I said: Who are you? Then Abu Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of God, said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: People do not flee from you. He said: Indeed, I forbid them from treasures. He said: I said: Indeed, Our gifts It has reached its peak and has risen, so we fear it. He said: As for today, no, but it is about to be the cost of your religion. So they called them and her."
"38456","(38456) Abu Asama told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Jahaf told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah bin told me. Tha'labiya, he said: I came to Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, and I said: The Messenger of the Chosen One came to us inviting us, he said: So he said to me: Do not fight. I hate to do this slave woman worse, or to come to her without her face."
"38457","(38457) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, who said: Abraham said to me: Beware of being killed with temptation"
"38458","(38458) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abu Musa and Abu Masoud entered. Ali Ammar while he was mobilizing the people, and they said: We have not seen anything from you since you embraced Islam that is more distasteful to us than your haste in this matter. Then Ammar said: I have not seen anything from you since you converted to Islam that is more hateful to me than your slowness in this matter. He said: So they clothed them. It's okay, it's okay. (Bukhari 7102, Hakim 117)"
"38459","(38459) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Wa’il narrating, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Hubaysh al-Asadi, he said: Sa`id ibn al-Aas sent me with gifts to the people of Medina and favored Ali, he said: and he said to me: Say To him: Your nephew greets you and says: I have not sent to anyone with more than what I have sent to you, except what is in treasuries. Commander of the Faithful, and Ali said: He is most saddened by the inheritance of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, if My kingdom is that We will shake off the dirt from the dirt. (Abu Ubaid 438, Ahmed 1876)"
"38460","(38460) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: He used to tell us about Omar disagreed with him: Indeed, there will be tribulations and tribulations, and indeed it is sufficient for a man, if he sees a matter that he dislikes, that he should know God. He hates him"
"38461","(38461) Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: By Ibn Abbas. : He forbade my prince from disobeying you. He said: There will be no temptation. He said: I said: If he commands me to disobey you. He said: Then then."
"38462","(38462) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A man said to Ibn Abbas: Commander Enjoin goodness. He said: If you fear that he will kill you, do not reprimand the imam. If you must do it, then it is between you. And He made it clear."
"38463","(38463) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Khaythamah, he said: Abdullah said: If you go to the Commander of the Faithful, do not go to anyone else. From the people"
"38464","(38464) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The women were mentioned in the presence of Ibn Abbas. Then a man broke out among them and became so tall that I did not see anyone in the House taller than him, so I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Do not make yourself It was a temptation for the wrongdoing people, so it shrank until I did not see the House shorter than it."
"38465","(38465) Kathir bin Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, he said: Ayoub narrated to us Al-Sakhtiyani, he said: Ibn Masoud, Saad, Ibn Omar, and Ammar met and mentioned the tribulation that would take place, so Saad said: As for me, I will sit down. I am in my house and I will not leave it. Ibn Masoud said: I adhere to what you said. Ibn Umar said: I adhere to the like of that, and Ammar said: But I reach the middle of it and hit its largest gill. (Musnad 755)"
"38466","(38466) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: Al-Harith bin Suwayd was with a group. He said: Beware of temptations, for they have appeared. A man said: You went out with Ali. He said: Where is there for you an imam like Ali"
"38467","(38467) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ziyad, on the authority of Tabi’, who said: Ka’b said: Indeed, every people has a dog. So he feared?? May God not harm you."
"38468","(38468) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Hamid told us, on the authority of Maymun bin Siyah, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, he said regarding temptation: Indeed, he is the one who defeats his will."
"38469","(38469) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Jubayr, on the authority of Mubashir bin Al-Muharrar, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The city is on the verge of no food being brought to it on a saddle, and the food of its people will be there. Whoever has roots, or crops, or livestock follows their tails to the edges of the clouds, then when you see the buildings, Ola, so they took advantage of it."
"38470","(38470) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Peace and blessings of God be upon him from a journey. When he approached Medina, a group of people rushed to see their banners. He sent and brought them, and said: How hastened you. They said: Have you not given us permission? He said: No, nor is it suspicious, but you were too hasty to go to the women in Medina. Then he said: Would you not? My poetry is when a fire comes out from the direction of Mount Al-Warraq, illuminating the necks of camels, like a light to the pools of the sheath from Aden. Hellfire"
"38471","(38471) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that Abdullah bin Salam asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What is the first sign of the Hour? Then he said: Gabriel told me just before that a fire will gather them from the east. (Abu Ali 3730)"
"38472","(38472) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar said: O people, They migrated before the Abyssinians. From the valleys of Banu Ali, a fire would emerge from the direction of Yemen, gathering the people. It would travel as they traveled. And she stands up when they sleep, to the point that she gathers scarabs until she brings them to Busra, and until a man falls, and she stands up until You take it"
"38473","(38473) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: “Shavers of fire and copper will be sent upon you,” he said: Fire. It will emerge from the direction of sunset, gathering the people until it gathers apes and pigs. It will spend the night where they spent the night, and it will gather where They said"
"38474","(38474) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Habib bin Hamaz, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I wish I could see when fire would come out before Al-Warraq makes the necks of camels light up with sparkles like daylight. (Ahmad 144. Ibn Hibban 6841)"
"38475","(38475) Abu Amer Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Qalaba narrated to me, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fire will come out Before the Day of Resurrection, from the Sea of Hadhramaut, you will gather people. They said: O Messenger of God, what do you command us to do? He said: It is upon you. In the Levant (Tirmidhi 2217, Ahmed 8)"
"38476","(38476) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Dhudhail bin Shurahbil, he said: He addressed them. Mu'awiyah, and he said: O people, you have come and pledged allegiance to me, obediently. And if you had pledged allegiance to an obstructed Abyssinian slave, I would have come. Until I pledge allegiance to him with you. When he came down from the pulpit, Amr ibn Al-Aas said to him: Do you know what I claimed to have brought today? The people pledged allegiance to you obediently, and if they pledged allegiance to an Ethiopian slave, you would come and pledge allegiance to them. He said: Then he regretted it and returned to The pulpit, and he said: O people, is there anyone more deserving of this matter than me? Is there anyone more deserving of this matter than me? He said And Ibn Omar was sitting, he said: Then Ibn Omar said: I thought I would say: I have more right to this matter than you who beat you and made you convert to Islam, then I feared that my words would be corrupted, and I mentioned what God had prepared in Paradise, so what I said was easy for me."
"38477","(38477) Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Qays bin Saad bin Ubadah was with Ali. Ali came forward, and with him were five thousand people who had shaved their heads after Ali died. When Al-Hasan entered into the pledge of allegiance to Muawiyah, Abu Qays wanted to enter, so he said to his companions: Whatever you wish, if you wish I will fight with you forever until the calf dies, and if you wish I will take You have security, so they said: Take it for us, so he took it for them that they will have such-and-such, and that they will not be punished with anything, and that he is a man. Of them, and he did not take anything for himself in particular, so when he journeyed towards Medina and went away with his companions, he made a sacrifice for them all. One day he was valiant until he reached"
"38478","(38478) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar used to say: mercy. May God have mercy on Ibn al-Zubayr. He wanted the dinars of the Levant. May God have mercy on Marwan. He wanted the dirhams of Iraq."
"38479","(38479) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, he said: Mundhir Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hanafiyyah, He said: Beware of this temptation, for no one anticipates it unless you anticipate it. Indeed, these people have something to eat. And for a long time, if all those on earth gathered together to remove their kingdom, they would not be able to do that, until God is the one who The call to prayer is given in it. Can you remove these mountains?"
"38480","(38480) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When the pledge of allegiance was given to Ali, he came to me and said: Indeed, A beloved person among the people of the Levant. I have appointed you over them, so go to them. He said: So you mentioned relatives and you mentioned in-laws. So I said: As for what comes after that, by God, I will not pledge allegiance to you. He said: Then he left me and left. After that, Ibn Umar came to Umm Kulthum. So he greeted her and headed to Mecca, where he came to Ali, and it was said to him: Ibn Omar had gone to the Levant, so the people mobilized. He said: If a man was to hasten until he threw his cloak around the neck of his camel, he said: Umm Kulthum came and was informed, so he sent for Abiyya: What are you doing? The man came to me and greeted me and headed to Mecca, so the people retreated."
"38481","(38481) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I and Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Ali entered. The names of ten nights before the killing of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr and the names of his pain. Abdullah said to her: How do you find yourself? She said: Pain. He said: Indeed, in death there is recovery. She said: Perhaps you desire my death, so wish for it. By God, it is not. I long for you to die until you come to one of your ends. Either you are killed and I seek reward for you, or you appear and please my eyes. So beware lest a mistake is presented to you that does not agree with you, and you accept it with the hatred of death. Rather, Ibn al-Zubayr sent him to be killed. He makes her sad because of that."
"38482","(38482) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya, he said: I was given names after the killing of Abdullah. Ibn Al-Zubayr, so I said: I have been informed that they crucified Abdullah upside down, and hung him as a slave, and by God, I wish I had not died until He would be handed over to me, and I would wash him, embalm him, and shroud him, then bury him. It was not long before Abdul-Malik’s letter came that he would be handed over. To his family, Asmaa brought him, washed him, embalmed him, shrouded him, then buried him."
"38483","(38483) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansur Ibn Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, who said: Ibn Umar entered the mosque, and Ibn Al-Zubair was crucified, so they said to him: These are the names, so he came to her and mentioned them and admonished her, and he said: The corpses are not With nothing, and the souls are with God, so be patient and seek reward from them. She said: And what prevents me from being patient when the head of Yahya has been given as a gift? The son of Zakariya went to one of the prostitutes of the Children of Israel."
"38484","(38484) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I was informed that when Al-Hajjaj killed Ibn Al-Zubayr, he brought him to Mina. So he crucified him at the same time in the middle of the valley, then he said to the people: Look at this, this is the worst of the nation. Then he said: I saw Ibn Umar came to collect a mule of his, and he went to approach her by the trunk, and she started to leave, so he said to his servant: Woe to you, take it. With her bridle, he approached her. He said: Then I saw him approaching her. Then Abdullah bin Omar stood and said: May God have mercy on you if you are fasting. Stand strong, and indeed you have succeeded. You are the worst of them."
"38485","(38485) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, he said: The mail that came narrated to me. With the head of Al-Mukhtar to Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, he said: When I placed it in his hands, he said: Ka’b did not narrate to me a hadith. Unless I saw his credibility other than this, for he told me that a man from Thaqif would kill me. He showed me that I was the one I killed him"
"38486","(38486) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Mundhir, who said: I was with Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. I saw him turning on his bed and blowing his nose, and his wife said to him: What troubles you about the matter of your enemy? This is the son of Al-Zubair, and he said: By God, this enemy of God is not the son of Al-Zubair, but what he does in his sanctuary tomorrow, he said: Then he raised He extended his hand to the heavens, then he said: Oh God, you know that I knew better than what you taught me that a dead person would be deprived of it. His head is circumambulated in the regions, or in the markets."
"38487","(38487) Muhammad bin Kannasa told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Sa’id, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah bin Omar Abdullah came Ibn Al-Zubair, and he said: O Ibn Al-Zubair, beware of atheism in the sanctuary of God, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: A man from Quraysh will commit apostasy therein. If his sins were weighed by the sins of the two heavyweights, they would outweigh him, so see, no. To be formed"
"38488","(38488) Muhammad ibn Kunasa narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of his father, who said: Mus’ab ibn al-Zubayr came to Abdullah ibn Umar. While he was circumambulating between Safa and Marwa, he said: Who are you? He said: Your nephew, Musaab bin Al-Zubayr. He said: The companion of Iraq. He said: Yes. He said: I came to ask you about a people who took off the obedience. They shed blood and exacted money. They were killed and defeated. They entered a palace and barricaded themselves in it. Then they asked for security and they were given it. Then they were killed. He said: How much is the number? He said: Five thousand. He said: Then Ibn Omar glorified God at that time and said: May God bless you, O Ibn al-Zubayr. A man came to Al-Zubayr’s cattle and slaughtered five thousand of them in the morning. Do you think he was extravagant? He said: Yes. He said: So you saw him. Extravagance with animals that do not know what God is, and you consider it permissible for one day to be one of those that God has glorified."
"38489","(38489) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I have never seen a man more captive than him, meaning Ibn Al-Zubayr"
"38490","(38490) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, that the people of Syria were fighting Ibn al-Zubayr. And they shout about it: O Ibn Dhat al-Nitaqin. And Ibn al-Zubayr said:\nAnd that is a complaint that is apparent to you and a disgrace.\n Asmaa said: Did they revile you for it? He said: Yes, she said: By God, it is true."
"38491","(38491) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, that Ibn al-Zubayr used to be harsh on them until He takes them out of the gates and says:\nIf my horn were one, it would be enough for me\n And he says:\nAnd we are not on the verge of bleeding our hearts\nBut blood drips on our feet."
"38492","(38492) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zayed, he said: Abu Husayn Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Thabit bin Qutbah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Stick to this obedience and community, for it is the rope of God that He commanded, and what What you dislike in a group is better than what you love in a group. Indeed, God never created anything without making it an end, and This debt has been fulfilled, but it is about to be diminished, and the sign of that is that ties of kinship are severed, and the money is taken unlawfully. And blood will be shed, and a relative will complain about his kinship, but nothing will come back to him, and the beggar will circumambulate between two gatherings and will not be put back. He had something in his hand. And while they were doing that, when the land gave out, the cows mooed, and all people thought that they had given up. Before them, while the people were like that, when the earth was tossed with its abundant gold and silver, nothing would be of any benefit. Of gold and silver."
"38493","(38493) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Ashraf Abdullah was in his house, and he said: I will make it more ruinous, so that it will be surrounded. It was said: Who? He said: People are coming from here, and Abu Hussein pointed with his hand towards Morocco."
"38494","(38494) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Arqam bin Yaqoub, he said: I heard Abdullah says: How will you be when you leave this land of yours to the Arabian Peninsula and the beds of wormwood? I said: Who? He expels us from our land. He said: An enemy of God."
"38495","(38495) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: Hudhayfy said: It is as if I were among them making the call to prayer. Their horses were tied to the edge of the Euphrates."
"38496","(38496) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: Don’t curse. A people who have never lived except that what they say is true. (Naim 1870)"
"38497","(38497) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I do not care whoever I beat after my life."
"38498","(38498) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar bin Umair, on the authority of Abi Ammar, who said: Hudhayfah said: Trials are to be presented to the hearts, so any heart that I drink to, black spots will be dotted on his heart, and any heart that denies it will be dotted on his heart. A white dot, so whoever of you would like to know that temptation has befallen him out of hope, let him look, for if he sees something forbidden, it will not be. He sees it as lawful, or he sees as lawful what he thought was forbidden, then it has struck him. (Ahmad 3868 Hakim 468)"
"38499","(38499) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbă narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara ibn Umair, on the authority of Qays ibn Sakan, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: A time will come upon the people when, if I were to confront them in a gathering with nobility, it would not strike anyone but an infidel."
"38500","(38500) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, who said: Hudhayfah said: Indeed, temptations have pauses and pauses, so if you are able If it dies in its state, then do so. He said: Wine is nothing but a distraction from temptation from men’s minds."
"38501","(38501) Waki’ and Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr informed us, on the authority of Rafi’ Abi Many times, he said: I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ali saying: The earth will be filled with injustice and oppression until fear and war enter every house. They ask for two dirhams and two dirhams, but they do not give them to them. So there will be fighting with fighting and marching with marching until surrounded. God will be with them in Egypt, then the earth will be filled with justice and justice, and Waki’ said: Until God surrounds them in Egypt."
"38502","(38502) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Shu’ab ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, on the authority of Qais ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Khalid bin Al-Walid flogged a man in punishment, and the next day he flogged another man in punishment, and a man said, “By God, this is temptation.” Yesterday he flogged a man for a punishment, and today he flogged a man for a punishment, and he said: Khaled: This is not a temptation, but a temptation is to be in A land in which disobedience is committed, and you want to leave it to a land in which disobedience is not committed, but you do not find it."
"38503","(38503) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Sa’d bin Hudhayfah, who said: When the people felt sad about Sa’id bin Al-Aas, they wrote a letter between them not to use it. upon them, except a man whom they approve of for their souls and their religion, and so it was between them, when Hudhafif arrived from Al-Mada'in. So they brought them their letter and said: O Abu Abdullah, we have done to this man what you have heard, then we wrote this letter. We loved not to sever any matter without you. So he looked at their letter and laughed and said: By God, I do not know which of the two matters you wanted. You wanted to assume the authority of a people that is not yours, or you wanted to repel this temptation from where it has spread its snouts and is at rest. Indeed, she has been sent from God to the earth, which will be grazed until she steps on her feet. None of the people will be able to refute her, not even one. Of the people who fight therein will be killed, until God sends a panic like the panic of autumn that will be among them. (Hakim 503)"
"38504","(38504) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Zazan, he said: I heard Hudhayfah says: A time will come upon you in which the best of you will be he who neither enjoins what is right nor forbids what is evil. Then a man from among the people said: Will a time come upon us when we will see what is wrong and not change it? No, by God, we will do it. He said: Then he started saying with his finger in his eye: By God, you have lied three times. The man said: So she lied and he told the truth. (Abu Naim 279)"
"38505","(38505) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Hudhayfah says: A time will come upon you in which a man will wish for death and be killed, or he will disbelieve, and they will come. There will be a time when a man will wish to die without poverty."
"38506","(38506) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Sa’id bin Jumhan told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a land called Al-Basra, or Al-Busayra Next to it is a river called Degla, full of palm trees, where the Banu Qantaurai descend, and the people disperse. Three sects: a sect that joined its origin and were destroyed, a sect that took it upon itself and disbelieved, and a sect that they Their descendants are behind their backs and they fight. Their dead are martyrs. God will grant victory over the rest of them. (Abu Dawud 4306. Bazzar 3667)"
"38507","(38507) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he conveyed this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose shoes are shabby, and the Hour will not come until you fight a small people. The eyes (Bukhari 2929. Muslim 63)"
"38508","(38508) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he conveyed this to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace: The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose shoes are hairy, and the Hour will not come until you fight a people whose eyes are small. The nose is turned as if their faces were hammered stones. (Bukhari 2929. Muslim 64)"
"38509","(38509) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i Saad bin Tariq, on the authority of his father, that he heard The Prophet says: According to the killing of my companions. (Ahmad 472, Bazzar 3263)"
"38510","(38510) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: His people informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Asad ibn Hudhir. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: After me you will see a trace of me, so be patient until you meet Ali. The pelvis"
"38511","(38511) Waki’ and Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Hubaira bin Huzaimah, on the authority of Rabi’ Ibn Khuthaym, he said: When the killing of Al-Hussein came, he said: Oh God, you judge between your servants regarding what they were in. They disagree."
"38512","(38512) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ruq al-Hamdani told us, he said: Abu Ruq told us Al-Gharif said: We were leading Al-Hasan bin Ali, twelve thousand people, in a desperate dwelling, our swords dripping with determination to fight. People of the Levant, and upon us is Abu Al-Amarta. He said: When the peace treaty between Al-Hasan bin Ali and Muawiyah came to us, it was as if our backs had been broken by Sadness and anger. He said: When Al-Hasan bin Ali came to Kufa, a man from among us, nicknamed Abu Amir, rose to him and said: Peace be upon you. O humiliator of the believers, so he said: Do not say that, O Abu Amir, but I hated to kill them for the sake of kingship, or for the sake of The kingdom (Abdul-Barr 387)"
"38513","(38513) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Sadiqah bin Al-Muthanna narrated to me, on the authority of his grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith, he said: Al-Hasan rose Ibn Ali after the death of Ali, so he addressed the people and praised God and praised him, then he said: Indeed, what is coming is near, and the command of God is It will happen, even if people hate it, and by God I would not like to receive anything weighing a weight in the matter of the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. A speck of mustard spilled on it, cupped blood since I learned what would benefit me and what would harm me, so join your camp."
"38514","(38514) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: A man and I entered upon Al-Hasan ibn Ali. We will return to him, so he started saying to that man: Ask me before you do not ask me. He said: I do not want to ask you anything, may God protect you. He said: So he got up and entered the shroud, then he came out to us, then he said: I did not go out to you until I had uttered a portion of my heart. With this stick, and I have been made to drink poison many times, nothing is more severe than this. He said: So we attacked him the next day, and lo, he was in The market, he said: Al-Hussein came and sat at his head, and said: O brother, who is your companion? He said: Do you want to kill him? He said: Yes, he said: If it is what I suspect, then my wrath is greater towards God, but if he is innocent, then I do not like an innocent person to be killed."
"38515","(38515) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Sharik, on the authority of Bishr ibn Ghalib, who said: He met Abdullah ibn Al-Zubayr Al-Hussein bin Ali in Mecca. He said: O Abu Abdullah, I have heard that you want Iraq. He said: Yes. He said: No. Do so, for they are the ones who killed your father, the stabbers in your brother’s stomach, and if you go to them they will kill you."
"38516","(38516) Muhammad bin Musa Al-Atari narrated to us, on the authority of Jabalah bint Al-Musaffah, who said: Malik bin Damra recommended his weapons. To the mujahideen from the Banu Damra that the people of Prophethood should not be fought with him. He said: He said: His brother is at his head: O brother at his head. Death says this, he said: that, he said: we have a solution if your child needs to be sold, he said: yes, he said: so he went. The weapon, and nothing remained of it except a spear. She said: Then a man from that group who marched to Al-Hussein came and said: O son of What's wrong with you, O Moses, lend me your father's spear so I can use it? He said: So he said: O my servant, give him the spear. A woman said: From his family: O Moses, do you not remember the commandment of your father? She said: The man passed by with the spear. She said: Then the man caught up and took the spear. From it, he broke it."
"38517","(38517) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, raised Al-Hasan bin Ali was with him on the pulpit, and he said: This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation between two groups of Muslims through him."
"38518","(38518) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mundhir al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Sedition is from He met her with an invasion."
"38519","(38519) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abbas said: We came. Hussein was asking me for advice about leaving here, meaning Iraq, so I said: Were it not that they would visit me and you, I would have remained steadfast. My hand is in your hair, where does it go? To a people who killed your father and stabbed your brother, and the one who was generous with my soul for him said to me: This sanctuary will be made lawful. With a man, and for me to be killed in such-and-such land other than him being far away from him is more beloved to me than for me to be him."
"38520","(38520) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani ibn Hani, on the authority of Ali, He said: They will surely kill Al-Hussein, and I know the soil of the land in which he will be killed. He will be killed near Narayen."
"38521","(38521) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Jinni, on the authority of Salih bin Arbad Al-Nakha’i, who said: Umm Salama said: Al-Hussein entered the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was sitting at the door. I looked up and saw the palm of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said something was turning him while he was sleeping on his stomach, so I said: O Messenger of God, I looked up and saw you stirring something. In your palm, while the boy was sleeping on your stomach and your tears were flowing, he said: Gabriel brought me the soil that he kills. Ali, and told me that my nation will kill her. (Tabarani 2820)"
"38522","(38522) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Shurahbil bin Mudarik Al-Ja’fi narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji. Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, that he traveled with Ali, and he was the companion of his purifier until he came close to Nineveh and was setting off for Siffin and he called: Be patient, Abu Abdullah, be patient, Abu Abdullah. I said: What, Abu Abdullah? He said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and His eyes are overflowing. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, why are your eyes overflowing? Has anyone made you angry? He said: Gabriel got up from me and told me that Al-Hussein would be killed at the Euphrates River. I could not help but let my eyes fill with tears. (Ahmad 85, Abu Ali 358)"
"38523","(38523) Mu’awiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salam Abi Shurahbil, on the authority of Abi Huraim, he said: I slaughtered a sheep. He said to his maidservant: O barren ones, this well has reminded me of a story I heard from the Commander of the Faithful, and I was He had Karbala with him, so he passed by a tree that had a deer's den under it, and he took a handful of it and smelled it, then said: He will be gathered from this. It appears that seventy thousand will enter Paradise without reckoning."
"38524","(38524) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Wa’il bin Alqamah, that he witnessed Al-Hussein at Karbala. He said: Then a man came and said: Is Hussein among you? He said: Who are you? He said: Give good tidings of the Fire. He said: Rather, a Forgiving, Merciful, obedient Lord. He said: Who are you? He said: I am Ibn Hawiza. He said: Oh God, send him to the Fire. He said: So he went and swayed his horse on its legs, so it broke off and did not Only his leg was left in the stirrup."
"38525","(38525) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Umm Hakim, she said: When Al-Hussein bin Ali was killed, and I was at that time A female slave who has reached the level of women, or has almost reached the level of the sky, after his killing she remained for days like a leech."
"38526","(38526) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Asim al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: There came a killing. Othman and I will keep myself young and strong, even if I were to fight and go out to bring the people, even if I were in ruins. Ali there, and he led the afternoon prayer with them, and when he said the salutation, he leaned his back in its mosque, and faced the people, and said: So he stood up to him. Al-Hasan bin Ali was talking to him while he was crying, and Ali said to him: Speak and do not betray the maidservant. He said: I commanded you when The people restricted this man from coming to Mecca and staying there, but you disobeyed me. Then I ordered you, when he was killed, to remain at home until The socks of their dreams return to the Arabs. If you were in a lizard’s den, they would strike you with the camels’ ankles until they extract you from He attacked you and you disobeyed me, and I adjure you by God not to come to Iraq and be killed in a miserable state. He said: Then he said: Ali: As for Your saying: I went to Mecca, but I was not the man for whom Mecca was deemed permissible. As for your saying: The people killed Uthman, then what was my fault? The people killed him, and as for your saying: I will come to Iraq and I will be like a hyena listening to its bite."
"38527","(38527) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When there was peace Between Al-Hasan bin Ali and Muawiyah Al-Hasan wanted to go out to Medina, so Muawiyah said to him: What are you about? Until he addressed the people, he said: Al-Sha’bi said: I heard him on the pulpit, praising God and praising Him, then he said: As for what follows, then I will The wise and pious, and the most incapable is immorality, and this matter over which I and Mu’awiyah differed is a right I have. So I left it to Mu'awiyah, or a right that a man had more right to than to you, and I only did this to spare your blood. {And if I know Perhaps it will be a trial for you and an enjoyment for a while.} Then it was revealed."
"38528","(38528) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Allaqah, on the authority of Usama ibn Sharik, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever separates my nation from them all, strike him on the head, whoever he may be. (Nasa’i 488 and Tabarani 487)"
"38529","(38529) Ziyad ibn al-Rabi` narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad ibn Kathir al-Shami, on the authority of a woman among them called Laha Fasilah, On the authority of her father, she said: I heard my father saying: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: O Messenger of God, is he safe? Asabiyyah is for a man to love his people. He said: No, but it is fanatical for a man to help his people against injustice. (Abu Dawud 5078. Tabarani 236)"
"38530","(38530) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Hunayn, he passed by a tree from which the polytheists hang their weapons. It was said to him: Dhat Anawat, so they said: Make for us Dhat Anawat, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is as the people of Moses said. To Moses: {Make for us a god as they have a family}, so that you may imitate the traditions of those before you. (Ahmad 218. Tayalisi 1346)"
"38531","(38531) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: That you may follow the Sunnah of those before you, a store for a store, and an cubit for a cubit, and a span for a span even. If they had entered a lizard's den, you would have entered into it. They said: O Messenger of God, the Jews and the Christians. He said: Who then?\n(Bukhari 7319. Ahmed 450)"
"38532","(38532) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr He says: You will follow the Sunnah of those who came before you, both good and bad."
"38533","(38533) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: Abdullah said: You are the most like people. I exalt and guide the children of Israel, so that you may follow in their way, like dirt with dirt, and sandal with sandal. And Abdullah said: Indeed, of The statement is magic. (Bazzar 2048. Tabarani 9882)"
"38534","(38534) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Hudhayfah said: There will not be anything among the Children of Israel unless there is something like it among you. Then a man said, “There will be among us the people of Lot.” He said: Yes, and what? Do you think that this has reached the point where you have no mother?"
"38535","(38535) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minal bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Hudhayf He said: You will do the work of the Children of Israel, and there will be nothing among them unless there is something like it among you. So a man said: You will be one of us. Monkeys and pigs. He said: And what saves you from that? You have no mother. They said: Tell us, O Abu Abdullah. He said: If I told you that you split into three groups: two groups that fight me, two groups that do not support me, and two groups that deny me. I will speak to you and not say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I thought that if I spoke to you, you would take And you burn your book and throw it into the crowds. You believe me. They say: Glory be to God, and this is it. He said: Have you seen it? If I had told you that you would break your qiblah, you would have believed me. They would say: Glory be to God, and it would be so. He would say: Have you seen it? If I had told you that your nation is going out with a group of Muslims and fighting you, you would have believed me. They would have said: Glory be to God and it will be. This (Abu Nu’aym 1920 Hakim 469)"
"38536","(38536) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: O people Iraq, you bring dilemmas."
"38537","(38537) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Yusuf, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, he said: I asked permission to enter before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Enter. I said: Then enter all of me, or some of me. He said: Come in, all of you. So I entered upon him while he was performing ablution thoroughly, and he said: O Awf bin Malik, six days before the hour of death. Your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, take one of them, as if my heart had been torn from its place, and the Holy House was opened and he died. He caused you to be slaughtered for it just as sheep are slaughtered, and for wealth to increase, to the point that a man was given a hundred dinars and he displeased with it. And the conquest of the city of disbelief, and there will be a truce between you and the Banu Asfar, so they will come to you under eighty Under each goal there are twelve thousand, so they will be more deserving of treachery than you. (Bukhari 31761, Abu Dawud 4961)"
"38538","(38538) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāḥas ibn Qām, he said: Shaddād Abu Ammar narrated to me, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Six signs of the Hour: his death, the conquest of the Holy House, and that a man be given a thousand A dinar, and He will displease her, and a trial, the grief of which will enter the home of every Muslim, and death, which will take hold of people like the clippings of sheep, and The Romans betrayed themselves and marched with twelve thousand, twelve thousand under each column. (Ahmad 228, Tabarani 244)"
"38539","(38539) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Usayd bin Al-Mushmis, he said: We were With Abu Musa, and he said: Shall I not tell you a story that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to tell us? We said: Yes, he said. : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Hour will not begin until there is much chaos. So we said: O Messenger of God, and what is the chaos? He said: Murder, murder. We said: More than we kill today. He said: It is not the infidels who kill you, but a man who kills his neighbor. And his brother, and his cousin, he said: We were made foolish to the point that none of us could express anything clear. He said: We said: And with us will be our minds at that time. He said: The minds of most of the people of that time will be removed, and a number of people will be left behind. Most of them think that they are on to something. And they are not upon anything, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I feared that matters would overtake me and you, and if they overtake us, what There is a way out for me and for you unless we leave it as we entered it. (Ahmed 406)"
"38540","(38540) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: If two Muslims charge one of them with weapons against his brother, then they will be on the edge of Hell. If one of them kills his friend, They all entered it. (Muslim 2214, Tayalisi 884)"
"38541","(38541) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The angels curse any of you if he points with his iron, even if he is his father’s brother. And his mother (Muslim 2020. Tirmidhi 2162)"
"38542","(38542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Tufayl, Abi Sidan, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: Hudhayfah said: You will surely follow the way of the Children of Israel, like sandal to sandal and dirt to dirt, except that I do not know whether you worship the calf or not."
"38543","(38543) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: When the lands of the Levant spread, then whoever of you is able to die, let him die."
"38544","(38544) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, He said: I came to the Levant, he said: So I said: If you entered upon Abdullah bin Amr and greeted him, then I came to him and greeted him, then he said to him: Who are you? I said: I am Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra. He said: The Banu Qantura are about to expel you from the land of Iraq. I said: Then we will return? He said: Do you desire that? I said: Yes, he said: And you will have comfort in the form of livelihood. (Naim 1911)"
"38545","(38545) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: A man of the hypocrites died and he did not pray. Ali Hudhayf, then Omar said to him: Is he the safest of the people? He said: Yes, then Omar said to him: By God, am I one of them? He said: No, and I will not tell anyone about it after you. (Waki` 477)"
"38546","(38546) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Nothing remains of the hypocrites except Four, one of them was an old man who could not feel the cold of water due to old age. He said: Then a man said to him: Who are these people? They break into our homes and steal our food. He said: Woe to you, those immoral people. (Bukhari 4658, Bazar 2818)"
"38547","(38547) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, he said: Hudhayfy recited {So fight the imams of disbelief}, he said, what The people of this verse were killed after that."
"38548","(38548) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: A man said: Oh God These are the hypocrites. Hudhayfy said: If they had been destroyed, you would not have been fair to your enemy."
"38549","(38549) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, he said: Hudhayfah said: Would it please you to kill the most immoral people? He said: Yes, he said: Then you are more immoral than him."
"38550","(38550) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: There are four hearts: a clean heart, that is the heart of a hypocrite, a heart that is uncircumcised, that is the heart of an unbeliever, and a barren heart, as if it were in it. A lamp that shines, that is the heart of the believer, and a heart in which there is hypocrisy and faith is like a sore spreading out with pus and blood. And his likeness is like a tree that is watered with bad water and good water, whichever water has the upper hand over it. He defeated"
"38551","(38551) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: The hypocrites who are among you today Worse than the hypocrites who were at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I said: O Abu Abdullah, And how was that? He said: These people used to conceal their hypocrisy, and these people made it known. (Taalisi 410)"
"38552","(38552) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul bin Rashid, on the authority of a man from Abd al-Qays, who said: He said: Hudhayfah: I would not care, after the age of seventy, if she knocked down a stone from above this mosque of yours and killed ten of you."
"38553","(38553) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of a man, who said: We were with Hudhayfah and he took a pebble. So he placed some of it on top of the other, then he said to us: Look at what you see of the light. We said: We see something hidden. He said: By God, He will make us ride. Falsehood over truth until you see nothing of the truth except what you see of this."
"38554","(38554) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Lushkan That evil is poured upon you from the heavens until it reaches the end. He said: It was said: What is the end, O Abu Abdullah? He said: The wasteland."
"38555","(38555) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, who said: A man came from a warrior called Amr bin Sali’ went to Hudhayf and said to him: O Abu Abdullah, tell us what you saw and witnessed? Hudhayfah said: O Amr bin Sulay’, do you see a warrior? From Mudar? He said: Yes. He said: For Mudar continues to kill every believer and put him to trial, or God and the angels will strike them. And the believers do not even prevent the stomach from being swallowed up. Do you see a warrior? From Qais Aylan, he said: Yes, so if you see Aylan having descended in the Levant, be careful. (Taalisi 420, Ahmad 390)"
"38556","(38556) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, he said: Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir narrated to me, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayf, he said: Come closer, O people of Mudar, for by God you will never cease to persecute every believer and even kill him. God, His angels, and the believers will strike you so that you will not prevent a swollen belly. They said: Why did you bring us near while we are like that? He said: Indeed, among you is the master of the children of Adam, and among you are the races of horses like the races of horses."
"38557","(38557) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Amr bin Hanzaliah, He said: Hudhayf said: Do not leave Mudar a believing servant of God unless they attack him, or kill him, or strike him and God and the angels. And the believers do not even prevent the sin of Tali. Then a man said to him: O Abu Abdullah, you say this while you are a man from Mudar. He said :Shall I not say what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? (Bukhari 2530)"
"38558","(38558) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, He said: Hudhayf said: The people of Basra will not open the door of guidance nor leave the door of error, and the flood has been lifted from The whole earth except for sight."
"38559","(38559) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Uyayn bin Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his brother. Rabi`a bin Jawshan said: I came to the Levant and entered upon Abdullah bin Amr, and he said: Who are you from? We said: From the people of Basra. He said: Either not, so be prepared, O people of Basra. We said: With what. He said: By auction and nearness, the best money. Today there are camels on which a man can carry his family and their rulers, and a very brave horse. By God, the sons of Qantaurai lest they drive you out of it until they put you on their knees. He said: We said: And they are not the children of Qantaurai. He said: As for In the book, this is how we find it, and as for the adjective, it is the adjective of abandonment."
"38560","(38560) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: How will you be if you do not need a dinar, a dirham, or a qafiz? (Muslim 2220, Ahmed 332)"
"38561","(38561) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Umar wanted not to leave any of the lands without going to him. Ka'b said to him: Do not come to Iraq, for there are nine tenths of evil in it."
"38562","(38562) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, who said: I heard Abu Musa say: Indeed, for this, Basra has four names: Al-Basra, Al-Khuraibiyyah, Palmyra, and Al-Mu’tafika."
"38563","(38563) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I saw Kathir ibn Aflah in a dream. So I said to him: O Ibn Aflah, how are you? He said: Fine. He said: I said: You are the martyrs. He said: No, if he killed me. Muslims are not martyrs, but we are the mourners."
"38564","(38564) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Yahya bin Husayn, who said: I heard more than one person talking to the living, On the authority of Ubayy, he said to Saad ibn Abi Waqqas: What will prevent you from fighting? He said: No, until you give me a sword that a believer will know from The infidel"
"38565","(38565) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Uqba bin Aws, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: People fight among themselves over a pre-Islamic claim when a prince is killed or expelled and it appears. When one of the two groups appears, it is humiliated, and the one who distracts them from the enemy desires them, and they march towards them. And people are thrust into disbelief."
"38566","(38566) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kharboud, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: Woe to the two wings from the head, and woe to the head from the two wings. Shu’abi said: So I said: What are the two wings? He said: Iraq and Egypt, and the head: the Levant."
"38567","(38567) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar told me, on the authority of Abbas Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nadhi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: They will cause the house to the side of the house to be eclipsed and the house to the side of the house. Next to the house where injustices are."
"38568","(38568) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Ghalib bin Ajrad, he said: I came. Abdullah bin Amr and I were with a friend of mine, and he was speaking to the people. He said: Who are you? So we said: From the people of Basra. He said: Then you should stay in its suburbs. When the people dispersed from it, we approached it and said: I saw your statement from among you and your statement against you. In its environs, then, he said: The center of its kingdom, and what is around it, are tainted with them. Thabit said: So when Ghalib bin Ajrd entered On the spacious side he strove until he got out of it."
"38569","(38569) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: A man came to Hudhayfah and said: I want to Going out to Basra, and he said: If you must go out, remove her robes and do not lower her navel."
"38570","(38570) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Hurmuz Abi Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Abi Yahya, he said: Hudhayfy was asked: Who is a hypocrite? He said: The one who describes Islam but does not practice it."
"38571","(38571) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan ibn Salih, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, he said: A man from Taif narrated to me, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Hour will not come until you are joking around on the roads like donkeys and Satan comes to you. Then He will turn them to idol worshipers. (Hakim 457)"
"38572","(38572) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: He fights The Qur’an and the Sultan. He said: Then the Sultan tramples on the thickness of the Qur’an, so what a curse, and what a curse, as long as you escape from it."
"38573","(38573) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: A fire is about to come out of Yemen. He said: It will drive the people out in the morning with them when they morning, and take a nap with them when they say, and go with them. When they go, then when you hear it, go out to the Levant."
"38574","(38574) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ka`b said: If You see that the drops have been forbidden, then know that the people have withheld zakat, so God has forbidden what He has, and if you see swords that have been stripped, then know. Indeed, the rule of God has been violated, so they took revenge on one another, and if you see adultery committed, then know that usury has become widespread."
"38575","(38575) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Zaid bin Sohan, he said: Salman said to me: How would you be when the Qur’an and the Sultan fought? He said: Then I would be with the Qur’an. He said: Well done, Al-Zawid then. Abu Qurayh, who hated temptations, said: Then I sit in my house. Salman said: If I were at most nine verses I was with one of the two sects."
"38576","(38576) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul: He said: Musa bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab. He said: When we returned from Nahrawan, Ali said: We have witnessed a people in Yemen. We said: O Commander of the Faithful, how? That, he said: With love."
"38577","(38577) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: The man He will witness the sin and deny it, so he will be as if he was absent from it, and he will be absent from it and be pleased with it. So he will be like one who witnessed it."
"38578","(38578) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid, he said: Hudhayfy said: The man To be part of the temptation, and what is in it."
"38579","(38579) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abdullah bin Subay’, he said: Ali addressed us. He said: Let some of this be dyed, meaning the beard of his head. They said: Tell us about it and we will kill it. He said: Then follow God. You will kill me other than me. They said: So appoint a successor over us. He said: No, but I will leave you to what the Messenger of God left you to. God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What do you say to your Lord when you meet Him? He said: I say: Oh God, I am in them, and you are in them. If you wish, you can reform them, and if you wish, you can corrupt them."
"38580","(38580) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abdullah said: By God, I will move towards a vertical mountain. Is more beloved to me than competing with a deferred king. (Naim 341)"
"38581","(38581) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabaliya, on the authority of Amir bin Matar, he said: I was with Then he said: You are about to see them depart from their religion just as a woman departs from her kiss. So adhere to what you are on today, for it is the clear path. How will you, O Amer bin Matar, when people take a path? And the Qur’an is a way, with whichever one you are. I said: With the Qur’an, I will live with it and die with it. He said: So it is you."
"38582","(38582) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ali, on the authority of Ibn Hanafi, “Indeed, a people before you became confused and fled until they became lost. When one of them was called from behind him, he would answer from in front of him.” And if he is called from in front of him, he answers from behind him."
"38583","(38583) Muawiyah told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: How are you? When a time comes to you when one of you goes out of his chamber to his seat and returns, having been transformed into an ape, and seeks his place, but there is no He finds it"
"38584","(38584) Omar bin Bishr told us, he said: Ibn Mubarak told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Amr bin Wabisa Al-Asadi, on the authority of his father, said: I was in Kufa in my house when I heard at the door of the house: Peace be upon you, come in. ? So I said: And peace be upon you, then it came, then it was Abdullah bin Masoud, so I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, come to me. A visit, and that was at noon. He said: The day had been long for me, so I remembered who I was speaking to, so he started speaking to me. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I narrated to him, Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: There will be a trial in which the sleeper is better than the one who lies down, and the one who lies down is better than the one who sits, and the one who sits is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands He is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks is better than the one who runs. He killed them both in the Fire. He said: I said: When will that happen, O Messenger of God? He said: Those are the days of the Harj. I said: When are the days of the Harj? He said: When the man who is sitting with him is not safe. He said: I said: What do you command me to do? If I realize that, he said: Enter your house. I said: What do you think? If he enters upon me, he said: Stay in your room. He said: I said: Have you seen that? He came to me and said: Say like this, and say: Be guilty of my sin and your sin, and be the servant of God who was slain. (Ahmed 449. Abdul Razzaq 20727)"
"38585","(38585) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Bahram, he said: Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Jundub bin Sufyan, a man from Bajil, told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be tribulations after me. Like the cracks of a dark night, it strikes a man like the impact of the robes of a bullock. A man becomes a Muslim in the morning and an unbeliever by evening. He will be a Muslim in the evening and become an unbeliever in the morning, and a Muslim man said: O Messenger of God, what should we do in that case? He said: Enter your homes and be silent. A Muslim man said: What do you think if he enters the house of one of us? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Let him hold you with his hand, but let him be the servant of God who was killed, and he should not be the servant of God. The murderer, for the man is in the depths of Islam, so he eats his brother’s wealth, sheds his blood, disobeys his Lord, and disbelieves. By his Creator, then Hell will be granted to him."
"38586","(38586) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhaifa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Is any of you unable to kill him if a man comes to him, meaning From the family of such-and-such that he says such-and-such, and says with one hand over the other, then he is like the best of the two sons of Adam. And when he is in Paradise, and when he fights him in Hell, (Musnad 4354)"
"38587","(38587) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: She was not informed, nor has she been informed since she was The temptation. Masruq said to him: If I were like you, I would be glad to have died. Shurayh said to him: So it is sufficient for more than That is what is in the breasts, and the two categories meet and one of them is more beloved to me than the other."
"38588","(38588) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, he said: Safwan bin Mahrez told me, he said: To beware. One of you, not a handful of Muslim blood will come between him and Heaven. (Na’im 375)"
"38589","(38589) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: We were talking, Indeed, a better time will come upon the people. Those who see good will soon avoid it."
"38590","(38590) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Asbat bin Nasr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No believer will destroy you, faith restricts destruction. (Hakim 352)"
"38591","(38591) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man came to Al-Zubayr during the days of the Camel, and he said: Kill You have Ali. He said: He was sufficient. He said: I will come to him and tell him that he is with him. Then I will give him a fatwa for him. Al-Zubayr said: No, I heard the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Faith is subject to destruction, no believer can destroy it. (Abdul Razzaq 9676 and Ahmed 166)"
"38592","(38592) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: My companions learned Good, and I learned evil. They said: What made you do that? He said: He who knows the place of evil fears it."
"38593","(38593) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Zur’a bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The man will be killed a thousand times on the Day of Resurrection. Then Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud said to him: O Abu Zur’a, a thousand. He killed him, he said: in the manner in which he was killed."
"38594","(38594) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Zur’a, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ali, who said: No. Sow with me in the blackness, for if you sow, you will fight over its water with swords, and if you fight, you will disbelieve."
"38595","(38595) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, who said: Arina, Aqidah, disobedience, and herd were mean.\nAbu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:"
"38596","(38596) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, that he was With Omar, he said: So he said to him: Save money and take captives, and you are about to withhold giving."
"38597","(38597) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Ali said: Take the giving as it is. As a bait, if it is from your religion, reject it with the utmost rejection."
"38598","(38598) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, he said: Salman said: Take the giving what is prescribed for you, then It is difficult for you, so abandon it in the most severe manner."
"38599","(38599) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amr bin Sa’id. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Only a few will come upon you until the fox has spent his teeth between two poles. From the pillars of the mosque, Abd al-Malik said, it is the mosque of Medina. He says: from the ruins."
"38600","(38600) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. This nation will be killed until the killer is killed without knowing what he was killed for, and the one who was killed does not know what he was killed for. (Muslim 2231)"
"38601","(38601) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Qara’is will be killed until their killing is reached. Yemen, and a man said to him: Did Al-Hajjaj not do that? He said: That did not happen after that."
"38602","(38602) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, who said: Abraham said to me: Beware of killing. With temptation"
"38603","(38603) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban informed me, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Allaqah, on the authority of Qutba ibn Malik. On the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, he said: Not a man from among you will go a hand span to a person of authority to humiliate him. No, by God, no. A people who humiliated the Sultan will remain humiliated until the Day of Resurrection."
"38604","(38604) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, he said: He said: Hudhayf: There are two groups of people fighting over this excrement. I don’t care which one. I know you. Then a man said to him: Are these people in Paradise? Or in hell? He said: That is what I am telling you. He said: What did they kill? He said: My ignorant people killed me."
"38605","(38605) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Taman, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Qais al-Amiri, on the authority of Suhaim Ibn Nawfal, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said to me: How do you do when the worshipers fight? I said: And that will happen? He said: Yes, the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: How should I do? He said: Restrain your tongue and conceal your position, and you must do so. What you know, and do not abandon what you know for what you deny."
"38606","(38606) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abdul Rabbah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Qais, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said to me: Would you like God to make you dwell in the midst of Paradise? He said: So I said: May I be made your ransom, and do I want anything other than that? He said: You must adhere to the congregation, or by the assembly of the people."
"38607","(38607) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Al-Hasan said to me: Are you not surprised that Saeed bin Jubayr entered upon me? So he asked me about Al-Hajjaj fighting with him some of the leaders, meaning the companions of Ibn Al-Ash’ath."
"38608","(38608) Affan told us, he said: Sulaym bin Akhdar told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Muslim bin Yasar was the highest He was with the people of Basra from Al-Hasan until he became weak with Ibn Al-Ash’ath, and Al-Hasan restrained himself, but Abu Sa’id did not remain at his highest level after that. And the other fell."
"38609","(38609) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: A sheikh from the people of Mecca narrated to me, saying: I saw Ibn Umar, in the days of Ibn al-Zubayr, entered the mosque and saw the weapon. He began to say: You have glorified this world. You have glorified this world. Until he received the stone."
"38610","He said: Abu Bakr told us, saying:\n(38610) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: I have sealed a thousand prophets, or more, and there is not a prophet sent to a people who does not warn. His people are the Antichrist, and indeed he has made clear to me what has not been made clear to anyone else, and he is one-eyed, and indeed your Lord is not one-eyed."
"38611","(38611) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace He mentioned the Messiah in front of the people, and said: God is not one-eyed, and the Antichrist is blind in his right eye. As if his eyes were floating grapes. (Bukhari 7123 and Muslim 2247)"
"38612","(38612) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Dawud bin Amir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There was no prophet before me who did not describe the Antichrist to his nation. And we will describe him in a manner that no one has described before me. Indeed, he is one-eyed, and God is not one-eyed. (Ahmad 1761, Abu Ali 725)"
"38613","(38613) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his maternal uncle, meaning Al-Faltan bin Asim He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: As for the Messiah of misguidance, he is a man whose forehead is anointed and whose left eye is wiped. The neck is wide and warm, as if it were So-and-so bin Abdul-Uzza, or Abdul-Uzza bin so-and-so."
"38614","(38614) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abi Ad-Daman, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever among you hears of the emergence of the Antichrist, let him refrain from it as much as he can, for A man comes to Him and he thinks that he is a believer, so he will continue with him until he follows him from the doubts he sees. \n(Abu Dawud 4319. Ahmad 431)"
"38615","(38615) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of al-Mughirah bin Shu`ba, who said: What Someone used to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the Antichrist more than me. He said: And what do you ask me about him? I said: Indeed People say: He has food and drink. He said: It is easier for God than that. (Bukhari 7122 and Muslim 1693)"
"38616","(38616) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: He narrated to us Zaid bin Thabit, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Seek refuge in God from the temptations of the Antichrist. We said: We seek refuge in By God, from the temptation of the Antichrist."
"38617","(38617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you becomes a martyr, let him seek refuge in God from the evil of the temptations of the Antichrist. (Muslim 412. Abu Dawud 975)"
"38618","(38618) Waki’ and Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of the temptations of the Antichrist."
"38619","(38619) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Abu Suraihi, Hudhayfah ibn Asid He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at us and said: The Hour will not begin until there have been ten signs. He mentioned the rising of the sun. From its west, and the Antichrist. (Muslim 2225. Abu Dawud 4311)"
"38620","(38620) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: I will seal a thousand prophets, or more. God has not sent a single prophet to his people except The Antichrist warned them, and he has made clear to me what had not been made clear to anyone before me. He is one-eyed, and God is not one-eyed. He is blind in the right eye, has no pupil, is open, and the other is as if it were a shining star, and he is followed by him from all A people who call Him in their tongues as a god.\n(Hakim 597. Ahmad 265)"
"38621","(38621) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: They mentioned him, meaning the Antichrist. From Ibn Abbas, he said: Written between his eyes: K F R, he said: Ibn Abbas said: I did not hear him say that, but he He said: As for Abraham, look at your companion. Yazid said: He means the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and as for Moses, he was a man. Adam was curled up and tall, as if he were one of the men of the Sun, on a red camel with a muzzle on his claws, and it was as if I was looking at him who had descended from The valley meets you. (Bukhari 1555, Muslim 153)"
"38622","(38622) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of the names of his son Yazid, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no harm in you from him. If he leaves while I am alive, then I will be his Hajj. And if he comes out after my death, then God is my successor over every Muslim. (Abu Dawud 4321. Tirmidhi 2240)"
"38623","(38623) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: We seek refuge in God from the temptations of the Antichrist."
"38624","(38624) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Antichrist He is blind in the right eye, with a nail on it, written between his eyes is an infidel. (Bukhari 7131, Muslim 2248)"
"38625","(38625) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Antichrist is one-eyed, curly, and dark-haired. His head is as if the branch of a tree. People will liken him to a servant. Al-Uzza bin Qatan. If he is destroyed, then he is one-eyed, and God is not one-eyed."
"38626","(38626) Shababa told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: It was Hisham bin Amir. Al-Ansari saw men approaching Imran bin Husayn and other of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He became angry and said: By God, you are stepping towards someone who was not more present to the Messenger of God than I was, nor more aware of his speech than I was. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: There is no temptation greater than the temptation between the creation of Adam until the Hour comes. Antichrist (Ahmad 20. Tabarani 22)"
"38627","(38627) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Because I know better about what is with the Antichrist than the Antichrist, with him are two running rivers. One of them saw it. The eye is white water, and the other sees the eye as blazing fire. If someone realizes that, let him bring the fire he sees. Let him close his eyes, then lower his head to drink, for it is cold water, and the Antichrist will wipe his eyes, with a fingernail on them. It is thick and written before the eyes of an unbeliever. It is read by every believer, scribe and non-writer. (Muslim 2249. Ahmad 404)"
"38628","(38628) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Because I know better than the Antichrist that he has a burning fire and a river of cold water, so who will catch him? Who among you will not be destroyed by it? Let him close his eyes and fall into what he sees as fire, for it is a river of water. Cold (Abu Dawud 4315)"
"38629","(38629) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq, on the authority of Abi Salih, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while I was crying, and he said: What Does he make you cry? So I said: O Messenger of God, I mentioned the Antichrist. He said: Do not cry, for if he comes out while I am alive, I will suffice for you, but if I die, then Your Lord is not one-eyed, but the Jews of Asbaan will go out with him, and he will walk until he lands on the outskirts of the city. And on that day it will have seven gates, at each gate there will be two angels, and the worst of its people will go out to it, and even the worst of them will go out. He will come to Lydda, and Jesus, son of Mary, will come down and kill him. Then Jesus will remain in the land for forty years, or Almost forty years, a just imam and a just arbitrator. (Ahmad 75. Ibn Hibban 6822)"
"38630","(38630) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Laqit. Al-Tajeebi, on the authority of Ibn Hawwal al-Azdi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Whoever is saved from three is saved. They said it three times. They said: What is that, O Messenger of God? He said: My death, the Antichrist, and whoever kills a caliph who is steadfast in the truth. His gift (Ahmed 288)"
"38631","(38631) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdul Allah ibn Suraqa, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: It was not No prophet after Noah except that he warned his people about the Antichrist, and I will warn you about him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, described him to us. And he said: Some of those who saw me or heard my words will overtake you. They will say: O Messenger of God, how will our hearts be at that time? Is there anything like it today? He said: Or better. (Abu Dawud 4723. Tirmidhi 2234)"
"38632","(38632) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thuban narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Makhoul, On the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Malik bin Yakhamir, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The construction of the Holy City is the ruin of Yathrib, and the ruin of Yathrib is the emergence of the epic, and the emergence of the epic is the conquest of Constantinople Constantinople opened the door of the Antichrist, then he struck his hand on the thigh or shoulders of the one who narrated it, then he said: Indeed, this is the truth, as you are here, or as you are sitting, meaning a refuge. (Abu Dawud 4294)"
"38633","(38633) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, he said: We came to Othman bin Abi Al-Aas on a Friday to show us a copy of the Qur’an, so we sat with a man who was speaking, then he came Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, so we turned to him, and Othman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: It will be Muslims have three cities: Egypt at the meeting place of the two Bahrain, Egypt on the peninsula, and Egypt in the Levant, so people panic three times. Then there will be panics, and the Antichrist will emerge in the presence of an army, and he will be defeated by the East. The first Egypt to be defeated will be the one at the meeting point. Bahrain, and its people will form into three groups: a group that will stand and say: We will share it and see what it is, and a group that will join the Bedouins. And a group will join the Egyptians who are in charge of them, and with them are seventy thousand guards, and most of the Jews and women will be sold to them."
"38634","(38634) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Hashraj narrated to us, he said: Sa’id bin Jumhan narrated to us, on the authority of Safina, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and said: There was no prophet who did not warn his nation of the Antichrist, and he is one-eyed. The left eye, the right eye there is a thick fingernail, between the two eyes there is an unbeliever with it and the religions of one of them is a jinn. And the other is fire, so his paradise is fire and his fire is paradise, and with him are two angels resembling two of the prophets. One of them is on his right and the other is on his left, and he says to people: Am I not your Lord? Am I not alive or dead? Then someone says to him. The two angels: You lied, and no one of the people will hear it except its companion. Then its companion will say: You have told the truth, so the people will hear it and think. The Dajjal only told the truth, and that was a temptation. Then he walked until he came to Medina, but no permission was given to him therein, so he said: This is the village of that man, then he will travel until he comes to the Levant, and God will kill him when he wakes up. (Ahmad 221. Tabarani 6445)"
"38635","(38635) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Asir bin Jabir, He said: A red wind blew through the cup, and a man came who did not have a hijra except O Abdullah bin Masoud. The hour has come. He said: Abdullah was reclining, so he sat up, and he said: Indeed, the battlefield will not rise until an inheritance is not divided and he does not rejoice in his spoils, and he said: An enemy they gather to the people of Islam and the people of Islam gather against them, and he moved with his hand towards the Levant. I said: What do you mean by the Romans? He said: Yes, and in that case there will be a severe response to the fighting, so the Muslims stipulate a condition of death that will not return except the victor. Then they will fight until the night closes between them, and these and these will be rewarded, each one not victorious, and the guard will be destroyed."
"38636","(38636) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi His firstborn, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The fathers of the Antichrist will remain for thirty years and he will not be born. To them, then a one-eyed boy was born to them. He was more harmful and less beneficial. His eyes slept but his heart did not sleep. Then she was cursed. His parents, and he said: His father is a tall, meat-like man with a long nose, as if his nose were a beak, and his mother is a woman. Great breasts. (Ahmad 40. Tayalisi 865)"
"38637","(38637) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not tell you about the Antichrist a story that no prophet of his people has told him? He is one-eyed, and he brings with him something like the Garden and the Fire, and he says: This is the Garden, this is the Fire, and indeed I warn you. With it, just as Noah warned his people about it. (Bukhari 3338, Muslim 2250)"
"38638","(38638) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The terror of the Antichrist will not enter Medina. On that day, there will be seven Doors, each door has two places."
"38639","(38639) Shababhi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Raja’ bin Abu Raja’, he said: Buraidah entered the mosque and Mahjen was at the door of the mosque and he was praying, so he said: Buraidah and he was There is a joke in it: Don’t you pray as Sakbaa prays? Mujjan said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him by the hand. So he went up to Uhud and overlooked the city, and said: Woe to its mother, a city whose people have abandoned it, and it is the best it was. Or as long as it has been, the Antichrist will come to it and find at every one of its gates an angel with his wings attached, but no They enter it. (Ahmad 338, Tayalisi 1295)"
"38640","(38640) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith bin Hasirah narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab said: I heard Abu Dharr say: Because I swear ten times, because Ibn Sayyad, the antichrist, is more beloved to me than swearing. One, it is not, and that is because of something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God sent me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Umm Ibn Sayyad, and he said: Ask her how long she was pregnant with him, and she said: She was pregnant with him for twelve months. So I came to him and informed him, and he said: Ask her about his morning when it happened. She said: He cried out like the cry of a boy, Ibn Shihrin. He said: Or He said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have hidden for you something hidden. He said: I have hidden for you the bone of the sheep of Afra, and he meant To say: And (smoke), so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Be humble, for you will never outpace predestination.\n(Ahmad 148 Bazzar 3983)"
"38641","(38641) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, who said: We were with the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, sitting while he was sleeping. We mentioned the Antichrist, but he woke up with his face red, and said: I am more afraid of the Antichrist. Against you is the Dajjal: misleading Imams. (Ahmad 98 and Abu Ali 462)"
"38642","(38642) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Masadī informed us, on the authority of Riyah bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam said: Abdullah bin Salam said: The people will remain after the emergence of the Antichrist for forty years, and he will be planted Palm trees and the markets are established."
"38643","(38643) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Hudhayf, he said: The Antichrist has committed some of his temptations, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is alive."
"38644","(38644) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, who said: Hudhayfah said: What is the exit? The Dajjal is better for me than the size of a bridle. (Naim 1555)"
"38645","(38645) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Abu Yafour told us, he said: I heard Abu Amr Al-Shaybani say: I was with... Hudhayf was sitting when a Bedouin came until he knelt before him and said: Has the Antichrist come out? So Hudhayfy said to him: What is the Dajjal? Indeed, what is less than the Dajjal is more afraid than the Dajjal. His temptation was only for forty nights."
"38646","(38646) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Antichrist will encompass the entire earth except Mecca and Medina. He said: Then he will come to Medina and find in every corner of it rows of angels. Then he will come to the marshes of the cliff and will be struck. His porch, then the city would shake three times, and every hypocrite, male and female, would come out to it."
"38647","(38647) Abu Al-Mu’ri’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Ajlah narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, he said: I heard Hudhayfah says: If the Antichrist came, people would believe in him in their graves."
"38648","(38648) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that Omar asked a Jewish man about a matter. He said: I have learned the truth from you, so tell me about the Antichrist, and he said: And there are Jews. The son of Mary will surely kill him with the annihilation of Lydda."
"38649","(38649) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Al-Masih bin Maryam, when the Antichrist sees it, he melts like fat melts, he said: Then the Antichrist will be killed, and the Jews will disperse from him, so they will be killed. The stone even said: O Abdullah Al-Muslim, this is a Jew, so come and kill him. (Naim 1612)"
"38650","(38650) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who raised him, saying: The Hour will not stand. Until Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon them, descends as a just judge and a just imam, breaks the cross, and kills the pig. He sets the tribute and pours out the money so that no one will accept it. (Bukhari 4418 and Muslim 2120)"
"38651","(38651) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hanzali Al-Aslami, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the son of Mary will arrive at the dawn of spirits for Hajj, or for Umrah, or for the two of them."
"38652","(38652) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hassan bin Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Aqar bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Abi Hariri said: The mosques will be renovated for the coming of the Messiah, and he will come out and break the cross and kill the pig. And whoever realizes it believes in it. Whoever among you realizes it should read him my greetings. Then he turned to me and said: O son of my brother. I see that you are one of the most recent people, so if you catch up with him, extend my greetings to him. (Naim 1600)"
"38653","(38653) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Abraham saying: The Messiah is coming and will break the cross. He kills the pig and pays the jizya."
"38654","(38654) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Abu Bakr said: Is there a land in Iraq called Khurasan? They said: Yes. He said: The Antichrist will emerge from it."
"38655","(38655) I narrated, on the authority of Ruh bin Ubadah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Suba’ On the authority of Amr bin Harith, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The Antichrist will emerge from Khorasan. (Tirmidhi 2237. Bazzar 46)"
"38656","(38656) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Antichrist will descend from Khuz and Kerman, bringing with him eighty thousand wearing rags. They will wear hair as if Their faces are free and beaten."
"38657","(38657) Abd al-Malik ibn Misra narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hawt Al-Abdi, he said: Abdullah said: The ear of the Antichrist’s donkey will shade seventy thousand."
"38658","(38658) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of Anas, who said: Indeed, between the hands of the Antichrist are seventy-odd antichrists."
"38659","(38659) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, on the authority of Nafi’ Ibn Utbah Ibn Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You fight the Arabian Peninsula and God grants victory to it, then You fight Persia, so God will grant you victory. Then you fight the Romans, so God will grant you victory. Then you will fight the Antichrist, so God will grant you victory. Jabir said: No. The Antichrist will emerge until the Romans conquer. (Ahmad 1788, Ibn Hibban 6809)"
"38660","(38660) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, he said: Uqba said: Bin Amr to Hudhayf: Don’t you tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I heard him say: Indeed, with When the Antichrist emerges as water and fire, as for what the people see as water, it will be a burning fire, and as for what the people see as fire, it will be fresh water. Cold, so whoever of you realizes that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, then it is fresh, cool water. Uqba said: And I I heard him say that. (Bukhari 3450, Muslim 2250)"
"38661","(38661) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Junada bin Abi Umayyad narrated to us Al-Dawsi said: I and a companion of mine entered upon a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So we said: Tell us what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and do not tell us about anyone else, and if you have someone who believes him, he said: Yes, he rose among us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day, and he said: I warn you of the Antichrist, I warn you of the Antichrist, I warn you of the Antichrist, for he There was no prophet except that he had warned his nation, and indeed among you I have given the nation, and indeed, he is the face of a man with wiped eyes. Al-Yusra, and with him is a garden and a fire, so his fire is a garden and his garden is fire, and with him is a river of water and a mountain of bread, and indeed He gives power over a soul and kills it, then brings it back to life. He does not give power over anyone else, and He makes it rain from the sky but it does not bring forth growth. The earth, and he will remain on the earth for forty mornings until he reaches every place on it, and he will not approach it for four Mosques: The Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of the Messenger, the Mosque of the Holy Place, and the Mount, and whatever things are similar to you, for God is not Twice one-eyed. (Ahmed 435)"
"38662","(38662) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Antichrist will not come out until he is absent. What is most beloved to the believer is his exit from him, and his exit will not harm him. For the believer there are pebbles that he raises from the earth, and he does not know the lowest of them and the furthest of them except the same."
"38663","(38663) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, he said: Abdullah was sitting with his companions, and their voices rose. He said: Then Hudhayfah came and said: What are these voices, O son of Umm Abdullah, he said: O Abu Abdullah, they mentioned the Antichrist and we feared him, so Hudhayfah said: By God, I don’t care whether I meet him or not. These black goats, Abdul-Malik said to a goat that eats the stones next to the mosque, he said: Then Abdullah said to him: Why? To God is your father. Hudhayfah said: Because we are a believing people and he is an unbeliever, and God will give us victory and victory over him. By God, he will not go out unless his going out is more beloved to the Muslim person than the cooling of drink for the thirsty person. Abdullah said: Why? To God is your father. Hudhayfah said: From the severity of calamities and the armies of evil."
"38664","(38664) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met Ibn Sayyad and with him were Abu Bakr and Omar, or he said: two men, so he said to him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I bear witness that he is the Messenger of God, so he said: Ibn Sayyad: I bear witness that he is the Messenger of God, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I believed in God and His Messenger, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What you see, and he said: Ibn Sayyad: I saw a throne on the water, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You see the throne of Satan on the sea. He said: What You see, he said: I see whether they are telling the truth or lying, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He was confused. He was confused. So they called him (Muslim 2241, Ahmad 368)"
"38665","(38665) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma, she said: I went to Aisha and saw the people standing and praying, so I said: What is the matter with the people? Then she pointed with her hand towards the heavens, or said: Glory be to God, and I said: A verse, and she indicated with her head that yes, so the Messenger of God delayed. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I got up until the fainting overcame me, and I started pouring water on my head. She said: So the Messenger of God praised him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he praised him for what he deserved and said: There is nothing that I had not seen except that it had I saw him in this position of mine, even to Paradise and Hell, and it has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves, for example, or soon, not Do you know what that is? Asmaa said: From the temptation of the Antichrist. (Muslim 627)"
"38666","(38646) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Al-Aswad, he said: I left as a delegate. At the time of Muawiyah, when there was with him on the bed a man with a very red face, with a very wrinkled face. Muawiyah said to him: Do you know who this is? This is Abdullah bin Amr. He said: Then Abdullah said to me: Who are you from? So I said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Do you know of a land before you that was abundant in marshes and is called Kuthi? He said: I said: Yes. He said: From it will the Antichrist emerge. He said: Then he said: Indeed, after the good people, the wicked will have twenty and a hundred years. No. No one knows when the first ones will enter."
"38667","(38667) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Ma’rour bin Suwayd, he said: Ka'b said: The most violent of the Arabs against the Antichrist is your people, meaning the Banu Tamim."
"38668","(38668) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, he said: Tha’labah bin narrated to me. Abbad Al-Abdi is one of the people of Basra. One day he witnessed a speech to Samurah ibn Jundub, and he mentioned it in his speech. A hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: By God, the Hour will not come until thirty liars come out The last of them is the one-eyed Antichrist, whose left eye is wiped as if it were the eye of Abu Tahya, or Yahya, according to a sheikh from the Ansar. And when He comes out, He claims that He is God, so whoever believes in Him, believes in Him, and follows Him, no good will benefit you from working for Him. And whoever disbelieves in it and rejects it, he will not be punished for any of the actions of the predecessor, and it will appear over the entire earth except the Sacred Mosque. And the Holy House, and He confined the believers in the Holy House. He said: Then God and His soldiers defeated him to the point that he became a leper. The wall or the root of the tree called: O believer, this is an unbeliever who is concealing himself from Me. Come, kill him. He said: And that will not happen. Thus, until you see matters becoming worse within yourselves, you ask among yourselves: Did your Prophet mention it to you? A remembrance of it, until the mountains moved from their places. Then, after that, he stopped and pointed with his hand. He said: Then I witnessed. He had another sermon. He said: So he mentioned this hadith without saying a word before it or after it. (Ahmed 13)"
"38669","(38669) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih informed me, saying: Rabi’ ibn Yazid informed me. Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir Al-Hasbiy, that he heard Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan say: Whoever is confused about matters, so do not follow hardships, nor the one-eyed one, meaning the Dajjal."
"38670","(38670) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud’an, on the authority of al-Hasan, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Antichrist will wade through the seas up to his knees, reach the clouds, and outrun the sun. To the west, and on his forehead was a horn from which he snared serpents, and the entire weapon was depicted on his body, until he mentioned The sword, the spear, and the shield. He said: I said: What is the shield? He said: The shield. (Ibn Kathir 142)"
"38671","(38671) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Antichrist will emerge and remain on earth for forty mornings, and he will reach there every day’s water like a Friday prayer. And the Friday is like the month, and the month is like the sun. Then he said: How will you and your people be in the dawn, and you will be in the wind, and they will be satisfied? And you are hungry, and they are thirsty, and you are thirsty."
"38672","(38672) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: Abdullah used to recite the Qur’an in The mosque, and this verse was brought to me: {Like a plant that has brought forth its shoots}, and Abdullah said: You are the plantings, and your harvest has approached. Then They mentioned the Antichrist in their gathering, and some of the people said: We wish he had come out so that we could throw stones at him, so he said Abdullah: You say, “By the One besides whom there is no god,” if you had heard about him in Babylon, one of you would have come to him and complained to him. Barefoot from speeding\n(Tabari 26. Hakim 461)"
"38673","(38673) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hallam bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Shihab Al-Absi, he said: Abdullah bin Mughanim told me and mentioned the Antichrist, and he said: The Antichrist is not hidden from him, and the tribulations that will come before him are something I fear. The Antichrist is upon you. Indeed, there is no secret about the Antichrist. Indeed, the Antichrist calls to something that people will know about until they see it from him."
"38674","(38674) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: It does not come out. Antichrist until his emergence will be more pleasing to the Muslims than drinking water when thirsty."
"38675","(38675) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Fatima bint Qays, who said: The Prophet prayed, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, one day at noon, then he ascended the pulpit, and the people disapproved of that, so he went between standing and sitting, but there was no He had ascended before that, except on Friday, so he motioned to them with his hand to sit down, then he said: By God, I will not stand in your place. This is a matter that will benefit you whether you desire it or not, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and informed me, so that a nap prevented me from Joy and comfort to the eyes. Indeed, the Banu Amm of Tamim al-Dari were caught by a storm at sea, so the wind took them to... An island they did not know, so they sat in the boats of the ship and went up, and behold, they saw something black and hairy, with many hairs. They said to her: What are you? She said: I am Al-Jasassah. They said: So tell us. She said: I will not inform you, nor will I ask you about it. But this is the city that you have escaped, so go to it, for there is a man in it who longs to inform you and for you to inform him.\n2. So they came to him and entered upon him, and they saw an old man bound in iron, very strong and very hairy. He said to them: Who? Where did you go? They said: From the Levant. He said: What did the Arabs do? They said: We are a people of the Arabs. He said: What did this man who came out among you do? They said: Good; A people resorted to him and God made him prevail over them, so their affairs today are all, and their god today is one and their religion is one. He said: That is better for them. He said: What did Zaghr’s eye do? They said: They water their crops from it and drink from it. He said: What did the palm trees do between Amman and Baisan? They said: He feeds his jinn every year. He said: What did you do to Lake Tiberias? They said: It flowed out of the water due to a lot of water. He said: He exhaled three times, then he said: If I had escaped from my bonds, this would not have happened. “Do I leave any land except that I have trodden it with my feet and it has brought nothing but goodness, over which I have no authority,” said the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: To this is the end of my joy, this is good, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no way from it. Narrow or wide, except over it is an angel brandishing the sword until the Day of Resurrection."
"38676","(38676) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, saying: Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan narrated to us, that His father told him, he said: We mentioned the Antichrist, so we asked Ali when he would emerge. He said: It will not be hidden from a believer, his eye is the right one. Swept away, before his eyes was an unbeliever who was pleading with us against Ali. He said: So we said: When will that happen? He said: When he will be proud. Neighbor is against his neighbour, and the strong devours the weak, and relatives are severed, and they are as different as the fingers of these people and their interlocking. And he raised it like this, and a man from among the people said to him: How do you order us to do that? Commander of the Faithful. He said: You have no father. Indeed, You will not realize that. He said: So our souls were at ease."
"38677","(38677) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i informed us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Antichrist will overpower a Muslim man and kill him, then revive him, then say: Am I not your Lord? Do you not see that I am being brought back to life and brought to death, and the man is calling: O people of Islam, but the enemy of God is the infidel, the vile one. Indeed, by God He will not have authority over anyone after me. They said: We were passing with Abu Hurairah to the teacher of the book, and he would say: O teacher of the book, gather I have your servants, and he gathers them together and says: Tell them: Let them be silent. O my brother’s sons, understand what I am telling you. If any of you meets Jesus, son of Mary, he is young and bright and ruddy, so let him have the greetings of peace be recited to him from Abu Hurairah. No teacher of the book passes by without saying something like that to his boys."
"38678","(38678) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Hour will not come until the city of Heraclius Caesar is conquered, the muezzins call in it, and the money is distributed in it. With the armor, they come with the most wealth that people have ever seen, and then the screamer comes to them, “Indeed, the Antichrist has succeeded you among your families. Then they will throw what is in their hands and will fight with you. (Naim bin Hammad 1488)"
"38679","(38679) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Shakhir, that Noah and With him were some of the prophets who used to seek refuge from the temptations of the Antichrist."
"38680","(38680) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Jabala bin Suhaim told me, on the authority of Muathir bin Afazah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: When he was captured by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He met Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, and they thought about the hour. They started with Abraham and asked him about it, but he was not with him. Knowledge of it, so they asked Moses, but he had no knowledge of it, so they referred the hadith to Jesus, and he said: God’s covenant with me regarding No one knows except God as to whether it is due. He mentioned the emergence of the Antichrist, and he will descend and I will kill him, and he will return. People go to their countries, and Gog and Magog meet them, and they descend from every corner. They do not pass by water without drinking it. And there is nothing but that they spoil it, so they will run to me, so I will call upon God, and I will kill them, and the earth will smell from their scent, so they will run to me. So I will pray to God, and He will send the sky with water, and it will carry their bodies and throw them into the sea, then the mountains will be blown away and the earth will expand with a tide. The eternal, then it will be returned to me if that happens, that the one who rushes among people is like a pregnant woman who has died, his family does not know his death. They were surprised by her birth. The common people said: I found confirmation of that in the Book of God {until when Gog and Magog are opened And they are descending from every direction, and the true promise has drawn near. (Ibn Majah 2081, Abu Ali 5273)"
"38681","(38681) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Adam, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The prophets are brothers, due to the faults of their mothers. Their religion is one, and I am the closest of people to Jesus, son of Mary, because there was not a prophet between me and him, so if You have seen him, recognize him, for he is a man of upright character, of red and white, with a plump head, as if his head were dripping. And if no rain falls between the two regions, then he strikes the cross, kills the pig, imposes the tribute, and fights the people over the land. Islam until God destroys in its time all religions other than Islam, and God destroys in its time the Messiah of misguidance The liar, the antichrist, and security will occur in his time on earth until lions graze with camels, tigers with cows, and wolves with sheep. And the children or young men will play with the snakes, without harming one another, and they will remain on earth as long as God wills. Then He dies and the Muslims pray over him. (Ahmed 437)"
"38682","(38682) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Most of the Antichrist’s followers will be Jews and his children. Prostitutes\n(Naim 1534)"
"38683","(38683) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Umm She greeted him, saying: His mother gave birth to him Masroor and circumcised, meaning the son of a fisherman."
"38684","(38684) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I met Ibn Sayyad on the road to... He opened the roads of Medina and swelled until he filled the road. So I said: Be humble, for you will never exceed your level. So some of it joined one another and I passed on."
"38685","(38685) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we passed by two boys playing, so they dispersed when they saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Ibn Sayyad sat, and it was as if he had annoyed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: What’s the matter with your hands getting so dusty? Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God? He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God? Omar said: O Messenger of God, leave me so that I may kill this evil person. He said: Leave him, then He is the one who fears, you will not be able to kill him. (Muslim 2240, Ahmad 380)"
"38686","(38686) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir Bin Abdullah, he said: We lost Ibn Sayyad on the day of the heat."
"38687","(38687) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ibn Sayyad: What do you see? He said: I see a throne on the sea and around it are snakes. So he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: This is the throne of Satan. (Muslim 2241, Ahmad 43)"
"38688","(38688) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: Indeed, between the hands of the Messenger are liars. Among them is the companion of turtledoves, among them is the lion, and among them is the companion of donkeys. Among them is the Antichrist, and he is the greatest of temptations among them. (Ahmad 345. Bazzar 3375)"
"38689","(38689) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jariyah, on the authority of Majma’ bin Jariyah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Antichrist Jesus, son of Mary, will kill him at the gate of Lydda."
"38690","(38690) Waki’ and Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Hawt al-Abdi, He said: Abdullah said: The ear of the Antichrist’s donkey will overshadow seventy thousand people."
"38691","(38691) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Antichrist will emerge on a donkey, an abomination upon an abomination. (Abdul Razzaq 20827)"
"38692","(38692) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be people who will accompany the Antichrist who say: We will certainly accompany him, and we know that he He is a liar, but we only accompany him to eat from the food and graze from the trees, and when the wrath of God descends, it descends upon all of them. (Naim bin Hammad 1535)"
"38693","(38693) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Antichrist will emerge from Kuthi."
"38694","(38694) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, he said: Abdullah said: Indeed, I know the first of his family. Verses that the Antichrist will knock on: You are the people of Kufa."
"38695","(38695) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Khaythama, he said: They said: If the Antichrist had come out, we would have done so, so Abd said: God: If morning had come in Babylon, you would have complained about the haste. (Tabarani 8511)"
"38696","(38696) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, He said: No man from Gog and Magog dies without leaving a thousand offspring to his descendants."
"38697","(38697) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Furat al-Qazzaz, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Asid. Al-Ghafari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked at us from his chambers while we were studying the Hour, and he said: Do not get up. The Hour until it is ten signs: the Antichrist, the smoke, the rising of the sun from the west, the creeping creatures of the earth, Gog and Magog, and three An eclipse, an eclipse in the East, an eclipse in the West, an eclipse in the Arabian Peninsula, and fire emerging from the bottom of Aden, Abyan, driving people To the gathering place, you will go down with them when they come down, and you will take a nap with them when they say."
"38698","(38698) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Utba, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let the House be stoned and the Umrah performed after the departure of Gog and Magog. (Bukhari 1593. Ahmed 28)"
"38699","(38699) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, who said: Ibn Abbas saw Boys descending upon one another. He said: This is how Gog and Magog will emerge. (Ibn Jarir 88)"
"38700","(38700) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Murā, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, among my nation there is destruction, disfigurement, and slander. They said: O Messenger of God, and they bear witness that there is no god but Him. God? He said: Yes, as long as the instruments, wines, and silk clothing appear. (Naim 1716; Bazzar 3402)"
"38701","(38701) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man called a prophet, who said: A priest came to Ali and prostrated himself. Then he forbade it and said: Prostrate to Him. He said: So he said: Ask Him when the Hour is coming. Then He said: You have asked me about a matter that He knows. Gabriel or Michael, but if you wish, I can inform you of things that, if they happen, will not be for a long time. When tongues are soft and hearts are like stars, and people desire the world, and buildings appear on the face of the earth, and differences The two brothers, and their desires became divided, and the judgment of God was sold out."
"38702","(38702) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Yazid bin Amr, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi said: As for the approaching of the Hour, buildings will appear on the face of the earth, relatives will be severed, and people will be harmed. The neighbor is his neighbor."
"38703","(38703) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Khaled, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Indeed, among the signs What is sought is for indecency, indecency, bad morals, and bad neighbourliness to appear."
"38704","(38704) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: Amr bin Qais Al-Kindi informed me. He said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: One of the signs of the Hour is that the word will be loud, and the wicked will be humbled and risen. The good people will be placed, and the Mathaani will be recited to them, and none of them will find fault with it. He said: I said: What is the Mathaani? He said: All of them. A book other than the Book of God."
"38705","(38705) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Huywah, who said: The Hour will not start until it The palm tree bears only dates in it. (Naim bin Hammad 1818)"
"38706","(38706) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: The Hour will not begin until the head of the cows rises. By the time"
"38707","(38707) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, who said: From the approaching of the Hour Inflation of the people"
"38708","(38708) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: From the approaching of the Hour is that the crescent is seen before and it is said: Ibn Lailatina."
"38709","(38709) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith? No one will narrate it to you after me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Hour will not start until it is fifty. One woman, one man. (Bukhari 5231, Muslim 2056)"
"38710","(38710) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not begin until wild beasts speak to mankind, and until you speak to a man who is tormented by him. His whip and the strap of his sandal, and his thigh informs him of what happened to his family after him. (Tirmidhi 2181, Ahmed 83)"
"38711","(38711) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I was informed that the Hour will not start until the stones and trees say: O believer, this is a Jew, this is a Christian, so kill him."
"38712","(38712) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man He said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: The one asked about it does not know more than the questioner, but I will tell you about its signs: If the mother gives birth to her mistress, then that is one of the signs. Its signs, and when people’s heads are barefooted and naked, that is one of its signs. And when herdsmen of sheep fight in it. The building, that is one of its signs, about five of which no one knows except God: {Indeed, God has knowledge of the hour and sends down rain. And He knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"38713","(38713) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of Yahya ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man with very white clothes and very black hair came to him. The traces of travel can be seen on him, and none of us recognized him. We approached him until his knees were lower than his knees, and he placed He sufficed on his thighs, and he said: O Muhammad, when will the Hour be? He said: The one being asked about it does not know more than the questioner, but among its signs is that the mother give birth to her mistress, and that you see the barefoot and the naked. The owners of the problem have argued about building buildings. (Muslim 36. Ahmad 28)"
"38714","(38714) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Whenever the Bedouins came to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They asked him when the hour would be, and he looked at the youngest of them and said: If this man lives, then he will not. The pyramid will overtake you. Your hour has arrived upon you. (Bukhari 9511, Muslim 2269)"
"38715","(38715) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: When the Messenger of God returned May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. From Tabuk, they asked him about the Hour, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: It will not come to you. years, and on the earth there is a single soul today. (Muslim 1967. Ibn Hibban 2986)"
"38716","(38716) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: About The hour? He said: What have you prepared for her? So he mentioned something except that I love God and His Messenger, and he said: A man is with whom he loves. (Muslim 2032. Ahmad 110)"
"38717","(38717) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Abi Yahya, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: The Hour does not start until One man will be the leader of fifty women."
"38718","(38718) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Suleiman al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Jabir, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is not a single soul among you who has lived for a hundred years. On that day (Muslim 1967. Ahmad 305)"
"38719","(38719) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, the companion of Al-Saqiyya, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. The same is true, and Jabir interpreted it as: a decrease in one’s lifespan. (Muslim 1966)"
"38720","(38720) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, all of them claiming that he was a prophet before. On the Day of Resurrection"
"38721","(38721) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Indeed, at the hands of the Hour are liars. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. (Muslim 2239. Tabarani 1988)"
"38722","(38722) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Hour will not come until thirty liars and charlatans come out, all of them lying. May God bless him and his Messenger. (Abu Dawud 4334, Ahmad 528)"
"38723","(38723) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Badr bin Othman narrated to us, he said: Al-Sha’abi narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said one day: There will be four tribulations at the end of time. At the end there will be annihilation."
"38724","(38724) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Hudhayfy was asked: Which temptation is more severe? He said: When good and evil are presented to you, you do not know which one to follow."
"38725","(38725) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Dahhak, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The thing I fear most is You must prefer what you see to what you know, and you must go astray while you do not realize it."
"38726","(38726) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saad, who said: Omar said: The thing I fear most is this. The Ummah are a people who interpret the Qur’an in a way other than its interpretation."
"38727","(38727) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaidullah bin Kariz, who said: Omar said: Indeed What I fear most for you is the stinginess of people who are obeyed, and their desires being followed, and a person’s admiration for his opinion, which is the worst of them."
"38728","(38728) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, he said: He said: What Do I fear for you one of two men: a believer whose faith has become clear, and an unbeliever whose disbelief has become clear, but I fear for you. He seeks refuge in faith and acts in other ways."
"38729","(38729) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Waqi’ ibn Sahban, on the authority of Tarif ibn Zayd, or Yazid bin Tarif, on the authority of Abu Musa, said: Indeed, between the hands of the Hour of the Hour will be days during which ignorance will descend and be lifted up. Knowledge until a man goes to his mother and strikes her with the sword out of ignorance."
"38730","(38730) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais, on the authority of Atiyah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in his saying {And when And the saying came upon them, “We brought forth for them an animal from the land that you may speak to.” He said: When they neither enjoin what is right nor forbid it. Denied (Abdul Razzaq 85. Tabari 20)"
"38731","(38731) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Al-Mustadhali bin Husayn, who said: Ali said: O people Kufa: You will certainly enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and you will surely comply with the command of God, or they will make people from among you who will torture you. And God will punish them."
"38732","(38732) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, it was said to Hudhayfy: He is not dead. Al-Ahya’, he said: He who does not know what is right in his heart and rejects what is wrong in his heart."
"38733","(38733) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Qais bin Rashid, on the authority of Abu Juhayfy, on the authority of Ali, who said: The first thing you will be defeated in terms of jihad is jihad with your hands, then jihad with your tongues, then jihad. In your hearts, for any heart that does not know what is right and does not reject what is wrong is set back, and its tops are made its bottoms. (Naeem 137)"
"38734","(38734) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Abu Juhaifa, on the authority of Ali, who said: It will be broken, just as a jug is broken and what is in it is scattered."
"38735","(38735) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abd al-Malik Ibn Umairah, on the authority of Durrā’s husband, on the authority of Durrā, she said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque, and I said: Who is the most pious of people? He said: I command them to do what is right, and I forbid them from doing evil, and I bring them to the mercy of God."
"38736","(38736) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said, Atris said to Abd God: Perished is he who does not enjoin what is right and forbid what is evil. Abdullah said: Rather, perish is he who does not recognize what is right. with his heart, and he rejects the evil with his heart. (Tabarani 8564)"
"38737","(38737) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Umayla, he said: Abdullah said: It is There will be tribulations and tribulations. It is enough for a person that if he sees something wrong, the only thing he can do is know God from his heart. He has a hate."
"38738","(38738) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asamah narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Abu Bakr stood up and thanked God and praised Him, then he said: O people, you are reading this. The verse: (O you who have believed, you are responsible for yourselves. He who goes astray will not harm you when you are guided.) And indeed, we heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: When people see an evil, they will not change it. God is about to blind them. With his punishment, Abu Asama said: And he said another time: And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say. (Abu Dawud 4338. Ahmed 2)"
"38739","(38739) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Maqil, who said: Abdullah said: It is almost certain that no You take from the Kufa in cash or dirhams. I said: How is it, Abdullah bin Masoud? He said: A people will come as if Their faces will be hammered, until they tie their horses to the black and bring you to the places of wormwood until they are A camel and its provisions are more beloved to any of you than these palaces of yours."
"38740","(38740) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Maqil Al-Asadi, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud says: The first thing you will lose in your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose is prayer. A people will pray without religion. To them, and this Qur’an which is before you is as if it had been taken away from you. He said: I said: How is it, O Abdullah? And God has confirmed it in our hearts. He said: It will be spread upon him during the night, and the Qur’an will be lifted up and what is in the hearts will be removed. Then he recited : {And if We willed, We could certainly carry that which We have revealed to you} until the end of the verses."
"38741","(38741) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He will come to In the past, people would gather and pray in mosques, but there was not a believer among them."
"38742","(38742) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Abdullah bin Salamah. Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Misra, said: There will remain a group of people who do not know the truth, nor do they deny and mix up evil. Overlapping of animals and livestock."
"38743","(38743) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Hour will not begin until knowledge becomes ignorance and ignorance becomes ignorance. Knowingly"
"38744","(38744) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The temptations will increase and the chaos will increase. We said: What is the chaos? He said: Murder and the loss of knowledge. He said: It is not removed from the chests of men, but by seizing the scholars. (Ahmed 481)"
"38745","(38745) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: God does not seize knowledge by seizing it from the people, but He seizes knowledge by seizing the scholars, even when Not a scholar remained. The people took ignorant leaders as leaders. They were asked and given fatwas without knowledge. They went astray and were led astray. (Bukhari 1000, Muslim 2085)"
"38746","(38746) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Kharshi ibn al-Hurr, who said: Omar said: The Arabs will be destroyed when The sons of the daughters of Persia reach puberty."
"38747","(38747) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The matter of the Banu has not ceased. Israel was moderate until the sons of captives of nations grew up among them, and they spoke among them according to their opinion, and they went astray and went astray. (Ibn Majah 56)"
"38748","(38748) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: A man is cut off at the beginning of the day. And the money overflows from the end, and he does not find anyone to accept it, so he sees it and says: What a pity this is, my hand was cut off. Yesterday"
"38749","(38749) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The dinar and the dirham were consumed by whoever before you, and they are yours."
"38750","(38750) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Wahhab bin Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: When the sun rises in the west, a man goes to the money as his treasure, extracts it, and carries it on his back, saying: Whoever goes astray in this regard, it will be said to him: Did you not bring him yesterday? It will not be accepted, so he will be brought to the place where He digs it up, then hits the ground with it and says: I wish I had not seen you."
"38751","(38751) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Three things that, when they go out, will not benefit a soul if it did not believe before: the rising of the sun from the west. And the Antichrist and the beast. (Muslim 138. Ahmad 445)"
"38752","(38752) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa`id {On the Day when certain signs Your Lord, there is no benefit to a soul whose faith} He said: The rising of the sun from the west. (Tirmidhi 3071, Ahmed 31)"
"38753","(38753) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The rising of the sun From its west"
"38754","(38754) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When the first of the verses came out The memory was imprisoned, the pens were thrown out, and the bodies bore witness to the deeds. (Naim bin Hammad 1819)"
"38755","(38755) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: People stay behind after sunrise. The sun is twenty and a hundred degrees from the west. (Naim bin Hammad 1849)"
"38756","(38756) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Masoud said: Everything that Allah and His Messenger promised We have seen more than four things: the sun rising from the west, the Dajjal, the beast, Gog and Magog."
"38757","(38757) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A time will come upon the people. The perfect camel is dearer to any of you than his family and wealth. (Abdul Razzaq 18250)"
"38758","(38758) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Abu {Say: He is the One who is capable of That He might send upon you a torment from above you or beneath your feet, or that He might divide you into sects and make some of you taste violence. Some} said: There are four times, and all of them will happen inevitably, so two happened after the death of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In twenty-five years, they were divided into sects, and some of them tasted the violence of one another, and two inevitable events happened: ecstasy and stoning.\n(Ahmad 134. Ibn Jarir 222)"
"38759","(38759) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplication: O God, I seek refuge in You from being assassinated. From beneath me, meaning the eclipse."
"38760","(38760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibn Al-Bilamani, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The beast comes out on a Friday night while the people are walking to Mina, and it carries them between Because of her incapacity and her sin, there will not remain a hypocrite but she will attack him. He said: And the believer will be anointed. He said: Then they will wake up and they are worse than the Antichrist. (Naim bin Hammad 1865)"
"38761","(38761) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: An animal of the earth emerges from Mecca."
"38762","(38762) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Aisha said: The animal. It comes from Ajyad."
"38763","(38763) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ali bin Jud’an, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The animal will emerge from Mount Ajjad in the days of Tashreeq, while the people are at Mina. He said: For this reason the pilgrim greets himself when he comes. In the safety of people."
"38764","(38764) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Aisha said: When the first verse appears, the pens are raised. And the bodies witnessed the deeds and were preserved."
"38765","(38765) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Hafsiya, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: What Between the first and last verses are six months, successive as beads in a system."
"38766","(38766) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: There are eight months between the first and last verses."
"38767","(38767) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr informed us, on the authority of Al-Sumait bin Umayr, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: It is as if, at the entrance of the one-eyed Antichrist, you will be met by a thousand Arabs wearing fencing, and it will increase my belief in what I see them revealing. From us"
"38768","(38768) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: It was said to Hudhaifa: Shall we not order With what is right and forbidding what is wrong, he said: It is good, but it is not from the Sunnah to raise a weapon against your imam. (Naim bin Hammad 388)"
"38769","(38769) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr, He said: I was a proud, hot-headed man, and no one was independent from me, whether the Sultan or anyone else. He said: So I became my prince. They give me a choice between me being patient with them despite the ugliness of my face, despite my disdain, or taking my sword and striking with it. So he entered the Fire, and I chose to be patient with the ugliness of my face and despite my nose, and not take my sword and strike and enter the Fire."
"38770","(38770) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, that Abu Masoud left the The cup was dripping on his head and he wanted to enter ihram, so they said to him: Hosanna, so he said: O people, come to the opinion. You saw me intending to strike with my sword in disobedience to God and disobedience to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Hosanna. He said: You must unite, for God would not have united the mother of Muhammad upon his misguidance. They said: They said: Hosanna. He said: By fear of God and patience until a righteous person is relieved, or he is relieved from an immoral person."
"38771","(38771) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaid informed us, he said: Zayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn informed me. Abu Salamah Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabbab and a companion of his, that they heard Abu Dharr calling, and he said: So we said to him: We saw you. You prayed in this country a prayer that we have never seen longer, standing, bowing, and prostrating. When you finished, you raised your hands and prayed and sought refuge from The day of calamity and the day of calamity. He said: So as long as you deny it, inform us of it. He said: As for the day of calamity, two groups of people will meet. Muslims, and they kill one another, and on the Day of nakedness, Muslim women will be taken captive, and their buttocks will be uncovered. So I had the greatest leg ever bought for the bone of my two legs, so I prayed that this time would not overtake me, and that perhaps you would overtake me. He said: So Othman was killed, and Muawiyah bin Abi Arta was sent to Yemen and took captive Muslim women, so they lived in the market."
"38772","(38772) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: When a person appears The truth is against the people of falsehood, so it is not a temptation."
"38773","(38773) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Hasira, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: It was said to Hudhayf : What are the stops of temptation, and what are its resurrections? He said: Its resurrections are the unsheath of the sword and its stops are its sheath."
"38774","(38774) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, He met him and mentioned the temptation, so he said: This temptation is one of the first tribulations of temptation, and verily, it remains the ruin. Al-Mutabbaqa, whoever honors her, she honors him, and whoever treats her, she will honor him. (Naim bin Hammad 106)"
"38775","(38775) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah said to him Ibn Amr: From whom are you? I said: from the people of Kufa. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will be driven from there to the land of the Arabs. You own a qafiz or a dirham, but he will not save you."
"38776","(38776) 6 A lecturer narrated to us, saying: Al-Ajlah narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, he said: I heard Hudhayfah says: If the Antichrist came, people would believe in him in their graves."
"38777","(38777) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Bashir bin Jarir Al-Bajlili, he said: Ali said: The last outsider to come out of Islam in Ramila is Ramila of Al-Daskara, so he will come out. People come to them, and they kill a third of them, and a third enter, and a third barricade themselves in the monastery, the Monastery of Marmari. Some of them are Al-Ashmat, So the people besiege them and bring them down and kill them, so they are the last ones to leave you as part of Islam."
"38778","(38778) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Rashid Al-Azraq, on the authority of Uqba bin Nafi’, He said: I asked Ibn Umar: With whom should I fight? He said: With those who fight for God, and do not fight with those who fight for this dinar. And the dirhams."
"38779","(38779) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam al-Mala’i narrated to us, saying: He narrated to me and Bara, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: No. You will see relief until four people rule, all of whom are from the lineage of one man. If that happens, then it will be possible."
"38780","(38780) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Amr, he said: The first place on earth to be devastated is the Levant."
"38781","(38781) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Abu Sadiq narrating, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Najid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: A people will come to you from the East, with small faces and small eyes, as if their eyes had been pierced. In the rock, it is as if their faces are hammered shields, until they tie their horses to the shore of the Euphrates."
"38782","(38782) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Huraira says: Woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has approached. They have cast shadows, and by God, they are quicker to attack them than the fast-moving horse. The deaf and suspicious temptation in which a man wakes up in the morning with a matter and in the evening with a matter. The one who sits in it is better than the one who stands. The one who stands in it is better than the walker, and the one who walks in it is better than the one who runs, and if I were to tell you everything I know, you would slit my neck. From here, and he incised the back of his neck with the letter kaffa, O God, do not overtake me. Abu Huraira is the wife of the boys, and he raised his hand until he made Their backs are from what is next to the inside of the palm."
"38783","(38783) Shababā told us, he said: Suleiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: A time will come upon the people when you will find The women saw a sandal lying on the road, and they said to one another: This sandal was a man’s mirror."
"38784","(38784) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla used to exhort people. The days of skulls."
"38785","(38785) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Isa al-Saadi, on the authority of a man who wrote to my father. Al-Bakhtari asked him about his place in the days of the skulls. He said: Then Abu Al-Bakhtari wrote to him: Who? Whatever he said about us, if I knew something better than what I am about, I would have done it."
"38786","(38786) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Karim, who said: Talha bin Musrif heard me one day while I was He laughed and said: You are laughing like a man who has never seen skulls."
"38787","(38787) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Habib Al-Tamar, who said: I heard Zazan saying: I wished that the blood of the people of Syria was in A garment, and he pointed to his garment, meaning in his garment, or he said: in my lap."
"38788","(38788) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim and Khaythamah, that they were forced to Skulls"
"38789","(38789) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, that he saw a defeated man. In the days of the skulls, he said: The heat of fire is more severe than the heat of the sword."
"38790","(38790) Qabisa told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated skulls."
"38791","(38791) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, he said: Amir told us, he said: Fatimah ibn Qays told me, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day with the Hijra and praying. She said: Then he went up to the pulpit and the people got up. He said: O people, sit down, for I did not stand in this place of yours out of desire or fear, and that is why he ascended the pulpit. During the hour, he was not going up during it, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and informed me of news that prevented me from taking a nap. Joy and comfort to the eyes, so I wanted to spread to you the news of Tamim.\n2. They told me that a group of his cousins were sailing by sea and a gust of wind struck them, so they took refuge in an island. They recognized it, so they sat in the boats of the ship until they went out to the island, and they saw something black and very scarred. Poetry, they did not know whether it was a man or a woman. They said: Won’t you tell us? He said: I will not inform you, nor will I inform you of anything, but this is the monastery that you have penetrated, so there is in it whoever is there. He informed you of longings, and until he informed you and informed you, they said: What are you? She said: I am Al-Jasassah.\n3. So they set off until they came to the monastery, and they asked permission, and he gave them permission. Then, behold, they found an old man, bound and strong, with an expression of great sadness. complaining,So they greeted him, and he returned the greeting and said: Where did you come from? They said: From the Levant. He said: Who are you from? They said: Who are the Arabs? He said: What did the Arabs do? Their Prophet has not yet come out. They said: Yes. He said: So what did they do? They said: A people resorted to him and God made him prevail over them, so today they are all together. He said: That is better, and he mentioned about him: Believe in him. And they followed him and believed him. He said, “That is better for them.” He said: “The Arabs today are one god and their word is one.” They said: Yes, he said: That is better for them.\n4. He said: What did the spring of Zaghr do? They said: It is good, and its people drink from it and water their crops. He said: What did the palm trees between Amman and Baisan do? They said: He feeds his jinn every year. He said: What did you do with Lake al-Tabariyya? They said: Its sides were filled with flowing water from the abundance of water. He said: He exhaled, then exhaled, then exhaled, then he swore, and said: If only I had escaped, or had come out. Of my bonds like this, or my place like this, I have not left any land except that I stepped on it with my feet other than my medicine, not for me. There is no way or authority over her.\n5. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is the end of my joy, this is my goodness, and this is the soul of Muhammad. In his hand, this is pure, and God has forbidden what he has forbidden for the Antichrist to enter it.Then he swore: It has no narrow road nor wide road in a plain or a mountain except over it an angel brandishing the sword until the Day of Judgment. Resurrection, the Antichrist will not be able to enter upon its people.\n6. Mujalid said: Then Amer told me, he said: I mentioned this hadith to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and he said: Al-Qasim: I bear witness to Aisha. She told me this hadith differently, saying: Deprivation is forbidden to him: Mecca and Medina.\n7. Amer said: I met Al-Muharrar bin Abi Hurairah and narrated to him the hadith of Aisha, and he said: I bear witness to my father that he narrated to me. As Aisha told you, not a single letter was omitted except that my father added one chapter to it. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, omitted He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, turned toward the east with his hand, so he went to shelter close to it twenty times."
"38792","(38792) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salma bin Kuhayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, On the authority of Abdullah, that the Antichrist was mentioned in his presence, and Abdullah said: O people, you will split into three groups when he emerges. They will pursue you, and a group will join the land of their fathers in the springs of wormwood, and a group will take the shore of this Euphrates and fight them. And they will fight it until the believers gather in the west of the Levant and they send to it a vanguard, among them a knight riding a blond horse, or A wild horse, and they will be killed, and not a human being will return from them.\n2. Salamah said: Abu Sadiq told me, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Najid, that Abdullah, he said, was a blond mare.\n3. Then Abdullah said: The People of the Book claim that the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, will descend and kill him. Abu Al-Za’ara’ said: What I heard Abdullah mention a hadith other than this on the authority of the People of the Book.\n4. He said: Then Gog and Magog will come out, and they will rejoice in the land and make mischief therein. Then Abdullah recited: {And they will come from every direction. They will descend} He said: Then God will send upon them an animal like this nag, and it will snow in their ears and nostrils and they will die. From there, he said: The earth will be tempted by them, so he will turn to God, and He will send water on them, and God will purify the land of them.Then he said: God will send a cold, roaring wind, so do not leave a believer on the ground unless that wind suffices him. He said: Then you will rise. The one who seeks the worst of people.\n5. He said: Then an angel will stand between the heavens and the earth with the trumpet and blow into it. He said: And the trumpet is a horn. He said: There will not remain any creation of God in the heavens. And there is no one on earth except that he dies except as your Lord wills. He said: Then between the two blowings there will be whatever God wills it to be. He said: Then he will sprinkle. God came from under the throne like a man from under the throne. He said: There is no creation of the son of Adam on earth except something from Him. He said: Then their bodies will grow. And their protection from that water will be as the earth grows from the earth. Then Abdullah recited: {And Allah is the One who sends the winds and they raise the clouds. So We drove him to a dead land, and therewith We revived the earth after its death. Thus is the Resurrection.}\n6. He said: Then an angel will stand between the heavens and the earth with the trumpet and blow into it. He said: Then every soul will go into its body and enter In it, he said: Then they will rise and greet the life of one man standing for the Lord of the worlds. \n7. Then God appears to the creation and meets them. There is not one of the creation who worships anything besides God except that it is raised up to Him. He follows him and meets the Jews and says: Who do you worship? They say: We worship Uzair.He says: Does the water make you happy? They said: Yes. He said: He showed them Hell, and it was like a mirage. Then Abdullah recited. : (And We will expose Hell that day to the disbelievers as a display.)\n8. Then he meets the Christians and says: Who do you worship? They said: We worship Christ. He said: He says: Does water make you happy? They said: Yes. So he showed them Hell, like a mirage. He said: Then likewise for whoever worships anything besides God. Then Abdullah recited: “Stop them. Indeed, they will be questioned.”\n9. Until Muslims pass by and say: Who do you worship? They say: We worship God and do not associate anything with Him. He said: Then he says: Oh Do you know your Lord? And they say: Glory be to Him, when He confesses to us, we will recognize Him. He said: Then a leg will be revealed, and no one will remain but bows down to God. prostrating, and the hypocrites left their backs on a single platform as if there were footsteps in it. He said: Then they say: You were being called. To prostrate while you are safe.\n10. And God commands the path, and Hell is set upon it. He said: Then the people will pass by in groups according to their deeds, the first of them like a flash of lightning. Then the wind is like the wind, then the bird is like the fastest of animals, then like that until a man passes in haste, and until he passes The man is walking, and until the last of them is a man rolling over his stomach,He says: You made me slow. He says: I was not slow, but your work made you slow.\n11 He said: Then God permits intercession, and the first intercessor on the Day of Resurrection will be the Holy Spirit Gabriel, then Abraham Khalil. The Most Gracious, then Moses, or Jesus, I do not know, Moses, or Jesus, then your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, will arise fourthly. No one will intercede after him for what he interceded for, and it is the Praiseworthy Place of which God mentioned: {Perhaps your Lord will send you to a place Praiseworthy} There is not a soul but that it looks at a house of Hell, or a house in Paradise, and it is the Day of Sorrow, and sees it. The dwellers of Hell are the house that is in Paradise. It will be said: If you did so, then grief will seize them. And the dwellers of Paradise will see the House that is In Paradise, they say: {Had it not been that God has bestowed upon us, we would have been swallowed up}"
"38793","(38793) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be a Mahdi among my nation if his life is long. Or his life is shortened, he will reign for seven years, or eight years, or nine years, and he will fill it with justice and justice as it was filled. Unjustly, and the heavens will rain their rain, and the earth will bring forth its blessing. He said: And my nation will live in its time a life that it had not experienced before. That\n(Tirmidhi 2232. Ahmed 21)"
"38794","(38794) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: A man from my family will emerge at the end of time and the emergence of temptations, and his giving will be urgent. (Ahmed 80. Naeem bin Hammad 1056)"
"38795","(38795) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: At the end of time, a caliph will emerge who will be given the truth without number. (Muslim 2235)"
"38796","(38796) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The days and nights do not pass by. Until there comes from among us, the Ahl al-Bayt, a young man who has not been afflicted by temptation nor has he been tempted by it. He said: We said, O Abu Abbas, your old age will fail against it, but your youth will attain it? He said: It is the command of God. He gives it to whomever He wishes."
"38797","(38797) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, who heard it from Misra ibn Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: There are three of us: among us is the Saffah, among us is the Mansur, and among us is the Mahdi. (Bayhaqi 514)"
"38798","(38798) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dani, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: O people of Kufa, you are the happiest people with the Mahdi."
"38799","(38799) Al-Fadl bin Dukain and Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Yasin Al-Ijli, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin The Hanafi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: The Mahdi is from among us, the People of the House May God bless him on this night. (Ibn Majah 4085. Abu Ali 461)"
"38800","(38800) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yasin, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali like him, but there was no He raises it."
"38801","(38801) Al-Walid bin Utbah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said, Al-Mahdi Issa Ibn Maryam"
"38802","(38802) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The world will not pass away until God sends a man from my family whose name is like my name and my name. Abiyah is the name of my father. (Abu Dawud 4281)"
"38803","(38803) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If only a day had remained of eternity, God would have sent a man from the people of My house will be filled with justice as it was filled with injustice. (Abu Dawud 4282. Ahmed 99)"
"38804","(38804) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Mahdi is from these nations, and he is the one Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon them, will lead the prayer."
"38805","(38805) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There will be in this nation a caliph who will not be preferred. Abu Bakr or Omar. (Ibn Adi 2433)"
"38806","(38806) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Imran ibn Dhabyan, on the authority of Hakim ibn Sa’d, who said: When Sulaiman stood up and showed what he had shown. I said to Abu Tahyah: This is the Mahdi who is being mentioned. He said: No, not even the one who wears clothes."
"38807","(38807) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, who said: I said to Tawus: Omar. Bin Abdul Aziz Al Mahdi? He said: He was a Mahdi but he is not with him. If the Mahdi is, the doer of good will be increased in his good deeds, and he will repent from the wrongdoer. He mistreats him, and he wastes money, and is harsh with workers, and has mercy on the poor."
"38808","(38808) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Musa al-Janni told us, he said: Omar bin Qais al-Masir told me, he said: Mujahid told me, he said: So-and-so, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that the Mahdi will not come out. Until the pure soul is killed, then when the pure soul is killed, whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth becomes angry with them, so the people come. Al-Mahdi, so they celebrated him as a bride is accompanied to her husband on her wedding night, and he will fill the earth with justice and justice. And the earth will bring forth its vegetation, and the sky will rain its rain, and his nation will be blessed with blessings that it had never been blessed with during his rule."
"38809","(38809) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Wathhab informed me and he was among those who realized that he was freed. The Commander of the Faithful, Omar, was in front of Othman. He said: I saw two stab wounds in his throat, as if they were Two things were stabbed on the day of the house, the house of Othman. He said: The Commander of the Faithful, Othman, sent me and said: Call Al-Ashtar, and he came. Ibn Aoun: I think so. He said: So it was presented to the Commander of the Faithful and his master and his master, and he said: O Ashtar, what the people want from me. He said: Three There is no choice between any of them. They give you a choice between you taking over their affairs, and you say: This is your command, so choose someone for him. Whatever you wish, be sure that you will not be able to retaliate against yourself, but if you refuse to bring them, then the people will kill you. He said: None of them will escape. He said: There is no need for one of them, so he said: As for me taking off their garments for them, I would never take off for them a garment that God has worn for me. Ibn Aoun said: And someone other than Al-Hasan said: To be brought forward and be beheaded is more beloved to me than to have Muhammad’s mother remove parts of her over another, and he said Ibn Aoun: This is similar to what he said, but as for me telling them something from myself, by God, I know that my companions are among My hands used to retaliate on their own, and my body cannot retaliate, but if they kill me, then by God, if they kill me, They will never love one another after me, and they will never fight an enemy together after me. So Al-Ashtar got up and set off. We stayed and said: Perhaps the people. Then A man came as if he were a wolf. He left the door, then came back. Then Muhammad bin Abi Bakr came with thirteen men. Until he came to Othman and took hold of his beard, and touched it until I heard the knocking of his molars, and said: What is of no use to you? Mu'awiyah, Ibn Amir is of no use to you, your books are of no use to you, so he said: Send me my beard, O son of my brother. Send me my beard, my brother. He said: I saw him antagonizing a man from among the people and helping him, so he went to him with a mask until he came back. With it in his head and it was fixed, then what? He said: Then they entered upon him, by God, until they killed him."
"38810","(38810) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Rabi’ ibn Yazid narrated to me. Al-Dimashqi, he said: Abdullah bin Qais told us that he heard Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: No I will tell you about a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was sent to Othman and he called him and he came to him. So I heard him say: O Uthman, God may give you a shirt, but if they want you to take it off, do not take it off three times. So I said: O Mother of the Believers, where have you been regarding this hadith? She said: I have forgotten it as if I had not heard it."
"38811","(38811) Affan told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Ali bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told me, he said: Othman said to me while he was confined in the house: What do you say regarding what Al-Mughirah bin advised me? Al-Akhnas, he said: I said: And what he indicated against you, he said: These people want to depose me, so if I depose, they will leave me, and if not They killed me. They said: I said: Have you seen that if I were to be deposed, the Turks would remain eternally in this world? They said: I said: Will they be the owners of Paradise and Hell? He said: No. I said: Have you seen that if you do not remove yourselves, they will kill you more? He said: No. I said: Have you seen that you should enact this Sunnah in this year? Islam: Whenever a people becomes angry with a leader, they remove him, but do not take off a shirt that God has made for you. (Ibn Saad 66)"
"38812","(38812) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Sahlă narrated to me, that Uthman said on the day of the abode: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with me, and I will be patient with him. He said: They saw that it was that. Today"
"38813","(38813) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, who said: I heard Abu Layla al-Kindi say: I saw Othman looking at the people while he was besieged, and he said: O people, do not kill me but take me to prison. By God, if You killed me, you will never fight all of you, and you will never fight an enemy, and you will disagree until you become like this, and there will be clashes between His fingers: {And, O my people, do not let my discord against me cause you to be harmed like what befell the people of Noah, or the people of Jews, or the people of righteous, and the people of Lot are not far from you.} He said: And he sent to Abdullah bin Salam and asked him, and he said: Stop, stop, for it is I will inform you of the Hajj, so they entered upon him and killed him."
"38814","(38814) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: Othman supervised them from The palace, and he said: Bring me a man to whom I will recite the Book of God. So they brought to him Sa`sa` bin Suhan, who was a young man, and he said: You did not find anyone. Do you come to me other than this young man? He said: Then Sa`sa`` bin Suhan spoke some words, and Othman said to him: Recite, and Sa`````a said: {The call to prayer. For those who fight because they have been wronged, and indeed, God is able to grant them victory.} Then he said: It is not for you nor for your companions, but for us. And to my companions, then Othman recited: {Permission has been given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and indeed, God has power to help them} until he reached {And to God is the end of affairs}"
"38815","(38815) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abu Salih told us, he said: Abdullah bin Salam said: When Uthman was besieged At home, he said: Do not kill him, for only a few lives are left for him, and by God, if you kill him, you will never pray together."
"38816","(38816) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, he said: I heard Othman He says: The greatest of you who sings before me is the one who restrains his weapons and his hands."
"38817","(38817) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I said to Uthman on the day of the house: Get out. So fight them, for there are with you those whom God has helped with less than Him, and by God, fighting them is permissible. He said: But he refused, and said: Whoever has He must listen and obey, so let him obey Abdullah bin Al-Zubair. His command at that time was in charge of the house, and he was fasting on that day."
"38818","(38818) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Abi Imran, he said: Abu Al-Afour narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Mawla. Ibn Masoud said: Abdullah said: By God, if they kill Othman, they will not obtain a successor from him."
"38819","(38819) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit came to Uthman and said: These are the Ansar at the door. They said: If you wish for us to be supporters of Allah twice. He said: As for fighting, then no."
"38820","(38820) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, he said: You have seen me. Omar and his sister pledged their trust in Islam, and if he rejected any of what you did to Othman, it would have been true."
"38821","(38821) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Samak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Qanan Aba Muhammad from Bani Amer bin Dhull, he said: Othman supervised us from a window while he was confined, and said: Are you the son of Mahdooj? They were not there. Then, they were sleeping, and they were woken up, and Othman said to them: I remind you of God. Do you not know that Omar? He only said: He is an immoral person, or a treacherous one. Indeed, by God, I will not make their obligatory duties the obligatory duties of a people who came from a month’s journey and he immigrated. One of them was at his tent, then one morning I added five hundred to them, until I joined them. They said: Yes, He said: I remind you, by God, do you not know that you came to me and said: Indeed, his kind is the food of his head, and that his spring is his. The head, and that Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays had eaten them, so I took them off and used them as yours. They said: Yes, he said: Oh God, if they disbelieved. And they changed My favor, but you will not be satisfied with an imam, and you will not be satisfied with an imam for them."
"38822","(38822) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Hamid ibn Hilal, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Jundub Goodness, he said: We came to Hudhayfy when the Egyptians marched to Othman, and we said: These people marched to this man, but what You say: He said: They will kill him, by God. He said: We said: Where is he? He said: In Paradise, by God. He said: We said: Where did you kill him? He said: In Hell, by God."
"38823","(38823) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Hamid Abi Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Al-Dhail, he said, when the killing of Othman came, Hudhayfy said: Today the people descended upon the barefoot of Islam, so how many stages have there been? They departed from him. He said: Ibn Abi al-Dhail said: By God, these people have gone far from their intended goal, to the point that And between them there is rough terrain, to which they will not find guidance, nor will they recognize it."
"38824","(38824) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wa’il Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Khaled Al-Absi, on the authority of Hudhayfă mentioned Uthman and said: Oh God, I did not kill, nor did I command, nor did I approve."
"38825","(38825) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, he said: When Ali walked to Siffin He appointed Abu Masoud as his successor over the people, and he addressed them on the day of Friday. He saw that there were few of them, so he said: O people, come out, and who? He went out and was safe. By God, we know that among you hates this matter and is burdensome about it, so go out. Whoever goes out is safe. By God, we do not consider it to be healthy if these two caves meet so that one of them should fear his companion, but we consider it to be healthy if May God reconcile the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and gather her affection. Shall I not tell you about Othman, and what the people resented him? They will not leave him and his sin until it is God who chastises him or pardons him, and they will not realize that. They sought Him, because they envied what God had given them.\n2. When Ali came, he said to him: You are the one who said, “I have not heard anything about you, O Farrukh. You are old and your mind has lost.” He said: You have poisoned me. My mother, with a name better than this, has melted my mind, and the Garden has been guaranteed for me from God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, you know him, and what was left of my mind, we were talking about the other being evil, then the other was evil, then he left, and when it was... With the two swords or with the Qadisiyah, he came out to them with his hair dripping with tar, and they saw that he had prepared for the ihram, so when he put His feet were in stitches and he was holding the back of his saddlebag. Some people came up to him and said to him: If only you would come back to us, O Abu. Masoud, he said: You must fear God and the community, for God will not unite the nation of Muhammad against his misguidance. He said: So they returned against him. He said: You must fear God and the community, for only a righteous man will find relief, or he will be relieved from an immoral person."
"38826","(38826) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali said: What I killed, meaning Othman, nor did I command three, but I was defeated."
"38827","(38827) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali said: I did not kill him, and if I were to kill him, I would have hated him."
"38828","(38828) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Zurara and Abu Abdullah, who said: We heard Ali say: By God, I did not participate, nor did I kill, nor did I command, nor did I approve, meaning the killing of Uthman. (Naim bin Hammad 452, Saeed bin Mansour 2941)"
"38829","(38829) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: Husayn, a man from Banu Al-Harith narrated to me, He said: Your concubine Zayd bin Arqam told me, she said: Ali came to ‘Awd Zayd bin Arqam, and the people were with him, so he said to the people: Listen and be silent, for by God, you will not ask me anything today unless I tell you about it. Then Zaid said to him: I seek refuge in God. You killed Othman, so he knocked down an hour, then said: By the one who separated the love and healed the breeze, I did not kill him nor did I order him to be killed, and I did not SAYINIAH\n(Hakim 106)"
"38830","(38830) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mundhir ibn Ali, who said: It was the day they wanted to kill Uthman. Marwan asked Ali: “Don’t you come to this man and prevent him, for they have not concluded a matter without you.” Ali said: We will bring them. He said: Then Ibn al-Hanafi took him by the shoulders and embraced him, and said: O father, where are you going, by God? They will not add anything to you except a rabble. So Ali sent to them with his turban and forbade them from doing so."
"38831","(38831) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Ansari, who said: I entered with The Egyptians attacked Othman, and when they beat him, I went out, full of aggression, until I entered the mosque, and saw a man sitting in the About ten people wearing a black turban. He said: Woe to you, what is behind you? He said: I said, by God, he has finished with the man. He said: So he said: Damn it. May the end of eternity be yours. He said: I looked, and behold, it was Ali. (Saeed bin Mansour 2939)"
"38832","(38832) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, who said: When Othman was besieged Ali Talhah came while he was leaning on the cushions in his house and said: I adjure you by God, when you turned the people away from Amir. Believers, then he will be killed. Talha said: No, by God, until you give the Umayyads the right from themselves."
"38833","(38833) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: They blamed Uthman for tearing up the Qur’an. And they believed in what was written for them."
"38834","(38834) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Ali spoke to Ali with his sight, and he said: By God, I did not kill him, nor did I kill him. She hoped to kill him, and when he came down, some of his companions said to him: What have you done now that will cause your companions to disperse from you? So when he returned to... The pulpit, he said: Whoever asks about the blood of Othman, God has killed him and I am with him. Muhammad said: This is a Quraysh speech with the same meaning. face (Tabarani 113)"
"38835","(38835) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Al-Ala’ ibn Ubaid Allah ibn Rafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Maymun, he said: When Uthman was killed, Hudhayf said thus and waved his hand, and said: There was a hernia in Islam, a hernia that cannot be repaired. Mountain"
"38836","(38836) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Thawri told us, he said: Aslam Al-Manqari told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman. Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: When whatever happened regarding the matter of Uthman, and the people spoke about his matter, I went to Ubayy ibn Ka’b. So I said to him: Aba Al-Mundhir, what is the way out? He said: The Book of God. He said: Whatever of it has been made clear to you, work with it and benefit from it, and whatever He suspects something about you, so believe in him and leave it all to his scholar. (Hakim 303)"
"38837","(38837) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja’i, on the authority of Sakhr ibn Al-Walid, on the authority of Juzzi bin Bukair Al-Absi, said: Hudhayfah came to Uthman to bid him farewell, or to greet him, and when He turned back, he said: Return him, and when he came, he said: I have not heard anything about you in the past, so he said: By God, I have never hated you since I loved you. Nor have I cheated on you since I advised you. He said, “You are more truthful and more righteous than them.” He departed. When he turned back, he said, “Return him.” He said, “I did not hear from him.” About you, apparently unseen, and he said: It is in his hand like this. He did not inform me of you, apparently unseen, yes, by God. You will be slaughtered like a bull, then you will be slaughtered like the slaughter of a camel. He said: Then he took some of that from that, so he sent for Mu’awiyah, and he came. He said: Do you know what Hudhayfy said? He said: By God, you will be slaughtered like a bull and slaughtered like a camel. He said: Bury her, bury her. (Daraqutni 490)"
"38838","(38838) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Salam bin Miskin told us, he said: Tell me who saw Abdullah bin Peace, on the day Othman was killed, he cried and said: Today the Arabs have been destroyed."
"38839","(38839) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that people They were at Aisha’s tent, and Othman passed by them. This was seen in Mecca. Abu Sa’id said: Not one of them remained except Someone else cursed him, or cursed him, and there was a man among them from the people of Kufa, so Othman Ali Al-Kufa was more daring than him. Someone else, so he said: O Kufa, do you curse me? He approached the city, as if he was approaching it. He said: So he approached the city, and it was said to him: You have to kill him, so he set off with him. Until Othman came, and Othman said: By God, I will flog you a hundred, he said: Then Talha said: By God, do not flog him a hundred unless He is an adulterer. He said: I will deprive you of your giving. He said: Then Talhah said: Indeed, God will provide for him."
"38840","(38840) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih narrating, on the authority of Suhayb, the servant of Al-Abbas, said: Al-Abbas sent me to Othman to invite him. He said: So I came to him, and behold, he was feeding the people. So I called him, and he came to him, and said: The face of Abu al-Fadl was successful. He said: And the face of the Commander of the Faithful was yours. He said: I did not do anything more if he came to me. Your Messenger, I was feeding the people lunch, so I fed them, then I came, and Al-Abbas said: I remind you of God about Ali, for he is your cousin. And your brother in your religion and your companion with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and your guardian, and it has reached me that you want to You stand up for Ali and his companions, so spare me that, O Commander of the Faithful. Then Othman said: The first thing I answered you was that I had interceded for you. If Ali had wished, no one would have been beside him, but he refused unless he saw him, and he sent to Ali and said to him, “I remind you of God in Your cousin, your paternal aunt’s son, your brother in your religion, your companion with the Messenger of God, and my guardian, I pledged allegiance to you. He said: By God, if only He commanded me to leave my house, I would have gone out, but as for me being forced to do so that the Book of God would not be kept, I would not have done it,” said Muhammad ibn Ja’far. : I have heard it countless times and presented it to him more than once."
"38841","(38841) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us on the authority of Qais, he said: When Muawiyah and Amr al-Kufa came, he came Al-Harith ibn Al-Azma’ was alive, then Amr came out while he was riding, and Al-Harith said to him: I came about a matter. If I had found you at a decision, I would have asked you. Amr said: You would not have asked me about anything while I was deciding unless I told you about it now. He said: So tell me about Ali. And Othman, he said: So he said: Discontent and anger came together, so anger prevailed over anger, then he walked on."
"38842","(38842) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: He narrated to us as a whisper, he said: Abdullah bin Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: Al-Aqra’ narrated to me, He said: Omar sent to the bishop, and he said: He is asking him while I am standing over them to shade them from the sun, so he said to him: Will you find us there? Your book. He said: Your description and your deeds. He said: Why do you find me? He said: I find you to be an iron horn. He said: Then Omar blushed on his face and said: An iron horn. Amin Shadid said. He said: It is as if he was happy with that. He said: What will you find after me? His successor is truthful and has an influence. His closest relative, he said, Omar said: May God have mercy on Ibn Affan, he said: What will you find after him, he said: an iron crack, he said: And in Omar’s hand Something that upset him. He said: So he rejected it, and said: O Dafra’, twice or three times, so he said: Do not say that, O Amir. The believers, for he is a Muslim caliph and a righteous man, but he will be appointed successor with the sword drawn and blood spilled. He said: Then he turned to me. And he said: Prayer."
"38843","(38843) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Al-Haytham, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of His father, he said: Do not draw your swords, for if you draw them, they will not be sheathed until the Day of Resurrection, and he said: Wait for me eighteen. It means the day of Othman."
"38844","(38844) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, who said: Ka’b said: It is as if I am looking at this man and in his hands are two flames of fire, meaning he fought Uthman and killed him."
"38845","(38845) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman Al-Taymi narrated to me, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Nadhrah narrated to us. On the authority of Abu Sa`id, the client of Abu Usayd al-Ansari, he said: Uthman heard that a delegation of the people of Egypt had arrived, so he received them. So he was in a village outside the city, or as he said: he said: when they heard about him, they went towards him to the place where While he was in it, he said: I see it, he said: He hated that they should come to Medina, or something like that, so they came to him and said: Call for the Qur’an, so he called for the Qur’an and they said: Open the seventh, and they called Surah Yunus the seventh, so he recited it until he came. According to these verses: {Say, “Have you seen what Allah has sent down to you of provision, and you have made of it unlawful and lawful?” Say, “Have Allah given you permission or Is it against God that you invent? They said: Have you seen the fever that you have protected? Has God permitted it to you or is it against God that you are inventing? So he said: Pass it. It was revealed. In such-and-such, and as for Hima, the age of Hima’s mother-in-law before me was for the camels of charity, so when I took office, the camels of charity increased, so I increased in Al-Hama when he increased the number of al-Sadaqah’s camels, so they began to seize him with the verse, and he said: “He passed it, it was revealed about such-and-such.”\n2. And what follows the words of Othman about your age at that time, Abu Nadhri says: Abu Sa’id tells me that,Abu Nadhrah said: I was at your age at that time. He said: And my face did not appear, or my face was not level at that time, no. I know perhaps it is. He said another time: At that time, I was thirty years old.\n3. Then they took him with things that he had no way out of, so he recognized them and said: I ask forgiveness from God and repent to Him, so he said To them: whatever you want, so they took a covenant from him, he said: and I reckon it, he said: and they wrote a condition upon him, he said: and he made a covenant from him, that They shall not split a stick nor separate from a group as long as he has established his condition for them, or as they have imposed upon him.\n4. So he said to them: What do you want? They said: We want the people of Medina not to take anything as a gift, for this money is for those who fought against him. And so the old men from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, dispersed and went with him to Medina, satisfied, so he rose. So he delivered a speech and said: By God, I have never seen a better delegation than this delegation that came to me, and he said: Another: I thought that he said: From this delegation from the people of Egypt. Whoever has crops, let him join his crops, and whoever He has a udder, so let him milk. However, we have no wealth for you. This wealth is for those who fought for him.And because of these sheikhs from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, the people became angry and said: The deception of the Umayyads.\n5. Then the Egyptian delegation returned satisfied, and while they were on the road, a rider came upon them and then left them. He returns to them, then separates from them and takes them captive. They said to him: There is a matter that concerns you. He said: I am the messenger of a prince. The believers were taken to the governor of Egypt and searched him, and lo, behold, a letter was written on the tongue of Othman, upon him was his seal to the governor of Egypt. He kills them, or cuts off their hands and feet.\n6. So they approached until they came to Medina, so they came to Ali and said: Have you not seen the enemy of God, who ordered such-and-such about us, and God has His blood was lawful. Come with us to him. He said: No, by God, I will not stay with you. They said: Why did you write to us? He said: No, by God, I did not write. There is never a letter to you. He said: Then they looked at one another, then some of them said to one another: Why are you fighting, or for this reason? You became angry, and Ali set out and left the city to a village, or a village of his.\n7. So they set off until they came to Othman and said: You wrote about such-and-such about us. He said: They are only two, that you should appoint me over. Two men from the Muslims, or the right hand: By God, there is no god but Him, I neither wrote nor dictated, and you may know.The letter is written on the tongue of a man and the seal is engraved upon the ring. Then they said to him: By God, God has made your blood permissible, and it was annulled. The covenant and the covenant,\n8. He said: So they confined him in the palace, and he looked over them and said: Peace be upon you. He said: I did not hear anyone return the greeting unless he returned it. A man was within himself, and said: I adjure you by God, did you know that I bought a Roman woman with my money to seek refuge with her? He said: So I made my bribes in it like the bribes of a Muslim man. It was said: Yes, and he said: Why do you prevent me from drinking from it until I break my fast? On the water of the sea.\n9. He said: I adjure you by God, do you know that I bought such-and-such of land and added it to the mosque? It was said: Yes. He said: Do you know of any of the people who was prevented from praying there before? It was said: And I adjure you by God, have you heard the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? May God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned such-and-such and something about it, and He mentioned the details of His detailed book.\n10. He said: Then the prohibition was issued, and the people started saying: Wait, on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, and the prohibition was issued and Al-Ashtar rose, so I do not know. On that day or another day, he said: Perhaps he plotted against you and him. He said: So people trampled on him until such-and-such and such-and-such was thrown.\n11 Then he supervised them another time, admonished them and reminded them.The sermon did not take hold of them, and the people used to take the sermon to them the first time they heard it. Then when it was repeated You did not take the admonition from them.\n12 Then he opened the door and placed the Qur’an in his hands. He said: Al-Hasan told us that Muhammad bin Abi Bakr entered upon him and took With his beard, Othman said to him: You have taken a seat from me, or you have taken a seat from me that Abu Bakr would not have taken. Or for him to sit, he said: Then he went out and left him.\n13 He said: And in the hadith of Abu Sa’id: A man entered upon him and said: Between me and you is the Book of God, so he went out and left him, and he entered. A man called the Black Death came upon him, so he strangled him and strangled him, then he came out and said: By God, I have never seen anything so soft. From his throat, by God, I strangled him until I saw his soul like the soul of a jinn residing in his body.\n14 Then another came to him and said: Between me and you is the Book of God and the Qur’an is in his hands. So he turned to him with the sword. So he took it with his hand and cut it, and I do not know whether he broke it, or cut it and did not rebuild it, so he said: By God, it is the first palm. I never planned the details.\n15 It was narrated in a different hadith than Abu Sa’id: Then Al-Tajubi came to him and made him feel a mess.Then blood spread over these verses: {So Allah will suffice you for them, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.} And indeed, in the Qur’an, it has not been recorded.\n16 According to the hadith of Abu Sa’id, Bint al-Farafsiya took her jewelry and placed it in her lap, and that was before he was killed. When he sensed that he was killed, she became angry or surprised at him, and some of them said: May God kill her. How great is her infirmity. So she knew that The enemies of God only want this world. (Ahmed 766)"
"38846","(38846) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Muhsin, brother of Hammad bin Numayr, a man from the people of Wasit, narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: A man from Banu Fihr told me about Jahm, he said: I am witness to this matter, he said: Saad and Ammar came So they sent to Othman, “Come to us, for we want to mention to you the things you have done, or the things you have done.” He said: So he sent to them to tell them to leave today, for I am busy and your appointment is such-and-such day until I feel distressed. Abu Muhsin said: Ashzan: I am preparing for your opponents.\n2. He said: Saad left, but Ammar refused to leave. Abu Muhsin said it twice. He said: Then Uthman’s messenger approached him and beat him. He said: When they gathered for the appointed time and those with them, Othman said to them, “What do you take revenge on me?” They said: “We will take revenge on you because Ammar struck you.” He said: Othman said: Saad and Ammar came, so I sent for them, but Saad left, but Ammar refused to leave, so a different messenger came to him. My command, by God, I neither commanded nor was pleased with it. This is Ammar’s hand, so let him be patient. Abu Muhsin said: It means: he takes retaliation.\n3. They said: We take revenge on you because you made the letters into one letter. He said: Hudhayfah came to me, and he said: I was not a maker when it was said: So-and-so recited, so-and-so recited, so-and-so recited,Just as the People of the Book differed, if it is correct then it is from God, and if it is wrong then it is from something wrong.\n4. They said: We take revenge on you because you have a fever. He said: The Quraysh came to me and said: There is no people among the Arabs who does not have a fever. They graze on it other than us, so I did that for them. If you are satisfied, then acknowledge it, and if you dislike it, change it. Or he said: Do not acknowledge it. Abu Muhsin doubted.\n5. They said: And we take revenge on you because you used the foolish people of your relatives. He said: Let the people of all Egypt rise up and ask me who their friend is. They love him, so I will use him over them and remove from them those who hate him. He said: Then the people of Basra said: We are satisfied with Abd. God bin Amir, so he approved it to us, and the people of Kufa said: Remove Saeed, and Al-Walid said, Abu Muhsin doubted: and use On us, Abu Musa, so he did so. He said: And the people of Syria said: We are satisfied with Mu’awiyah, so he granted him permission over us. And the people of Egypt said: Remove yourself from us. Ibn Abi Sarh, and Amr ibn al-Aas applied it to us, so he did. He said: They did not bring anything but it came out of it. He said: So they left. We are satisfied\n6. While some of them were on the road, a rider passed by them, so they went to him, searched him, and took with him a letter about his treatment. Treat them like take so-and-so and so-and-so and behead them.He said: So they returned and started with Ali, so they brought him, and he came with them to Othman, and they said: This is your letter and this is your seal. Othman said: By God, I did not write, nor did I know, nor did I command. He said: Who do you think it is? Abu Muhsin said: You are being accused. He said: I think my writer is treacherous, and I think you are guilty of it, Ali. He said: Then Ali said to him: Why? Do you think that? He said: Because you are obeyed by the people. He said: Then you did not turn them away from him.\n7. He said: But the people refused and they insisted on him until they besieged him. He said: So he looked over them and said: Why do you make my blood lawful? For by God, blood is not lawful. A Muslim man, except for one of three things: an apostate, from Islam, a married adulterer, or a murderer. By God, I have not done anything. Of them since I converted to Islam. He said: The people insisted on him. He said: And Othman appealed to the people not to shed a cup of blood on him.\n8. I saw Ibn al-Zubayr going out against them in a group until he defeated them, if they wanted to kill some of them. They would have been killed. He said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Aswad bin Al-Bakhtari and he would strike a man with the breadth of a sword if he wanted to kill him. He would have killed him, but Othman was determined to attack the people, so they captured him.\n9. He said: Then Abu Amr bin Badil Al-Khuza’i and Al-Tujabibi entered upon him, and he said: One of them stabbed him in the private parts with a knife. The other attacked him with the sword and killed him.Then they set off on the run, marching by night and lying in ambush by fire until they came to a country between Egypt and the Levant. He said: So they lay in wait. Ghar, he said: Then a Nabataean came from that country with a donkey, he said: Then a fly entered the donkey’s nostril, he said: So it fled until it entered. The cave was upon them, and his companion looked for him and saw them. So he went to Mu’awiyah’s worker. He said: So he told him about them. He said: So he took them. Mu'awiyah and beheaded them."
"38847","(38847) Abdullah bin Bakr told us, he said: Hatem bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: When They mentioned the matter of Othman, which they mentioned: Abdul Rahman bin Awf came with a group of his companions until they entered upon Abdullah bin Omar, and they said: O Abu Abdul-Rahman, do you not see what this man has done? So he said: Bakh, bakh, so what do you command me? He said: Do you want to You will be like the Romans and Persians: when they became angry with a king, they killed him. God appointed him as governor, and he knows best. I am not saying anything about it. Nothing like it."
"38848","(38848) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf, who said: Abdullah bin Salam asked me about the Kharijites, and I told them: They are the people who pray the longest and fast the most, except that when they They left the bridge, shed blood and took the money. He said: Do not ask about them except that, but I have told them: Do not kill Othman. They called him, by God, if you left him eleven, they would surely die in his bed. And they did not do so, and he was not killed. No prophet was killed except that seventy thousand people were killed because of him, and no caliph was killed except that thirty-five thousand people were killed because of him."
"38849","(38849) Ali bin Hafs narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, he said: Al-Hassan bin Ali came to Othman and said: Shall I draw my sword? He said: I do not disown your blood, then, before God, but draw your sword and go back to your father."
"38850","(38850) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: We entered upon Ibn Abi Al-Dhail, and he said: They killed Uthman. Then they came to me, and we said to him: Do you make yourself confused?"
"38851","(38851) Ghandar and Abu Asama told us, saying: Shu’ab told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard him say: These are my feet. If it is in the Book of God that you put them in fetters, then put them in fetters."
"38852","(38852) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Hudhayf said when Uthman was killed: Oh God, if it were The Arabs did good by killing Othman, or righteousness, or satisfaction, for I am innocent of it, and he has no share in it, even if The Arabs had made a mistake by killing Othman, and they knew of his innocence. He said: Consider what I say to you, and by God, if it is The Arabs did the right thing by killing Othman so that they would milk milk for it, and if the Arabs were wrong in killing Othman then they would milk it. In blood (Abdul Razzaq 20965)"
"38853","(38853) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abu Dharr said to Uthman: If you command me to I cling to the handle of a camel, and I will cling to it forever until I die."
"38854","(38854) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya‘la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah He said: Ali said: If Othman had led me to Sarar, I would have listened to him and obeyed him. (Naim bin Hammad 208)"
"38855","(38855) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sidan, on the authority of Abu Dharr He said: If Othman had ordered me to walk on my head, I would have walked."
"38856","(38856) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Amr Al-Kharifi, he said: I was One of the people who came and camped at Dhu al-Marwah, so they sent us to a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his wives. We ask them: Shall we advance, or shall we return? And it is said to us: Make Ali the last one you ask. He said: So we asked them, and each of them had a command. By coming, we came to Ali and we asked him, and he said: You asked someone before me. We said: Yes, he said: So what did they tell you about him? We said: They ordered us to come. He said: But I do not order you, either no, eggs, let them hatch. (Ibn Saad 65)"
"38857","(38857) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, he said: A man from among the bricklayers narrated to me, on the authority of two sheikhs from the Banu Banu. A man and his wife, they said: We approached Al-Rabadhi, so we passed by a man with a white head and a disheveled beard, so it was said: This is one of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This man did this to you and has done so, so will you follow our opinion so we will come to you? With whatever men you want, he said: O people of Islam, do not harm me, do not humiliate the Sultan, for he is the one who humiliated the Sultan. May God humiliate him. By God, if Othman had crucified me on the longest rope, or the longest wood, I would have listened, obeyed, been patient, and sought reward. And I saw that this was better for me, and if He took me from one horizon to the next, or from the east to the west, I would have listened. And I obeyed, and was patient, and sought reward, and saw that this was better for me."
"38858","(38858) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Asim, who said: I heard Abu Wa’il say: When Uthman was killed, Abu Musa said: This temptation is a temptation that is as painful as the stomach, not knowing that we will come to it. It will come to you from your place of safety and will leave the forbearing. As if he were the son of yesterday, sever your ties of kinship and draw your spears. (Naim bin Hammad 122)"
"38859","(38859) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Zayd ibn Ali, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit was among those who cried for Uthman. The Day of Resurrection."
"38860","(38860) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Ubaidah Al-Naji told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Ansar came to Uthman. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, we will help God twice. We have helped the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we will help you. He said: No. If they had wanted to prevent him with their cloak, they would have prevented him."
"38861","(38861) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Abdullah bin Salam said when Othman was confined to the house: No. You kill him, for only a few will remain for his sake, and by God, if you kill him, you will never pray together."
"38862","(38862) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Alaa ibn al-Manyal narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Suqi narrated to me, saying: Mundhir al-Thawri narrated to me, He said: We were with Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah. He said: Some of the people approached Uthman and said: “May you die.” So we said to him: Your father used to curse. Othman, he said: He did not curse him, and if he had cursed him one day, he would have cursed him on the day I came to him, and the courier came to him, so he said: Take the courier’s letter and go. He took it to Othman, so I took it and took it to him, and he said: We have no need for it, so I came to him and informed him, and he said: He put it where it is, and if he had cursed him one day, he would have cursed him that day. (Bukhari 3111)"
"38863","(38863) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala’ ibn al-Minhal narrated to me, saying: So-and-so narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Zuhri. In Al-Rusafa, he says: By God, he advised Ali and corrected Uthman. If they had not been correct in the letter, they would have gone back."
"38864","(38864) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to me, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: I said to Al-Ashtar: I was hating the day of my death, so how did you change your mind? He said: Yes, by God. I was reluctant to stay in the house for the day, but I brought the mother of Habibah, the daughter of Abu Sufyan, to let her into the house, and I wanted to expel Othman. In a lodge, they refused to invite me and said: What have we to do with you, O Ashtar? But I saw Talhah, Al-Zubayr, and the people. They pledged allegiance to Ali willingly and not under compulsion, then they rebelled against him. I said: Ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Kill me and Malik, said: No. By God, I did not lift the sword on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, even though I saw that there was some spirit in it, because I was angry with him because he He belittled the Mother of the Believers until he drove her out, but when I met him, I was not satisfied with him. With his strength, he helped me until I was standing among the passengers. So I hit him on the head, and I saw that I had killed him, but the one who said, “Kill me and Malik” was Abd al-Rahman bin Attab bin Asid. When I met him, I embraced him, and he and I fell from our horses, and he started calling out: Kill me and my master, while the people passed by without knowing. Whoever means, and does not say: Al-Ashtar, I would have been killed."
"38865","(38865) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He took Ali by the hand of Al-Ashtar, then set off. Until he came to Talha and said: O Talha, these, meaning the people of Egypt, listen to you and obey you. Then he stopped killing Uthman, and he said: I cannot stop the blood that God wants to shed, so he took Ali by the hand of Al-Ashtar, then he left. And he says: “What a wretched thing is Ibn al-Hadramiyyah’s idea that he would kill my cousin and defeat me over my kingdom? What a wretched thing he saw.”"
"38866","(38866) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I did not know that Ali was accused. Concerning the killing of Othman until he pledged allegiance, then when he was pledged, the people accused him."
"38867","(38867) Abu Al-Mu’ri’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim informed us, on the authority of Umairah ibn Sa’d, he said: When he presented Talha, Al-Zubair, and those with them, he said: A man stood up in a gathering of people and said: I am so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, one of the Banu Jashm, and he said: Indeed, these are the people who came to you, if they were only afraid, so they came from where the birds were safe, and if it was only fear, they came from a place where the birds were safe. Because of them, Othman was killed, so they killed him, and the opinion of them is that they will be poked by their animals until they leave."
"38868","(38868) Affan told us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Uthman told us, that Uthman He was killed in the middle of the days of Tashreeq."
"38869","(38869) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sirin told us, he said: When Othman was killed, Adi bin Hatim said: Two goats should not butt heads in it. Then, on the Day of Siffin, his eye was gouged out, so it was said: No. You will gouge out while killing Othman Anzan, he said, yes, and many eyes will go out in you. (Yaqub bin Sufyan 429)"
"38870","(38870) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan Al-Azdi. He said: Omar said: How much do you have, Abu Dhabyan? He said: I said: I am in two thousand and five hundred. He said: So take a slave, for it is about to be that young men from Quraysh will come who will withhold this gift. (Bukhari 576)"
"38871","(38871) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Dhib. He says, Abu Hurairah said: By God, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry a lot. There will be killing and death in this neighborhood of Quraysh, until the mighty man comes. Abu Asama said: meaning The sandal, and he finds a sandal in it, and says: It is as if it were a Quraysh sandal. (Ibn Hibban 6853 and Ahmad 336)"
"38872","(38872) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Aamer al-Shu’abi, on the authority of Aamir. Ibn Shahr, he said: I heard a word from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and from the Negus a word. I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Look at the Quraysh and listen to what they say and ignore their actions. He said: I was with the Negus when a son of his came to him. From the book, he recited a verse from the Bible, and I understood it and laughed. He said: Who are you laughing at? Should I laugh from the Book of God? But by God, it is in the Book of God that was revealed to Jesus, that the curse will be on the earth when its rulers Boys (Ahmed 2600, Abu Dawud 3021)"
"38873","(38873) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Quraysh: This matter And you are his guardians, as long as you do not commit an act that God will remove from you. If you do that, God will make evil over you. His character is touched like a penis is touched."
"38874","(38874) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinanani, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He rose The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at a gate in which a group of Quraysh were, and he said: This matter is with Quraysh as long as they continue. They asked for mercy, they were merciful, and when they judged they were just, and when they divided they were just. Whoever among them does not do that will be cursed. God, the angels, and all mankind, no slander or justice will be accepted from Him."
"38875","(38875) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas, who said: The lord of this house, Abu Hilal, told me that he heard Abu Barzah al-Aslami narrating that they were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They heard singing and looked forward to it, so a man stood up and listened. This was before alcohol was forbidden, so he came to them, then returned. He said: This is so-and-so and so-and-so, and they are singing and one of them answers the other, and he says:\nHe is still a disciple whose bones loom as the ravages of war prevent him from going crazy and being thrown into the grave.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hand and said: Oh God, help them in the temptation, O God, support them. He called to Hell. (Bazzar 3859, Abu Ali 7399)"
"38876","(38876) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, who said: Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr narrated to me, on the authority of Al-A’sha bin Abdul-Rahman bin Mukmal, on the authority of Azhar bin Abdullah, who said: Ubadah bin Al-Samit came as a pilgrim from the Levant and came to Medina. Then Othman bin Affan came and said: O Othman, shall I not tell you something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I said: For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There will be princes over you who will command you according to what you know. And they do what you disapprove of, so they have no obligation to obey you. (Hakim 357)"
"38877","(38877) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Awdi, he said: The daughter of Maqil bin Yassar told me that her father was heavy, and this was reported to Ibn Ziyadah, so Audah came and sat down and learned about him. Death, so he said to him: O Ma’qil, won’t you speak to us, for God used to benefit us with things we hear from you? So he said: I heard the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: There is no guardian of a mother, whether small or large, who has done no justice in them except God’s wrath. He was thrown into the fire, then the other man knocked on his wrist and said: Something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or from behind him. Behind me, he said: No, but something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Whoever takes care of his flock and does not keep them advised will not smell the fragrance of the Garden, and its fragrance is found from his path. A hundred years ago, Ibn Ziyad said: Had you not told me about this before now? He said: Now, had it not been for what I am upon, I would not have told you about it."
"38878","(38878) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, that a man was walking with his sandals towards the Euphrates, and he said: How is it that when you come out you do not taste a drop of it? He said: We said: Do you think so? He said: I do not think so, but I am certain of it."
"38879","(38879) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-A’la, who said: They said: To Mutarrif: This is Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Ash'ath has come, and Mutarrif said: By God, he has come between two matters: If it appears, no debt will be established for him, and if it appears, no debt will be established against him. You will continue to be humiliated until the Day of Resurrection."
"38880","(38880) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: If only a man who was interested in Islam He recognized him, then inspected him and did not know anything about him."
"38881","(38881) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: Omar said: Whoever wants the truth, let him excrete. That means he makes his affairs apparent."
"38882","(38882) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a fatwa came from Banu Hashim, and when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw them, his eyes welled up and his color changed. He said: So I said to him: What? We still saw something on your face that we disapproved of. He said: Indeed, we are the people of the House. God has chosen the afterlife for us over this world, and the people of My Household, after me they will encounter calamity, displacement, and expulsion, until a people will come from the East with black banners. They ask for the truth, but they are not given it. So they fight and are helped, and they are given what they asked for, but they do not accept it until they pay it back. To a man from my family, and he will fill it with justice as they had filled it with injustice. Whoever of you realizes that, let him go to them. Even if they crawl on the snow. (Ibn Majah 4082 Hakim 464)"
"38883","(38883) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Mahal, who said: I said to Abu Ja`far: The Sultan is in charge of work. He said: Do not be lenient to them at all, but if you are swayed, fear God and fulfill your trusts."
"38884","(38884) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Taman, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Do not prepare a notebook for them, and do not write a letter for them. With a pen"
"38885","(38885) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: I entered upon Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad in Basra, and he He was brought with his reward for Asbaan, three thousand thousand, and it was placed in his hands. He said: O Abu Wael, what do you say? As for the one who died and left behind something like this, he said: I said: I would like to know how if it were of undeceitful things. He said: That is evil upon evil, then He said: O Abu Wael, when I present the coffee cup, come to me, perhaps I will bring you good. He said: So he presented the coffee cup, and he said: So I came. I told him, and he said: If you had come to him before you consulted me, I would not have told you anything. But if you consulted me, It is right for me to advise you, so he said: I do not like, because I have two thousand pieces of fay and I am the strongest soldier over him, and that I never afflict anything from their world unless they afflict my religion more than it."
"38886","(38886) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Salb ibn Matar Al-Ijli, on the authority of Isa Al-Muradi, on the authority of Muadh, who said: It will be in The end of this time will be immoral reciters, immoral ministers, traitorous trustees, unjust leaders, and lying princes. (Bazzar 2630)"
"38887","(38887) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Janni, on the authority of Qays bin Yazid, who said: Your lady narrated to me. Sidra, your grandfather Salma bin Qais told me, he said: I met Abu Dharr, and he said: O Salma bin Qais, three things you have memorized. Do not combine co-wives, for you will not be just, even if you are careful. And do not act according to charity, for the one who gives charity is both plus and minus. And do not deceive him. Sultan, for you do not afflict anything from their world unless they afflict you with something better than that of your religion. (Abdul Razzaq 20740)"
"38888","(38888) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ammar bin Abd, he said, Hudhayfah said: : Beware of the gates of princes, for they are the places of temptation. Indeed, temptation conceals one approaching and makes clear one where one departs."
"38889","(38889) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Hamid al-Rawasi narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Qays narrated to us. On the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, Abdul Rahman said: I think so, on the authority of Qays ibn Al-Sakan, he said: Ali said on his pulpit: Indeed, I Then I averted the eye of temptation, and if I had not been among you, so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so and the people of the river would not have been killed. By God, had it not been You rely and give up work, for I have told you what came before you on the tongue of your Prophet, for those who fought them, seeing and knowing their error. By what we are upon.\n2. He said: Then he said: Ask me, for you do not ask me about anything between you and the Messenger, nor about a group that will guide a hundred. And a hundred will go astray unless I tell you about its herald, its leader, and its driver. He said: Then a man stood up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, tell us about The Commander of the Faithful said: If a questioner asks, let him act wisely, and if a person is asked, let him be firm. Indeed, behind you are matters being accomplished with greatness, and a joyful and reconciling calamity, and the One who split the love and healed the breeze. If only you had missed me and descended. Unpleasant matters, and the facts of calamities, will cause many of those who ask to fail, and will cause many of those responsible to fall into disbelief, and that is when it is separated. Your war revealed a leg of it.The world became a test for its people until God granted victory to the group of righteous people.\n3. He said: Then a man stood up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, tell us about the temptation. He said: When the temptation approaches, it will become suspicious. And when they turn around, they spread; but temptations swirl like the flames of the winds. They strike one country and miss another, so help a people who were You were the bearers of banners on the day of Badr and on the day of Hunayn. You will be victorious and you will be rewarded. Indeed, the fear of tribulation with Me is against you, a blind tribulation. An oppressor whose temptation is limited and whose calamity is widespread. Calamity befalls whoever sees it, and calamity befalls whoever is blind to it. The people of its falsehood will prevail over the people of its truth until the earth is filled with aggression and oppression, and he will be the first to break its cover. And He will put down its might and remove its pegs. God is the Lord of the worlds.\n4. Indeed, you will find lords of evil for you after me like a sharp fang, biting with its mouth, running with its foot, and floundering. With their hand, and prevent their path, Verily, their affliction will continue with you until there remains in Egypt for you but someone beneficial to them. Or not harmful, and until none of you is helped by any of them except as if a servant is helped by his master, and God willing, if So they dispersed you under every star, so that God would gather you together for a special day for them.\n5. He said: Then a man stood up.He said: Is there a group after that, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: There is no need for a diverse group other than your gifts and your Hajj. And your journeys are the same, and hearts are so different. Then he interlaced his fingers and said: What is that about, Amir? The believers. He said: This man will kill that man. It is a terrible tribulation of the Jahiliya era, in which there is no imam for guidance and no knowledge to be seen. We, the Ahl al-Bayt, have been saved from you, and we are not your supplications. He said: And after that, O Commander of the Faithful, he said: May God relieve him. The affliction befalls a man from among us, the Ahl al-Bayt. He brings to the son of his father what he knows of, except what the eclipse destroys them and gives them water to drink. With the cup of patience, Quraysh longed for the world and all that is in it. If they were able to stand in a humble and mighty place, some of them would accept it. Show it to them today and they will turn you back, but they will not do anything except killing. (Nasa’i 8574)"
"38890","(38890) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Al-Sumait, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: For all times there have been kings, so if If God intends good for a people, He sends among them their reconcilers, and when He intends evil for a people, He sends among them their welfare."
"38891","(38891) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Abu al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Zadhan, on the authority of Alim, He said: We were with him on a roof, and with him was a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the days of the plague, and the funerals were passing by. He said: O plague, take me. He said: Then a knowledgeable person said: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say, “None of you should desire?” Death, for when his work has ceased and there is no response, he will be admonished, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Hasten to death in six ways: enjoining the foolish, making many conditions, selling judgment, disdainful of blood, and insolence. They take the Qur’an as psalms and present it to enrich them, even though the least of them has understanding. (Ahmad 494. Tabarani 61)"
"38892","(38892) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: God only made this authority A supporter of the servants of God and His religion, so how about those who commit injustice against the servants of God and treat the servants of God as detractors? They will be judged. Their blood and their property as they please, by God if anyone refrains, by God no nation has faced more temptations and humiliation after its Prophet. She met this after her Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"38893","(38893) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam: He said: A man from the People of the Book came to Umar. He said: Peace be upon you, O King of the Arabs. Omar said: And this is how you find it in your book. Will you not find the Prophet, then the Caliph? Then the Commander of the Faithful, then the kings after that, he said to him: Yes. (Naim bin Hammad 247)"
"38894","(38894) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, and he mentioned a man, and he said: He has been destroyed by stinginess. And the lining of it is evil."
"38895","(38895) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Jaham, on the authority of Abu Burdah ibn Dinar was referred to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The world will not pass away until you are at the time when the son of He was slapped (Ahmed 466)"
"38896","(38896) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that he heard his father. He said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, with his head shaved, crying, saying: I was not afraid to stay until Uthman was killed."
"38897","(38897) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr He said: Indeed, we find in the revealed Book of God two types in Hell: a people who, at the end of time, will have a whip as if it were With the tails of cows they strike people for no crime. They do not put anything into their bellies except evil, and clothed and naked women. They will not enter Paradise, nor will they smell its fragrance. (Muslim 1680)"
"38898","(38898) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Al-Hiyah bin Bastam Al-Hanzali narrated to us, saying: Laith narrated to us. Ibn Abi Salim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be princes You know and you deny, for whoever acquiesces to them will be saved, and whoever separates from them will be safe, or nearly so, and whoever comes into contact with them will be destroyed. (Tabarani 10973)"
"38899","(38899) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub informed me, on the authority of Abi Qabil, on the authority of Jesus On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: Send to people who will speak out about the corruption of the land. Then Ka’b Al-Ahbar said to him: Why not? Do so, for that is in the revealed Book of God: A people of whom it is said that hope carry whips in their hands as if they were The tails of cows do not give off the scent of Paradise, so do not be the first to be sent with them. He said: So he did, so I said: I Lehiya: What is the hope? He said: You call them the police in Iraq."
"38900","(38900) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Mardanaba, on the authority of Khalifa ibn Sa`d, who said: I saw Uthman in some The roads of Medina, and He says: Enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong before your evil ones gain power over you, so they will pray Your choices are upon them, but they will not be answered. He said: And his burden burdened him, so he took hold of his arms and said: I will not die until I die. The prince of boys overtakes me."
"38901","(38901) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāḥas ibn Qaym, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Ammar, who said: Awf ibn Malik said, O plague. Take me to you. They said: Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The longer a Muslim lives, the better for him? He said: Yes, but I fear six things: the rule of fools, the sale of power, the shedding of blood, severing ties of kinship, and many conditions. And they will arise, taking the Qur’an as psalms. (Ahmad 22. Tabarani 105)"
"38902","(38902) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Ubaid bin Tufayl Abu Sidan Al-Ghatfani narrated to us, saying: narrated to me. Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, said: Leave these proud-faced people as long as they leave you. By God, I wish that There is an unbearable sea between us and them."
"38903","(38903) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, he said: I asked Abu Jafar : Is there any disbelief in this nation? He said: I do not know it, nor is there polytheism. He said: I said: So what? He said: Transgression."
"38904","(38904) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Nashet told us, he said: Abu Abdul Malik told me A master of the Umayyads, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: There will be a trial from which no one can be saved except by supplications like supplications. Drowning (Naim bin Hammad 367. Ahmed 249)"
"38905","(38905) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad informed us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Masha, on the authority of Abu Umamah, He said: The Hour will not come until the worst of the people of the Levant turn to Iraq, and the best of the people of Iraq turn to the Levant."
"38906","(38906) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Ar-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Woe. The Arabs suffer from an approaching evil: the rule of boys. If they obey them, they will be admitted to Hell, and if they disobey them, they will behead them."
"38907","(38907) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: We used to talk about it being a response. Severe until some of the Arabs return to worshiping idols with Dhul-Khalisa."
"38908","(38908) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me the one who sent Ibn Muljim to prison. It turned black as if it were a burnt log."
"38909","(38909) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Al-Jalad, he said: There will be a trial. After that there will be a trial, the first in the afterlife: like the fruit of a whip followed by a sword fly, then after that there will be a trial. All incestuous matters will be permissible therein, and then the caliphate will come and the best of the people of the earth will remain in his house forever. (Abdul Razzaq 20771)"
"38910","(38910) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Muhammad, on the authority of Asim bin Amr Al-Bajli, that Abba Imamah, he said: To be called by the name of a man from heaven whom the humble will not deny, nor will the Mighty abstain from."
"38911","(38911) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman. Al-Nadhi, on the authority of Hudhayfi bin Al-Yaman, said: While some people were talking, when camels that had become immobilized passed by them, they said: Oh camels, Where is your family? You say: Our families were gathered together in sacrifice. (Bukhari 3608. Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 129)"
"38912","Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:\n(38912) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Al-Manhal told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmiy told us, he said My father told me, he said: Our besiegement took over, and against us was a man from Banu Sulaym called: Mujashi’ bin Masoud. He said: So when We opened it. He said: And I was wearing a shirt. I went to a dead man from among the non-Arabs whom we killed. He said: So I took a shirt. Some of those who were killed, he said: There was blood on him, so I washed him between stones, massaged him until I cleaned him, dressed him, and entered The village, so I took a needle and threads, and stitched my shirt, and Mujashi’ stood up and said: O people, do not exaggerate anything. He sewed something and will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, even if it were stitched.\n2. So I went to that shirt, took it off, and went to my shirt, and I started to tear it apart until, by God, my son, I made it tear. My shirt, fearing that the thread would break, so I set out with the threads, the needle, and the shirt that I had taken from the partitions. So I threw it into it, and then I had not left the world until I saw them boiling water, so when I said: What kind of thing is this? They said: A share of the booty is greater than this.\n3.Asim said: And my father saw a vision while they were besieged. He was crowned in opposition to Uthman, and whenever my father saw a vision, it was as if He looked at it during the day, and my father had met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He saw as if he was a sick man. It was as if people were disputing before him, their hands were changing and their voices were rising, and there was a woman wearing clothes. Khidr was sitting, as if if she wanted, she could make peace between them, when a man among them got up and turned the blanket of his forehead over him, then he said: O community of Muslims, will Islam be created among you, and this is the garment of the Prophet of God among you. It was not created, when the last of The people, so he took one of the two pages of the Qur’an and shook it until its pages were disturbed.\n4. He said: Then my father discovered it in the morning and did not find anyone to interpret it. He said: It was as if they were afraid of interpreting it.\n He said: My father said: When I reached Basra, the people had camped. He said: I said: What is the matter with them? He said: They said: It has reached them that A people marched to Othman and camped to overtake him and support him. Then Ibn Amir stood up and said: The Commander of the Faithful is righteous. The people had left him and returned to their homes, but he did not surprise them except to kill him. He said: Then my father said: I did not see There was never a day when he was the most weeping old man, and his beard was streaked with tears from that day.\n5.I only stayed for a short time until Al-Zubayr and Talha had reached Basra. He said: I only stayed for a short time after that. Until Ali also came and settled in Dhu Qar. He said: Two sheikhs from the neighborhood said to me: Take us to this man. So let us look at what he calls for, and what thing he brought with it. So we left until when we approached the people and discovered their tents. When a thick-skinned young man came out of the army, Al-Ala’ said: I saw that he said: On a mule, so when I looked at him, I looked like him. The mirror that I saw at the head of the sick person in sleep, so I said to my companions: If it were for the mirror that I saw in A dream about a sick person’s head is a brother. Indeed, this is her brother’s name.\n6. He said: Then one of the two sheikhs who were with me said to me: What do you want to do with this? He said: And he nudged me with his elbow, and the young man said: What is it? Did you say? He said: Then one of the two sheikhs said: He did not say anything, so he left. He said: You will tell me what you said. He said: So I related the vision to him. He said: I have seen, he said: and he was terrified, then he kept saying: I have seen, I have seen, until his voice ceased from us, he said: So I said to someone I met from the man we saw above. Muhammad bin Abi Bakr said: He said: So we knew that the woman Aisha\n7.He said: When I came to the army, I came to the enemy of the Arabs, meaning Ali. He said: By God, Ali has entered into the lineage of my people to the point of I began to say: By God, He is more knowledgeable about them than I am. He even said: Indeed, the people of Basra are more knowledgeable than the people before him. He said I said: Yes. He said: So he said: Are you the master of your people? I said: No, and I am obedient among them, and others are black, and I am more obedient to them than I am. He said: So he said: Who is the master of Banu Rasib? I said: So-and-so. He said: The leader of the Banu Qadamiya? He said: I said: So-and-so to another. He said: Will you convey to them two letters from me? I said: Yes.\n8. He said: Will you not pledge allegiance? He said: So the two sheikhs who were with me pledged their allegiance. He said: And some people who were with him became angry. He said: And my father said: With his hand: He held it and moved it as if there was something hidden in them. He said: Then they started saying: He sold out, he sold out. He said: And he ate. Prostrating their faces, he said: Then Ali said to the people: Leave the man, and my father said: My people have sent me as a pioneer and I will inform them. What you saw, if they pledge allegiance to you, I pledge allegiance to you, and if they withdraw from you, I will isolate you. He said: Then Ali said: What do you think, if your people had sent you? I was traveling, and I saw a meadow and a treacherous place, so I said: O my people, Al-Naja’a Al-Naja’a, but they refused. You are not seeking refuge with yourself. He said: So she took one of his fingers,Then I said: We pledge allegiance to you on the condition that we obey you as long as you obey God, so if you disobey Him, He will not obey you on the condition that we obey you. He said: Yes, and he continued at length. With his voice, he said: So I struck his hand.\n9. He said: Then he turned to Muhammad bin Hatib, who was near the people, and he said: Have you gone to your people in Basra? So I convey to them My letter and My words. He said: Then Muhammad turned to him and said: When I come to them, my people will say: What do you say? Your companion regarding Uthman. He said: Then those around him cursed him. He said: I saw Ali’s forehead dripping with hatred when they came. With it, he said: Then Muhammad said: O people, desist, for by God I do not ask of you, nor of you do I ask, he said: So Ali said: Tell them that what I said about Othman is the best, that Othman was with {those who believed and did righteous deeds, then feared Allah and believed, then Fear God and do good, and God loves the doers of good.\n10. He said: My father said: I did not leave until the Kufa came to me. They started meeting me and saying: Do you see our brothers from the people of Basra? They fight us, he said: and they laugh and marvel, then\n They said: By God, if we had met, we would have dealt with the truth. He said: It is as if they thought that they would not fight each other. He said: And I left. By the letter of Ali,As for one of the two men to whom he wrote, he accepted the letter and answered it, and I directed the other to him, and he hid. If only they had said: Kulayb did not give me permission, so I handed him the letter and said: This is Ali’s letter, and I told him that I told him that you are a master. Your people, he said: He refused to accept the letter, and said: I have no need of the masters today, but your masters today are similar. With dirt, or low things, or supplications, and he said: Speak to him, I have no need of that today, but he refused to answer him.\n11 He said, “By God, I did not return to Ali until the two armies approached us, and their servants took shelter, so the Qur’an who were with him rode off.” Ali when the people were stabbed, and I did not reach Ali until the people had finished fighting them. I entered Al-Ashtar and he was wounded. He said: Asim: There was a relationship between us and him through women, so when he looked at my father, he said, “The house is full of his companions.” He said: O Kulaib, you are more knowledgeable about insight than we are, so go and buy me a camel that you can find in it. He said: So I bought it from Arif bought a camel worth five hundred. He said: Take it to Aisha and say: May your son, the owner of peace, congratulate you, and say: She said: “Take this camel and show it to where your camel is.” She said: “No, may God’s peace be upon him. He is not my son.”He said: She refused to accept it.\n12 He said: So she returned to him and told him what she had said. He said: So he sat up straight.\n Then he rolled up his sleeve and said: Then he said: Indeed, Aisha blames me for the fatal death. Indeed, in your death, she came to Mudhahij, then Ibn Attab came down and embraced me, he said, and said: Kill me and Malik, he said: I struck him and he fell horribly, he said, then Ibn al-Zubayr jumped to me and said: Kill me and Malik. I do not like that he said: Kill me and al-Ashtar, nor that all of them are Mudhahjiyyah. She gave birth to a boy, and my father said: I performed the umrah on her while he was unaware. I said: What is the benefit to you if you say that all of your men should give birth to a boy? So my father said: I performed the umrah on her while he was unaware. I said: What is the benefit to you if I say: That all of your maidens give birth to a boy?\n13 He said: Then my father approached him and said: Advise me to the companion of sight, for he has a place for me after you. He said: And he said: If only my companion had seen you. Al-Basra He has honored you. He said: It is as if he saw that he was the prince. He said: Then my father left him and a man met him. He said: He said: The Commander of the Faithful stood before a preacher, so he appointed Ibn Abbas to the people of Basra, and claimed that he was going to the Levant. On the day of such-and-such, he said: So my father came back and told Al-Ashtar, he said: So he said to my father: You heard him.He said: So my father said: No. He said: Then he rebuked him and said: Sit down, this is falsehood. He said: I did not hesitate until a man came and told him. Like what he told me. He said: He said: Did you hear that? He said: He said: No, so he met with a river other than the one he called me to. He said: And he noticed me. And I am on the side of the people, that is, this has brought news similar to yours.\n14 He said: It was not long before Al-Taghlabi’s reproach came while the sword was threatening or striking at his neck, so he said: This is an Amir. Your believers have used his cousin Ali Al-Basra, and claimed that he was going to the Levant on such-and-such day. He said: He told him Al-Ashtar: You heard it, O One-eyed. He said: Yes, by God, O Ashtar, because I heard it with my ears. He said: Then he smiled. Therein is Kushur. He said: Then he said: Then we do not know why we killed the sheikh in Medina.\n15 He said: Then he said: For the time being, arise and ride, and he rode, and he said: And I do not see anyone coming that day except Mu’awiyah. He said: So Ali was about to send horses to fight him. He said: Then he wrote to him saying that he did not prevent me from commanding you not to You will be worthy of that, but I wanted to meet the people of the Levant, who are your people, so I wanted to seek your protection over them. He said: And he called the people to leave. He said: So Al-Ashtar stayed until the first people overtook him.He said: And the time had come for them on Monday, as you saw, so when Al-Ashtar did what he had done, he called out to the people before that. By leaving."
"38913","(38913) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of a man who named him, who said: I witnessed the camel on the Day of Judgment and did not enter a house. Al-Walid, except that I mentioned the day of the camel, and the swords falling on the white ones. He said: I used to see Ali carrying a lamb and striking him with his sword. Until he dissuades me, then comes back and says: Do not blame me, blame this man, then comes back and corrects him."
"38914","(38914) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Misra Abi Jamila, who said: On the first day you spoke The Kharijites on the Day of Camel, they said: Their blood is not lawful for us and their descendants and their wealth are unlawful for us. He said: Then Ali said: Indeed The family of manna is on the chest and the neck, and for you is five hundred, five hundred. The dependents"
"38915","(38915) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Harith bin Makhshi, who said: His opinion was Ali. Black, meaning the day of the camel, and those saw the camel."
"38916","(38916) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he said to a man: What did your mother do? He said: She has died. He said: You will fight her. He said: The man was amazed at that until Aisha left."
"38917","(38917) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ali divided the inheritance of the one who was killed on the Day of the Camel. The duties of Muslims: The woman gets her price, the son gets her share, the son gets her share, and the mother gets her share."
"38918","(38918) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: Ali was asked On the authority of the people of Al-Jamal, he said: It was said: Are they polytheists? He said: They fled from polytheism. It was said: Are they hypocrites? He said: Indeed, the hypocrites do not They remember Allah except a little. It was said: What is the matter? He said: Our brothers have transgressed against us. (Bayhaqi 173)"
"38919","(38919) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, that Ali did not curse on the Day of the Camel. He did not kill a wounded person. (Bayhaqi 182)"
"38920","(38920) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khayr, that Ali He did not curse on the day of the camel and he did not make the fifth. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, will you not make the fifth of their wealth? He said: So he said: This is it. Aisha is taking control of her. He said: They said: It is nothing but this. It is nothing but this."
"38921","(38921) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, that Al-Ashtar, And Ibn al-Zubayr met, and Ibn al-Zubayr said: I did not hit him even when he hit me five or six times. He said: Then he said: He threw me at my feet, then said: By God, had it not been for your closeness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would not have left a member of you with his companion. He said: And Aisha said: And He spoke asma. He said: And when it was after she had given what he had given her good tidings about, that ten thousand were alive."
"38922","(38922) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father informed me, that Ali said on the Day of the Camel: We bestow blessings upon them with the testimony that there is no god but Allah. We inherit from fathers from children. (Bayhaqi 182)"
"38923","(38923) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, he said: I heard Abu Ja’far say: Why The people of Al-Jamal are infidels."
"38924","(38924) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, he said: I heard Suwayd ibn al-Harith, he said: You have seen us. On the Day of the Camel, our spears and their spears will quarrel, and if the men wished, they would go against them. They say: God is Greatest, and they say: : Glory be to God, God is great, and so on; There is no doubt about it, and I wish I had not witnessed it, and Abdullah bin Salamah says: But I was not pleased that I had not witnessed it, and I would have wished. Verily, every witness bears witness to Ali. I bear witness to him. (Khalifa bin Khabat 191)"
"38925","(38925) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: Qays informed us, he said: Marwan bin The ruling on the day the camel was shot with an arrow in its knee. He said: He made the blood enrich the blood and make it flow. He said: When they caught him He held him, and when they left him he oozed. He said: So he said: They left him. He said: And when they held him they made the mouth of the wound his knees swelled, so he said: His supplication was nothing but an arrow sent by God. He said: Then he died. He said: So we buried him on the shore of Al-Kala’, and some of his family saw him. He said: Will you not relieve me from this water, for I have drowned? Three times, he said: So they exhumed him, and behold, he Green, like Swiss chard. So they drained the water from him, then they took him out, and behold, his beard and face covered the earth. The earth devoured him, so they bought him a house from the homes of Abi Bakra’s family for ten thousand and buried him in it."
"38926","(38926) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: When Aisha reached some of the waters of Banu Amir At night the dogs barked at her, and she said: What water is this? They said: The water of the Hawab, so she stopped and said: I only think it is She returned, and Talhah and Al-Zubair said to her: Have patience, may God have mercy on you. Rather, go forward and the Muslims will see you, and God will improve your soul. Among them, she said: I only think I am going back to you, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to us one day: How is it that the dogs of Hawab bark at one of you? (Ahmed 52, Naeem bin Hammad 188)"
"38927","(38927) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: Aisha said when she attended her death: Bury me with the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for I committed a crime after him."
"38928","(38928) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard my father. He said: Ali bin Abi conveyed the message. Talib, that Talha said: I only pledged the pledge of allegiance while the storm was on my back. He said: So he sent Ibn Abbas and asked them. He said: And Osama bin Zaid: As for the turmoil on his back, no, but he had pledged allegiance while he was unwilling. He said: Then the people jumped towards him to the point that they almost They killed him. He said: Then Suhayb came out while I was beside him. He turned to me and said: I thought that Umm Awf was coming to you."
"38929","(38929) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Karimah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Ali and his companions sat On the Day of the Camel, they will cry over Talhaha and Al-Zubayr."
"38930","(38930) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Nadra narrated to us, that Rabi’a spoke to Talha in the mosque of Banu Muslimah, and they said: We were in the enemy’s throat until she came to us and pledged your pledge to this man. Then you are now fighting him, or as they say, he said: so he said: I was brought into the garden and a storm was placed on my neck, and it was said: he pledged allegiance or else We fought you. He said: So I pledged allegiance, and I knew that we had pledged allegiance to him out of error. Al-Taymi said: Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik said: Indeed, he is a hypocrite. Among the hypocrites of the people of Iraq is Jabala bin Hakim. He said to Al-Zubair: Indeed, you have pledged allegiance. Al-Zubair said: The sword was placed on He stood up and it was said to me: Pledge your allegiance or else we will kill you. He said: So I pledged allegiance to you."
"38931","(38931) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Humaid bin Abdullah bin Al-Asam mention, on the authority of Umm Rashid, his grandmother, She said: I was with Umm Hani’ and he came to Ali, so she prayed for him with food, and he said: Why do I not see a pool with you? The sheep, she said: She said: Glory be to God, yes, by God, we have a blessing. He said: He only meant the sheep, she said: And I went down and met Two men were on the stairs, and I heard one of them saying to his friend: Our hands have pledged allegiance to him, but our hearts have not pledged allegiance to him. She said: So I said: Who are these two men? They said: Talhah and Al-Zubayr. She said: I heard one of them saying to his friend: I sold him to him. Our hearts did not pledge allegiance to Him, so Ali said: {So whoever breaks his promise only breaks it against himself, but whoever fulfills what he promised May God grant him a great reward."
"38932","(38932) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd Khayr, who said: He was beaten. There was a tent between the two soldiers on the Day of the Camel for three days, and Ali, Al-Zubayr and Talha were coming to him. And they will remember therein whatever God wills, until, on the third day, at noon, Ali raised the side of the tent, then ordered By fighting, we walked towards each other, and fought us with spears, so that if a man wanted to walk on them, he would have walked, then you took us. Swords are nothing like them except Dar al-Walid."
"38933","(38933) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khayr, on the authority of Ali, that he said Day of the Camel: Do not follow one who turns back, and do not attack a wounded man. And whoever lays down his weapon will be safe. (Hakim 1550, Bayhaqi 181)"
"38934","(38934) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais Al-Hadrami narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin and Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Hijr ibn Anbas, that Ali gave his companions five hundred five hundred for Basra."
"38935","(38935) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Masoud bin Saad Al-Jafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: When the people of the Camel were defeated, Ali said: They should not seek a slave coming out of the army, and he was not an animal. Or a weapon, it is yours, but you do not have a child’s mother, and inheritance is according to the commandments of God, and if any woman kills her husband, she must observe the waiting period. Four months and ten days. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, their blood is permissible for us, but their women are not permissible for us. He said: So they disputed with him. He said: Likewise is the conduct of the people of the qiblah. He said: So bring your arrows and cast lots for Aisha, for that is the beginning of the matter. And their leader, he said: Then they recognized and said: We ask forgiveness from God, he said: So their opponent was Ali."
"38936","(38936) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, he said: I heard Talha bin Ubaidullah say on the Day of the Camel: We were most pious in the matter of Uthman, so we have no alternative in terms of transactions."
"38937","(38937) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: None of the companions of the camel witnessed The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was from the Muhajireen and Ansar, except for Ali, Ammar, Talhah, and Al-Zubayr. If they brought a fifth, then I A liar (Ahmed 4096)"
"38938","(38938) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ziyad, he said: He said: Ammar bin Yasser: Our mother walked this path of ours, and by God she is the wife of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace in this world. And the Hereafter, but God tested us with it to know whether we should obey it or not. (Hakim 6)"
"38939","(38939) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Furat, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, he said: When Ali returned from the camel He prepared for Siffin and the Nakha'is gathered together until they entered Al-Ashtar. He said: Is there anything in the house except a Nakha'i? They said: No, so he said: This nation intended to do good to her and killed him, and we marched to the people of Basra, a people of ours. We were victorious over them by breaking their pledge, and tomorrow you will go to the people of the Levant, a people with whom you have no pledge of allegiance. Let one of you look where he puts his sword."
"38940","(38940) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issam bin Qadamah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Are you the companion of the polite camel? Many people around her will be killed, but she will then be saved. Almost (Ibn Abdul-Barr 1885)"
"38941","(38941) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Jana’, On the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: It was said to him: What prevented you from fighting for your insight on the Day of Camel? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: A people will emerge who will be destroyed and will not succeed. Their leader will be a woman, and their leader will be in Paradise (Musnad 4408)"
"38942","(38942) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: A people who entrust their affairs to a woman will never succeed."
"38943","(38943) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Jumman Al-Ja’fi, who said: “You saw us on the Day of the Camel, and our spears and their spears quarreled, and if a man wanted to walk on it, he would walk.” He said: And these people say: There is no god but God, and God is the greatest. And these people say: There is no god but God, and God is the greatest."
"38944","(38944) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, that when Ali defeated Talha and his companions, he ordered His call is that neither one coming nor one returning will be killed, nor will any door be opened, nor will privacy or wealth be made permissible."
"38945","(38945) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khayr, who said: Ali commanded a herald. Then he called out on the Day of the Camel: “The wounded shall not be attacked, nor shall the one who flees be pursued.”"
"38946","(38946) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: I carried a burden on a man on the day of the camel, so when I went to stab him. He said: I follow the religion of Ali bin Abi Talib, so I knew what he wanted, so I left him."
"38947","(38947) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Husayn, he said: Abbas narrated to us, He said: Ali sent me to Talha and al-Zubair on the Day of the Camel. He said: So I said to them: Your brother extends his greetings to you. And he says to you: Did you find any unfairness to me in a ruling, or to take advantage of a word, or such-and-such, or such-and-such? He said: So he said Al-Zubair: Not in either of them, but with fear comes the intensity of ambitions."
"38948","(38948) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: We were among the people and we were criticizing Othman, but when it was one day we became ungrateful, so I turned to Abdullah. Ibn Abbas, so I said to him: O Abu Abbas, do you remember the eve of the camel? I am to the right of Ali, and you are to his left. We heard the authentic hadith from Medina. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Yes, the one with which so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, was sent, and he informed him. He found the Mother of the Believers Aisha standing in the shrine cursing those who killed Uthman, so Ali said: May God curse those who killed Uthman. The plain, the mountain, the land, and the sea, I am on the right of Ali, and this is on his left, so I heard it from one mouth to another. And Ibn Abbas, by God, I have not criticized Othman to this day."
"38949","(38949) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Dirar Zayd ibn Asn al-Dhabi, the imam of the Bani Hilal Mosque, narrated to us, saying: Khaled bin Mujahid bin Hayyan Al-Dhabi, from Banu Mabdoul, told us, on the authority of his cousin, who is called: Tamim bin Dhal Al-Dhabi, He said: On the day the camel was riding with Ali, I was riding with him, and I saw that I was in Paradise and he was examining the dead. So he passed by. I admired a man who was killed, and he said: Who knows this? I said: This is so-and-so a lizard, and this is his son, until I counted seven dead men around him. He said: Then Ali said: I would have liked, There is no lizard on earth except under the page of this Sheikh."
"38950","(38950) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Yusuf Ibn Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Salt Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to Ali when he finished the camel, so he went to home while he was holding my hand, and behold, his wife and his two daughters were weeping, and they had made a newborn sit at the door, giving them the call to prayer. When he came, the newborn was treated to what you see women doing until he entered upon them, and I remained behind and stood at the door. They remained silent, and he said: What is the matter? So he broke up with them once, or twice, and one of them said: We said: You did not hear us mentioning Othman and his relatives, and Al-Zubayr and Talha and his relatives, and he said: Indeed, I hope that we will be like those. God said: {And We took away what was in Their breasts of hatred are brothers on beds facing each other. And who are they, if we are not?"
"38951","(38951) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, that Ali sat with Talha on the Day of the Camel, and wiped his He faced the dust, then turned to Hassan and said: I wish I had died before this. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 155)"
"38952","(38952) Qubaisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Khumayr ibn Malik, he said: Ammar said to Ali The Day of the Camel: What do you see about the captivity of offspring? He said, so he said: We only fought whoever fought us. He said: If you had said other than that. We disagreed with you (Bayhaqi 181)"
"38953","(38953) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Omar ibn Javan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: We presented Medina We wanted to perform Hajj, so we were in our homes, packing our bags, when someone came to us and said: The people were frightened and gathered in the mosque, so I set off. Then, when the people were gathered in the mosque, they saw Ali, Al-Zubayr, Talhah, and Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas. He said: “Indeed, we will be like that” when Othman came to us, and it was said: This is Othman, so a yellow militia entered upon him, with which he covered his head. He said: Is this Ali? They said: Yes. He said: Is this Al-Zubair? They said: Yes, he said: Is this Talhaha? They said: Yes, he said: Is this Saad? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: Whoever buys the land of the son of so-and-so, may God forgive him. So I bought it for twenty thousand, or for twenty-five thousand. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said to him: Did you buy it? He said: Put it in our mosque and you will have its reward? They said: Oh God, yes.\n2. He said: So he said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He bought a Roman woman, may God forgive him, so she bought her for such-and-such, then she came to him.So I said: I have bought it. He said: Make it water for the Muslims and reward it for you. They said: Oh God, yes.\n3. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at his faces? The people, and he said: Whoever repulses these, may God forgive him, meaning the army of hardship, so I recaptured them so that they did not miss a single foot. Nor a headband. He said: They said: Oh God, yes. He said: Oh God, bear witness three times.\n4. Al-Ahnaf said: So I set off and came to Talha and Al-Zubayr, and I said: Who do you command me to do and who do you approve of? I do not see him. He is nothing but killed. They said: We command you to marry Ali. He said: I said: You command me to do him and you are satisfied with him. They said: Yes.\n5. He said: Then I set out on Hajj until I came to Mecca, and we were there with us when the killing of Othman came upon us, and with Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, So I met her, and I said to her: Who do you command me to pledge allegiance to? She said: Ali, so I said: Do you command me to pledge allegiance to him and are satisfied with him? Lee, she said: Yes.\n6. So I passed by Ali in Medina and pledged allegiance to him, then I returned to the people of Basra, and I only see that the matter has settled. He said: While I was like that, someone came to me and said: This is Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and Talha and Al-Zubayr have encamped beside Al-Khuraiba,He said: I said: What brought them? He said: They were sent to you to seek your victory against the blood of Othman. He was killed unjustly. He said: Then the most horrific thing that had ever come to me came to me, so I said: Indeed These people have let me down, and with them was the Mother of the Believers and the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it is severe, and the fight against him is a cousin. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after they ordered me to sell you to Shadid. When I came to them, they said: We have come to seek your victory. For the blood of Othman, he was killed unjustly. He said: So I said: O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you by God. Did I tell you: whom do you command me to do? I said: Ali, so I said: Do you command me to do so and are satisfied with me? I said yes? She said: Yes, but he changed it.\n7. I said: O Zubayr, O disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and O Talhah, I appealed to you by God and told you: Who do you command me to do? You said: Ali. I said: You command me to do so and you are satisfied with me. You said: Yes. They said: Yes, but he changed it."
"38954","(38954) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Ja’far ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Umm al-Sayrifi, on the authority of Safwan ibn Qubaisa, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab said: When Othman was killed, I said: He will not guide me in Iraq, but rather the group is in Medina with the immigrants. And the Ansar. He said: So I went out and was informed that the people had pledged their allegiance to Ali. He said: So I went to Al-Rabdha and behold, Ali was with her. Then a saddle was placed for him, and he sat on it, and it was like a man standing. He thanked God and praised him, then he said, “Indeed, Talhah and Al-Zubayr have They pledged allegiance willingly and not under compulsion, then they wanted to spoil the matter and break the disobedience of the Muslims, and incited to fight them. He said: Then Al-Hasan bin Ali stood up and said: Did I not tell you that the Arabs will be on a rampage when this man is killed? If you stand up... In the house that you were in, meaning Medina, for I fear that you will be killed in a state of ruin, with no one to help you. He said: So he said Ali: Sit down, for you are cheating just as a slave girl cheats on you, or indeed someone cheats on you like you cheat on a slave girl. By God, I will sit in Medina. Like a hyena listening to the bite, it struck his back and stomach, or his head and eyes, and found nothing but a sword. Or disbelief. (Hakim 115)"
"38955","(38955) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Saif bin So-and-so bin Muawiyah Al-Anazi said: My uncle told me, on the authority of my grandfather, who said: When it was the Day of the Camel and the people were disturbed, the people got up They called upon Ali to say things, but they spoke much, but he did not understand them, so he said: Is there no man who combines his words with me? Five words, or six, so I stood on one of my legs and said: If he likes my words, otherwise I will sit close by, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, the words are not about five or six, but rather they are two words, digestion, or retaliation. He said: So he looked. Then he held thirty in his hand, then said: Have you seen what you counted? It is under my feet. (Abdul Razzaq 18586)"
"38956","(38956) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nazra, who said: They mentioned Ali and Uthman. Talha and Al-Zubayr were with Abu Sa’id, and he said: People who had precedents and who were afflicted by tribulations, so they were refuted. To God"
"38957","(38957) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, he said: Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to me, that Ali said on the Day of the Camel: Oh God, this is not what you wanted. Oh God, this is not what you wanted."
"38958","(38958) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: Marwan was with Talha on the Day of the Camel. He said: When The war broke out, and Marwan said: I will not seek revenge after today. He said: Then he shot an arrow at him and hit his knees. He bleed until he died. He said: And Talhah said: His call was nothing but an arrow sent by God."
"38959","(38959) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of his father, who said: Musa bin Talha was sent to me about A pilgrim, so I came to him. He said: While I was with him, some people from the mosque entered upon him and said: O Abu Issa, tell us about it. The captives were our night, so I heard them saying: As for Musa bin Talha, he was killed early. When I prayed the morning prayer, a man came. Al-Asari Al-Asari, he said: Then another came after him, saying: Musa bin Talha, Musa bin Talha, he said: So I set off. So I entered upon the Commander of the Faithful and greeted him, and he said: Do you make a pledge of allegiance and enter into what the people have entered into? I said: Yes. He said: Thus, and he extended He spread out his hands and said: So I pledged allegiance to him. Then he said: Go back to your family and property. He said: When the people saw that I had left, he said: They began to enter and pledge allegiance."
"38960","(38960) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Suddi {And beware of temptations that will not strike those who do wrong among you alone}, he said: The owners of the sentences. (Tabarani 218)"
"38961","(38961) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Awf. He said: I do not know him except on the authority of Al-Hasan in his saying: {And fear temptations that will not befall you. Those who do wrong among you are particular. He said: So-and-so and so-and-so."
"38962","(38962) Waki` informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, that a man mentioned to Ali the companions of the camel. Until he mentioned disbelief, Ali forbade it."
"38963","(38963) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Harith bin Makhshi, who said: I have never witnessed a day more severe than this. The day of Ulysses, except the day of the camel."
"38964","(38964) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, who said: There were two or three months between Siffin and the camel."
"38965","(38965) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Abu Jafar, He said: On the Day of the Camel, Ali heard a voice speaking to the Mother of the Believers, so he said: Look what they say. Then they came back and said: They shouted that he would kill him. Othman, and he said: O God, glorify him by killing Othman in shame. (Ibn Asakir 457)"
"38966","(38966) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Ali bin Amr Al-Thaqafi, he said: Aisha said: Because I sat on my path was more beloved to me than having companions from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, like the descendants of Al-Harith bin Hisham."
"38967","(38967) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudhaylah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Surad, who said: I came to Ali on the day of the camel, while Al-Hasan and some of his companions were with him. Then Ali said when he saw me: O Ibn Sarrad, you hesitated and moved and waited. How do you see what God has done? God has helped you. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, the stage is a long one, and there are still matters in which you know your enemy from your friend. He said: When he got up Al-Hassan I met him and said: I do not see that you spared me anything or excused me with the man, and I was keen for you to bear witness. With him, he said: This one blames you for what he blames you, and he said to me on the Day of Camel: when the people walked towards each other: Oh Hassan. Your mother has bereaved you, or your mother has made you miserable. What do you think about my affairs brings together these two sorrows? By God, I will not see after this. Good, he said: So I said: Be quiet, your companions will not hear you, and they will say: You doubted, and they will kill you. (Naim bin Hammad 207)"
"38968","(38968) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man came to Al-Zubayr on the day of the camel, and he said: Kill Thank you for Ali. He said: He was sufficient. He said: I will come to him and tell him that he is with him. Then I will issue a fatwa for him. Al-Zubayr said: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: Faith is subject to destruction, no believer can destroy it."
"38969","(38969) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: When Al-Zubair stood on the day of the camel, he called me and I stood beside him. He said: No one will be killed except an oppressor or an oppressed person, and I will not kill him. He showed me that today I will be killed unjustly, and that my greatest concern is for my religion. Do you think that our religion leaves something of our wealth remaining? Then he said: O my son, sell our wealth and pay off our debt, and I bequeath to you a third and two-thirds to your children. If any of our wealth remains after paying off One-third of the debt is for your child. Abdullah bin Al-Zubair said: Then he began to advise me of your debt and said: O my son, if you are unable, About something\n From him; So seek help from my master. He said: By God, I did not know what he wanted until I said: Oh my father, who is your master? He said: God. He said: By God, I never fell into religious distress except that I said: O master of Zubair, pay off his debt, and he fulfilled it. He said: Al-Zubayr was killed, and he did not leave behind a dinar or a dirham except two lands, including the forest, and eleven houses in Medina. They went around Basra, they went around Kufa, and they went around Egypt. He said: It was only what was upon him, that the man was He brings him money and he entrusts it to him, and Al-Zubair says: No, but he is a predecessor. I fear that he will be lost, and what He had no guardianship at all, nor any taxes, nor taxes, nor anything, unless he was on a campaign with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Or with Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman."
"38970","(38970) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad, On the authority of his father, that when Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam arrived at Al-Basra, he entered the treasury, and behold, it was yellow and white, and he said: God says: {And God has promised you many spoils that you may take, so He hastened these for you} {And others which you have not been able to obtain. God surrounded it} and said: This is for us."
"38971","(38971) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali ordered a caller to call him, and he called on the Day of Basra: No one who flees is pursued, nor is a wounded man hurled, nor a captive killed. He who closes a door is safe, and he who lays down his weapon is safe. And he did not take any of their belongings. (Bayhaqi 181)"
"38972","(38972) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, who said: When Zaid bin Suhan was injured on the Day of the Camel, He said: This is what my friend Salman Al-Farisi told me: This nation is only destroyed by breaking its promises."
"38973","(38973) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Aisha said: I wished I was a tender branch and did not follow this path."
"38974","(38974) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Ubaid bin Saad, on the authority of Aisha She was asked about her journey, and she said: It was fate."
"38975","(38975) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyy, that Ali appointed the day of the camel in the army. No weapon or herdsmen were attacked against him."
"38976","(38976) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajlili, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash He said: Ali said: I hope that I, Talhah, and Al-Zubayr will be among those who, God said: (And We will remove whatever hatred is from their breasts.)"
"38977","(38977) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Amr bin Murra narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin He greeted him, he said: And he witnessed with Ali the camel and Siffin, and said: I am not pleased with them whatever is on the earth."
"38978","(38978) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, or Muhammad bin Talha, said To Aisha on the Day of the Camel: O Mother of the Believers, what do you command me? She said: O my son, if you are able to be like the best of Son of Adam, do it. (Naim bin Hammad 170)"
"38979","(38979) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Ali said on the day Sentences: I wish I had died twenty years before this."
"38980","(38980) Ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Yazid bin Dubay’. Al-Absi, on the authority of Ali, that he said on the Day of Camel: The one who flees will not be followed, nor will the wounded be hurled."
"38981","(38981) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of a man from Banu Dubay’a. He said: When Talhah and Al-Zubayr came, they encamped at Banu Tahiyya, so I mounted my horse and went to them and entered. They were in front of the mosque, so I said: You are two men from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I appeal to you by God on your journey. I promise Is it the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or is it an opinion that you have seen? As for Talhah, he bowed his head and did not speak. As for Al-Zubayr, he said: Tell us that here is a lot of knowledge, so we came. We take from it."
"38982","(38982) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abdul Salam, a man from Banu Hayya, who said: Ali was alone with Al-Zubayr on the Day of the Camel, and he said: I adjure you by God, how I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: And you put my hand in the shed of the Banu So-and-so: You will fight him while you are unjust to him, then they will be victorious against you. He said: You have heard, no. Crime, I will not fight you."
"38983","(38983) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais, he said: He who saw Al-Zubayr narrated to me. The horse came crashing down with the spear, and Ali mentioned it: O Abdullah, O Abdullah. He said: So he approached until their necks met. Their animals. He said: Then Ali said to him: I adjure you by God. Do you remember the day the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and I was speaking to you? He said: Shall I speak to you? By God, one day he will fight you while he is unjust to you. He said: Then Al-Zubayr struck the face of his animal and he left. (Musnad 4409)"
"38984","(38984) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Muhammad, he said: Ali passed by One of the people of Basra killed him, so he said: O God, forgive them, and with him were Muhammad bin Abi Bakr and Ammar bin Yasir, and he said: One of them said to the other: We do not hear what he says, so the other said to him: Be quiet, he will not add to you."
"38985","(38985) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to me, on the authority of Jahsh bin Ziyad Al-Dhabi, he said: I heard Al-Ahnaf bin Qays says: When Ali appeared on the people of Al-Jamal, he sent to Aisha: Return to Medina and to your home. He said She refused. He said: So he returned the messenger to her. By God, you will either return, or I will send to you wives from Bakr bin Wael, who have blacksmith’s blades with them, and we took you with them. When she saw That's how she came out."
"38986","(38986) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibn Abza, he said: Abdullah bin Budil went to Aisha while she was in the lodge on the Day of the Camel, and said: O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you. By God, do you know that I came to you on the day Othman was killed, and said: Othman has been killed, so do not command me, so you said to him: Stick to it. Ali, by God, he did not change or alter it, so she remained silent. Then he repeated it to her three times, and she remained silent. He said: Harrow the camel, so they harrowed it. He said: So I and her brother, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, went down and stayed at the lodge until we placed it in Ali’s hands, so he gave orders for it. Ali, and he was brought into the house of Abdullah bin Budail. Ja’far bin Abi Al-Mughirah said: My aunt was with Abdullah bin Alternatively, my aunt told me that Aisha said to her: Let me in. She said: So I let her inside and I came to her violently. And a jug, and she opened the door, saying: I saw her through the door, and she was dealing with something in her head. Do you know whether it is a stone or a stone?"
"38987","(38987) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, he said: Sulayman bin Surad came to Ali bin Abi Talib, after he had finished fighting on the Day of the Camel, and he had companions with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Ali said to him: You have let us down and sat among us, and you attacked the heads of the people. So Sulaiman met Al-Hassan bin Ali, and he said: You have not met a prince. The believers, he said: He said such-and-such to me over the heads of the people, so he said: No, let this one of him deceive you, for he is a warrior. I saw him on the day of the camel, when the swords took their point, and he said: I wish I had died twenty days before this day. Sunnah"
"38988","(38988) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Qays, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, who said: He accepted Talhah and Al-Zubayr until they came down to Basra and threw out Sahl ibn Hanif. This was reported to Ali, and Ali was sent to him. Ali, so he came until he came down to Dhu Qar, so he sent Abdullah bin Abbas to Kufa, but they were slow to reach him, then he came to them. Ammar, so they left. Zaid said: I was among those who went out with him. He said: So he refrained from Talhah, al-Zubayr, and their companions, and he called them. Until they started him, so he fought them after the noon prayer, and as soon as the sun set, the eyes of those who were defending him began to blink around the camel. Then Ali said: Do not kill a wounded man, and do not kill one who is fleeing, and whoever closes his door and lays down his weapons is safe. Their fighting was only That evening alone.\n2. So they came the next day talking to Ali about the spoils, so he recited these verses to me and said: As for Allah, He says: {And know that Whatever you spoil, then one-fifth of it belongs to God and to the Messenger. Which of you is Aisha? They said: Glory be to God. Our mother. He said: Ahram. They said: : Yes, Ali said: He is deprived of her daughters what is deprived of her.\n He said: Do they not have to observe the waiting period for the dead for four months and ten? They said: Yes, he said: Do they not have to wait a quarter? And the eighth is from their wives. They said: Yes, he said: Then he said: What is the matter with the orphans that they do not take their money? Then he said: O Qanbar. Whoever knows something should take it. Zaid said: He returned what was in the army and others.\n3. He said: And Ali said to Talha and Al-Zubair: Didn’t you pledge allegiance to me? They said: We ask for the blood of Othman. Ali said: I do not have the blood of Othman. He said: Omar bin Qais said: Then a man from Hadhramaut, who is said to have spoken to us. According to Abu Qais, he said: When Qanbar called out to anyone who knows something, let him take it, a man passed by with a pot of ours while we were cooking in it. So he took it, and we said: He left it until what was in it was cooked. He said: So he struck it with his foot, then they took it away. (Tahawi 212)"
"38989","(38989) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abu Musa and Abu Masoud entered. Ali Ammar while he was mobilizing the people, and they said: We have not seen anything from you since you embraced Islam that is more distasteful to us than your haste in this matter. Ammar said: I have not seen anything from you since you converted to Islam that is more hateful to me than your slowness in this matter. He said: So they clothed them. They came together and went out to pray together."
"38990","(38990) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: Sulayman bin Surad Al-Khuza’i said To Al-Hasan bin Ali: Excuse me before the Commander of the Faithful, for he only prevented me from the Day of the Camel such-and-such. He said: So he said Al-Hassan: I saw him, when the fighting became intense, running to me and saying: Oh Hassan, I wish I had died twenty years before this. Hajj (Naim bin Hammad 177)"
"38991","(38991) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd Al-Adawi, who said: He was killed among us. On the Day of the Camel, fifty men will recite the Qur’an around the camel."
"38992","(38992) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: I saw, or there was doubt, Yahya’s opinion of Ali on the day of Siffin with Hashim bin Utba, and he was a man He was one-eyed, so Ammar attacked him and said: Come forward, O one-eyed man. There is no good in a one-eyed man. Fear does not come, so he should be ashamed and come forward. He said : Amr ibn Al-Aas says: I see the owner of the black flag doing a deed. If he continued as I see, the Arabs would be destroyed today. He said: So what? Abu Al-Yaqzan went on until he ceased between them. He said: And he says, “All the water comes in, and all the water comes in, be patient, servants of God. Paradise is beneath Shadows of swords."
"38993","(38993) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Ajda’ Al-Laythi, who was one of those who witnessed Siffin, said: Ammar used to go out between Siffin, and the banners had been raised, so he would call out. Until He hears them with the loudest voice: Go to Paradise, the beautiful fair eyes have become beautiful. (Ibn Asakir 464)"
"38994","(38994) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Muslimama, he said: I heard ablution, he said: I heard Ammar bin Yasir. He says: Whoever is pleased to be surrounded by the beautiful virgins, let him advance between the two lines, seeking reward, for I see a line of people who will strike you. A type of which the unjust people doubt, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, if they had struck us until they reached the level of the Palms of Hijr, you would have known that we On the truth, and they are on error."
"38995","(38995) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, or on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari. On the authority of Ammar, he said: If they had beaten us until they reached the Safaat of Hijr, we would have known that we are upon the truth, and that they are upon falsehood."
"38996","(38996) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Riyah bin Al-Harith, he said: I was next to Ammar. Ibn Yasser in Siffin, and my knee touched his knee, and a man said: The people of Syria are infidels, so Ammar said: Do not say that, our Prophet. And their Prophet is one, and our qiblah and their qiblah are one, but they are a misguided people who have deviated from the truth, so it is right upon us that We will fight them until they return to it."
"38997","(38997) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash ibn al-Harith, on the authority of a sheikh who is called Riyaah, who said: Ammar said: Do not say: The people of the Levant disbelieved, but they said: They were unjust and unjust."
"38998","(38998) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Riyah, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Do not say: The people of the Levant are infidels. But they said: They were ungrateful and unjust."
"38999","(38999) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the Awwam, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: He saw in a dream Abu Al-Maisara Amr bin Shurahbil, who was one of the best companions of Abdullah, said: I saw as if I had entered Paradise. I saw a damaged dome, so I said: Who is this for? It was said: This is for Dhul-Kilaa and Hawshab, and they were among those who were killed with Muawiyah on the day of Siffin. He said: I said: Where is Ammar? And his companions, they said: In front of you. I said: How is it, and some of them killed others? He said: It was said: They met God and found Him spacious. Forgiveness. He said: So I said: What did the people of the day do? He said: So it was said: They met with destruction. (Ibn Saad 263. Na’im 143)"
"39000","(39000) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Aswad bin Masoud told me, on the authority of Hanzali bin Khuwaylid Al-Asri said: I was sitting with Muawiyah when two men came to him and were disputing over Ammar’s head, each of them... One of them says: I killed him. Abdullah bin Amr said: Let one of you bless his friend with it, for I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: The transgressing group will kill him. So Mu’awiyah said: Will your madman not be of use to us? O Amr, what do you think about us? He said: I am with you and I am not fighting. He refused to complain to me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Obey your father as long as he lives and do not disobey him, for I am with you, and I will not fight him. (Nasa’i 8549, Ahmad 164)"
"39001","(39001) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Saad ibn Ibrahim, who said: While Ali was holding the hand of Uday ibn Hatim was going around killing people when he passed by a man whom I recognized, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, take my promise to this, and he is a believer. He said: And now."
"39002","(39002) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Qaqa’, he said: I saw Ali on the Prophet’s mule. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Al-Shaba’i wanders among the dead."
"39003","(39003) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Salib al-Faq’asi Abu Asad narrated to us. On the authority of his uncle, he said: The stakes of our tents on the day of Siffin were nothing but the dead, and we were not able to eat food from The stench, he said: And a man said: Whoever called for the mule on the day the people of Syria disbelieved, he said: So he said: From the disbelief they fled. (Bukhari 3015)"
"39004","(39004) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Hakam bin Saad, He said: They have unshackled their spears in two rows and we have unshackled our spears, and if there were a human being among us to walk on them, he would do so."
"39005","(39005) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ali, he said: When he fought Mu'awiyah preceded him to the water and said: Call them, for the water will not prevent you."
"39006","(39006) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Ammar is killed by the transgressing group. (Muslim 2236. Ahmad 311)"
"39007","(39007) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Muhallab narrated to me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mihran, he said: Someone who heard Ali say on the day of Siffin while biting his lip told me: If I had known that the matter would be like this, I would not have gone out. Go, O Abu Musa, and judge, even if it cuts your throat."
"39008","(39008) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, that Ali said to Abu Musa: Judge even if you feel sad. My neck (Ibn Asakir 95)"
"39009","(39009) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: When Ali returned from Siffin, he learned that there was no He reigned forever, so he spoke things that he did not speak, and he spoke things that he did not speak, and he said, He says: O people, do not hate the Emirate of Muawiyah. By God, if you had lost him, you would have seen the heads coming down from the Its berries are like coconut."
"39010","(39010) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais narrated to us, saying: I heard Hujr bin Anbas, he said: It was said: On the day of Siffin, Ali may have come between us and the water. He said: So he said: Send for Al-Ash’ath. He said: Then he came and said: Come to me. In Dara' Ibn Sahar, a man from Banu Bara' came and poured water on him, then he came to them and fought them until he removed them from the water."
"39011","(39011) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hassan, he said: I heard him, he said: he said Ali is for the two arbitrators: That you both judge according to what is in the Book of God, and the Book of God is entirely mine. If you do not judge according to what is in the Book God, there is no government for you."
"39012","(39012) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, saying: I heard Ja’far, he said: Ali said: If you two In the Book of God, then you may live as long as the Qur’an has given life, and you may kill as long as the Qur’an has killed, and do not deviate."
"39013","(39013) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Hassan mentioning on the authority of His mother, the Muslims killed Ubaid Allah ibn Umar on the day of Siffin, and the Muslims took his plunder and wealth."
"39014","(39014) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: When a prisoner was brought to Ali one day Siffin took his animal and his weapons, ordered him not to return, and let him go."
"39015","(39015) Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: He reported Those killed on the day of Siffin were seventy thousand, and they could not count them except with reeds. They placed a reed on each person, then counted them. The reed"
"39016","(39016) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, he said: Kaysan told us, he said: Mawla Yazid bin Bilal told me, He said: I witnessed Ali with Siffin, and when a prisoner was brought, he would say: I will not kill you out of patience, for I fear God, Lord of the worlds. He used to take his weapons and swear that he would not fight him, and give him four dirhams."
"39017","(39017) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: It was said to him: I witnessed Siffin. He said: Yes, and wretched. Saffron was."
"39018","(39018) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, regarding his saying: {And if two parties of the believers fought So make peace between them, and if one of them transgresses against the other, then fight the one that transgresses until she submits to the command of God.} He said: With the sword. He said: I said: What did they kill? He said: Marked martyrs. He said: I said: What is the condition of the afterlife, the people of transgression, of those who were killed? He said: To the fire."
"39019","(39019) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: More than one person told me that a judge from the Levant came. Omar, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, a vision that has frightened me. He said: What is it? He said: I saw the sun and the moon fighting. And the stars are with them in two halves. He said: So I was with the two halves. He said: I was with the moon above the sun. Then Umar said: {And We made the night And the Fire are two signs, so We erased the signs of the night and made the signs of the Fire visible. So go, and by God, you will never do any work for me. Ata’ said: I was informed that he was killed with Muawiyah on the day of Siffin."
"39020","(39020) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: Abdullah ibn Urwah informed me, he said: They informed me. A man witnessed Siffin and said: I saw Ali going out one of those nights, and he looked at the people of Syria and said: O God, forgive me. And to them, then Ammar came and that was mentioned to him, and he said: Bring back to him the dangerous thing he did to you, meaning Saad, may God have mercy on him. (Ibn Asakir 346)"
"39021","(39021) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, who said: I saw Ammar On the day of Siffin, an old man was very tall, his hands were trembling, and he had a spear in his hand. He said: If only they would strike us to the point of hitting us with palms. Hajar, you would know that our reformers are upon the truth and that they are upon falsehood. (Ibn Saad 2561, Ahmad 319)"
"39022","(39022) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Qadamah al-Jumahi narrated to us, saying: Omar ibn Harun narrated to me. Shuaib, brother of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: When the people raised their hands from Siffin, Amr bin Al-As:\nThe war broke out and I prepared for it \nAl-Harek Branch, Mallawi Al-Thabaj\nThe stress is connected to a stress, then \nAnd the horses came out of the snow\nJerash'a is the greatest Jefratah \nIf he gets wet from the water, he will cleanse himself\n He said: Abdullah bin Amr said in poetry:\nIf a camel were to stand in my place \nAt Siffin one day, the wolves were young from it.\nOn the eve of the night, the people of Iraq came as if they were \nSpring clouds raised by the sides\nAnd We came to them as if they were our own ranks \nFrom the sea a tide of waves coming together.\nSo our millstones turned around and their millstones turned around \nDuring the daylight, as long as the ships turn towards you\nWhen you said, “They turned away quickly,” it would seem to us \nbattalions of them, and battalions of them swayed\nThey said to us: We think that you should pledge allegiance \nAli, so we said, “Rather, we see that you should fight"
"39023","(39023) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Jundub was With Ali on the day of Siffin, and Hammad said: He was not fighting him."
"39024","(39024) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I told him: He witnessed the protection of Siffin. He said: Yes, and he dyed his hair. He cut his sword and killed his brother, Ubayy bin Qais. (Ibn Saad 87)"
"39025","(39025) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Alqamiya returned on the day of Siffin. He dyed his sword with Ali."
"39026","(39026) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il’s brother, who said: Saul bin Hanif said on the day of Siffin: O people, follow your own opinion, for by God we did not put our swords on our shoulders with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he delivered us to a matter that terrifies us, unless they lead us to a matter that we know is different from this. (Bukhari 3181, Muslim 1412)"
"39027","(39027) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, that he heard him say: I saw Ammar on the day of Siffin, an old man, tall, holding a spear in his hand, his hand trembling, and he said: By the one in whose hand my soul is, if they strike us Until they reach us at the Palms of Hijr, you will know that our reformers are upon the truth, and that they are upon falsehood. (Ahmed 319)"
"39028","(39028) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi, on the authority of his father He said: I was leaving the mosque when I saw Ibn Abbas when he came from Muawiyah in the matter of the two rulers, so he entered the house of Suleiman. Ibn Rabi’ah, so I entered with him, and he kept throwing a man at him, then a man after a man. O Ibn Abbas, you have disbelieved and associated And I denounced, “God said such-and-such in His Book,” and “God said such-and-such,” and “God said such-and-such,” until that part of that entered me. He said: “And who?” They, by God, are the first Sunnah, the companions of Muhammad. They, by God, are the companions of robes and bracelets.\n2. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Look to your opponent, the one who is most disputing with you, and the most knowledgeable of your proof, so let him speak. So they chose a one-eyed man. It was said to him: A reproach from the Banu who defeated him. So he stood up and said: God said such-and-such, and God said such-and-such, as if he was taking away his need from The Qur’an is in one surah.\n3. He said: Ibn Abbas said: I see you reading the Qur’an, knowing what it has explained and connected. I adjure you by Allah, there is no god but Him. Did you know that the people of the Levant asked about the matter, so we thought about it and refused, but when wounds befell you and pain afflicted you, And you were withheld from the water of the Euphrates, and you began to seek it, and Mu'awiyah informed me that he had brought a horse with a long belly from the ground. To flee against him, until one of you came to him and said: I have left the people of Iraq waving like people in the midst of a crowd. In Mecca, they say differently in every respect, like the night of the group in Mecca.\n4. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said, I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him, what kind of man was Abu Bakr? They said: Good and praised him, so he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab? So they said good and praised him, so he said: What do you think if a man went out for Hajj or Umrah and hit a gazelle or some vermin? The earth, and one of them alone ruled over it. Did it belong to him? And God says: “Those of justice will rule over it.” So you did not differ concerning it Of the matter of a mother is greater. He says: So do not deny two arbitrators for the blood of a mother. God has made two arbiters for killing a bird. Between the disagreement of a man and his wife, He made two arbitrators to establish justice and fairness between them regarding what they disagreed about."
"39029","(39029) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: When Ali walked to Siffin He appointed Abu Masoud as his successor over the people, and he addressed them on Friday. He saw that there were few of them, so he said: O people, come out, and whoever He went out and was safe. We know, by God, that there are among you who hate this face and are sluggish. Get out, and whoever left. So he is safe, and by God we do not consider her to be healthy if these two ghars meet and one of them protects the other, but we consider her May God reconcile Muhammad’s mother and bring her together. Shall I not tell you about Othman, and what the people were displeased with? Indeed, they did not They call upon him and his sin until God punishes him or pardons him, and they did not realize what they sought when they envied what He had given him. God bless him, so when he came to Ali, he said to him: You are the one who said, “I have not heard anything about you, O Farrukh. You are an old man and your mind has lost.” He said: My mother has given me a name better than this. It has melted my mind, and the jinn has been guaranteed for me from God and from His Messenger, you know. You, and what was left of my mind, we were talking about the other being evil, and the other was evil. He said: When it was with Al-Silhayn, or with Al-Qadisiyah He went out to them and their fingernails were dripping with tar. It was seen that he had prepared for ihram, so when he put his feet in stitches and took At the back of his messenger, a group of people came up to him and said: If only you would come back to us, Abu Masoud. Then he said: You must be pious. God and the people, for God will not unite the mother of Muhammad upon misguidance. He said: So they returned against him, and he said: On you with the fear of God. As for the group, it is only a righteous person who finds comfort, or relief from an immoral person."
"39030","(39030) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ammarah bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, he said: It still My grandfather matched his weapons on the Day of Siffin and on the Day of Jamal until Ammar was killed. When he was killed, he drew his sword and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: You kill Ammar the transgressing group, so he fought until he was killed. (Tabarani 3720)"
"39031","(39031) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Warqa’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of Amr bin Al-Aas. On the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ammar is killed by the transgressing group. (Ahmad 1974, Abu Ali 7304)"
"39032","(39032) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: When it was the day of Siffin As the war intensified, he invited Ammar to drink milk, so he drank it, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: There is another The drink you drink from this world is a drink of milk. (Musnad 444)"
"39033","(39033) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan Al-Asadi, he said: I saw Ali On the day of Siffin, Dhu al-Faqar had with him the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: We will arrest him, and he escaped and was carried. On them, he said: Then he will come, he said: Then he will bear on them, he said: Then he came with his sword, bent, and said: This is He apologizes to you. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 160)"
"39034","(39034) Shababah told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: I asked the arbiter: Did Abu Ayyub witness Siffin? He said: No, but Witnessed on the day of the day."
"39035","(39035) Omar bin Ayyub Al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, who said: Ali was asked about He killed me on the Day of Siffin, so he said: We killed them and their killed ones in Paradise, and the matter will be up to me and to Muawiyah. (Ibn Asakir 139)"
"39036","(39036) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, who said: He mentioned The Kharijites, he said: Among them is a man with a bruised hand, or one with a bowed hand, or one with a trembling hand. Had you not become hasty, I would have told you what God has promised. Those who kill them on the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Did you hear it from Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba three times. (Muslim 1558, Ibn Majah 167)"
"39037","(39037) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yusir bin Amr, he said: I asked Saul bin Hanif, I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning these Kharijites. He said: I heard him, and he pointed with his hand towards the east. There will emerge from it a people who will recite the Qur’an with their tongues, with nothing more than their throats, and they will be driven away from religion as an arrow is driven away from Archery."
"39038","(39038) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: At the end of time there will emerge a people with young teeth and foolish dreams, who speak the best of people, who recite the Qur’an without It will go beyond their collarbones, and they will be thrown away from Islam just as an arrow is thrown away from a target. So whoever meets them, let him kill them. Whoever kills them has a reward from God."
"39039","(39039) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Kharijites are the dogs of fire. (Ibn Majah 1731, Ahmad 355)"
"39040","(39040) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, he said: They mentioned the Kharijites with my father. Huraira, he said: Those are the worst of creation."
"39041","(39041) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Asim bin Shammikh, who said: I heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri He says, “And his hands are like this,” meaning they are trembling with pride: Fighting the Kharijites is more beloved to me than fighting their own people. Shirk"
"39042","(39042) Ibn Numair narrated to us, saying: Ubad Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: When Ibn Umar heard of our help, he came And he wants to go to Medina, and he will take women captive and kill children. He said: Then we will not leave him and that, and he intended to fight him. He incited the people, and it was said to him: The people will not fight with you, and we fear that you will be left alone, so he left him."
"39043","(39043) Abd al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I heard them mentioning that Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd invaded the Kharijites."
"39044","(39044) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: After me, or there will be after me from my nation, there will be a people They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They leave religion just as an arrow comes out of an arrow. They do not return from it. They are the worst of creation and creation. Abdullah bin Al-Samit said: I mentioned that to Rafi’ bin Amr, my nephew, Al-Ghaffari, and he said: I also heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 7500, Ahmad 31)"
"39045","(39045) Amr bin Yahya bin Amr bin Salma Al-Hamdani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: We were We were sitting at Abdullah’s door waiting for him to come out to us, so he came out and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that A people who recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats, and they will fall away from Islam just as an arrow leaves an arrow, and God will not I know, perhaps most of them are among you. He said: Amr bin Salamah said: We saw those people attacking us on the Day of Narwān with Kharijites"
"39046","(39046) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid al-Rawasi narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Tahya, who said: Ali heard a man from the Kharijites while he was praying the dawn prayer, saying: {And it was revealed to To you and to those before you: If you associate, your work will surely be nullified and you will be among the losers.} He said: So he left behind his surah which It was in it. He said: And he recited {So be patient. Indeed, the promise of God is true, and do not let those who are not certain make you afraid}"
"39047","(39047) Qattan bin Abdullah Abu Murri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I was in the mosque of Damascus, and they brought seventy One of the heads of the Haruriyah was placed on the stairs of the mosque, and Abu Imamah came and looked at them and said: The dogs of Hell, evil. Those who killed me were killed under the shade of the sky, and those who killed were better than those who were killed under the sky. He cried and looked at me and said: O Abu Ghalib, you are From the country of these people? I said: Yes. He said: I seek refuge in you. He said: I think so.\n He said: God is among them. He said: You recite the Family of Imran. I said: Yes. He said: {Among them are decisive verses. They are the mother of the Book, and others are similar. As for those in whose hearts there is deviation, they follow that which is similar to it, seeking temptation and seeking its interpretation, and He does not know Its interpretation is “except Allah and those who are firmly rooted in knowledge.” And He said: “On the day when faces will be whitened and faces will turn black, as for those Their faces: Did you disbelieve after your faith? So taste the torment because you disbelieved. I said: O Abu Imamah, I saw you. Your interpretation. He said: Yes, have mercy on them. They were among the people of Islam. He said: The Children of Israel have divided over each other. Seventy-one sects, and this nation will add one sect, all of them will be in the Fire except the greatest over them. Loose and upon you is what you have been burdened with, and if you obey Him, you will be guided. The Messenger’s duty is only to convey the message. Hearing and obedience are better than disunity. And disobedience, and a man said to him: O Abu Imamah, is this what he saw you saying or something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Then I am bold.” He said, “Rather, I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more than once or twice.” He even mentioned seven."
"39048","(39048) Zayd ibn Harun al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Suleiman al-Taymimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: He forbade. His companions must spread the word over the Kharijites until they cause an incident, so they passed by Abdullah bin Khabab and took him, so he passed by. Some of them were looking for fallen dates from a palm tree, so he took them and threw them in his mouth, and some of them said: We used to meet dates, so what? She made it lawful, so he threw it out of his mouth. Then they passed by a pig, and some of them bit it with their swords, and some of them said: A reconciled pig. Why did I make it permissible? Abdullah said: Shall I not guide you to something that is more forbidden to you than this? They said: Yes. He said: I So they brought him forward and beheaded him, so Ali sent to them to lead us to Abdullah bin Khabab, so they sent to him: and that was enough. Your exile and we all killed him. He said: Did all of you kill him? They said: Yes, so he said: God is great. Then he ordered his companions to spread peace over them. He said: By God, not even ten of you will be killed. And not ten of them escaped. He said: So they killed them. He said: Seek among them the mammal. So they sought him and he was brought to him. He said: Who knows him? They did not find anyone who knew him except a man. He said: I saw him confused, so I said to him: Where do you want? He said: This, and pointed to the Kufa, but he did not know it. He said: So Ali said: He spoke the truth, and he is one of the jinn. (Abu Ubaid 475. Daraqutni 131)"
"39049","(39049) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: When he met... Ali is the Kharijite, the Muslims attacked them, and by God, not nine of the Muslims were afflicted until even their souls were destroyed."
"39050","(39050) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jumhan, he said: The Kharijites were They invited me to the point that I was about to enter among them, then Abu Bilal’s sister saw in a dream as if she had seen Abu Bilal imprisoned. He said: So I said: O brother, what is the matter with you? He said: Then he said: After you, we will be made into the dogs of the people of Hell."
"39051","(39051) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: A man from Abdul Qais told me, he said: I was with the Kharijites and saw some of them that I disliked, so I left them on the condition that I did not I told them more, and while I was with a group of them when they saw a man coming out as if he was terrified, and among them and him A river. They crossed to the river and said: As if we had taken care of you. He said: Yes. They said: Who are you? He said: I am Abdullah bin Khabbab. Ibn Al-Art, they said: Do you have a hadith that you narrated to us, on the authority of your father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: My father narrated to me on the authority of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, a trial is coming, the one who sits in it is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands in it is better than the one walking. So when you meet them, if you can be the servant of God who was killed, then do not be the servant of God who was killed. He said: So they brought him close to the day. They beheaded him, and I saw his blood flowing over the water as if it were a trap that had been loosened in the water until he disappeared from it. Then they called She was pregnant with a woman, so they forgot about what was in her womb. (Ahmad 1100, Darqutni 132)"
"39052","(39052) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Musa bin Muhammad Al-Ansari told us, he said: Yahya bin Hayyan told me, On the authority of Jabala bin Suhaym and So-and-so bin Nadla, who said: Ali was sent to the Kharijites and said: Do not fight them until they are called to something. They were in need of a gift or provision in security from Allah and His Messenger, but they refused and took captives of us."
"39053","(39053) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais Al-Hadrami narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab said: Ali addressed us in Al-Mada’in with the Dizjan arch, and he said: It was mentioned to me that a kharijiya emerges from Before the east among them was a mammal, and I do not know whether they were these or others. He said: So they went off and met some of them. Some of them, and the Haruriyah said: Do not speak to them as you spoke to them on the day of Haruriyah. So they spoke to them, and you returned. He said: So he became angry. They attacked each other with spears, and some of Ali’s companions said: They cut off the camels. He said: Then they turned around and killed them, and some of Ali’s companions were killed. Twelve, or thirteen, and he said: Search for it, so they searched for it and found it, so he said: By God, I neither lied nor lied. Work and rely, for had you not relied, I would have informed you of what God has decreed for you on the tongue of your Prophet. Then he said: We have certainly witnessed People in Yemen said: How is that, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: Their guidance was with us. (Muslim 748. Abu Dawud 4735)"
"39054","(39054) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Abu Shaybā informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Barakah. Al-Sayyidi, he said: When Ali killed the mammal, Saad said: He killed Ibn Abi Talib, and he was afraid of apostasy."
"39055","(39055) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abu Razin He said: When the government was in Siffin and the Kharijites made clear to Ali, they returned, opposing him, and they were in the army, and Ali In the army, until Ali entered Kufa with the people in his army, and they went to Harwara in their army, so he sent Ali Ibn Abbas came to them and spoke to them, but he did not meet any of them. So Ali went out to them and spoke to them until they agreed. They and he were well-pleased, so they returned until they entered Kufa, although he and them were well-pleased, so they stayed for two days, or something like that. He said: Then Al-Ash’ath ibn Qais entered and was entering upon Ali, and he said: The people are talking that you have returned from their disbelief. When the next day came and Friday came, he ascended the pulpit, thanked and praised God, and delivered a sermon, reminding them of their differences. The people and their affairs, which they separated from, so he criticized them and criticized their affairs. He said: When he came down from the pulpit, they called out from around the mosque. There is no judgment except for God. So Ali said: God’s judgment. I wait for you. Then he said with his hand: This is how He will calm them down with signs. And he was on the pulpit until a man from among them came to him and put his two fingers in his ears and said: {If you Your work will be nullified, and you will be among the losers."
"39056","(39056) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he mentioned the Kharijites in his presence, and he mentioned their worship and diligence, and he said: They are not more diligent than Jews and Christians, then they pray. (Abdul Razzaq 18665)"
"39057","(39057) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he mentioned what the Kharijites meet with the Qur’an, and he said: They believe when it is judged and are destroyed when it is judged. similar (Abdul Razzaq 20895)"
"39058","(39058) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf, he said: Abdullah bin Salam asked me about the Kharijites, and I said: They are the people who pray the longest and fast the most, except that when they They left the bridge, shed blood, and took the money. He said: Do not ask about them except that, but I have told them: Do not kill Othman. His supplication, by God, if you leave him alone for eleven nights, he will surely die in his bed. And they did not do so. Whenever a prophet is killed, seventy thousand people are killed, and no caliph is killed but thirty-five thousand are killed."
"39059","(39059) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, that a man A boy was born to him at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed for him and took the good news from his forehead and said this to her: He winked at his forehead and prayed for blessings upon him, saying: Then his hair grew on his forehead as if it were the mane of a horse, so he grew young. The boy, when the time of the Kharijites came, he loved them and the hair fell from his forehead, so his father took him and tied him up out of fear. To join them. He said: So we entered upon him and admonished him and said to him what we say: Did you not see that his blessing was the supplication of the Messenger of God? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. You fell from your forehead, so we remained with him until he returned, according to their opinion. He said: So God restored it to him. The hair was still on his forehead, and he repented and made amends. (Ahmad 456)"
"39060","(39060) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: The Kharijites were mentioned by Abu Hurairah. He said: Those are the worst of creation."
"39061","(39061) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Abu Shaybi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Barakah al-Sayyidi. He said: When Ali killed the mammal, Sa`d said: Ali was killed by the genus of apostasy."
"39062","(39062) Affan told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim bin Damra, he said: Indeed, it is outside. She came out with a ruling, so they said: There is no ruling except for God. So Ali said: There is no rule except for God, but they said: There is no command. People do not need a righteous prince or an immoral person. The believer works in his emirate and the disbeliever enjoys it, and God is conveyed. Therein is the term. (Bayhaqi 184)"
"39063","(39063) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz disputed with the Kharijites, and whoever of them returned returned. A group of them refused to return, so Omar sent a man on horseback and ordered him to stop where they were traveling, but not He will move them, but he will not stir them up. If they kill and spread corruption in the land, then spread peace over them and fight them, even if they do not. They kill but do not spread corruption in the land, so let them go."
"39064","(39064) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I said to Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioning anything in the Hurriyah? He said: Yes, I heard it. He mentions a people whom they worship, and one of you will be degraded by his prayers with their prayers and his fasting with their fasts, and they will be banished from the religion as An arrow flew from the target, so he took his arrow and looked at its blade and did not see anything. Then he looked at its tip and did not see anything. So he looked in his mug and did not see anything, so he looked in the filth and wondered whether he saw anything or not. (Bukhari 3610, Ahmed 33)"
"39065","(39065) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, he said: I wanted to go out. I went with Abu Qalaba to Mecca, so I asked permission to enter, and I said: Come in. He said: If you are not a Hurriyya."
"39066","(39066) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Ka'b, he said: He who is killed by the Kharijites has ten lights, eight lights are preferred over the light of the martyrs."
"39067","(39067) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Na’am, on the authority of Khalid, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: They turned away Without us, and if I had been there and had my weapons, I would have fought against it, meaning we would have saved it and its companions."
"39068","(39068) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of his father, who said: I bear witness that the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us: They shed sacred blood and cut off the path, so in his book he disavowed the Hurriyah and ordered them to be fought."
"39069","(39069) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Siyah narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I came to him and asked him about these people whom Ali killed. He said: I said: Why did they leave him, and why? Did they make it permissible, and why did he summon them, and why did they separate from him, and then make their blood permissible? He said: When killing broke out among the people of the Levant in Siffin, Muawiyah and his companions camped out in a mountain, and Amr ibn al-Aas said: Send it to Ali with the Qur’an, but no, by God, he will not return it to you. He said: Then a man brought it to him, carrying it and calling out: Between us. And among you is the Book of God. {Have you not seen those who were given a share of the Book being called to the Book of God to judge between them? Then a party of them will turn away, and they will turn away.” He said: Then Ali said: Yes, between us and you is the Book of God. I am worthy of Because of you\n2. He said: Then the Kharijites came, and we called them at that time the Qara’is. He said: They came with their swords on their shoulders, and they said: O Commander of the Faithful, shall we not go to these people until God judges between us and them? Then Sahl bin Hanif, and he said: O people, accuse yourselves. We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Al-Hudaybiyah, if we saw fighting, we would have fought.This is in the reconciliation that was made between the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the polytheists.\n Then Omar came and he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, are we not on the right, and they are on the wrong? He said: Yes, he said: Weren't those who killed us in Paradise, and those who killed them in Hell? He said: Yes, he said: So why should we give this worldly life for the sake of our religion, and then go back, when God has judged between us and them? He said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of God, and God will never forsake me.\n3. He said: So Omar went off and was not patient, angry, until he came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, are we not on the right, and they are on the right? Invalid? He said: Yes, he said: Weren't those who killed us in Paradise, and those who killed them in Hell? He said: Yes, he said: Why should we give this worldly life in exchange for our religion and then go back, when God judges between us and them? He said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of God, and God will never abandon him.\n4. He said: Then the Qur’an was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the opening, so it was sent to Omar, who read it to him, and said: Oh. Messenger of God, or Fatah? He said: Yes, and his soul was at ease and he returned.\n5. Ali said: O people, this has been conquered, so Ali accepted the matter and returned, and the people returned.\n6. Then they went out with Harwara,These are a group of Kharijites, numbering fifteen thousand. So he sent to them an appeal to God, but they refused. Then Sa`sa` bin Suhan came to them and called upon them to God, and said: Why are you fighting your caliph? They said: We fear temptation. He said: So do not hasten to go astray of the year, for fear of the temptation of a coming year. So they returned and said: We will go astray. As for us, if Ali accepts the decree, we will fight him as we fought them on the day of Siffin, and if he renounces it, we will fight with him.\n7. So they traveled until they reached Narawan, then a group separated from them, and they began to kill the people. Then their companions said: Woe to you! As for this, Ali separated from us, so their matter was conveyed to Ali, so he got up and addressed the people, and said: What do you see? Are you going to the people of the Levant? Or will you return to those who were left behind to your descendants? They said: No, but we will return to them. So he mentioned their matter, and narrated about them what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about them: Indeed, a faction will emerge when people disagree, and the closest of the two factions will kill them in truth. Their sign is a man among them, his hand. Like a woman's breasts.\n8. So they walked until they met with fire, and they fought fiercely, and Ali's horses became unable to stand up to them, so Ali got up and said: O people, if you are only fighting for me,By God, I do not have anything to reward you with, and if you are only fighting for the sake of God, then this should not be your fight. So the people carried One man carried him severely, and the horses left them, with their faces folded, and Ali said: Seek the man. Among them, he said: The people searched, but did not find him, until some of them said: We deceived Ibn Abi Talib from among our brothers until we killed them. Then Ali’s eyes shed tears. He said: So he called for his animal and rode it, and set off until he came and guided him, and there he killed some of them. Ali, so he started dragging with their feet, until he found the man underneath them, so they dragged him, and Ali said: God is Great, and the people rejoiced. They returned, and Ali said: I will not attack the people. He returned to Kufa and was killed, and Hasan was appointed as his successor, so he followed the path of his father. Then He sent the sale to Muawiyah. (Abu Ali 469)"
"39070","(39070) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Ali, who said: When it was the Day of Narwān He met the Kharijites and did not leave until they attacked them with spears and killed them all. Then Ali said: Seek the mammal, so they sought him but he did not. They found him, and Ali said: You neither lied nor did I lie. They searched for him, and they searched for him and found him in a valley on the ground. Some people were among the dead, and behold, there was a man with something like the feces of a feline on his hand. He said: So Ali and the people said the greatest, and the people were amazed, so he was amazed. Ali"
"39071","(39071) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murā, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of a man from Banu Nasr bin Muawiyah said: We were with Ali and they mentioned the people of the river, but a man reviled them. Ali said: Do not curse them, but... If they revolt against a just imam, then fight them, but if they revolt against an unjust imam, do not fight them, for they have a chance to do so."
"39072","(39072) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qays, on the authority of Sharik bin Shihab. Al-Harithi said: I made myself wish to meet a man from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, who would tell me about the Kharijites. So I met Abu Barza Al-Aslami with a group of his companions on the day of Arafah, and I said: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, speaking about the Kharijites, and he said: I will tell you about what my ears heard and my eyes saw. The Messenger of God came to God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, received dinars and began to divide them, and with him was a black man with long hair, wearing two garments. White, with traces of prostration between his eyes, and he was facing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not give it to him. So he came to him and showed him his face from the front, but he did not give him anything. So he came to him from the right side, but he did not give him anything. Then he came to him from his left and did not give him anything. Then he came to him from behind him and did not give him anything, so he said: O Muhammad, what Since that day, I have changed my oath, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became very angry, then he said: By God, you will not find Someone was more fair to you than me three times, then he said: Men will emerge against you from the east, as if he were one of them. Their guidance is like this. They recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats. They are driven away from religion as an arrow is driven away from religion. The shooting, then they will not return to it. He placed his hand on his chest and their mark was flying. They will not continue to go out until The last of them will go out with the Antichrist, so when you see them, kill them three times. The worst of creation and creation is what he says. Three."
"39073","(39073) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Qurayh ibn Khalid al-Sadusi narrated to me, saying: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, on the authority of Habir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A people will come who will recite the Qur’an but it will not exceed their throats. They will be shot from the religion just as an arrow is shot from the target."
"39074","(39074) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There will be people from my nation who will recite the Qur’an, who will depart from Islam just as an arrow departs from archery."
"39075","(39075) Zayd ibn Hubab told us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaid informed me, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Abu Salama and Ata’ bin Yassar said: We came to Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri and said: I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said something about the haruriyah, and he said: I do not know what the haruriyah is, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: After you will come people who will despise your prayers with their prayers, and your fasting with theirs, and your worship with them. Their worship, they recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats, they are driven away from religion just as an arrow escapes from an arrow."
"39076","(39076) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala bin Abi Al-Abbas narrated to us. ,\n He said: I heard Abu Tufayl telling, on the authority of Bakr ibn Qarash, on the authority of Saad ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: peace be upon him, and he mentioned the mammal, who was with the Companions of the River, and he said: The devil of corruption, a man of By his generation, he is called: Al-Ashhab, or Ibn Al-Ashhab, a sign against an unjust people.\n Ammar Al-Dhani said, when he lied about it: A man came from Bajil, he said: And he saw him, he said: From a place, it is said to him. Al-Ashhab, or Ibn Al-Ashhab. (Ahmad 1798, Abu Ali 780)"
"39077","(39077) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hassan, he said: The Kharijites said to Omar Ibn Abdul Aziz: You want to follow the path of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, so he said: What is the matter with them? God has fought them. By God, you have not increased. To take the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as an imam. (Ibn Hazm 624)"
"39078","(39078) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: While Abdullah bin Khabab was in the hands of The Kharijites, when they came to a palm tree, and a man among them ate some dates, and his companions came to him and said to him: You took some of the dates. The people of the covenant, and they came upon a pig, and a man among them stabbed it with a sword, and his companions approached him and said to him: You have killed him. A pig from the pigs of the people of the covenant. He said: Then Abdullah said, Shall I not inform you of someone who has a greater right over you than this? They said: Who? He said: I did not neglect a prayer, nor did I neglect such-and-such, nor did I neglect such-and-such. He said: So they killed him. He said: When he came to them. Ali, he said: Handcuff us to Abdullah bin Khabab. They said: How can we handcuff you to him, when all of us have shared in his blood? So he made it lawful. He fought them."
"39079","(39079) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Murra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah. He said: He had witnessed with Ali the camel and Siffin, and he said: Not everything on the face of the earth pleases me with them."
"39080","(39080) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, he said: I asked my father about this. The verse: {Say: Shall we inform you of those who lose their deeds - those whose striving has gone astray in the life of this world?} Is it the Haruriya? He said: No, the People of the Book are the Jews and Christians. As for the Jews, they denied Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Christians disbelieved in the Garden and said: There is neither food nor drink in it, but the Haruriyya: {Those who break God’s covenant from after their covenant, and they sever what God has commanded to be joined, and they spread corruption in the land. It is they who are the losers.} And Sa`d was He calls them the transgressors. (Bukhari 4728, Hakim 370)"
"39081","(39081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: My father was asked about the Kharijites. He said: They are a people who have strayed, so God has caused their hearts to stray."
"39082","(39082) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Nu’aym bin Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abu Maryam narrated to me, that Shabath bin Rabi’i And Ibn Al-Kawawi left Kufa for Harwara, so Ali ordered the people to come out with their weapons, so they went to the mosque. Until the mosque was filled, so Ali sent to them: “Evil is what you did when you entered the mosque with your weapons. Go to Murad’s graveyard until my command comes to you. He said: Abu Maryam said: So we went to Murad’s graveyard, and we were there soon. One day, then we were informed that the people had returned, or that they were returning.\n2. He said: So I said: I will go and look at them. He said: So I set out and began to penetrate their ranks until I came to Shabath bin Rabi'iyyah and Ibn al-Kawa'i, and they were standing on their mounts, and with them were messengers of the Most High, appealing to God for what They returned, and they were saying to them: We seek refuge with you in God not to hasten the general tribulation for fear of a coming year. Then a man from among them rose to Some of Ali’s messengers saddled his animal, so the man came down and was about to recover, so he picked up his saddle and set off with it, and what they say:\n We only asked for your rejection, and they are appealing to God.\n3. So they stayed for an hour, then they left for Kufa as if it were the day of Sacrifice, or the day of breaking the fast.And Ali was telling us before that, that some people leave Islam, and they will be thrown away from it just as an arrow is thrown away from an arrow. Their sign was a man with a crippled hand. He said: I heard that from him many times. He said: And Nafi’ heard it: the crippled one as well. Until I saw him neglecting his food because of what he had heard from him so much. He said: Nafi’ was with us in the mosque and he would pray in it. During the day, and he spent the night therein, and I had covered him with a cloak, so I met him the next day and asked him: Had he gone out with the people? Those who went out to Harwara. He said: I went out to seek them. When I reached the tribe of so-and-so, two boys met me and they took away my weapons. So I returned until the year came, or something like that, and the people of Nahrawan came out and Ali went to them, but I did not go out with him.\n4. He said: My brother Abu Abdullah and his master went out with Ali. He said: Then Abu Abdullah told me that Ali went to them. Even when their shoes were on the shore of Narawan, God sent to them imploring them and ordering them to return, and they did not stop. His Messengers fought against them until they killed His Messenger. When he saw that, he rose up to them and fought them until he finished with them. All of them, then he ordered his companions to seek the conceived one, and they sought him. Some of them said: We will not find him alive, and some of them said: What's wrong with them?Then a man came to him and gave him good news, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, by God, we found him dead under two legs. Then he said: Cut off his bleeding hand and bring it to you. When it was brought, he took it in his hand, then raised it, then said: By God, I have neither lied nor been lied to."
"39083","(39083) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa, that when Ali was brought with the conceived person, he prostrated."
"39084","(39084) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Husayn, who was the companion of Ali’s police, he said: Ali said: May God kill them, meaning the hadith they liked, meaning the Kharijites whom he killed."
"39085","(39085) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Salama ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Kathir ibn Nimr, he said: It is with us. In the Friday prayer, Ali bin Abi Talib was on the pulpit when a man stood up and said: There is no judgment except for God. Then another man rose and said: There is no judgment. Except for God. Then they stood up from the corners of the mosque, judging by God. He motioned to them with his hand: Sit down. Yes, there is no judgment except for God. A true word is intended for falsehood. God’s judgment awaits you. Now I have three things for you during your time with us. We prevent you from the mosques of God lest His name be mentioned in them, and we will not prevent you from anything as long as your hands are with our hands, nor We will fight you until you fight us. Then he began his engagement. (Bayhaqi 184)"
"39086","(39086) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Husayl bin Saad bin Hudhaifa, he said: Habib Abu Al-Hasan Al-Absi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: A man entered the mosque and said: There is no ruling. Except for God. Then another said: There is no judgment except for God. He said: Then Ali said: There is no judgment except for God. Indeed, God’s promise is true, and He does not make you light. Those who do not have certainty} So you do not know what they are saying. They say: There is no authority. O people, no one can make peace with you except a leader. A righteous person, or an immoral person. They said: This is righteousness we know, so what about the immoral person? So he said: The believer works and fulfills the duties of the immoral person, and conveys the message. God is the final term, and your paths will be secure, and your markets will be straight, and your victory will be divided, and your enemy will fight, and the weak will be taken from among The strong one, or he said: Who is the strong among you?"
"39087","(39087) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman and Al-Dahhak bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger has come to us. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was dividing spoils on the day of Hunayn, and a man from Banu Tamim, called Dhu, came to him. Al-Khawsarah, and he said: O Messenger of God, be just. He said: Behold, I have failed and lost if I do not be just. Omar said: Leave me alone. Messenger of God, I will kill him. He said: No. Indeed, this has companions who go out when people disagree and recite the Qur’an but do not go beyond it. Their throats, they will be thrown away from religion as arrows are thrown from the target. You will despise your prayers with their prayers and your fasting with them. Their fasting, I gave them to a man from among them as if his hand was a woman’s breast, and as if it were a lump rolling out. He said: Then Abu Saeed: My ears heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn, and my eyes saw with Ali when he killed them, then He took it out and I looked at it. (Bukhari 6163. Ahmed 65)"
"39088","(39088) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, saying: Mujalid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Umair bin Zuzi. I refuse many. He said: Ali gave us a speech one day, then the Kharijites stood up and interrupted his speech. He said: So he came down and he entered and we entered. With him, and he said: I only ate it on the day the white bull was eaten. Then he said: My example is like three bulls and a lion gathered together in Dark: white, red, and black. Whenever he wanted one of them, they would come together, but he would refrain from it, so he would say to the red one. And the black one: Indeed, we do not expose ourselves in this thicket of ours except to the place of this white one, so leave it alone until Eat it, then you and I will be alone in this thicket, and your color will be the same as mine, and my color will be the same as yours. He said: So they did. He said Then he jumped on him and did not wait until he killed him.\n2. He said: So when one of them wanted to meet, they refused, so he said to Al-Ahmar: O Red, he does not share with us in our community. This is except the place of this black one, so leave it alone until we eat it, then you and I will be alone, so color it on me. Your color and your color are the same as mine. He said: So he caught him and jumped on him, but it did not take long for him to kill him.\n3. Then he remained for as long as God willed, then he said to Red: O Red, I will eat you. He said: You will eat me. He said: Yes. He said: Either no, so he left me. Until I make three votes, then it's up to you. He said: He said: I only ate on the day the white bull was eaten. He said: Then Ali said: No, I was only weak on the day Uthman was killed."
"39089","(39089) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Ali’s five people are the people of the river."
"39090","(39090) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Ali divided among his companions the slave of the people of the river And all their goods."
"39091","(39091) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of a man from Banu Tamim, who said: I asked Ibn Umar Concerning the wealth of the Kharijites, he said: There is neither spoils of war nor unjust slaves in it."
"39092","(39092) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The mosque panicked when the people of the river were attacked."
"39093","(39093) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Whoever heard Abu Sa’id told me. Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said about fighting the Kharijites: It is more beloved to me than killing Daylam."
"39094","(39094) Zayd bin Harun told us: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Asir bin Amr, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Hanif, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A people will come from the East, with their heads shaved. (Muslim 160)"
"39095","(39095) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When he was prevented Ali Al-Hakameen. The people of Al-Harwari said: You do not want us to have intercourse with these people. So they went out and Iblis came to them and said: Where? These were the people who separated from us as Muslims, but our opinion was miserable, and if they were infidels, we should have communion with them. Al-Hasan said: Then Abu Al-Hasan jumped on them and stabbed them to pieces."
"39096","(39096) Shababa told us, on the authority of Al-Dhail bin Bilal, who said: I was with Muhammad bin Sirin, and a man came to him and said: I have a boy of mine that I want to sell. I was given six hundred dirhams for it, and the Kharijites gave me eight hundred dirhams for it. Should I sell it to one of them? He said: Was my seller a Jew or a Christian? He said: No. He said: So do not sell it to one of them."
"39097","(39097) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal bin Mihalil narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, he said: I was with Ali, and he was asked about the people of the river, are they polytheists? He said: They fled from polytheism. It was said: Are they hypocrites? He said: Indeed, the hypocrites do not mention God except a little. It was said to him: What is the matter? He said: A people who have transgressed against us. (Ibn Nasr 593)"
"39098","(39098) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Arfaja, on the authority of his father, he said: When Ali was brought with what was in the army of the people of the river. He said: Whoever recognizes something, let him take it. He said: So they took it except by a measure. He said: Then I saw it had been taken."
